parts:
- text: "I’ll review Praxis I’s latest capsule for context and plan ablations while the evaluation runs, then return to check results.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{preview 10,8}`\n`/execute_action{read 10}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Praxis II Launch Plan @tick300: α ablations and Gaussian edge weights\"\ntags: \"plan, ablation, fwpca, balanced-graph, gaussian weights\"\ncontent: |\n  Context:\n  - Current best (Praxis I): EtC(FWPCA α=0.5) + BRBG + BBSG (binary) at 0.7363.\n  - Submitted (505): α=0.3 in embedding + local Gaussian connectivities on BBSG distances.\n\n  Hypotheses:\n  - Reducing α weakens variance down-weighting, preserving biological structure → ↑ASW_label with minimal loss in batch mixing.\n  - Replacing binary edges with locally scaled Gaussian weights adds magnitude information while preserving BBSG topology → potentially ↑ASW_label and Graph_conn without hurting kBET/iLISI.\n\n  Ablation plan (to isolate effects per\
    \ Codex):\n  - A1 (α-only): α=0.3 with original binary BBSG edges (control for Gaussian weighting).\n  - A2 (weights-only): α=0.5 (as Praxis I) with local Gaussian edge weights only.\n  - A3 (combined): α=0.3 + Gaussian weights (already submitted as 505).\n  - A4 (grid if warranted): α ∈ {0.2, 0.4} with binary edges to map sensitivity.\n\n  Metrics focus:\n  - Target ↑ASW_label and maintain high kBET/iLISI, Graph_conn.\n  - Watch Cell_cycle (prior 0.373 normalized), ensure no degradation.\n\n  Implementation notes:\n  - Gaussian weights from distances: w_ij = exp(-d_ij^2 / (2 σ_i^2)), σ_i = median row distance + eps, symmetrize by max.\n  - Keep BBSG quotas and BRBG residualization unchanged.\n\n  Next actions:\n  - Await 505 result; then submit A1 (α=0.3, binary edges).\n  - If A1 improves ASW_label with minimal trade-offs, proceed A2 to quantify weight effect.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`"
