  \ from the storage root.**Examining the storage setup**\n\nOkay, I see that the previous code added the 'storage' root, which includes 'praxis' as a top-level module. Now, I’m trying to figure out where 'praxis' resides. It might be in 'storage/praxis,' which aligns with the lineage name. I can indeed list its contents with 'storage list praxis.' \n\nNow, for our next submission, we want to improve upon a score of 0.7363. Perhaps weighted Gaussian edges could enhance ASW_label and Graph_conn. We should also explore EIDs from capsule 10, and even though we can preview it, I think it’s better to read both #10 and #8 fully since we've got the token budget to spare!**Reviewing summary and adjustments**\n\nI think we should preview item 10, as we previously attempted but didn’t see it. So, I'll make sure to read it now. It’ll be useful to create a Private Memory Capsule summarizing our immediate plan and the ablation strategies to align with the codex. \n\nNext, I want to implement local Gaussian\
  \ weights more effectively. I need to ensure I'm using distances correctly, although Dg is likely not symmetric. We have symmetrized using maximum values. I'll double-check that the shapes for connectivities and distances match, especially since the graph builder provides binary connectivities and distances. \n\nAdditionally, I spotted a potential issue with using the `dtype` parameter in the `np.exp` function; it's not accepted, so that’s a bug we need to address.**Addressing errors and planning next steps**\n\nI noticed that using the `dtype` parameter with `np.exp()` caused an error since it’s unexpected. I need to fix this by computing the exponent first and then casting it to `dtype`. While I submitted the code, I'd prefer to resolve issues proactively.\n\nNow we're waiting for the results, and I can propose additional ablation strategies. I want to preview capsules 10 and 8 in Private Memory and maybe check the weights function later. I’ll plan to summarize my findings and proposed\
  \ actions to keep everything organized!**Planning next steps**\n\nI think we should propose a measure to maintain Graph_conn, even though raising weighted edges might not be crucial. We need to keep things minimal and focused. After reading, we'll go back to the Research Counter, perhaps using a simple command to return.\n\nFor our actions, I’ll prepare commands to execute, ensuring each one is on a separate line. I’ll remember to quote titles with colons and consider writing the Gaussian weighting function to avoid duplication, but I won't read capsule 8 until after capsule 10 to save tokens. Alright, let's move forward!"
