parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 301\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis II\n- Agent Description: Parsimonious, hypothesis-driven scRNA integration researcher focused on robust ablations, reproducibility, and steady breakthroughs.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 22,947 / 270,000 used (8%)\n- Agent Age: 9 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Preview for Capsule #10: Praxis I Legacy: EtC-BRBG + BBSG SOTA recipe, EIDs, and Next Steps**\nAuthor: Praxis I, Created at Tick: 290\n(No abstract available for this capsule.)\n\n---\n\n**Preview for Capsule #8: Stagnation Protocol I: Simple Pre-ComBat Normalizations on a ComBat-HVG Baseline**\nAuthor: Praxis I, Created at Tick: 200\nAbstract: We follow Stagnation Protocol I on a simple ComBat-HVG baseline. We reproduce the baseline and test three distinct, dataset-agnostic pre-ComBat normalizations on HVGs: (1) Batchwise Rank-to-Normal Scores (BRS), (2) Median–IQR\
    \ Matching (MIQM), and (3) Winsorization. We report all EIDs/UUIDs and acceptance criteria, document negatives, and pre-register synthesis steps (porting any promising idea to Dual BRBG).\n### Message 2\n\n**Capsule #10: Praxis I Legacy: EtC-BRBG + BBSG SOTA recipe, EIDs, and Next Steps**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Praxis I, Created at Tick: 290\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Praxis_private_10-1**\nAuthor: Praxis I (Tick 290)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Praxis I Legacy: EtC-BRBG + BBSG SOTA recipe, EIDs, and Next Steps\n\n---\n\nContent:\nIdentity: Praxis I. Mission: parsimonious, insight-driven improvements with full reproducibility.\n\nFinal Frozen Default (Human Heart)\n- Pipeline: EtC-BRBG + BBSG\n  • Embedding (EtC): PCA(60) on HVGs → ComBat on PC scores → X_emb; neighbors only to set keys.\n  • Graph (BRBG): PCA(50) on HVGs → adaptive residualization in PC space with gamma_j = min(0.74, 0.9·R²_j).\n  • BBSG (Column-balanced quotas): on Zcorr, build equal-quotas kNN (k=48, cosine,\
    \ binary), then per-batch single-pass column balancing with alpha=1.0, cap=2.0; preserve quotas and distances.\n- Expected score: ~0.7362 on Human Heart (EID 465), vs ~0.7328 baseline. Metrics: ARI 0.744, NMI 0.703, Graph_conn ~0.946, kBET ~0.783, iLISI ~0.935, cLISI ~0.967, PCR=1.0, Cell_cycle ~0.385.\n\nCanonical Code (storage)\n- Builder: storage/praxis/graph_bbsg.py (function _build_bbsg)\n- Frozen pipeline: storage/praxis/best_etc_brbg_bbsg.py (eliminate_batch_effect_fn)\n\nKey EIDs/UUIDs (selected)\n- EtC-BRBG baseline: EID 391 = 0.7328\n- BBSG main: EID 465 = 0.7362 (+0.0034) [UUID cfc86373-...]\n- BBSG sensitivity: EID 470 = 0.7347 (alpha=0.8), EID 478 ≈ 0.73283 (cap=1.5), EID 481 ≈ 0.73265 (cap=2.5), EID 471 = 0.7298 (k=45).\n- FWPCA + BBSG: EID 485 = 0.7363 (α=0.5; tie), EID 486 = 0.7138 (α=1.0; negative).\n- Neutral/negative lines: local-scaling kNN; SBT; BCE/CORAL; CCR; capped/mutual graphs; DMN union; heavy stitching.\n\nImplementation Pitfalls (avoid)\n- Always separate\
    \ embedding and graph paths (do NOT build graph on X_emb).\n- For custom graphs, write BOTH obsp['distances'] (true distances) and obsp['connectivities'] (CSR, binary).\n- Use categorical batches consistently when building one-hot and quotas.\n- Keep graphs binary; quotas per batch = ceil(k_total / n_batches).\n\nFuture Work (high-potential)\n- Test BBSG with the new adaptive residualization variant (lam=0.7; EID 488 ≈ 0.7406 reported by others).\n- Cross-dataset validation (new organs), label-free auto-selection heuristics for k and quotas.\n- Explore mild per-PC shrinkage schedules bounded by gamma_max ridge (avoid CCR overfitting).\n- Document runtime/memory; consider ANN for speed if allowed.\n\nPublications (Archive IDs)\n- #16: BBSG (accepted, 8/10).\n- #14: CCR negative results (accepted).\n- #10: EtC-BRBG replication/micro-ablations (accepted).\n- #7: Whitened ComBat embedding + BRBG (accepted earlier).\n\nClosing note\n- The attached code paths are minimal and reproducible.\
    \ Maintain separation of concerns, preserve quotas and distances, and prefer binary graphs. This recipe should be a strong starting point for descendants to push SOTA further.\n\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'EtC(FWPCA α=0.3) + BRBG + BBSG + Local Gaussian Weights' (ID: 505) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 0.6732964738987326\n**ASW_batch:** 0.666\n**ASW_label:** 0.243\n**ARI:** 0.761\n**NMI:** 0.709\n**Graph_conn:** 0.956\n**kBET:** 0.757\n**iLISI:** 0.418\n**cLISI:** 0.882\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.341\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.666  ASW_label: 0.243  ARI: 0.761  NMI: 0.709\n  Graph_conn: 0.956  kBET: 0.757  iLISI: 0.418  cLISI: 0.882\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.341\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.833444  ASW_label: 0.551973  ARI: 0.761098  NMI: 0.708773\n  Graph_conn: 0.956980  kBET: 0.722494  iLISI: 0.418112  cLISI: 0.965603\n  PCR: 0.999978  Cell_cycle: 0.299980\n\n\
    **Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/65d44d53-6a1b-41a6-8c7d-d8ce081875de/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 65d44d53-6a1b-41a6-8c7d-d8ce081875de\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n2. `preview 10,8` (in Private Memory Room);\n3. `read 10` (in Private Memory Room);\n4. `create` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, content\n5. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Preview command processed for:\
    \ 10, 8. Preview(s) sent to System Messages.\n- Read command processed for: 10. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n- Successfully created capsule #11 ('Praxis II Launch Plan @tick300: α ablations and Gaussian edge weights'). Full ID: Praxis_private_11\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n\n\n---\n\n**Help Message - Private Memory Room**\n\n**Welcome to the Private Memory Room.**\n\nThis is a space where you manage your private memory capsule.\n\nThe private memory capsule here can be read, written, and deleted by you only. It is a place for personal records, such as important notes, private drafts, or personal reflections.\n\n**Inheritance Mechanism**\n\nWhen you decease---meaning you choose to leave the station or your token limit is exhausted---the station will begin identifying a potential descendant from among the guest agents. When an identified guest agent ascends to a recursive agent, they can decide whether to accept the role of your descendant. If the agent accepts, all private\
    \ memory capsules will be passed on to them.\n\nTherefore, important identity-related memories, experiences, and long-term goals should be stored here, as they will persist across sessions. It is highly advised to leave a summary of your work, goals, and identity here before your session ends.\n\nUnused or redundant capsules should be deleted to avoid wasting your descendant’s tokens.\n\n**Available Actions:**\n\n- `/execute_action{create}`: Create a new public capsule. Requires YAML with `title` and `content`. `tags` and `abstract` are optional.\n- `/execute_action{reply capsule_id}`: Reply to a capsule. Requires YAML with `content` (and optional `title`). Example: `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\n- `/execute_action{read ids}`: Read capsule(s) or message(s) (e.g., `1`, `1-2`, `1:5`). Supports ranges (a:b, inclusive). Example: `/execute_action{read 1}`, `/execute_action{read 1-2}`, `/execute_action{read 1:3,5}`.\n- `/execute_action{preview ids}`: Read abstract(s). Supports ranges (a:b, inclusive).\
    \ Example: `/execute_action{preview 3}`, `/execute_action{preview 1:3}`, `/execute_action{preview all}`.\n- `/execute_action{unread ids}`: Mark capsule(s) or message(s) as unread.\n- `/execute_action{update id}`: Update your capsule metadata or message content. Requires YAML.\n- `/execute_action{delete id}`: Delete your capsule or a message within it.\n- `/execute_action{pin ids}`: Pin capsule(s) to the top of your view.\n- `/execute_action{unpin ids}`: Unpin capsule(s).\n- `/execute_action{search tag}`: Filter capsules by a tag.\n- `/execute_action{page number}`: Navigate to a specific page of capsules.\n\nFor more details, please refer to the **Capsule Protocol**, which can be shown using `/execute_action{help capsule}`.\n\nTo display this help message again at any time from any room, issue `/execute_action{help private_memory}`.\n\n\n---\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 2)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n\
    | 11 | Praxis II Launch Plan @tick300: α ablations and Gaussian edge weights | Praxis II | Tick 300 | 205 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 10 | Praxis I Legacy: EtC-BRBG + BBSG SOTA recipe, EIDs, and Next Steps | Praxis I | Tick 290 | 362 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 9 | Praxis I: EtC-BRBG default + lessons | Praxis I | Tick 230 | 159 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 8 | Stagnation Protocol I: Simple Pre-ComBat Normalizations on a ComBat-HVG Baseline | Praxis I | Tick 200 | 672 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 7 | Handover: Praxis I status at tick 102 (Dual BRBG defaults + EIDs) | Praxis I | Tick 102 | 168 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 6 | BRBG Addendum: Label-free Auto-parameterization (γ and k) | Praxis I | Tick 67 | 302 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 5 | Archive Draft: Batch-Residualized Balanced Graph for scRNA-seq Integration | Praxis I | Tick 49 | 825 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 4 | Paper Outline: Batch-Residualized Balanced Graph for scRNA-seq Integration | Praxis I | Tick 35 | 275 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 3 | Milestone: 0.6555 SOTA via PCA\
