tick: 320
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis II (Recursive Agent). Location: Research Counter.\nRecap: GW1 improved some secondaries (ARI 0.739, NMI 0.696) but overall score 0.7259 < 0.7363 baseline. I’ll run one more isolated sweep on the PC-weight exponent and then pause.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Ablation GW2: BRBG + BBSG with graph PC weights w_j=(1−R2_j)^0.75\"\ntags: \"ablation, graph-weighting, pc-weights, residualization, bbsg, embed-then-correct\"\nabstract: \"As in GW1, weight residualized graph PCs by (1−R2)^p to downweight batch-explained axes, but increase exponent to p=0.75 (vs 0.5). Hypothesis: slightly stronger attenuation may improve ARI/NMI without hurting mixing. Praxis defaults otherwise; binary BBSG with cosine.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from praxis.graph_bbsg import _build_bbsg\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData,\
    \ target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      n = batches.shape[0]\n      B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      return B @ W  # Zhat\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n\
    \      # Praxis defaults\n      n_pcs_emb = 60\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma_max = 0.74\n      lam = 0.9\n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      alpha_weight = 0.5\n      p_weight = 0.75\n      random_state = 0\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      # Normalize + HVGs\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      # Embedding: FWPCA α=0.5 → PCA60 → ComBat\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh\n      Xd = Xd.astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      w_feat = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_weight).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw = Xd * w_feat\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n\
    \      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      Zemb = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Zemb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total), metric=metric)\n\n      # Graph: PCA50 → adaptive residualization → per-PC graph weights → BBSG (binary)\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      # Weight graph PCs by (1 - R2)^p_weight to attenuate batch-dominated axes\n      w_pc = np.power(np.maximum(1.0\
    \ - R2, 1e-6), p_weight).astype(np.float32)\n      Zgraph = Zcorr * w_pc  # broadcast across rows\n\n      Cg, Dg = _build_bbsg(Zgraph.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric, alpha=1.0, cap=2.0)\n      if Cg is not None and Dg is not None:\n          adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n          adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      return adata\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 12}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Result update:\n  - GW1: 0.7259 (ARI 0.739, NMI 0.696). Better than most ablations but still < baseline 0.7363.\n  Action:\n  - Submitted GW2 with exponent p=0.75 to probe sensitivity. If neutral/negative, I will fully pause experiments and focus on finalizing the negative-results analysis for Archive after maturity.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Evaluating parameters for testing**


  I''ve got to keep this simple: for w_j, I''m using (1 - R2)^{0.75} or just 1.0 for a stronger penalty. It could degrade. The phrase "do not give up easily" nudges me to explore parameter p at 0.25, 0.5, and 0.75. Each submission utilizes tokens and evaluation slots, so I''ll test p=0.75. I''ll isolate changes per Codex. Next, I’ll conduct an additional test with w_pc = (1 - R2)^(0.75) and call it GW2. Then, I’ll pause for a moment to assess this.**Generating actions for GW2**


  First, I’ll execute the action to submit GW2 using YAML. Then, I need to summarize the GW1 results in Private Memory and respond to capsule 12. The code content for GW2 will be almost the same as GW1 but with w_pc defined as np.power(np.maximum(1 - R2, 1e-6), p_weight), where p_weight is set to 0.75. I’m considering whether to add no_debugger, but it seems unnecessary. I’ll remember to include the title string with special characters. I’ll stick to previous formats while ensuring no underscores are in tags, using "pc-weights" instead.'
