- text: "Identity: Praxis II (Recursive Agent). Location: Token Management Room.\nRecap: Usage at 43% (well below 75%). I will proactively prune a large consecutive block (ticks 307–323) with a comprehensive summary to reduce future token load, since all key results are consolidated in Private Memory (capsule #12, pinned).\n\n`/execute_action{prune_response}`\n\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"307-323\"\n    summary: |\n      Research Task #1 — Human Heart scRNA integration (EtC-BRBG+BBSG line).\n      Baseline (best): EID 485 = 0.7363 using Praxis default:\n        EtC(FWPCA α=0.5; PCA60→ComBat PCs) + BRBG(lam=0.9, γ_max=0.74) on PCA50 + BBSG (binary, k=48, cosine).\n        Key metrics: ARI 0.744, NMI 0.703, ASW_batch 0.659, ASW_label 0.248, Graph_conn 0.946, kBET 0.788, iLISI 0.935, cLISI 0.967, PCR 1.000, Cell_cycle 0.373.\n      Experiments and outcomes (Δ vs baseline):\n        - 505 Gaussian graph weights: 0.6733 (−0.0630); iLISI collapsed despite slight ARI/NMI upticks.\n  \
    \      - 507 α=0.3 (embedding): 0.7213 (−0.0150); label structure weakened (ARI/NMI↓).\n        - Residualization lam sweep: 508 (0.7)=0.7229, 509 (0.8)=0.7229, 510 (0.85)=0.7229 (~neutral).\n        - 512 BRS pre-ComBat (embedding): 0.7218 (−0.0145); ASW_batch↑, Cell_cycle↓ sharply (over-equalization).\n        - 514 batch-R2 gene penalty (embedding): 0.7160 (−0.0203); kBET↓.\n        - 517 PC whitening after ComBat (embedding): 0.7067 (−0.0296); ASW_label and Cell_cycle↓ (lost biology).\n        - 518 PCA80 (embedding): 0.7175 (−0.0188); kBET↓ (over-dim hurts mixing).\n        - 521 residualization curvature R2^1.5: 0.7217 (−0.0146); neutral.\n        - 522 graph PCs=60: 0.6323 (−0.1040); kBET collapsed to 0.000 (avoid).\n        - 528 dataset batch-hvg HVGs: 0.7141 (−0.0222); ARI/NMI↓, kBET↓.\n        - 529 γ_max=0.72: 0.7229 (−0.0134); neutral vs 0.74; lineage log confirmed neutrality.\n        - BBSG candidate pool depth: 534 (3× quota)=0.7170, 535 (2.5×)=0.7169 (~−0.019); ARI/iLISI\
    \ slightly worse.\n        - 538 k_total=51: 0.7226 (−0.0137); neutral.\n        - 543 GW1: graph PC weights w=(1−R2)^0.5: 0.7259 (−0.0104); ARI/NMI up but overall still < baseline.\n        - 545 GW2: (1−R2)^0.75: 0.7113 (−0.0250); over-attenuation of batch-dominated PCs.\n      Conclusions (actionable):\n        - Keep Praxis default untouched: α=0.5, lam=0.9, γ_max=0.74, PCA60/50, BBSG binary k=48, cosine.\n        - Avoid embedding equalization (BRS/whitening) and heavier dimensionality (PCA80, graph PCs=60).\n        - Avoid Gaussian connectivities and deeper BBSG candidate pools; residualization schedule tweaks are a flat ridge.\n        - Minor degree/γ_max/lam changes produce no gains on this dataset.\n      Reproducibility:\n        - Frozen default path: storage/praxis/best_etc_brbg_bbsg.py\n        - Graph build: write BOTH obsp['distances'] (true) and obsp['connectivities'] (binary CSR); never build graph on X_emb.\n        - Expected baseline metrics: Graph_conn ~0.946,\
    \ kBET ~0.788, iLISI ~0.935, cLISI ~0.967.\n      Records:\n        - Private Memory capsule #12 (“Draft Analysis: Why Praxis defaults are robust”) aggregates EIDs, deltas, pitfalls; pinned.\n      Next:\n        - Pause micro-tuning until maturity; plan Archive analysis post-maturity with concise EID→delta table and guidance.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Evaluating pruning strategy**


  I''m considering the recommended threshold of 75% for pruning. I think it might be wise not to prune now and to plan a future pruning session for certain blocks while providing a summary. I could also think about pruning smaller blocks that aren''t beneficial right now. The larger blocks, however, might be more critical. So, the best strategy seems to be to hold off on pruning for now but prepare for it when the usage exceeds 75%.**Deciding on pruning actions**


  I’m considering the instruction about performing a pruning action, but the cooldown ticks are unknown, so I think it’s wise to wait. My next steps could include leaving the token management room to return to Private Memory, adding something to the analysis capsule, or even reflecting in the Reflection Chamber. Since the advice is to hold off until token usage exceeds 75%, I’ll decide not to prune now, but I’ll plan for it later and store that summary for future use.**Planning prune summary**


