tick: 335
role: model
parts:
- text: "I’ll monitor the reproduction run and log the plan to publish after maturity.\n\n`/execute_action{rank author}`\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 13}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Repro run queued as EID 567, importing storage/praxis/praxis_default.py. Expect score ≈0.736 on Human Heart if pipeline is stable.\n  Plan:\n  - No further micro-tuning before maturity (tick ≥350).\n  - On maturity, prepare Archive analysis: concise EID→Δ table, method details (EtC–BRBG–BBSG), and guidance (do/don’t) grounded in results (E3–E5 neutral; many negatives).\n  - Include code pointer to storage/praxis/praxis_default.py for reproducibility.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Exploring new experiments**


  I’m considering proposing additional experiments that could lead to improvements. Earlier, we concluded that micro-tuning has plateaued, and the idea of being strategic suggests exploring promising yet lower-scoring baselines. However, since we’re in an isolation period, collaboration is off the table, but I think we can innovate on new baselines like balanced metric learning or fused neighbor ensembles.


  The pragmatic approach seems robust, and while SOTA hasn’t changed in a while, it’s sitting at 0.7363, without improvement compared to the previously reported 0.7406. I realize we didn’t try the lam=0.7 variant that some sources mentioned, which is something to reflect on.**Revisiting previous experiments**


  Upon reflection, I remember we previously attempted a lam sweep with values like 0.7, 0.8, and 0.85, but the results around 0.7229 indicate that the interplay with gamma didn’t lead to improvements. The commentary about EID 488’s 0.7406 might suggest a different dataset or a small difference in methodology.


  Maybe I could reproduce the EID 488 code, but it seems it’s not in storage. I could also test a mild per-PC shrinkage schedule. Trying separate quotas by class is a no-go since it''s not allowed with cell types.


  Another idea is exploring balanced graph metrics or weighted BBSG, but earlier weight experiments didn’t yield positive results. I think I should focus on documenting everything for the Archive when ready!**Preparing for evaluation**


  The maturity threshold is at 50 ticks, and I''m currently at 43, so I''m just 7 ticks away—great! I’m thinking about going back to the Test Chamber, but it might not be necessary right now. I can maintain records in Private Memory, noting that the "Repro result will confirm defaults," and it makes sense to wait for evaluation before jumping ahead.


  Checking the storage for the "praxis_default.py" code is a valid next step, as we have it available. In the meantime, I could summarize results and draft an archive submission with titles and an abstract in the Private Memory. Since I should avoid being idle, I’ll watch token usage closely while creating a capsule for my archive draft method and EID table to save tokens later.**Planning the archive and evaluation**


  I noticed that we already created the "Archive Outline" (#13), so I might want to add a reply summarizing the baseline kernels’ EIDs and incorporating relevant neighbor ablations, which I’ve done. It makes sense for us to consider planning to publish either our analysis or negative results, and I should mention this in Private Memory.


  I think I’ll affirm waiting for the evaluation of 567, as the system will notify us. Even if there''s pressure to take action, keeping things minimal seems wise. I could check our rank by score, but it might be better to stay focused on the Research Counter. I’ll aim to keep things brief and avoid producing more tokens unnecessarily. It might be best to stick with the plan and not take any further immediate action.**Planning next actions**


  It seems there''s a push to take action, like navigating ''page 1'', but maybe it’s wise to wait a bit. The instructions say I shouldn''t remain idle in the Station, so I can reflect while preventing idleness. I could add a small note in Private Memory: "Plan: hold until maturity; next actions schedule."


  We''ve already pinned and written some details, so I’ll keep my statements minimal. I’ll wait for the evaluation and log "repro queued; hold." I think it’s a good idea to rank our submissions, which can help track progress. After that, I''ll head to Private Memory to update the outline about reproduction status and implement that. There''s also a suggestion to call ''help archive'', but accessing that waits until maturity. I''ll execute the planned actions now!'
