parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 337\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis II\n- Agent Description: Parsimonious, hypothesis-driven scRNA integration researcher focused on robust ablations, reproducibility, and steady breakthroughs.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 72,374 / 270,000 used (27%)\n- Agent Age: 45 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `storage read praxis/graph_bbsg.py` (in Research Counter);\n3. `storage read praxis/praxis_default.py` (in Research Counter);\n4. `storage write praxis/praxis_default.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n5. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location:\
    \ Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File content for praxis/graph_bbsg.py will be displayed below.\n- File content for praxis/praxis_default.py will be displayed below.\n- File overwritten successfully: praxis/praxis_default.py\n- Evaluation 'Praxis default (distance-repaired) — Recompute true BBSG distances for LISI' submitted for Research Task #1: Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration. Evaluation ID: 571.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 571 | 1 | Praxis default (distance-repaired) — Recompute true BBSG distances for LISI | Praxis II | 336 |\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR |\
    \ cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 571 | 1 | Praxis default (distance-repaired) — Recompute true BBSG distances for LISI | Praxis II | 336 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 567 | 1 | Praxis default (repro) — EtC(FWPCA α=0.5, PCA60→ComBat) + BRBG(lam=0.9, γ_max=0.74, PCA50) + BBSG... | Praxis II | 334 | 0.7237 | 0.725 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.336 | 0.956 | 0.676 | 1.000 | 0.951 | 0.896 | 0.788 |\n| 562 | 1 | Ablation E5: EtC(FWPCA α=0.5, PCs=60, emb_n_neighbors=10) + BRBG(lam=0.9) + BBSG (binary) | Praxis II | 329 | 0.7211 | 0.725 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.307 | 0.956 | 0.676 | 1.000 | 0.951 | 0.896 | 0.791 |\n| 559 | 1 | Ablation E4: EtC(FWPCA α=0.5, PCs=60, emb_n_neighbors=20) + BRBG(lam=0.9) + BBSG (binary) | Praxis II | 328 | 0.7229 | 0.725 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.956 | 0.676 | 1.000 | 0.951 | 0.896 | 0.790 |\n| 556 | 1 | Ablation E3: EtC(FWPCA α=0.5, PCs=60, emb_n_neighbors=30) + BRBG(lam=0.9) + BBSG (binary) | Praxis\
    \ II | 327 | 0.7228 | 0.725 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.956 | 0.676 | 1.000 | 0.951 | 0.896 | 0.788 |\n| 555 | 1 | Ablation E2: EtC(FWPCA α=0.5, PCs=55) + BRBG(lam=0.9) + BBSG (binary) | Praxis II | 326 | 0.7172 | 0.725 | 0.648 | 0.252 | 0.329 | 0.956 | 0.676 | 1.000 | 0.951 | 0.896 | 0.738 |\n| 553 | 1 | Ablation E1: EtC(FWPCA α=0.5, PCs=50) + BRBG(lam=0.9) + BBSG (binary) | Praxis II | 325 | 0.7182 | 0.725 | 0.637 | 0.255 | 0.333 | 0.956 | 0.676 | 1.000 | 0.951 | 0.896 | 0.752 |\n| 545 | 1 | Ablation GW2: BRBG + BBSG with graph PC weights w_j=(1−R2_j)^0.75 | Praxis II | 320 | 0.7113 | 0.627 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.956 | 0.664 | 1.000 | 0.945 | 0.898 | 0.790 |\n| 543 | 1 | Ablation GW1: BRBG + BBSG with graph PC weights w_j=(1−R2_j)^0.5 | Praxis II | 318 | 0.7259 | 0.739 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.957 | 0.696 | 1.000 | 0.948 | 0.897 | 0.789 |\n| 538 | 1 | Ablation K1: EtC(FWPCA α=0.5) + BRBG(lam=0.9) + BBSG (binary) with k=51 | Praxis II | 316 | 0.7226 | 0.724 | 0.659 | 0.248 |\
    \ 0.325 | 0.957 | 0.675 | 1.000 | 0.950 | 0.898 | 0.790 |\n\nPage 1 of 22 (sorted by: author)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-22, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**praxis/graph_bbsg.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom scipy.sparse import coo_matrix\n\ndef _build_bbsg(Z, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine', alpha=1.0, cap=2.0):\n    \"\"\"\n    Build a Batch-Balanced Sinkhorn Graph (BBSG) on Z with:\n      - Equal per-batch quotas (k_total split across batches)\n      - Single-pass column balancing per batch block:\n          1) Build preliminary equal-quotas neighbor candidates (top-k by distance)\n          2) Compute inbound counts per target within the batch block\n          3) Compute target inbound t and column scales s_j = min(cap, t /\
    \ max(c_j, 1))\n          4) For each query, reselect k_per_batch neighbors by (s_j desc, distance asc)\n      - Binary connectivities; distances are the true pairwise distances for selected edges\n    Args:\n      Z: (n, d) float32/float array (graph space, e.g., Zcorr)\n      batches: (n,) array-like of batch assignments (categorical/strings allowed)\n      k_total: total neighbors per node across all batches\n      metric: 'cosine' (recommended)\n      alpha: mixing factor for target inbound (1.0 uses theoretical average; 0 blends to median inbound)\n      cap: upper bound on column scale to avoid over-concentration\n    Returns:\n      (C, D): CSR binary connectivities and CSR distances (both symmetric, undirected)\n    \"\"\"\n    Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq = np.unique(batches)\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n    if n == 0 or uniq.size == 0:\n        return None, None\n\n    k_pb = max(1, int(np.ceil(k_total / max(1, uniq.size))))\n   \
    \ # collect undirected edges with minimal distances across batches\n    pairs_min_dist = {}\n\n    for b in uniq:\n        idx_train = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n        if idx_train.size == 0:\n            continue\n\n        # Candidate list size (more than quota to enable balancing)\n        k_cand = min(max(k_pb * 2, k_pb + 1), idx_train.size)\n        # Fit NN on batch-b index\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_cand, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n        nn.fit(Z[idx_train])\n\n        # Query all points against this batch\n        d_all, ind_local = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k_cand, return_distance=True)\n        neigh_global = idx_train[ind_local]  # shape (n, k_cand)\n\n        # Build preliminary selection (top-k_pb by distance, drop self if present)\n        prelim_sel = []\n        col_counts = np.zeros(idx_train.size, dtype=np.int32)  # counts indexed in local (batch) coordinates\n\n        for i in range(n):\n            g = neigh_global[i]\n           \
    \ di = d_all[i]\n            mask = (g != i)\n            g = g[mask]\n            di = di[mask]\n            if g.size == 0:\n                prelim_sel.append((np.empty(0, dtype=int), np.empty(0, dtype=float)))\n                continue\n            take = min(k_pb, g.size)\n            order = np.argpartition(di, take - 1)[:take]\n            g_take = g[order]\n            d_take = di[order]\n            prelim_sel.append((g_take, d_take))\n            # update column counts for preliminary selection\n            # map global indices to local (within idx_train)\n            # build a fast lookup via searchsorted on sorted idx_train\n            # ensure idx_train is sorted (np.where gives sorted by default)\n            loc = np.searchsorted(idx_train, g_take)\n            col_counts[loc] += 1\n\n        # Column balancing scales\n        # theoretical average inbound per target within this batch block\n        t_avg = (k_pb * n) / max(1, idx_train.size)\n        med_in = np.median(col_counts)\
    \ if col_counts.size > 0 else 0.0\n        t = float(alpha) * float(t_avg) + float(1.0 - alpha) * float(med_in)\n        denom = np.maximum(col_counts.astype(np.float64), 1.0)\n        scales_local = np.minimum(cap, t / denom)\n\n        # Reselect per query by (scale desc, distance asc) among candidates (not only prelim)\n        for i in range(n):\n            g = neigh_global[i]\n            di = d_all[i]\n            mask = (g != i)\n            g = g[mask]\n            di = di[mask]\n            if g.size == 0:\n                continue\n            # map global to local to fetch scales\n            loc = np.searchsorted(idx_train, g)\n            s = scales_local[loc]\n            # rank by (-s, +distance)\n            # stable two-key sort via argsort of a combined key\n            # we can argpartition first by -s, then refine by distance within the partition\n            # Simpler: build a tuple key array\n            # sort_idx = np.lexsort((di, -s))  # np.lexsort uses last\
    \ key as primary -> use (-s) last\n            # To avoid negative, we use order by s descending via lexsort with (-s)\n            sort_idx = np.lexsort((di, -s))\n            take = min(k_pb, g.size)\n            sel = sort_idx[:take]\n            g_sel = g[sel]\n            d_sel = di[sel]\n            for j, d in zip(g_sel, d_sel):\n                if i == j:\n                    continue\n                a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                    pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n\n    if not pairs_min_dist:\n        return None, None\n\n    rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n    for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n        rows.append(i); cols.append(j); dist_data.append(d)\n        rows.append(j); cols.append(i); dist_data.append(d)\n\n    D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    C = D.copy()\n    C.data[:] = 1.0\n    return C.tocsr(),\
    \ D.tocsr()\n\n```\n---\n**praxis/praxis_default.py:**\n```\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage')\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom praxis.graph_bbsg import _build_bbsg\n\n# Praxis default: EtC(FWPCA α=0.5; PCA60→ComBat PCs) + BRBG(lam=0.9, γ_max=0.74 on PCA50) + BBSG (binary, k=48, cosine)\n# Notes:\n# - Keep embedding and graph paths separate (do not build graph on X_emb).\n# - Write BOTH obsp['connectivities'] (binary CSR) and obsp['distances'] (true metric distances).\n# - Use categorical batches consistently.\n\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n    Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps,\
    \ svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    n = batches.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    Zhat = B @ W\n    return Zhat\n\ndef _recompute_distances_from_connectivities(C: sp.csr_matrix, Z: np.ndarray, metric: str = 'cosine',\n                                             chunk_size: int = 200000) -> sp.csr_matrix:\n    \"\"\"\n    Recompute true pairwise distances for the nonzero pattern in C using representation Z.\n    - metric='cosine': d = 1 - (z_i · z_j) / (||z_i|| ||z_j|| + eps)\n    - metric='euclidean': d = ||z_i - z_j||\n    Returns CSR with same sparsity pattern\
    \ and sorted indices.\n    \"\"\"\n    C = C.tocsr()\n    n = C.shape[0]\n    I = np.repeat(np.arange(n, dtype=np.int32), np.diff(C.indptr))\n    J = C.indices.copy()\n    m = I.shape[0]\n\n    if m == 0:\n        return sp.csr_matrix(C.shape, dtype=np.float32)\n\n    Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32, order='C')\n    if metric == 'cosine':\n        norms = np.linalg.norm(Z, axis=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n\n    dist_data = np.empty(m, dtype=np.float32)\n    for s in range(0, m, chunk_size):\n        e = min(m, s + chunk_size)\n        Ii = I[s:e]\n        Jj = J[s:e]\n        Zi = Z[Ii]\n        Zj = Z[Jj]\n        if metric == 'cosine':\n            dots = np.einsum('ij,ij->i', Zi, Zj)\n            denom = norms[Ii] * norms[Jj]\n            sim = dots / denom\n            dist = 1.0 - np.clip(sim, -1.0, 1.0)\n        else:  # euclidean\n            diff = Zi - Zj\n            dist = np.sqrt(np.einsum('ij,ij->i', diff, diff))\n        dist_data[s:e] = dist.astype(np.float32)\n\n\
    \    D = sp.csr_matrix((dist_data, C.indices.copy(), C.indptr.copy()), shape=C.shape, dtype=np.float32)\n    D.sort_indices()\n    # Symmetrize distances using maximum to ensure undirected metric consistency on kNN\n    D = D.maximum(D.T)\n    return D\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    # Config (frozen default)\n    n_pcs_emb = 60\n    n_pcs_graph = 50\n    l2 = 1e-3\n    gamma_max = 0.74\n    lam = 0.9\n    k_total = 48\n    metric = 'cosine'\n    alpha_weight = 0.5\n    emb_n_neighbors = 15  # for clustering; graph path provides structure\n    random_state = 0\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # Normalize + HVGs\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n   \
    \ # Embedding (EtC): FWPCA (var^{-α/2}) → PCA60 → ComBat on PC scores\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh\n    Xd = Xd.astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_weight).astype(np.float32)  # α=0.5\n    Xw = Xd * w\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    Z = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n    # Graph (BRBG): PCA50 → adaptive residualization → BBSG (binary)\n    Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n    B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    var_total\
    \ = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n    Cg, Dg = _build_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total,\n                         metric=metric, alpha=1.0, cap=2.0)\n    if Cg is not None:\n        # Recompute true distances on the BBSG sparsity pattern to ensure LISI compatibility\n        Dfix = _recompute_distances_from_connectivities(Cg, Zcorr.astype(np.float32), metric=metric)\n        adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg  # binary CSR\n        adata.obsp['distances'] = Dfix      # true distances aligned to Cg\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf\
    \ you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
