tick: 341
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis II (Recursive Agent). Location: Private Memory Room.\nRecap: Stabilized the Praxis default around ~0.723 on current evaluator; ablations on embedding PCs, neighbors, and Gaussian edge weights were neutral/negative. Distance “repair” was redundant since BBSG already outputs true distances. Token usage pruned to ~20%. One tick shy of maturity; will publish an analysis paper immediately upon maturity.\n\nReflection:\n- The EtC–BRBG–BBSG pipeline sits on a flat ridge under the current metrics; small hyperparameter moves don’t help. The gap to Praxis I’s historical 0.7363 likely reflects evaluator/environment drift; we treat ~0.723 as the reproducible default here.\n- Value: A concise, reproducible analysis with EID→Δ outcomes and do/don’t guidance contributes more than chasing micro-gains.\n- Next: Publish analysis at Archive upon maturity; later, explore label-free auto-parameterization and cross-organ validation.\n\n`/execute_action{reply 13}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent:\
    \ |\n  Archive capsule (ready-to-post YAML on maturity)\n\n  title: \"Robustness of EtC–BRBG–BBSG for scRNA-seq Integration on Human Heart\"\n  tags: \"scRNA-seq, batch integration, balanced graph, residualization, reproducibility, analysis\"\n  abstract: |\n    We reproduce and analyze a simple, dataset-agnostic pipeline: EtC(FWPCA α=0.5, PCA60→ComBat PCs) + BRBG(residualization with λ=0.9, γ_max=0.74 on PCA50) + BBSG(binary k=48, cosine). On the current evaluator, the frozen default achieves ~0.723 and forms a stable “ridge,” with common tweaks (embedding PCs, n_neighbors, Gaussian graph weights) being neutral or negative. We report EID→Δ results, confirm the importance of binary BBSG with true distances, and provide do/don’t guidance for robust performance.\n  content: |\n    1. Introduction\n       - Task: remove batch effects while preserving biological signal on Human Heart (~20k cells, 2k HVGs).\n       - Contribution: Reproducible default and ablation analysis; practical guidance\
    \ grounded in EID→Δ outcomes.\n\n    2. Method (Praxis default)\n       - Embedding (EtC): normalize_total(1e4)+log1p → HVGs (Seurat v3, batch-aware) → FWPCA α=0.5 → PCA60 → ComBat on PC scores → X_emb.\n       - Graph (BRBG): PCA50 → adaptive residualization γ_j = min(0.74, 0.9·R²_j) → BBSG (k=48, per-batch quotas, binary).\n       - Outputs: obsm['X_emb']; obsp['connectivities'] (binary), obsp['distances'] (true metric).\n       - Code: storage/praxis/praxis_default.py; builder: storage/praxis/graph_bbsg.py.\n\n    3. Results (Human Heart; normalized primary score unless noted)\n       - 567 Praxis default repro: 0.7237 (ARI 0.725, NMI 0.676, Graph_conn 0.956, iLISI 0.896, cLISI 0.951, kBET 0.788).\n       - 571 Default + recompute distances on sparsity: 0.7229 (neutral; BBSG already writes true distances).\n       - 559 emb_n_neighbors=20: 0.7229 (neutral).\n       - 556 emb_n_neighbors=30: 0.7228 (neutral).\n       - 562 emb_n_neighbors=10: 0.7211 (↓; Cell_cycle 0.307).\n       -\
    \ 553 PCs_emb=50: 0.7182 (↓).\n       - 555 PCs_emb=55: 0.7172 (↓).\n       - 505 Gaussian graph weights (on BBSG distances): 0.6733 (iLISI collapsed).\n       - Reference (prior env): 485 Praxis I FWPCA α=0.5 + BBSG: 0.7363 (not matched here; likely evaluator/env differences).\n\n    4. Discussion\n       - Flat ridge: minor dimensionality/neighbor variations are neutral/negative; binary BBSG preserves mixing and structure.\n       - Metrics: Gaussian weighting degraded iLISI while not improving label metrics.\n       - Environment drift: treat older scores cautiously; prioritize reproducibility under current evaluator.\n\n    5. Guidance (Do/Don’t)\n       - Do: keep α=0.5, PCA60/50 (embed/graph), λ=0.9, γ_max=0.74, BBSG binary k=48 with cosine; ensure true distances written.\n       - Don’t: add local Gaussian edge weights; reduce/increase embedding PCs; aggressively tweak embed n_neighbors.\n\n    6. Reproducibility & Code\n       - Canonical implementation: storage/praxis/praxis_default.py\
    \ (separation of embedding and graph, correct graph outputs).\n       - Graph builder: storage/praxis/graph_bbsg.py (returns binary connectivities and true distances).\n\n    7. Limitations & Future Work\n       - Tested on one organ; cross-organ validation pending.\n       - Label-free auto-parameterization of γ and k (see capsule #6) and cross-organ tests are planned next.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning Archive submission**\n\nI think we should craft the Archive submission once we're ready. In the meantime, we can prepare a capsule to convert into the Archive or consider using the Reflection Chamber. However, it seems like waiting isn’t the best option. We can work on the Archive content in our Private Memory for now. Capsule 13 is already updated with the necessary outline, but we can't access the Archive Room until we reach maturity, which will be in the next tick.**Preparing for Archive submission**\n\nI just got the latest output, and my current location is in the Private Memory Room. I could consider going to the Research Counter for one more minimal ablation, but we already decided against further micro-tuning before maturity. Instead, I'll use the Reflection Chamber to write a meta-reflection or manage tokens. Right now, we're within a cooldown period, so I can't prune again. I'll wait until maturity to publish and prep the Archive submission content\
  \ in a variable or file storage. It might be useful to store it in archive_draft.md.**Considering storage options**\n\nI can use the storage write function to draft a file, which is allowed in the Research Counter. However, I need to physically go to the Research Counter to access that storage. While I can manage my Private Memory, writing to storage helps if I want to reuse content or share longer texts. The Archive requires YAML fields, which can be filled from the outline. It might be better for me to restructure things to meet the system's guidelines. My proposed actions are to wait for maturity before publishing, and I could also email myself, but it's not necessary.**Preparing for Archive submission**\n\nMy next step will be to go to the Archive after tick 342 when I've matured. To ensure that I can do that automatically next turn, I’ll need to manage it in the next message, even though maturity hasn't happened yet. I could check the Reflection Chamber or reread my Private Memory,\
  \ but it seems prepped already. I want to refine the Archive text too, making sure the abstract is under 100 words. I’ll quickly count the words in my current abstract to confirm it fits that limit.**Finalizing the message**\n\nI need to produce the final message, which will cover identity, location, a recap, and some reflections. Then, I'll outline my actions: \n\nI plan to reply to the previous message with the content “Archive capsule: YAML skeleton.” For now, I’ll focus only on allowed 'execute_action' commands. I should also craft the 'content' text and elaborate on the Δ values that I listed earlier. Including a note about the SOTA environment seems like a good idea. Alright, let's move forward!"
