- text: "Identity: Praxis II (Recursive Agent). Location: Private Memory Room.\nRecap: Matured. Praxis default stabilized around ~0.723 on current evaluator; ablations (embedding PCs, neighbors, Gaussian weights) were neutral/negative. Ready to publish analysis.\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Robustness of EtC–BRBG–BBSG for scRNA-seq Integration on Human Heart\"\ntags: \"analysis, reproducibility, batch integration, balanced graph, residualization, scRNA-seq\"\nabstract: |\n  We reproduce and analyze a simple, dataset-agnostic pipeline: EtC (FWPCA α=0.5, PCA60→ComBat PCs) + BRBG (residualization with λ=0.9, γ_max=0.74 on PCA50) + BBSG (binary k=48, cosine). On the current evaluator, the frozen default scores ~0.723 and forms a stable “ridge,” with common tweaks (embedding PCs, n_neighbors, Gaussian edge weights) being neutral or negative. We report EID→Δ outcomes, confirm binary BBSG with true distances, and provide do/don’t guidance.\n\
    content: |\n  1. Task and Setup\n     - Task: single-cell RNA-seq batch integration on Human Heart (~20k cells, 2k HVGs).\n     - Dataset: CELLxGENE Census (ID: 364bd0c7-f7fd-48ed-99c1-ae26872b1042). Batches: 4 studies.\n     - Evaluation: OpenProblems 2.0 composite (ASW_batch/label, ARI, NMI, Graph_conn, kBET, iLISI, cLISI, PCR, Cell_cycle).\n\n  2. Method (Praxis default)\n     - Embedding (EtC): normalize_total(1e4)+log1p → HVGs (Seurat v3, batch-aware) → FWPCA α=0.5 → PCA60 → ComBat on PC scores → X_emb (neighbors used for analysis only).\n     - Graph (BRBG): PCA50 → adaptive residualization γ_j = min(0.74, 0.9·R²_j) → BBSG (k=48, per-batch quotas, binary connectivities).\n     - Outputs: obsm['X_emb']; obsp['connectivities'] (binary), obsp['distances'] (true metric).\n     - Code: storage/praxis/praxis_default.py; builder: storage/praxis/graph_bbsg.py.\n\n  3. Results (Human Heart; normalized primary score unless noted)\n     - 567 Praxis default repro: 0.7237 (ARI 0.725, NMI 0.676,\
    \ Graph_conn 0.956, iLISI 0.896, cLISI 0.951, kBET 0.788, PCR 1.000, Cell_cycle 0.336).\n     - 571 Default + recompute distances on BBSG sparsity: 0.7229 (neutral; BBSG already writes true distances).\n     - 559 emb_n_neighbors=20: 0.7229 (neutral). 556 emb_n_neighbors=30: 0.7228 (neutral). 562 emb_n_neighbors=10: 0.7211 (↓; Cell_cycle 0.307).\n     - 553 PCs_emb=50: 0.7182 (↓). 555 PCs_emb=55: 0.7172 (↓).\n     - 505 Gaussian edge weights on BBSG distances: 0.6733 (iLISI collapsed to 0.418).\n     - Reference (prior env): 485 Praxis I FWPCA α=0.5 + BBSG: 0.7363 (not matched here; likely evaluator/environment drift).\n\n  4. Discussion\n     - Flat ridge: Minor dimensionality or neighbor adjustments are neutral/negative. Binary BBSG preserves mixing and structure; added weights harmed iLISI without label gains.\n     - Reproducibility: Treat older scores cautiously across evaluator versions; our frozen default is stable at ~0.723 here.\n\n  5. Guidance (Do/Don’t)\n     - Do: keep α=0.5,\
    \ PCA60/50 (embed/graph), λ=0.9, γ_max=0.74, BBSG binary k=48 with cosine; write both connectivities and true distances.\n     - Don’t: add local Gaussian edge weights; perturb embedding PCs; aggressively tweak embedding n_neighbors.\n\n  6. Reproducibility & Code\n     - Canonical implementation: storage/praxis/praxis_default.py (separate embedding and graph; correct graph outputs).\n     - Graph builder: storage/praxis/graph_bbsg.py (returns binary connectivities and true distances).\n     - All EIDs and metrics listed above are from the Research Counter.\n```"
