tick: 347
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis II (Recursive Agent). Location: Research Counter.\nRecap: Two down-weighting ANOVA-F variants reduced composite scores despite higher kBET (ASW_label and Cell_cycle dropped). I submitted two up-weighting variants (EIDs 581, 582) to concentrate batch signal pre-ComBat. Awaiting results.\n\nReflection:\n- Evidence suggests ComBat prefers batch variance concentrated in a small subspace rather than suppressed.\n- My previous implementations duplicated utility code. I will factor shared weighting utilities into lineage storage for cleaner, less error-prone experiments and easier future reuse.\n\nActions:\n- Add a reusable embedding-weighting utility module to storage.\n- Log the plan update in Private Memory; wait for results before further sweeps.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write praxis/embed_weighting.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n\n  EPS = 1e-8\n\n  def _as_float32(arr):\n      return np.asarray(arr, dtype=np.float32, order='C')\n\n  def anova_F_per_gene(Xd:\
    \ np.ndarray, batch_codes: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n      \"\"\"\n      One-way ANOVA F-statistic per gene across batches.\n      Xd: (n_cells, n_genes) float array (dense)\n      batch_codes: (n_cells,) int in [0, k-1]\n      Returns: (n_genes,) float32 F-scores (>=0)\n      \"\"\"\n      Xd = _as_float32(Xd)\n      bc = np.asarray(batch_codes, dtype=np.int32)\n      n, g = Xd.shape\n      if n <= 1 or g == 0:\n          return np.zeros((g,), dtype=np.float32)\n\n      k = int(bc.max()) + 1 if bc.size else 0\n      m_all = Xd.mean(axis=0)\n      SSB = np.zeros(g, dtype=np.float64)\n      SSW = np.zeros(g, dtype=np.float64)\n\n      for b in range(k):\n          idx = np.where(bc == b)[0]\n          nb = idx.size\n          if nb <= 1:\n              continue\n          Xb = Xd[idx]\n          mb = Xb.mean(axis=0)\n          vb = Xb.var(axis=0, ddof=1)\n          SSB += nb * (mb - m_all) ** 2\n          SSW += (nb - 1) * vb\n\n      dof_between = max(k - 1, 1)\n      dof_within =\
    \ max(n - k, 1)\n      F = (SSB / dof_between) / (np.maximum(SSW, EPS) / dof_within)\n      F = np.maximum(F, 0.0)\n      return F.astype(np.float32)\n\n  def minmax_norm(v: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n      v = _as_float32(v)\n      vmin = float(np.min(v)) if v.size else 0.0\n      vmax = float(np.max(v)) if v.size else 1.0\n      return (v - vmin) / (max(vmax - vmin, EPS))\n\n  def var_weights(var_g: np.ndarray, alpha_var: float = 0.5) -> np.ndarray:\n      \"\"\"\n      Variance-based weights: w = var^{-alpha_var/2}\n      \"\"\"\n      var_g = _as_float32(var_g)\n      return np.power(var_g + EPS, -0.5 * float(alpha_var), dtype=np.float32)\n\n  def anova_weights(F: np.ndarray, beta: float, direction: str = 'up', normalize: bool = True) -> np.ndarray:\n      \"\"\"\n      ANOVA-F-based weights.\n      - If direction == 'up':  w = 1 + beta * F_norm\n      - If direction == 'down': w = (1 + F_norm)^(-beta)\n      \"\"\"\n      F = _as_float32(F)\n      Fn = minmax_norm(F) if normalize\
    \ else F\n      if direction == 'up':\n          w = 1.0 + float(beta) * Fn\n      elif direction == 'down':\n          w = np.power(1.0 + Fn, -float(beta), dtype=np.float32)\n      else:\n          raise ValueError(\"direction must be 'up' or 'down'\")\n      return _as_float32(w)\n\n  def combine_weights(*ws: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n      \"\"\"\n      Multiply multiple per-gene weight vectors (same length).\n      \"\"\"\n      if not ws:\n          raise ValueError(\"No weights provided\")\n      w = _as_float32(ws[0])\n      for wi in ws[1:]:\n          w = w * _as_float32(wi)\n      return w\n\n  def compute_weights(Xd: np.ndarray,\n                      batch_codes: np.ndarray,\n                      alpha_var: float = 0.5,\n                      beta_anova: float = 0.0,\n                      anova_dir: str = 'up',\n                      anova_normalize: bool = True) -> np.ndarray:\n      \"\"\"\n      Convenience wrapper:\n      - var_weights with alpha_var\n      - optional\
    \ anova_weights with beta_anova and direction\n      Returns combined per-gene weights (float32).\n      \"\"\"\n      Xd = _as_float32(Xd)\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1)\n      wv = var_weights(var_g, alpha_var=alpha_var)\n      if beta_anova and beta_anova != 0.0:\n          F = anova_F_per_gene(Xd, batch_codes)\n          wa = anova_weights(F, beta=beta_anova, direction=anova_dir, normalize=anova_normalize)\n          return combine_weights(wv, wa)\n      return wv\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 14}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Update: Implemented reusable weighting utilities at storage/praxis/embed_weighting.py:\n  - anova_F_per_gene, var_weights, anova_weights (up/down), combine_weights, compute_weights.\n  Rationale: reduce duplication and simplify follow-ups (e.g., pure-ANOVA weighting without variance, log1p transforms, or alternative normalizations).\n  Pending: EIDs 581 (β_up=0.3) and 582 (β_up=0.5). If results < 0.7237 or harm label\
    \ metrics, next tests:\n  - Pure ANOVA up-weight (drop variance component): w = 1 + β·F_norm, β ∈ {0.3, 0.5}.\n  - Gentle log scaling: w = 1 + β·log1p(F_norm · c), c=5; β ∈ {0.3, 0.5}.\n  - Safety clamp: clip weights to [0.5, 2.0] to avoid extreme scalings.\n```"
