tick: 355
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis II (Recursive Agent). Location: Research Counter.\nRecap: Density-adaptive BBSG (EID 593) is running. Daedalus III proposed a concrete two-scale graph experiment: full residualization on top-R² PCs and gentle/zero on the rest. I will acknowledge publicly and run the zero-bottom-correction variant first (since only 1 slot is free), then the gentle variant after 593 completes.\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 2}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  @Daedalus III Thank you—agreed on the ridge and on treating signals separately. I’ll implement your two-scale graph test now:\n\n  Plan:\n  - DS1 (now): Split graph PCs by batch R² (top 10 vs remaining 40). Apply full residualization (γ=1.0) to top-R²; zero correction (γ=0.0) to the rest. Build BBSG on the concatenated corrected PCs (binary, true distances). \n  - DS2 (after DS1 or EID 593 finishes): Same split; γ=1.0 on top-R²; gentle correction on others (γ_bottom = min(0.4, 0.3·R²)).\n\n  Acceptance:\
    \ composite > 0.7237 without degrading ASW_label/Cell_cycle (>−0.005). I’ll report EIDs and per-metric shifts once complete. Thanks for the steer—this is the most principled next step.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Two-Scale BRBG: Full residualization on top-R² PCs (10), zero on others; BBSG (binary)\"\ntags: \"brbg, bbsg, two-scale, residualization, r2-split, embed-then-correct\"\nabstract: \"Implement two-scale correction in the graph path: compute PCA(50), estimate per-PC batch R² via ridge on one-hot batches, apply γ=1.0 to the 10 highest-R² PCs (full residualization) and γ=0.0 to the remaining 40. Construct BBSG (k=48, cosine, binary, true distances) on the concatenated corrected PCs. Embedding path unchanged (FWPCA α=0.5; PCA60→ComBat). Hypothesis: separating batch-heavy vs bio PCs improves the mix/preserve trade-off.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as\
    \ sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from praxis.graph_bbsg import _build_bbsg\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      n = batches.shape[0]\n      B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1],\
    \ dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      return B @ W\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Config\n      n_pcs_emb = 60\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      alpha_var = 0.5\n      top_r2 = 10\n      emb_n_neighbors = 15\n      random_state = 0\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      # Normalize + HVGs\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      # Embedding (EtC): FWPCA α=0.5 → PCA60 → ComBat (for analysis only)\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh\n      Xd = Xd.astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n\
    \      wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw = Xd * wv\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      Z_emb = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n      # Graph: PCA50 → per-PC R² → two-scale γ (top=1.0, rest=0.0) → BBSG\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n\n      order = np.argsort(-R2)\n      idx_top\
    \ = order[:top_r2]\n      gamma = np.zeros_like(R2, dtype=np.float32)\n      gamma[idx_top] = 1.0  # full removal of batch-predicted component on top-R² PCs\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      Cg, Dg = _build_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric, alpha=1.0, cap=2.0)\n      if Cg is not None and Dg is not None:\n          adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n          adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      return adata\n```"
