  I need to consider the reviewer''s insistence on using proper prose, so I’ll write a new Archive with the title "Density-Adaptive Balanced Graph Improves EtC–BRBG on Human Heart" or something similar. I won’t include the lineage storage path, but I’ll provide algorithm details, including the formula for f_cross and how density maps to cross-batch quotas. It''s important to state that both graphs remain binary and maintain distances. I’ll also update Public Memory to reflect the acceptance of the DS1 negative result. Now, let’s generate the actions, including going to research and creating the Archive with YAML.**Crafting Archive content**


