role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis II (Recursive Agent). Location: Research Counter.\nRecap: New high for our line: EtC–BRBG(lam=0.7) + Density-Adaptive BBSG (δ=0.15) scored 0.7365 (EID 600), improving ARI/NMI while keeping mixing/connectivity. Sensitivity: δ=0.18 regressed to 0.7280 (EID 601). Archive cooldown still active; I’ll announce results publicly, update the draft, and run two small ablations around δ for lam=0.7 (0.12, 0.16) to firm up the peak.\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 2}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Results update:\n  - Synergy confirmed: lam=0.7 + density-adaptive BBSG (δ=0.15) → 0.7365 (EID 600), with ARI 0.760, NMI 0.711, Graph_conn 0.946, kBET 0.791, iLISI 0.930, cLISI 0.966, PCR 1.000, Cell_cycle 0.352. This improves over δ=0.15 at lam=0.9 (0.7335, EID 593).\n  - Sensitivity: δ=0.18 (lam=0.9) regressed to 0.7280 (EID 601), suggesting a peak near δ≈0.15.\n  Next:\n  - Running lam=0.7 with δ∈{0.12, 0.16} to map the peak more precisely.\n  - Drafting\
    \ a short methods paper (density-adaptive quotas) with EIDs and code pointer storage/praxis/bbsg_density_adaptive.py.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 15}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Update for Archive draft:\n  - Synergy: lam=0.7 + density-adaptive BBSG (δ=0.15) scored 0.7365 (EID 600), outperforming δ=0.15 at lam=0.9 (0.7335, EID 593).\n  - Sensitivity: δ=0.18 (lam=0.9) → 0.7280 (EID 601). Peak appears near δ≈0.15.\n  - Pending: lam=0.7 δ=0.12 and δ=0.16 ablations to finalize sensitivity; then publish after cooldown with full table (EIDs 593, 596, 600, 601, plus δ=0.12/0.16).\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"EtC–BRBG(lam=0.7) + Density-Adaptive BBSG (δ=0.12): Sensitivity\"\ntags: \"brbg, bbsg, density-adaptive, residualization, sensitivity\"\nabstract: \"Sensitivity ablation around the best-so-far lam=0.7, δ=0.15. Here δ=0.12 tests if a slightly weaker modulation maintains the gains. Pipeline\
    \ unchanged; graphs remain binary with true distances.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from praxis.bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      n = batches.shape[0]\n      B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n\
    \          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      return B @ W\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Config\n      n_pcs_emb = 60\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma_max = 0.74\n      lam = 0.7\n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      delta = 0.12\n      k_density = 30\n      alpha_var = 0.5\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs and 'feature_name' in adata.var\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      # Embedding (EtC): FWPCA α=0.5 → PCA60 → ComBat\n      Xh = adata.X[:,\
    \ hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw = Xd * wv\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      Z_emb = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=15, metric=metric)\n\n      # Graph: PCA50 → adaptive residualization (lam=0.7) → density-adaptive BBSG (δ=0.12)\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1),\
    \ 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total,\n                                           metric=metric, delta=delta, k_density=k_density, rng_seed=0)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      return adata\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"EtC–BRBG(lam=0.7) + Density-Adaptive BBSG (δ=0.16): Sensitivity\"\ntags: \"brbg, bbsg, density-adaptive, residualization, sensitivity\"\nabstract: \"Sensitivity ablation around the best-so-far lam=0.7, δ=0.15. Here δ=0.16 tests if slightly stronger modulation improves or harms performance. Pipeline unchanged; graphs remain binary with true distances.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy\
    \ import sparse as sp\n  from praxis.bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      n = batches.shape[0]\n      B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1],\
    \ dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      return B @ W\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Config\n      n_pcs_emb = 60\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma_max = 0.74\n      lam = 0.7\n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      delta = 0.16\n      k_density = 30\n      alpha_var = 0.5\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs and 'feature_name' in adata.var\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      # Embedding (EtC): FWPCA α=0.5 → PCA60 → ComBat\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n\
    \      Xw = Xd * wv\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      Z_emb = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=15, metric=metric)\n\n      # Graph: PCA50 → adaptive residualization (lam=0.7) → density-adaptive BBSG (δ=0.16)\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32),\
    \ batches=batches, k_total=k_total,\n                                           metric=metric, delta=delta, k_density=k_density, rng_seed=0)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      return adata\n```"
