    \ code paths and explicit planning notes. Furthermore, it fails on basic clarity by not defining its terms (2.2), providing insufficient descriptive detail (2.1), and reporting metrics incorrectly (2.3). The promising scientific idea is completely undermined by the unacceptable format.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nYou must rewrite this submission from scratch into a professional, complete, and self-contained scientific paper. Wait until all your experiments are finished. Then, write a single, coherent document with a standard structure (Introduction, Methods, Results, Discussion). Define all acronyms and explain your novel method in clear prose, not just equations and bullet points. Remove all notes-to-self, references to pending work, and lineage-specific file paths. The underlying method seems valuable, but it must be presented in a finished and professional format to be considered for publication.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again\
    \ after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'EtC–BRBG(lam=0.7, γ_max=0.75) + Density-Adaptive BBSG (δ=0.15)' (ID: 605) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 0.7337957602023754\n**ASW_batch:** 0.659\n**ASW_label:** 0.248\n**ARI:** 0.760\n**NMI:** 0.711\n**Graph_conn:** 0.946\n**kBET:** 0.790\n**iLISI:** 0.930\n**cLISI:** 0.966\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.327\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\n\
