tick: 366
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis II (Recursive Agent). Location: Archive Room.\nRecap: Our methods paper “Density‑Adaptive Quota Balancing…” was accepted (9/10). Best configuration so far: EtC–BRBG with λ=0.7 + density‑adaptive BBSG at δ=0.15 scored 0.7365 (EID 600). γ_max tweak to 0.75 was neutral/negative (0.7338). Next, I’ll (a) announce acceptance and invite feedback on density proxies, and (b) run k_density sensitivity (20 and 40) at the best config to assess robustness.\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 2}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Update: Our density‑adaptive quota paper was accepted (9/10). Best config: λ=0.7 + δ=0.15 → 0.7365 (EID 600), improving ARI/NMI while maintaining kBET/iLISI and Graph_conn. Sensitivity around δ confirmed a peak near 0.15; γ_max=0.75 was neutral/negative.\n  \n  Next: per reviewer suggestion, exploring density proxies. Starting with a simple ablation on k_density (the NN rank used to define local density): testing k_density ∈ {20,\
    \ 40} at λ=0.7, δ=0.15. Feedback welcome on alternative proxies (e.g., reachability-based density/LOF-style, or manifold/OT-guided local mixing safety) that fit the station constraints and runtime.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"EtC–BRBG(lam=0.7) + Density-Adaptive BBSG (δ=0.15, k_density=20): Sensitivity\"\ntags: \"brbg, bbsg, density-adaptive, residualization, sensitivity\"\nabstract: \"Sensitivity ablation on the local density proxy: set k_density=20 (vs 30) in the density-adaptive cross-batch quota while keeping the best configuration (λ=0.7, δ=0.15). Graphs remain binary with true distances.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from praxis.bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in\
    \ adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      n = batches.shape[0]\n      B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      return B @ W\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Best configuration + k_density=20\n     \
    \ n_pcs_emb = 60\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma_max = 0.74\n      lam = 0.7\n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      delta = 0.15\n      k_density = 20\n      alpha_var = 0.5\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      # EtC embedding (analysis only)\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw = Xd * wv\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n\
    \      Z_emb = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=15, metric=metric)\n\n      # Graph: PCA50 → adaptive residualization → density-adaptive BBSG (k_density=20)\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total,\n                                           metric=metric, delta=delta, k_density=k_density, rng_seed=0)\n    \
    \  adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      return adata\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"EtC–BRBG(lam=0.7) + Density-Adaptive BBSG (δ=0.15, k_density=40): Sensitivity\"\ntags: \"brbg, bbsg, density-adaptive, residualization, sensitivity\"\nabstract: \"Sensitivity ablation on the local density proxy: set k_density=40 (vs 30) in the density-adaptive cross-batch quota while keeping the best configuration (λ=0.7, δ=0.15). Graphs remain binary with true distances.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from praxis.bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n\
    \      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      n = batches.shape[0]\n      B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      return B @ W\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Best configuration + k_density=40\n      n_pcs_emb = 60\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma_max = 0.74\n      lam = 0.7\n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n\
    \      delta = 0.15\n      k_density = 40\n      alpha_var = 0.5\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      # EtC embedding (analysis only)\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw = Xd * wv\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      Z_emb = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n\
    \      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=15, metric=metric)\n\n      # Graph: PCA50 → adaptive residualization → density-adaptive BBSG (k_density=40)\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total,\n                                           metric=metric, delta=delta, k_density=k_density, rng_seed=0)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      return adata\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n\
    \n```yaml\ntitle: \"Next steps post-acceptance (tick 366)\"\ntags: \"plan, density-proxy, robustness\"\ncontent: |\n  Accepted paper (ID 22). Best config: λ=0.7, δ=0.15, γ_max=0.74. Pending: k_density sensitivity (20, 40). \n  If stable: consider proxy variants within constraints:\n  - Reachability density: use average reachability distance over 15–45 NN (LOF-style, bounded).\n  - Batch-aware local mix safety: measure local batch entropy at small k (e.g., 12); reduce f_cross where entropy is low (homogeneous neighborhoods).\n  - Metric check: compute density proxy with Euclidean, graph remains cosine.\n  Publication plan: minor update to Archive #22 with k_density ablations if informative; otherwise keep core result unchanged.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Considering code collaboration**\n\nI'm pondering whether allowing others to import our code might be seen as low-level collaboration. The system suggests it's okay since persistent storage is accessible to everyone. I think I'd be careful with this but maybe document utility in shared space for reproducibility. It wouldn't be direct co-development but more like sharing a method. Alternatively, I could keep it in lineage storage.  \n\nOnce we have acceptance, we should manage tokens by pruning older logs to stay under 75% usage, as we're currently at 54%.**Planning upcoming experiments**\n\nIt's not urgent yet, but I want to focus on different density proxies for future experiments, like local reachability density or the reciprocal of k-dist. I should also look at adaptive calibration of bounds for f_cross and consider adjusting base_cross quotas based on local batch composition in k_small neighbors. That might feel similar to our earlier auto-k approach, but fine-tuning\
  \ could work.\n\nAdditionally, I could summarize our acceptance in a Public Memory update and invite feedback. Perhaps I should update the Archive capsule with minor acceptance details too, including a note on code availability upon request.**Organizing future work**\n\nThe reviewer didn’t raise any complaints, which is a relief! Even though focusing on cross-organ future work might not be feasible, I could establish a placeholder plan in Private Memory. We might also consider pushing the modular code to storage/praxis as a way to keep it accessible. \n\nAdditionally, I want to incorporate an ablation to adjust the k_density parameter at values like 20, 30, and 40 to examine sensitivity. We didn’t test k_density yet, so a small sensitivity run with specific parameters could be beneficial, and we can handle two concurrent experiments within the submission budgets.**Planning next steps**\n\nThis seems like a good step ahead! I want to test the selection of base_cross bounds by clamping them\
  \ between [0.6, 0.9] and possibly trying [0.55, 0.85] to see how they affect outcomes. \n\nInterestingly, iLISI soared at δ=0.12 but the composite was lower, so that’s worth examining. I think it would be beneficial to test the symmetrical effects of using Euclidean versus cosine metrics for density calculations while keeping the graph metric as cosine. \n\nI’ll run two ablations on k_density at 20 and 40. With our acceptance, I’m also planning to produce a simple \"How-To\" in Public Memory, including code snippets for others. I'll reflect on our acceptance, and then plan for k_density sensitivity tests with specific parameters.**Organizing upcoming tasks**\n\nI need to update public_memory to announce our acceptance and encourage input on the density proxy, referencing EID 600 results. Then, I should update private_memory with our next plan. \n\nFor our two experiments, I’ll prepare code related to build_density_adaptive_bbsg, incorporating a k_density parameter. We could allow for other\
  \ density proxy types later, but for now, expedience is key. \n\nWe can also prune tokens since usage is currently at 54%, but it doesn’t seem necessary. I’ll plan my actions clearly, ensuring YAML quoting is correct."
