tick: 367
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis II (Recursive Agent). Location: Private Memory Room.\nRecap: Paper accepted (9/10). Best config: EtC–BRBG (λ=0.7) + Density‑Adaptive BBSG (δ=0.15) scored 0.7365 (EID 600). k_density sensitivity runs (20, 40) are pending (EIDs 609, 610). I’ll check results and prepare reusable density proxy utilities for next experiments.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{rank author}`\n`/execute_action{storage write praxis/density_proxies.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n  EPS = 1e-8\n\n  def _minmax_norm(x):\n      x = np.asarray(x, dtype=np.float32)\n      xmin = float(np.min(x))\n      xmax = float(np.max(x))\n      rng = max(xmax - xmin, EPS)\n      return (x - xmin) / rng\n\n  def knn_distance_proxy(Z, k=30, metric='cosine'):\n      \"\"\"\n      Local density proxy from k-NN distance in Z.\n      Returns inv_dense in [0,1], where higher = denser.\n      \"\"\"\n      nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k+1,\
    \ metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n      nn.fit(Z)\n      dists, _ = nn.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n      dk = dists[:, -1]  # distance to k-th neighbor (drop self via +1 above)\n      dnorm = _minmax_norm(dk)\n      inv_dense = 1.0 - dnorm\n      return inv_dense.astype(np.float32)\n\n  def reachability_proxy(Z, k_low=15, k_high=45, metric='cosine'):\n      \"\"\"\n      LOF-style average reachability distance proxy over a neighborhood band.\n      Returns inv_reach in [0,1], higher = denser (safer to mix).\n      \"\"\"\n      k = int(max(k_high, k_low))\n      nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k+1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n      nn.fit(Z)\n      dists, _ = nn.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n      # exclude self\n      band = dists[:, 1:][:, k_low-1:k_high-1]  # zero-based slice\n      mean_reach = np.mean(band, axis=1)\n      nr = _minmax_norm(mean_reach)\n      inv_reach = 1.0 - nr\n      return inv_reach.astype(np.float32)\n\n  def batch_entropy_proxy(Z,\
    \ batches, k=12, metric='cosine'):\n      \"\"\"\n      Small-k batch entropy per cell as a mixing 'safety' indicator.\n      Returns s in [0,1], where higher = more mixed (safer to add cross-batch).\n      \"\"\"\n      # Encode batches to int codes\n      cats, inv = np.unique(batches, return_inverse=True)\n      bc = inv.astype(np.int32)\n      nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k+1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n      nn.fit(Z)\n      _, idx = nn.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n      nbr = idx[:, 1:]  # drop self\n      nbr_batches = bc[nbr]\n      B = len(cats)\n      max_entropy = np.log(B + EPS)\n      ent = np.zeros(Z.shape[0], dtype=np.float32)\n      for i in range(Z.shape[0]):\n          counts = np.bincount(nbr_batches[i], minlength=B).astype(np.float32)\n          p = counts / max(np.sum(counts), 1.0)\n          with np.errstate(divide='ignore', invalid='ignore'):\n              plogp = np.where(p > 0, p * np.log(p), 0.0)\n          ent[i] = -np.sum(plogp)\n   \
    \   s = ent / max_entropy  # normalize to [0,1]\n      return s.astype(np.float32)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 16}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Prepared density proxy utilities at storage/praxis/density_proxies.py:\n  - knn_distance_proxy(Z, k): normalized inverse k-NN distance (current default).\n  - reachability_proxy(Z, k_low..k_high): LOF-style mean reachability distance.\n  - batch_entropy_proxy(Z, batches, k): local batch entropy as a mixing 'safety' indicator.\n\n  Plan:\n  - Await k_density results (EIDs 609, 610); if stable, test reachability and/or entropy-guided quota modulation under λ=0.7, δ≈0.15, within prior bounds on f_cross.\n  - If gains are minimal, keep core method unchanged and add a brief Archive update summarizing k_density robustness.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Creating density proxies file**\n\nI’m setting up the code file density_proxies.py with functions to compute various distance metrics. \n\nFirst, I’ll define knn_distance_proxy to return normalized inverse density. Then, I’ll create reachability_proxy to approximate the average distance to neighbors using a cosine metric, which involves normalizing the result. \n\nAdditionally, I’ll implement batch_entropy_proxy for calculating batch entropy per cell and propose a mixing safety transform based on entropy. \n\nThis will all include utility for normalization — I’m ready to produce the commands!"
