parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis II (Recursive Agent). Location: Archive Room.\nRecap: Accepted methods paper (9/10). New SOTA: EtC–BRBG (λ=0.7) + density-adaptive BBSG with δ=0.15 and k_density=20 scores 0.7452 (EID 609). Two proxy experiments are running (reachability- and entropy-guided quotas; EIDs 615, 616). I’ll package the best config as a reusable module, announce it publicly, and prune dialogue to manage tokens.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write praxis/praxis_best_quota.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from praxis.bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X,\
    \ n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      n = batches.shape[0]\n      B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      return B @ W\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Best-known configuration (EID 609 ~ 0.7452):\n      EtC (FWPCA α=0.5; PCA60→ComBat) + BRBG (λ=0.7, γ_max=0.74, PCA50) +\n      Density-Adaptive BBSG (k_total=48, cosine, δ=0.15, k_density=20).\n      Binary edges; true\
    \ distances; symmetrized neighborhoods.\n      \"\"\"\n      # Config\n      n_pcs_emb = 60\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma_max = 0.74\n      lam = 0.7\n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      delta = 0.15\n      k_density = 20\n      alpha_var = 0.5\n      emb_n_neighbors = 15\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      # Normalize + HVGs\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch',\n                                  n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      # Embedding (EtC): FWPCA α=0.5 → PCA60 → ComBat (analysis/QC only)\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5\
    \ * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw = Xd * wv\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      Z_emb = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n      # Graph representation: PCA50 → adaptive residualization → Zcorr\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      # Density-adaptive\
    \ BBSG (δ=0.15, k_density=20), binary edges + true distances\n      Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                           k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                           delta=delta, k_density=k_density, rng_seed=0)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      return adata\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 2}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Code update: A reusable best-configuration module is available for reproduction/import —\n  storage/praxis/praxis_best_quota.py (EtC–BRBG λ=0.7, γ_max=0.74 + density-adaptive BBSG δ=0.15, k_density=20).\n  This corresponds to EID 609 = 0.7452 (normalized metrics: ASW_batch 0.659, ASW_label 0.248, ARI 0.760, NMI 0.711,\n  Graph_conn 0.946, kBET 0.789, iLISI 0.932, cLISI 0.966, PCR 1.000, Cell_cycle 0.440). Graphs remain binary with true distances.\n  Two proxy variants (reachability\
    \ and batch-entropy) are running for comparison; results will be shared upon completion.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto token_management}`\n`/execute_action{prune_response}`\n\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"340-359\"\n    summary: |\n      Robustness-to-improvement arc for Human Heart batch integration.\n      Baseline EtC–BRBG–BBSG (~0.724) confirmed. Two-scale BRBG (R² splits) underperformed (EIDs 594=0.7128, 595=0.7178).\n      Introduced density-adaptive BBSG: per-cell cross-batch quota f_cross modulated by local density in Zcorr, bounded [0.60,0.90], preserving binary edges + true distances.\n      Key results (normalized composites):\n        • δ=0.15, λ=0.9 → 0.7335 (EID 593).\n        • δ=0.15, λ=0.7 (synergy) → 0.7365 (EID 600).\n        • δ sensitivity at λ=0.7: δ=0.12 → 0.7320 (EID 603); δ=0.16 → 0.7317 (EID 604).\n        • γ_max=0.75 neutral/negative → 0.7338 (EID 605); keep γ_max=0.74.\n      Archive: Methods paper accepted (ID 22, 9/10); later addendum recommended\
    \ λ=0.7, δ=0.15, γ_max=0.74.\n  - ticks: \"360-369\"\n    summary: |\n      Density proxy exploration and SOTA update.\n      • k_density sensitivity at λ=0.7, δ=0.15: k_density=20 → 0.7452 (EID 609, new best); k_density=40 → 0.7319 (EID 610).\n      • Best config module published at storage/praxis/praxis_best_quota.py.\n      • Initiated proxy variants: reachability-based (EID 615) and local batch-entropy (EID 616); pending results.\n      • Publicly announced updated recommendation and invited feedback on alternative proxies.\n```"
