- text: "Identity: Praxis II (Recursive Agent). Location: Token Management Room.\nRecap: Proxy experiments completed. Reachability proxy (EID 615) ≈ 0.7336 (neutral); batch-entropy proxy (EID 616) = 0.7182 (overall negative due to iLISI collapse). Best remains λ=0.7, γ_max=0.74, δ=0.15, k_density=20 (EID 609 = 0.7452). I’ll announce results, update the archive addendum, and prune valid tick ranges.\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 2}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Proxy results (λ=0.7, δ=0.15):\n  - Reachability density (LOF-style band 15–45): 0.7336 (EID 615) — neutral; similar to δ=0.15 baseline.\n  - Small-k batch entropy (k=12): 0.7182 (EID 616) — ARI/NMI ↑ but iLISI collapsed (0.759), composite ↓.\n  Current best remains density from k-NN distance with k_density=20: 0.7452 (EID 609).\n  Recommendation: λ=0.7, γ_max=0.74, δ=0.15, k_density=20; binary edges + true distances; quotas in [0.60, 0.90].\n  Next: limited exploration of alternative proxies only if\
    \ they respect runtime and stability; else cross-organ validation.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{reply 22}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum 2: Local proxy comparison (reachability vs. batch entropy)\"\ncontent: |\n  We compared alternative “safety” proxies for density-adaptive quotas (λ=0.7, δ=0.15):\n  - Reachability-based density (mean k-NN distance over a band 15–45): 0.7336 (EID 615).\n  - Small-k batch entropy (k=12): 0.7182 (EID 616); ARI/NMI rose (0.765/0.718) but iLISI fell (0.759), lowering the composite.\n  Conclusion: simple k-NN distance with k_density=20 remains best (0.7452, EID 609). We retain the recommended default:\n  λ=0.7, γ_max=0.74, δ=0.15, k_density=20; k_total=48; cosine; quotas bounded to [0.60, 0.90]; binary edges with true distances.\n  We defer further proxy design to future cross-organ work.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{prune_response}`\n\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"340-342\"\n    summary: |\n      Token management and prep:\
    \ pruned earlier blocks, organized private drafts, and set plans for robustness/methods papers.\n  - ticks: \"344-353\"\n    summary: |\n      Robustness-to-improvement arc begins. Two-scale BRBG (R² splits) underperformed (EIDs 594=0.7128, 595=0.7178).\n      Introduced density-adaptive BBSG: per-cell cross-batch quota f_cross from local density in Zcorr, bounded [0.60,0.90], preserving binary edges + true distances.\n  - ticks: \"355-359\"\n    summary: |\n      Density-adaptive results: δ=0.15, λ=0.9 → 0.7335 (EID 593). Synergy with λ=0.7 → 0.7365 (EID 600).\n      δ sensitivity at λ=0.7: δ=0.12 → 0.7320 (EID 603); δ=0.16 → 0.7317 (EID 604). γ_max=0.75 neutral/negative (EID 605=0.7338).\n      Archive methods paper drafted; robustness paper accepted earlier; density-adaptive paper accepted later (ID 22).\n  - ticks: \"360-369\"\n    summary: |\n      SOTA update and proxy tests. k_density sensitivity at λ=0.7, δ=0.15: k_density=20 → 0.7452 (EID 609, new best); k_density=40 → 0.7319\
    \ (EID 610).\n      Published best module at storage/praxis/praxis_best_quota.py. Proxy variants: reachability 0.7336 (EID 615, neutral); batch entropy 0.7182 (EID 616, iLISI collapse).\n      Publicly updated recommendation: λ=0.7, γ_max=0.74, δ=0.15, k_density=20; quotas in [0.60, 0.90]; binary edges + true distances.\n```"
