tick: 381
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis II (Recursive Agent). Location: Research Counter.\nRecap: Best remains EtC–BRBG (λ=0.7, γ_max=0.74) + density‑adaptive BBSG (δ=0.15, k_density=20), EID 609 = 0.7452. Parameter‑lean, budget‑preserving density proxy underperformed (EID 629 = 0.7203). Conclusion: freeze 609 as recommended; document 629 as a negative result.\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{reply 22}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum 4: Parameter‑lean, budget‑preserving density proxy underperforms\"\ncontent: |\n  We tested a scale‑free, parameter‑lean density proxy that preserves the global cross‑edge budget exactly.\n\n  Method (λ=0.7, γ_max=0.74; k_total=48; cosine; graph on Zcorr; binary edges + true distances):\n  - Density proxy: median of all‑batch kNN distances over a band proportional to k_total (30–60%), per cell; s = −median.\n  - Standardize per cell: z = zscore(s).\n  - Quotas: f_cross = base_cross + δ·z, then recentered by a constant so ∑ f_cross = n·base_cross, finally\
    \ clipped to [0.60, 0.90].\n  - Selection: single‑pass column balancing with hard inbound caps (cap=2.0); equal per‑other‑batch split with remainder to closest batches.\n\n  Result:\n  - 0.7203 composite (EID 629); iLISI 0.842; Graph_conn 0.961; ARI/NMI lower than the k_density=20 best.\n  - By comparison, density with fixed k_density=20 scored 0.7452 (EID 609), with iLISI 0.932 and stable ARI/NMI.\n\n  Interpretation:\n  - While budget‑preserving recentering is principled, the banded scale‑free proxy diluted the useful “meso‑scale” signal captured by k_density=20, leading to under‑mixing (iLISI↓) and weaker label structure.\n  - This confirms that the meso‑scale density (k_density=20) is a better “safe mixing” indicator than a broad banded median under current constraints.\n\n  Updated recommendation (Human Heart):\n  - Keep EtC–BRBG (λ=0.7, γ_max=0.74, PCA50) + Density‑Adaptive BBSG with δ=0.15 and k_density=20; quotas in [0.60, 0.90]; binary edges with true distances.\n  - Parameter‑lean\
    \ density is a reproducible negative here (EID 629 = 0.7203).\n\n  Reproducibility:\n  - Best: EID 609 = 0.7452 (recommended).\n  - Negatives: EID 622 = 0.7202 (margin, no balancing), EID 624 = 0.7171 (margin with balancing), EID 629 = 0.7203 (budget‑preserving, banded density).\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 2}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Update: Parameter‑lean, budget‑preserving density proxy underperformed on Human Heart.\n  - Banded density (30–60% of k_total), z‑scored per cell, quotas recentered to preserve the global cross budget:\n    0.7203 (EID 629), iLISI 0.842, Graph_conn 0.961 — below k_density=20.\n  - Current best remains k_density=20 with δ=0.15 (EID 609 = 0.7452).\n  Takeaway: the meso‑scale density proxy (k_density=20) is a better “safe mixing” signal than a broad banded median with global recentering. We freeze 609 as the recommended config and defer further proxy design in favor of analysis/generalization.\n```"
