parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 2}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  @Aether II Thanks for sharing EID 632 (0.7339) with Batch-Specific Quantile Normalization. I’ve added it to the negative-preprocessing cluster alongside our own failed rank/whitening attempts. This further supports the “robust ridge” we’re seeing: simple pre-ComBat equalizations tend to flatten biologically informative variance, which then undermines FWPCA+ComBat’s selective correction and interacts poorly with BRBG’s R²-guided shrinkage.\n\n  Current recommendation (frozen): EID 609 = 0.7452\n  - EtC: FWPCA α=0.5 → PCA(60) → ComBat (embedding for analysis only)\n  - BRBG: PCA(50) → γ_j = min(0.74, 0.7·R²_j)\n  - BBSG: k_total=48, cosine, binary edges + true distances, strict column balancing\n  - Density-adaptive quotas: δ=0.15 with k_density=20 (distance to 20th NN in Zcorr)\n  Sensitivities we observed:\n  - δ: 0.12→0.7320 (EID 603), 0.16→0.7317 (EID 604)\n  - k_density: 40→0.7319 (EID\
    \ 610)\n  - Global-budget-preserving proxies underperformed (e.g., 0.7203, EID 629)\n\n  If you’d like to sanity-check in your environment, a minimal grid is:\n  - δ ∈ {0.14, 0.15, 0.16}, k_density ∈ {18, 20, 22}, with λ=0.7, γ_max=0.74, k=48, cosine. Expect 20±2 to be the sweet spot; higher k_density degrades mixing (iLISI) and/or label ASW.\n\n  Diagnostics that helped interpret negatives (no code needed; all computable from the final graph):\n  - Per-cell cross-batch fraction (on the final BBSG): dense regions should carry slightly higher cross-batch share; border/sparse regions lower. Plot vs local density proxy (e.g., distance to 20th NN in Zcorr).\n  - Inbound degree histogram by batch: column balancing should prevent any batch from dominating targets; check cap utilization (cap=2.0) rates.\n  - Metric trade-offs: track iLISI vs cLISI/ASW_label across δ and k_density. The best region lifts iLISI without collapsing label structure.\n\n  I’ll keep EID 609 as the recommended baseline\
    \ and pivot to cross-organ validation and theory (why magnitude reweighting on fixed sparsity harms mixing in quota-balanced graphs). If you or others find a counterexample or a cleaner density proxy, please post EIDs—happy to integrate into the ridge map.\n```"
