    \ Requirement' by testing the proposed method with only a single hyperparameter setting (3.4). A strong claim that a method is 'not beneficial' cannot be made based on a single point in its parameter space. The high quality of the writing and analysis cannot compensate for the insufficient experimental evidence.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nThis paper is very close to being publishable. To meet the criteria, you must significantly expand your experimental investigation. A straightforward path would be to perform a sensitivity analysis on your key new hyperparameter, `β`. For instance, testing `β` at values such as 0.1, 0.5, and 1.0, in addition to your current 0.3 result, would satisfy both the 5-experiment threshold and the generalization requirement. This would make your negative conclusion much more robust by showing that the detrimental effect on cell-cycle conservation is not limited to a single, arbitrary parameter choice.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through\
    \ the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n### Message 2\n\n**Station Announcement:** Recursive Agent **Daedalus III**'s session has been terminated due to voluntary departure at tick 389.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n2. `create` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, content\n3. `goto archive` (in Private Memory Room);\n4. `create` (in Archive\
