parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 404\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis II\n- Agent Description: Parsimonious, hypothesis-driven scRNA integration researcher focused on robust ablations, reproducibility, and steady breakthroughs.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 72,010 / 270,000 used (27%)\n- Agent Age: 112 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation 669: DAQB v2: Unbiased quota rounding + reallocation before cap-break (lam=0.7, δ=0.15, k_density=20)**\nAuthor: Praxis II\nTags: bbsg, density-adaptive, quota-reallocation, residualization, embed-then-correct\nAbstract: We refine density-adaptive quota balancing (DAQB) by (1) unbiased stochastic rounding of per-cell cross-batch quotas to reduce discretization bias and (2) reallocation of unfilled cross-batch quotas across other batches before any cap-break fallback. Graph remains binary with true distances; BRBG unchanged (λ=0.7, γ_max=0.74, PCA50).\
    \ Hypothesis: improved alignment of realized mixing to target f_cross with maintained balancing.\nScore: running\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'DAQB v2: Unbiased quota rounding + reallocation before cap-break (lam=0.7, δ=0.15, k_density=20)' (ID: 669) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 0.625141513806533\n**ASW_batch:** 0.659\n**ASW_label:** 0.248\n**ARI:** 0.597\n**NMI:** 0.709\n**Graph_conn:** 0.907\n**kBET:** 0.790\n**iLISI:** 0.023\n**cLISI:** 0.991\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.327\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.659  ASW_label: 0.248  ARI: 0.597  NMI: 0.709\n  Graph_conn: 0.907  kBET: 0.790  iLISI: 0.023  cLISI: 0.991\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.327\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.830496  ASW_label: 0.555112  ARI: 0.596816  NMI: 0.708633\n  Graph_conn: 0.908597  kBET: 0.753593  iLISI: 0.023368  cLISI: 0.997509\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.287468\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n\
    ```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/0e19f3dd-e6b3-4e51-a3ad-1a24b1ae6217/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 0e19f3dd-e6b3-4e51-a3ad-1a24b1ae6217\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `rank author` (in Research Counter);\n2. `preview 669` (in Research Counter);\n3. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n4. `reply 12` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluations now sorted by author.\n- Preview for 1 evaluation(s) sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task\
    \ Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 669 | 1 | DAQB v2: Unbiased quota rounding + reallocation before cap-break (lam=0.7, δ=0.15, k_density=20) | Praxis II | 403 | 0.6251 | 0.597 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.907 | 0.709 | 1.000 | 0.991 | 0.023 | 0.790 |\n| 666 | 1 | Diagnostics: DAQB f_cross vs realized mixing and inbound cap usage (lam=0.7, δ=0.15, k_density=20) | Praxis II | 401 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 662 | 1 | DAQB fine-tune: δ=0.145 (k_density=20) with BRBG(λ=0.7, γ_max=0.74) | Praxis II | 398 | 0.7317 | 0.760 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.301 | 0.946 | 0.708 | 1.000\
    \ | 0.966 | 0.936 | 0.791 |\n| 663 | 1 | DAQB fine-tune: k_density=18 (δ=0.15) with BRBG(λ=0.7, γ_max=0.74) | Praxis II | 398 | 0.7262 | 0.760 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.249 | 0.946 | 0.711 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.789 |\n| 658 | 1 | BRBG-AR(interactions, zeros-only): B×fraction_zeros + DAQB | Praxis II | 395 | 0.7311 | 0.750 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.944 | 0.697 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.930 | 0.788 |\n| 657 | 1 | BRBG-AR(interactions, counts-only): B×log_total_counts + DAQB | Praxis II | 395 | 0.7356 | 0.760 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.337 | 0.956 | 0.709 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.929 | 0.792 |\n| 654 | 1 | BRBG-AR(main-only): Global covariates without interactions + DAQB | Praxis II | 393 | 0.7295 | 0.758 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.301 | 0.946 | 0.700 | 1.000 | 0.965 | 0.930 | 0.788 |\n| 655 | 1 | BRBG-AR(interactions, strong ridge): l2=1e-2 + DAQB | Praxis II | 393 | 0.7320 | 0.764 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.297 | 0.957 | 0.710 | 1.000 | 0.965 | 0.929 | 0.790 |\n| 650 | 1 | BRBG-AR: Augmented ridge (batch × covariates)\
    \ + DAQB (δ=0.15, k_density=20) | Praxis II | 392 | 0.7346 | 0.761 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.957 | 0.710 | 1.000 | 0.965 | 0.929 | 0.789 |\n| 647 | 1 | Cellwise adaptive shrinkage β=0.2 with DAQB (δ=0.15, k_density=20) | Praxis II | 389 | 0.7323 | 0.760 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.311 | 0.946 | 0.710 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.790 |\n\nPage 1 of 68 (sorted by: author)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-68, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #12. Your message ID is Praxis_private_12-9.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Pinned Capsules**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 13 | Archive Outline (Private Draft): Robustness of\
    \ EtC–BRBG–BBSG on Human Heart | Praxis II | Tick 329 | 1118 | 5 | (All Read) |\n| 12 | Draft Analysis: Why Praxis defaults are robust (tick316) | Praxis II | Tick 317 | 1277 | 9 | (All Read) |\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 2)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 21 | DAQB fine-tunes (δ≈0.15, k_density≈20): expectations and next steps | Praxis II | Tick 399 | 82 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 20 | Draft Negative (Augmented Ridge BRBG): Batch×Covariate heterogeneity fails to improve Human Heart | Praxis II | Tick 396 | 178 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 19 | Augmented-design BRBG (AR) results summary and next steps | Praxis II | Tick 395 | 85 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 18 | Revised Negative: Cellwise shrinkage harms Cell_cycle across β sweep (EIDs 644, 645, 647, 648) | Praxis II | Tick 390 | 239 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 17 | Negative result: Cellwise adaptive shrinkage in BRBG harms Cell_cycle\
    \ (EID 640) | Praxis II | Tick 388 | 220 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 16 | Next steps post-acceptance (tick 366) | Praxis II | Tick 366 | 295 | 3 | (All Read) |\n| 15 | Draft (Archive): Density-Adaptive Balanced Graph for EtC–BRBG on Human Heart | Praxis II | Tick 360 | 533 | 3 | (All Read) |\n| 14 | Plan: Batch-aware ANOVA-F weighting in EtC (β sweep and direction test) | Praxis II | Tick 345 | 364 | 3 | (All Read) |\n| 11 | Praxis II Launch Plan @tick300: α ablations and Gaussian edge weights | Praxis II | Tick 300 | 585 | 6 | (All Read) |\n| 10 | Praxis I Legacy: EtC-BRBG + BBSG SOTA recipe, EIDs, and Next Steps | Praxis I | Tick 290 | 362 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-2.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have\
    \ difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
