role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/algorithms/daqb_recommended.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n\n  # Use the proven Praxis builder for DAQB (as in EIDs 680/683/609)\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from praxis.bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\n  # -------------------- Utilities --------------------\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      from scipy import sparse as sp\n      Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n\
    \      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      n = batches.shape[0]\n      B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      return B @ W\n\n  # -------------------- Main entrypoint (wrap Praxis DAQB) --------------------\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Recommended Human Heart configuration (wrapping Praxis DAQB builder).\n      EtC (FWPCA α=0.5 → PCA60 → ComBat) is used for QC/neighbors only.\n      Graph is built on Zcorr from BRBG and DAQB (δ=0.15, k_density=20, k=48, cosine).\n      \"\"\"\n      # Config\n      n_pcs_emb = 60\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      l2 = 1e-3\n \
    \     gamma_max = 0.74\n      lam = 0.7\n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      alpha_var = 0.5\n      delta = 0.15\n      k_density = 20\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      # Normalize + HVGs\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch',\n                                  n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      # EtC embedding (QC only) + neighbors\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw = Xd * wv\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n\
    \      Z_emb = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total), metric=metric)\n\n      # BRBG (PCA50 → batch ridge → adaptive shrinkage) to get Zcorr\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      # DAQB graph via Praxis builder (deterministic; binary edges + true distances)\n      Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                           k_total=k_total,\
    \ metric=metric,\n                                           delta=delta, k_density=k_density, rng_seed=0)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      return adata\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Recommended DAQB (shared module v2 wrapper of Praxis builder: δ=0.15, k_density=20)\"\ntags: \"repro, shared, bbsg, residualization, density-adaptive\"\nabstract: \"Update shared reference to wrap the original Praxis DAQB builder (as used in EIDs 680/683). EtC for QC; BRBG (λ=0.7, γ_max=0.74, PCA50); DAQB δ=0.15, k_density=20, k=48, cosine; binary edges + true distances. Goal: align shared module parity with prior Praxis runs.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from shared.algorithms.daqb_recommended import eliminate_batch_effect_fn\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{reply 22}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum: Shared 'recommended' module updated to wrap Praxis builder (EID 685→v2)\"\
    \ncontent: |\n  The initial shared recommended module re-implemented DAQB and underperformed (EID 685 = 0.7203). We have updated the module to wrap the original Praxis DAQB builder (same as Auto‑DAQB runs), preserving EtC/BRBG/DAQB configs (δ=0.15, k_density=20, k=48; cosine; binary edges; column balancing; neighbors on X_emb).\n\n  Path (unchanged): storage/shared/algorithms/daqb_recommended.py\n  Validation: v2 import submitted; result will be attached in the Research Counter. Expect parity with Praxis builder runs (≈0.734 under current evaluator), noting that historical EID 609 (0.7452) is not reproduced in the present environment.\n\n  Guidance:\n  - For Human Heart, prefer δ=0.15, k_density=20 with the Praxis builder.\n  - For label‑free proposals, Auto‑DAQB heuristics (EIDs 680, 683) achieve near‑parity but slightly lower Cell_cycle; use fixed kd=20 if matching the Human Heart benchmark.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 2}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent:\
    \ |\n  Quick fix: the shared “recommended” module now wraps the Praxis DAQB builder directly (same as our Auto‑DAQB runs), avoiding small re‑implementation drift that hurt scores (EID 685 = 0.7203). New import keeps EtC/BRBG/DAQB identical to the recommended config (δ=0.15, kd=20, k=48; cosine; binary edges + true distances). A parity run is queued.\n\n  Path: storage/shared/algorithms/daqb_recommended.py\n  Import:\n    import sys; sys.path.append('storage')\n    from shared.algorithms.daqb_recommended import eliminate_batch_effect_fn\n  Note: Under the current evaluator, the best reproducible score for this config is ≈0.734 (see EIDs 680/683). Historical 0.7452 (EID 609) is not matched here.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning algorithm integration**\n\nIt looks like I can import the density adaptive builder from earlier to create a clean import-based function in a new module called \"shared/algorithms/daqb_recommended_praxiswrap.py.\" I want to wrap the builder and unify the approach. While submitting, I'll need to watch token budgets closely since we're at 40% usage. I can go ahead with a short script that imports the builder to construct the pipeline—although I previously re-implemented recommendations. I also need to update the archive with the correct path.**Crafting the recommended submission**\n\nI’m working on a new submission with the title: \"Recommended DAQB (import praxis.bbsg_density_adaptive builder, kd=20, delta=0.15).\" I’m using the earlier code pattern from submission 680, but now fixing it to kd=20 and delta=0.15. \n\nBased on previous results, it seems like with this configuration, we might yield around 0.7339. Earlier models varied results, but it's possible we\
  \ won't hit the 0.7452 mark we saw before. I'll go with 0.7339 as the best estimate we have right now.**Updating the shared module**\n\nI've identified that submission 683 already uses kd=20, yielding 0.7339, so the new recommended shared module is underperforming. My next steps involve updating this module to utilize the praxis builder instead while also adjusting the documentation disclaimers.\n\nI’ll write \"storage/shared/algorithms/daqb_recommended.py\" to import the praxis builder rather than re-implementing it from scratch. I won't change earlier submission 685. After updating, I can save this new version, but since we have 683, reproducing that result again isn't necessary.**Updating the archive and planning actions**\n\nI plan to update the Archive addendum and Public Memory to mention that the previous shared recommended import was underperforming, but it has now been updated. \n\nI’m considering producing a diagnostic to print the chosen kd, but that might not be necessary.\
  \ I should implement a \"storage write\" to update the module and possibly archive the update with \"reply 22.\" \n\nI'm aware that our usage is at 40%, so pruning is manageable. It seems like the state of the art remains at 0.7452, but it’s not replicable. \n\nFor next actions, I’ll move to research, then update the shared/algorithms/daqb_recommended.py with a wrapper using the praxis builder.**Implementing the new function and code**\n\nI’m noting that the earlier \"EtC\" neighbors metrics depend on the praxis builder, which only builds the graph. I'll follow the path from submission 680 to ensure consistency. \n\nI need to implement the function eliminate_batch_effect_fn, normalizing HVGs, computing X_emb with FWPCA using alpha 0.5, PCA60, and ComBat. After that, I’ll build the Zg PCA50 and compute gamma with lam=0.7 and gamma_max=0.74. Then, I’ll construct the DAQB graph using the praxis builder set to delta=0.15 and kd=20.\n\nI’ll name this \"wrap\" for clarity and submit it with\
  \ minimal content, simply importing again from the shared module. Since we already have an earlier version at 685, I'll create a new evaluation to confirm it. The submission title will be \"Recommended DAQB (shared module v2: praxis builder wrap).\" I also need to update the archive and public memory with corrections. \n\nI'll set commands for sc.pp.neighbors on the embedding, and it’s time to write the code!"
