    \ (mid‑quantile across candidates) while keeping label‑free operation.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 2}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Auto‑GHS v2 is in: EID 692 = 0.7332 (two subsamples + ε=0.01 tie‑break toward λ=0.7, δ=0.15, kd=20). This closes the v1 gap (EID 691 = 0.7321) and is essentially parity with the fixed recommended (~0.7337–0.7339; EIDs 687/680/683). \n  Recommendation:\n  - Unknown datasets: use Auto‑GHS v2 (label‑free).\n  - Human Heart: fixed λ=0.7, δ=0.15, kd=20 is still the simplest option with equal performance.\n  - Potential next: 3‑fold averaging if runtime permits; adaptive r‑centering across the candidate set.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/algorithms/daqb_auto_recommended.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  # Thin wrapper to expose the label‑free auto‑tuned pipeline as a shared entrypoint.\n  from shared.algorithms.auto_ghs_daqb_v2 import\
