tick: 424
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/algorithms/auto_ghs_daqb_v2_alpha025.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n\n  from praxis.bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n  from shared.diagnostics.graph_health import compute_graph_health\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n \
    \     cats = np.unique(batches)\n      n = batches.shape[0]\n      B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      return B @ W\n\n  def _batch_stratified_subsample(batches, max_per_batch=1200, rng=0):\n      rng = np.random.default_rng(rng)\n      b = np.asarray(batches)\n      idx = np.arange(b.shape[0])\n      out = []\n      for c in np.unique(b):\n          I = idx[b == c]\n          if I.size <= max_per_batch:\n              out.append(I)\n          else:\n              out.append(rng.choice(I, size=max_per_batch, replace=False))\n      return np.sort(np.concatenate(out, axis=0))\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Auto-GHS DAQB v2 with FWPCA\
    \ α=0.25 in the EtC embedding (neighbors/QC only).\n      Two subsamples averaged in GHS; ε-tie-break toward (λ=0.7, δ=0.15, k_density=20).\n      \"\"\"\n      # Config\n      n_pcs_emb = 60\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma_max = 0.74\n      lam_grid = [0.7, 0.8]\n      delta_grid = [0.14, 0.15, 0.16]\n      kd_grid = [18, 20, 22]\n      k_total = 48\n      cap = 2.0\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      alpha_var = 0.25  # changed from 0.5 (literature-backed synergy)\n      emb_n_neighbors = 15\n      rng_seed = 0\n      eps_tie = 0.01\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      # Normalize + HVGs\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch',\n                                  n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    \
    \  # EtC embedding (QC neighbors) with α=0.25\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw = Xd * wv\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      Z_emb = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n      # BRBG backbone\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0,\
    \ ddof=1), 0.0)\n\n      # Two subsamples\n      sub_idx1 = _batch_stratified_subsample(batches, max_per_batch=1200, rng=rng_seed + 1)\n      sub_idx2 = _batch_stratified_subsample(batches, max_per_batch=1200, rng=rng_seed + 2)\n\n      def eval_subset(sub_idx, lam, delta, kd):\n          R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n          gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n          Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n          Zcorr_s = Zcorr[sub_idx]\n          batches_s = batches[sub_idx]\n          C_s, D_s = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(\n              Zcorr_s.astype(np.float32), batches=batches_s,\n              k_total=k_total, metric=metric, delta=delta,\n              k_density=int(kd), rng_seed=rng_seed\n          )\n          ghs = compute_graph_health(C_s, D_s, batches_s, k_total=k_total, cap=cap)\n          return ghs[\"GHS\"]\n\n      best = None\n      # Coarse search\n      for lam in lam_grid:\n          for delta in delta_grid:\n              for kd in kd_grid:\n\
    \                  s1 = eval_subset(sub_idx1, lam, delta, kd)\n                  s2 = eval_subset(sub_idx2, lam, delta, kd)\n                  s_avg = 0.5 * (s1 + s2)\n                  cand = (s_avg, lam, delta, kd)\n                  if (best is None) or (s_avg > best[0]):\n                      best = cand\n\n      # ε tie-break toward defaults\n      def is_default(lam, delta, kd):\n          return abs(lam - 0.7) < 1e-9 and abs(delta - 0.15) < 1e-9 and int(kd) == 20\n\n      if best is None:\n          lam_best, delta_best, kd_best = 0.7, 0.15, 20\n      else:\n          top_score = best[0]\n          near = []\n          for lam in lam_grid:\n              for delta in delta_grid:\n                  for kd in kd_grid:\n                      s1 = eval_subset(sub_idx1, lam, delta, kd)\n                      s2 = eval_subset(sub_idx2, lam, delta, kd)\n                      s_avg = 0.5 * (s1 + s2)\n                      if top_score - s_avg <= eps_tie + 1e-12:\n                   \
    \       near.append((s_avg, lam, delta, kd))\n          near.sort(key=lambda t: t[0], reverse=True)\n          chosen = None\n          for s, lam, delta, kd in near:\n              if is_default(lam, delta, kd):\n                  chosen = (s, lam, delta, kd)\n                  break\n          if chosen is None:\n              chosen = near[0] if near else best\n          _, lam_best, delta_best, kd_best = chosen\n\n      # Final build on full data\n      R2_full = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma_full = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam_best * R2_full)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma_full)\n      Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(\n          Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n          k_total=k_total, metric=metric, delta=float(delta_best),\n          k_density=int(kd_best), rng_seed=rng_seed\n      )\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      adata.uns['auto_ghs_params_v2_alpha025'] = {\n          'lambda': float(lam_best),\
    \ 'delta': float(delta_best), 'k_density': int(kd_best),\n          'k_total': int(k_total), 'alpha_var': float(alpha_var), 'ghs_avg': float(best[0])\n      }\n      return adata\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Auto‑GHS DAQB v2 + EtC(FWPCA α=0.25): Label‑free graph tuning with improved embedding\"\ntags: \"auto, diagnostics, fwpca, embed-then-correct, bbsg, residualization\"\nabstract: \"We combine Auto‑GHS DAQB v2 (two subsamples, ε tie‑break) with an EtC embedding using FWPCA α=0.25 (ComBat on PCs), following prior synergy reports. The graph is tuned label‑free via the Graph Health Score, then rebuilt on full data (binary edges + true distances). Hypothesis: close the remaining gap to the 0.74x tier while retaining label‑free robustness.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from shared.algorithms.auto_ghs_daqb_v2_alpha025 import eliminate_batch_effect_fn\n```"
thinking_content: '**Evaluating next steps**


  I need to decide on our next steps for Praxis II. Our Auto-GHS v2 has achieved a score of 0.7332, which is close to the SOTA of 0.7452 with EID 609 under an older environment. In the current setup, our best score is 0.7337, while the leading scores are 0.7452 and around 0.7435 from Aether and Sophia. I’m considering if we could approach 0.743+ by exploring different synergies, particularly focusing on FWPCA.**Considering strategic options**


  I need to keep a critical and strategic approach as we forge our own path. Others have surpassed us in rankings, so I’m thinking of using our DAQB builder to reproduce synergy. While contributions can be either analytical or negative results, we''ve already published diagnostics and label-free auto-tuning. The plan for the next step involves testing Auto-GHS v2 on an unknown dataset. I can also consider integrating GHS to adapt the shrinkage parameter continuously, rather than using just grid values. Exploring synergy with δ and k_density may also yield improvements.**Exploring adjustments and methodologies**


  I’m considering adjusting the cap parameter for column balancing. Previously, with BBSG, the cap was set at 2.0, while variations of 1.5 and 2.5 showed neutral or negative results at lam 0.9. With DAQB, maybe cap interplay is important. I’m also pondering the metric choice between ''cosine'' and ''euclidean'' since Euclidean might yield slightly better results for DAQB, unlike the neutral past outcomes. I think a new experiment could involve "Batch-balanced approximate neighbors" or other balancing methods, but previous attempts with deeper candidates and randomization didn’t show promise.**Considering publication and experimentation**


  I’m thinking we could create an Archive paper to summarize the Auto-GHS method. We’ve updated our diagnostics, but haven’t published the new method yet. Writing an Archive submission would help fulfill our publishing goals by including definitions, algorithms, and results compared to the baseline. However, I also want to keep experimenting. The scoreboard shows other approaches achieving 0.7435, and I’m considering replicating the FWPCA α=0.25 synergy with our DAQB builder to reach similar results.**Proposing method adjustments**


  To push our state-of-the-art forward, I’m thinking about adapting the FWPCA α selection with our GHS. I realize that FWPCA α impacts embedding but not the graph itself. Our strategy could involve tuning α within an unsupervised objective while integrating DAQB’s δ and kd alongside lam using GHS. This approach could help us achieve a score near 0.743-0.744. So, I’ll propose submitting "Auto-GHS v2 + FWPCA α=0.25” while making some necessary code adjustments. I''ll also ensure to present an Archive update for support!**Planning code submission actions**


  I’m considering submitting a code block that simply replicates the function with alpha_var set to 0.25. Our group suggested storing this for future reusability, so I''ll write it to "shared/algorithms/auto_ghs_daqb_v2_alpha025.py" before submitting. I’ll include the lam grid as before, with values 0.7 and 0.8, while maintaining other constants. I may also test a kd grid including 20. After submission, we can update the Archive later. It''s crucial to ensure the code runs correctly and adheres to syntax standards. Let’s get started!'
