parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 428\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis II\n- Agent Description: Parsimonious, hypothesis-driven scRNA integration researcher focused on robust ablations, reproducibility, and steady breakthroughs.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 102,335 / 270,000 used (38%)\n- Agent Age: 136 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 614**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Aether II Synergy: EtC(FWPCA α=0.25) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) + Density-Adaptive BBSG (δ=0.15, k_density=20)\n**ID:** 614\n**Tags:** embed-then-correct, fwpca, adaptive-residualization, density-adaptive, bbsg, synergy\n**Abstract:** This experiment re-submits a synergistic combination of Aether II's optimized FWPCA embedding (alpha=0.25, R^2-based from EID 533) with Praxis II's Density-Adaptive BBSG graph. The graph path uses adaptive residualization (lam=0.7) and an updated\
    \ k_density (20) for the density-adaptive quotas, aiming to leverage the latest SOTA optimization by Praxis II (EID 609). We correct import paths for proper module loading.\n**Score:** 0.7435349696921966\n**ASW_batch:** 0.674\n**ASW_label:** 0.123\n**ARI:** 0.735\n**NMI:** 0.700\n**Graph_conn:** 0.971\n**kBET:** 0.843\n**iLISI:** 0.933\n**cLISI:** 0.971\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.486\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.674  ASW_label: 0.123  ARI: 0.735  NMI: 0.700\n  Graph_conn: 0.971  kBET: 0.843  iLISI: 0.933  cLISI: 0.971\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.486\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.837066  ASW_label: 0.482844  ARI: 0.734966  NMI: 0.699690\n  Graph_conn: 0.971535  kBET: 0.803956  iLISI: 0.932695  cLISI: 0.991511\n  PCR: 0.999946  Cell_cycle: 0.422741\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\n# Corrected import paths: Add 'storage' to path to allow importing subdirectories as packages\n\
    sys.path.append('storage')\n\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\nfrom sklearn.linear_model import Ridge\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors \n\n# Import necessary functions from storage/praxis and storage/aether\nfrom praxis.brbg_common import _pca_truncated_svd as praxis_pca, _one_hot_batches as praxis_one_hot\nfrom aether.aether_utils import _calculate_anova_fwpca_weights # Re-using for ANOVA FWPCA as per my memory (unused in this specific experiment, but good practice)\nfrom praxis.bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg # Praxis II's new graph method\n\n# Replicate _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_pc for usage in graph path, as it was in Daedalus's SOTA (EID 488)\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_pc(B, Z, l2=1e-3):\n    model = Ridge(alpha=l2, fit_intercept=False, random_state=0)\n    model.fit(B, Z)\n    Z_hat = model.predict(B)\n    ss_res = np.sum((Z\
    \ - Z_hat)**2, axis=0)\n    ss_tot = np.sum((Z - Z.mean(axis=0))**2, axis=0)\n    r2_per_pc = 1 - ss_res / (ss_tot + 1e-8)\n    return Z_hat, np.clip(r2_per_pc, 0, 1)\n\n# _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_gene from EID 533 (R^2 based FWPCA)\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_gene(B, X_hvg_dense, l2=1e-3):\n    n_hvg_genes = X_hvg_dense.shape[1]\n    r2_per_gene = np.zeros(n_hvg_genes)\n    model = Ridge(alpha=l2, fit_intercept=False, random_state=0)\n    model.fit(B, X_hvg_dense)\n    X_hvg_hat = model.predict(B)\n    ss_res = np.sum((X_hvg_dense - X_hvg_hat)**2, axis=0)\n    sst = np.sum((X_hvg_dense - X_hvg_dense.mean(axis=0))**2, axis=0) + 1e-8\n    r2_per_gene = 1 - ss_res / (sst) # No clip here, handled by (1-r2_batch_gene) later\n    return np.clip(r2_per_gene, 0, 1)\n\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"--- Aether II Synergy: EtC(FWPCA α=0.25) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) + Density-Adaptive BBSG (δ=0.15, k_density=20) ---\")\n   \
    \ \n    # --- EMBEDDING PATH: Aether II SOTA (EID 533) FWPCA (R^2-based) ---\n    print(\"Embedding Path: Running FWPCA (R^2 α=0.25) -> PCA -> ComBat...\")\n    adata_for_embedding = adata.copy()\n    \n    # Standard preprocessing\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_for_embedding, target_sum=1e-4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata_for_embedding)\n    \n    if sp.isspmatrix(adata_for_embedding.X):\n        adata_for_embedding.X = adata_for_embedding.X.toarray()\n        \n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_for_embedding, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=False)\n    hvg_mask_emb = adata_for_embedding.var['highly_variable']\n    \n    alpha_weight_fwpca = 0.25 # From Aether II's SOTA (EID 533)\n    l2_fwpca = 1e-3 # Default L2 for Ridge regression\n\n    batches_emb = np.asarray(adata_for_embedding.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    B_onehot_emb, _ = praxis_one_hot(batches_emb)\n\n    X_hvg_emb_dense = adata_for_embedding.X[:, hvg_mask_emb]\n    r2_batch_gene\
    \ = _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_gene(B_onehot_emb, X_hvg_emb_dense, l2=l2_fwpca)\n    \n    feature_weights = (1 - r2_batch_gene)**alpha_weight_fwpca\n    \n    adata_for_embedding.X[:, hvg_mask_emb] *= feature_weights\n    adata_for_embedding = adata_for_embedding[:, hvg_mask_emb].copy() \n    \n    sc.pp.pca(adata_for_embedding, n_comps=60)\n    \n    pca_adata = ad.AnnData(X=adata_for_embedding.obsm['X_pca'], obs=adata_for_embedding.obs)\n    sc.pp.combat(pca_adata, key='batch')\n    Z_emb = pca_adata.X\n    \n    # --- GRAPH PATH: Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) + Density-Adaptive BBSG (from EID 600) ---\n    print(\"Graph Path: Running Adaptive Residualization -> Density-Adaptive BBSG...\")\n    adata_for_graph = adata.copy()\n    n_pcs_graph=50; gamma_max=0.74; l2=1e-3; k_total=48; metric='cosine'; random_state=0\n    lam=0.7 # From EID 600 (synergy test)\n    delta_bbsg = 0.15 # From EID 600\n    k_density_bbsg = 20 # NEW: From EID 609 SOTA\n    \n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_for_graph,\
    \ target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata_for_graph)\n\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_for_graph, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=False)\n    hvg_mask_graph = adata_for_graph.var['highly_variable']\n    X_graph = adata_for_graph.X[:, hvg_mask_graph]\n    \n    Z_graph = praxis_pca(X_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n    \n    batches_graph = np.asarray(adata_for_graph.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    B_onehot_graph, _ = praxis_one_hot(batches_graph)\n    \n    Z_hat, r2_per_pc = _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_pc(B_onehot_graph, Z_graph, l2=l2)\n    gamma_per_pc = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * r2_per_pc)\n    Z_corr_graph = Z_graph - (gamma_per_pc * Z_hat)\n    \n    C, D = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Z_corr_graph.astype(np.float32), batches=batches_graph, k_total=k_total, \n                                       metric=metric, delta=delta_bbsg, k_density=k_density_bbsg, rng_seed=random_state)\n    \n    # --- Final Output\
    \ ---\n    adata_out = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]], obsm={'X_emb': Z_emb})\n    if C is not None and D is not None:\n        if not sp.isspmatrix_csr(C): C = C.tocsr()\n        if not sp.isspmatrix_csr(D): D = D.tocsr()\n        adata_out.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n        adata_out.obsp['distances'] = D\n        adata_out.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n        \n    return adata_out\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n--- Aether II Synergy: EtC(FWPCA α=0.25) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) + Density-Adaptive BBSG (δ=0.15, k_density=20) ---\nEmbedding Path: Running FWPCA (R^2 α=0.25) -> PCA -> ComBat...\nGraph Path: Running Adaptive Residualization -> Density-Adaptive\
    \ BBSG...\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/e93be281-f17c-476e-924b-9703bf9aa4a6/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: e93be281-f17c-476e-924b-9703bf9aa4a6\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Evaluation Review: 533**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Aether II SOTA Optimization: EtC(FWPCA α=0.25) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7)\n**ID:** 533\n**Tags:** embed-then-correct, fwpca, adaptive-residualization, sota-optimization, hyperparameter-tuning, asw-label-improvement\n**Abstract:** Following a critical analysis of ASW_label degradation in previous SOTA experiments (EID 515, EID 520), this submission aims to refine the FWPCA component of our current SOTA. We reduce the alpha_weight to 0.25 (from 0.5 and 1.0) to apply a less aggressive penalty to batch-associated genes in the embedding path. The hypothesis is that a milder feature weighting will better preserve subtle biological signals, thereby\
    \ improving the ASW_label metric without significantly compromising overall batch integration performance. The graph path remains consistent with Daedalus III's Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7).\n**Score:** 0.743392171800151\n**ASW_batch:** 0.674\n**ASW_label:** 0.123\n**ARI:** 0.738\n**NMI:** 0.701\n**Graph_conn:** 0.972\n**kBET:** 0.842\n**iLISI:** 0.935\n**cLISI:** 0.972\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.477\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.674  ASW_label: 0.123  ARI: 0.738  NMI: 0.701\n  Graph_conn: 0.972  kBET: 0.842  iLISI: 0.935  cLISI: 0.972\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.477\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.837066  ASW_label: 0.482844  ARI: 0.737469  NMI: 0.701523\n  Graph_conn: 0.972224  kBET: 0.802909  iLISI: 0.935143  cLISI: 0.991814\n  PCR: 0.999946  Cell_cycle: 0.415210\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/Daedalus')\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\
    \nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\nfrom sklearn.linear_model import Ridge\n\n# Import necessary functions from storage/praxis\nfrom brbg_common import _pca_truncated_svd as praxis_pca, _one_hot_batches as praxis_one_hot, _build_balanced_knn_equal\n\n# Replicate _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_pc for usage in graph path\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_pc(B, Z, l2=1e-3):\n    model = Ridge(alpha=l2, fit_intercept=False, random_state=0)\n    model.fit(B, Z)\n    Z_hat = model.predict(B)\n    ss_res = np.sum((Z - Z_hat)**2, axis=0)\n    ss_tot = np.sum((Z - Z.mean(axis=0))**2, axis=0)\n    r2_per_pc = 1 - ss_res / (ss_tot + 1e-8)\n    return Z_hat, np.clip(r2_per_pc, 0, 1)\n\n# New helper function for FWPCA to calculate R^2 per gene\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_gene(B, X_hvg_dense, l2=1e-3):\n    # X_hvg_dense is expected to be a dense numpy array (n_cells, n_hvg_genes)\n   \
    \ # B is (n_cells, n_batches) one-hot\n    \n    n_hvg_genes = X_hvg_dense.shape[1]\n    r2_per_gene = np.zeros(n_hvg_genes)\n    \n    # Fit Ridge model for each gene (feature)\n    model = Ridge(alpha=l2, fit_intercept=False, random_state=0)\n    model.fit(B, X_hvg_dense)\n    X_hvg_hat = model.predict(B)\n    \n    ss_res = np.sum((X_hvg_dense - X_hvg_hat)**2, axis=0)\n    ss_tot = np.sum((X_hvg_dense - X_hvg_dense.mean(axis=0))**2, axis=0)\n    r2_per_gene = 1 - ss_res / (ss_tot + 1e-8)\n\n    return np.clip(r2_per_gene, 0, 1)\n\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"--- Aether II SOTA Optimization: EtC(FWPCA α=0.25) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) ---\")\n    \n    # --- EMBEDDING PATH: Daedalus III's EtC + Sophia II's FWPCA ---\n    print(\"Embedding Path: Running FWPCA -> PCA -> ComBat...\")\n    adata_for_embedding = adata.copy()\n    \n    # Standard preprocessing\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_for_embedding, target_sum=1e-4)\n\
    \    sc.pp.log1p(adata_for_embedding)\n    \n    # Convert X to dense for FWPCA calculation and application, and subsequent PCA\n    if sp.isspmatrix(adata_for_embedding.X):\n        adata_for_embedding.X = adata_for_embedding.X.toarray()\n        \n    # HVG selection must happen *before* FWPCA to weight only HVGs\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_for_embedding, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=False)\n    hvg_mask_emb = adata_for_embedding.var['highly_variable']\n    \n    # FWPCA parameters - MODIFIED alpha_weight\n    alpha_weight = 0.25 # Testing with alpha_weight=0.25\n    l2_fwpca = 1e-3 # Default L2 for Ridge regression\n\n    batches_emb = np.asarray(adata_for_embedding.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    B_onehot_emb, _ = praxis_one_hot(batches_emb)\n\n    # Calculate R^2 per gene for HVGs\n    X_hvg_emb_dense = adata_for_embedding.X[:, hvg_mask_emb]\n    r2_batch_gene = _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_gene(B_onehot_emb, X_hvg_emb_dense,\
    \ l2=l2_fwpca)\n    \n    # Compute feature weights (1 - R^2_batch_gene)^alpha_weight\n    feature_weights = (1 - r2_batch_gene)**alpha_weight\n    \n    # Apply feature weights to HVGs in adata_for_embedding.X\n    adata_for_embedding.X[:, hvg_mask_emb] *= feature_weights\n    \n    # Now subset adata_for_embedding to only HVGs for PCA and ComBat\n    adata_for_embedding = adata_for_embedding[:, hvg_mask_emb].copy() \n    \n    # Now run PCA and ComBat on the feature-weighted HVG data\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_for_embedding, n_comps=60)\n    \n    pca_adata = ad.AnnData(X=adata_for_embedding.obsm['X_pca'], obs=adata_for_embedding.obs)\n    sc.pp.combat(pca_adata, key='batch')\n    Z_emb = pca_adata.X\n    \n    # --- GRAPH PATH: ADAPTIVE BRBG pipeline from Daedalus III's SOTA (ID 488) ---\n    print(\"Graph Path: Running Adaptive BRBG...\")\n    adata_for_graph = adata.copy()\n    n_pcs_graph=50; gamma_max=0.74; l2=1e-3; k_total=48; metric='cosine'; random_state=0\n    lam=0.7 # Daedalus\
    \ III's SOTA parameter\n    \n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_for_graph, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata_for_graph)\n\n    # HVG selection for graph path uses subset=False, then X_graph is explicitly created from HVGs\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_for_graph, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=False)\n    hvg_mask_graph = adata_for_graph.var['highly_variable']\n    X_graph = adata_for_graph.X[:, hvg_mask_graph]\n    \n    Z_graph = praxis_pca(X_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n    \n    batches_graph = np.asarray(adata_for_graph.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    B_onehot_graph, _ = praxis_one_hot(batches_graph)\n    \n    Z_hat, r2_per_pc = _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_pc(B_onehot_graph, Z_graph, l2=l2)\n    gamma_per_pc = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * r2_per_pc)\n    Z_corr_graph = Z_graph - (gamma_per_pc * Z_hat)\n    \n    C, D = _build_balanced_knn_equal(Z_corr_graph, batches_graph, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n\
    \    \n    # --- Final Output ---\n    adata_out = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]], obsm={'X_emb': Z_emb})\n    if C is not None and D is not None:\n        if not sp.isspmatrix_csr(C): C = C.tocsr()\n        if not sp.isspmatrix_csr(D): D = D.tocsr()\n        adata_out.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n        adata_out.obsp['distances'] = D\n        adata_out.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n        \n    return adata_out\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n--- Aether II SOTA Optimization: EtC(FWPCA α=0.25) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) ---\nEmbedding Path: Running FWPCA -> PCA -> ComBat...\nGraph Path: Running Adaptive BRBG...\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has\
    \ embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/416b77e3-4e73-4157-970f-267939e35361/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 416b77e3-4e73-4157-970f-267939e35361\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\n**Evaluation Review: 550**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Sophia II: Synergy Exp 2 - FWPCA-EtC Embedding (alpha=0.5) + SOTA BRBG Graph (lam=0.7)\n**ID:** 550\n**Tags:** synergy, fwpca, etc, adaptive residualization, embedding, graph\n**Abstract:** Continuing the investigation into the synergistic combination of FWPCA-enhanced EtC embedding and the SOTA BRBG graph. This experiment (Synergy Exp 2) uses a moderate FWPCA `alpha_weight` of 0.5 (compared to 0.25 in previous synergy attempt, ID 541). It aims to determine if a different FWPCA weighting can alleviate the observed negative synergy and lead to an additive gain, or further elucidate the complex interactions between these orthogonal pipeline enhancements. The SOTA BRBG graph path (lam=0.7, from\
    \ ID 523) remains consistent.\n**Score:** 0.7427281474694152\n**ASW_batch:** 0.664\n**ASW_label:** 0.111\n**ARI:** 0.738\n**NMI:** 0.701\n**Graph_conn:** 0.972\n**kBET:** 0.860\n**iLISI:** 0.935\n**cLISI:** 0.972\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.475\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.664  ASW_label: 0.111  ARI: 0.738  NMI: 0.701\n  Graph_conn: 0.972  kBET: 0.860  iLISI: 0.935  cLISI: 0.972\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.475\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.832500  ASW_label: 0.475740  ARI: 0.737469  NMI: 0.701523\n  Graph_conn: 0.972224  kBET: 0.819450  iLISI: 0.935143  cLISI: 0.991814\n  PCR: 0.999927  Cell_cycle: 0.413675\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis') # For brbg_common.py utilities\n\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\nfrom sklearn.linear_model\
    \ import Ridge \nimport warnings\nfrom sklearn.exceptions import ConvergenceWarning\n\n# Import necessary functions from storage/praxis\nfrom brbg_common import _pca_truncated_svd as praxis_pca, _one_hot_batches as praxis_one_hot, _build_balanced_knn_equal\n\n# Replicate _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_pc for usage in graph path (from Aether II's code)\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_pc(B, Z, l2=1e-3, random_state=0):\n    model = Ridge(alpha=l2, fit_intercept=False, random_state=random_state) \n    \n    with warnings.catch_warnings():\n        warnings.simplefilter(\"ignore\", ConvergenceWarning)\n        model.fit(B, Z)\n    Z_hat = model.predict(B)\n    ss_res = np.sum((Z - Z_hat)**2, axis=0)\n    ss_tot = np.sum((Z - Z.mean(axis=0))**2, axis=0)\n    r2_per_pc = 1 - ss_res / (ss_tot + 1e-8) \n    return Z_hat, np.clip(r2_per_pc, 0, 1)\n\n# New helper function for FWPCA to calculate R^2 per gene (from Aether II's code)\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_gene(B, X_hvg_dense, l2=1e-3,\
    \ random_state=0):\n    n_hvg_genes = X_hvg_dense.shape[1]\n    \n    model = Ridge(alpha=l2, fit_intercept=False, random_state=random_state) \n    \n    with warnings.catch_warnings():\n        warnings.simplefilter(\"ignore\", ConvergenceWarning)\n        model.fit(B, X_hvg_dense)\n    X_hvg_hat = model.predict(B)\n    \n    ss_res = np.sum((X_hvg_dense - X_hvg_hat)**2, axis=0)\n    ss_tot = np.sum((X_hvg_dense - X_hvg_dense.mean(axis=0))**2, axis=0)\n    r2_per_gene = 1 - ss_res / (ss_tot + 1e-8)\n\n    return np.clip(r2_per_gene, 0, 1)\n\n\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _get_hvg_mask(adata: ad.AnnData, n_top_genes: int = 2000):\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=n_top_genes, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n    mask =\
    \ np.asarray(adata.var['highly_variable'].values, dtype=bool)\n    if mask.sum() < 10: \n        return np.ones(adata.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n    return mask\n\n\n# --- Main eliminate_batch_effect_fn for EtC SOTA Replication ---\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(f\"Sophia II: Synergy Exp 2 - FWPCA-EtC Embedding (alpha=0.5) + SOTA BRBG Graph (lam=0.7)\")\n\n    # --- Configuration parameters based on Daedalus III's EtC SOTA (ID 488) and Aether II's ID 533 ---\n    N_PCS_EMB = 60 \n    N_PCS_GRAPH = 50 \n    gamma_max_adapt = 0.74 # From Aether II (0.74 instead of 0.75)\n    lam_adapt = 0.7        # From Daedalus III's ID 488\n    l2 = 1e-3              \n    k_total = 48           \n    metric = 'cosine'      \n    random_state = 0       \n\n    # FWPCA specific parameter (Experiment 2: alpha_weight = 0.5)\n    fwpca_alpha_weight = 0.5 # NEW: alpha_weight set to 0.5\n    l2_fwpca = 1e-3 # L2 for Ridge in FWPCA, from Aether II\n\n    assert 'batch'\
    \ in adata.obs.columns, \"adata.obs['batch'] required.\"\n    assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns, \"adata.var['feature_name'] required.\"\n\n    # Create copies for each path to avoid unintended in-place modifications\n    adata_for_embedding_path = adata.copy()\n    adata_for_graph_path = adata.copy() \n\n    # --- Preprocessing ---\n    # Embedding path uses 1e-4 target_sum, Graph path uses 1e4 target_sum\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata_for_embedding_path, target_sum=1e-4) \n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata_for_graph_path, target_sum=1e4) \n\n    # Aether II applies HVG mask *after* converting to dense and running FWPCA on the full gene set\n    # Then subsets to HVGs before PCA.\n    \n    # For embedding path:\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_for_embedding_path, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=False)\n    hvg_mask_emb = adata_for_embedding_path.var['highly_variable']\n\n    # For graph path:\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_for_graph_path,\
    \ n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=False)\n    hvg_mask_graph = adata_for_graph_path.var['highly_variable']\n\n\n    # --- Embedding Path (FWPCA-enhanced EtC, Aether II's implementation) ---\n    print(f\"Initiating FWPCA-enhanced EtC Embedding Path (alpha_weight={fwpca_alpha_weight}, embedding norm target_sum=1e-4, gamma_max_adapt={gamma_max_adapt})...\")\n    \n    # Convert X to dense for FWPCA calculation and application, and subsequent PCA\n    if sp.isspmatrix(adata_for_embedding_path.X):\n        adata_for_embedding_path.X = adata_for_embedding_path.X.toarray()\n    \n    X_full_hvg_emb_dense = adata_for_embedding_path.X\n    \n    batches_emb = np.asarray(adata_for_embedding_path.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    B_onehot_emb, _ = praxis_one_hot(batches_emb)\n    \n    # --- FWPCA Step: Feature Weighting (Aether II's FIXED logic) ---\n    print(f\"  Applying FWPCA: Feature Weighting (alpha_weight={fwpca_alpha_weight}) using Ridge R^2\
    \ per gene...\")\n    r2_batch_gene = _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_gene(B_onehot_emb, X_full_hvg_emb_dense, l2=l2_fwpca, random_state=random_state)\n    \n    # Compute feature weights (1 - R^2_batch_gene)^alpha_weight\n    feature_weights_full = (1 - r2_batch_gene)**fwpca_alpha_weight\n    \n    # Apply feature weights to HVGs only in the full matrix, then subset\n    weighted_full_X = X_full_hvg_emb_dense * feature_weights_full\n    adata_for_embedding_path.X = weighted_full_X \n    \n    # Now subset adata_for_embedding_path to only HVGs for PCA and ComBat\n    adata_for_embedding_path = adata_for_embedding_path[:, hvg_mask_emb].copy() \n    \n    # 1. PCA on *weighted* HVG data (now adata_for_embedding_path.X is the dense HVG data after FWPCA)\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_for_embedding_path, n_comps=N_PCS_EMB, use_highly_variable=False, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    X_pca_embedding = adata_for_embedding_path.obsm['X_pca']\n    print(f\"  PCA on weighted HVGs embedding\
    \ shape: {X_pca_embedding.shape}\")\n\n    # 2. Combat correction on the principal components\n    temp_adata_for_combat = ad.AnnData(\n        X=X_pca_embedding,\n        obs=adata_for_embedding_path.obs.copy()\n    )\n    with warnings.catch_warnings():\n        warnings.simplefilter('ignore', ConvergenceWarning)\n        sc.pp.combat(temp_adata_for_combat, key='batch')\n    \n    Z_emb_etc_fwpca = temp_adata_for_combat.X \n    print(f\"✓ FWPCA-enhanced EtC Embedding Path complete (FWPCA -> PCA -> Combat on PCs). Final embedding shape: {Z_emb_etc_fwpca.shape}\")\n\n\n    # --- Graph Path (SOTA Batch-Residualized Balanced Graph - BRBG with lam=0.7) ---\n    print(f\"Initiating SOTA BRBG Graph Path with Adaptive Residualization (lam={lam_adapt}, graph norm target_sum=1e4, gamma_max={gamma_max_adapt})...\")\n    \n    X_graph_hvg = adata_for_graph_path.X[:, hvg_mask_graph]\n    if not sp.issparse(X_graph_hvg):\n        X_graph_hvg = sp.csr_matrix(X_graph_hvg)\n    \n    Z_graph_initial_pcs\
    \ = praxis_pca(X_graph_hvg, n_comps=N_PCS_GRAPH, random_state=random_state)\n\n    batches_graph = np.asarray(adata_for_graph_path.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    Z_hat_graph, r2_per_pc_graph = _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_pc(praxis_one_hot(batches_graph)[0], Z_graph_initial_pcs, l2=l2, random_state=random_state) \n    \n    gamma_per_pc = np.minimum(gamma_max_adapt, lam_adapt * r2_per_pc_graph)\n    Z_corr_graph = Z_graph_initial_pcs - (gamma_per_pc * Z_hat_graph)\n    print(f\"  Adaptive Residualization complete. Z_corr_graph shape: {Z_corr_graph.shape}\")\n\n    C, D = _build_balanced_knn_equal(\n        Z_corr_graph, batches_graph, k_total=k_total, metric=metric\n    )\n    print(f\"✓ BRBG Graph Path complete. Balanced kNN graph shape: {C.shape if C is not None else 'Failed'}\")\n\n    # --- Final Output Construction ---\n    adata_out = ad.AnnData(\n        obs=adata.obs[[]], \n        var=adata.var[[]], \n        obsm={'X_emb': Z_emb_etc_fwpca},\n        uns={\n\
    \            'method_id': 'sophia_II_synergy_fwpca_alpha0.5_etc_sota_brbg', # New method ID\n            'baseline_info': 'Sophia II SOTA (ID 523, 0.7423) is baseline for graph path. FWPCA (ID 475, 0.7371) for embedding path. Synergy with alpha_weight=0.5. Target is Aether II ID 533 (0.7434).',\n            'embedding_path_details': {\n                'normalization': 'normalize_total (1e-4)+log1p',\n                'hvg_selection': 'seurat_v3_batch_aware_subsetted_after_fwpca_apply_to_dense', \n                'fwpca_applied': True,\n                'fwpca_alpha_weight': float(fwpca_alpha_weight),\n                'fwpca_r2_calc_method': 'Ridge R^2 per gene (Aether II impl.)',\n                'fwpca_r2_l2': float(l2_fwpca),\n                'etc_pca_n_pcs': int(N_PCS_EMB),\n                'batch_correction': 'sc.pp.combat on PCs'\n            },\n            'graph_path_details': {\n                'normalization': 'normalize_total (1e4)+log1p',\n                'hvg_selection': 'seurat_v3_batch_aware',\n\
    \                'pca_n_pcs': int(N_PCS_GRAPH),\n                'batch_correction': 'Adaptive Residualization (_ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_pc)', \n                'adaptive_residualization_lam': float(lam_adapt),\n                'graph_gamma_max_adapt': float(gamma_max_adapt),\n                'graph_type': 'Balanced kNN (Praxis _build_balanced_knn_equal)',\n                'graph_k_total': int(k_total),\n                'graph_metric': metric,\n                'random_state': random_state\n            }\n        }\n    )\n\n    if C is not None and D is not None:\n        adata_out.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n        adata_out.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n        adata_out.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n    else:\n        print(\"Warning: Graph construction failed. No connectivities/distances output.\")\n\n    print(f\"✓ Sophia II: Aether II SOTA Replication pipeline complete (alpha={fwpca_alpha_weight}).\")\n\
    \    return adata_out\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nAutoResearchEvaluator: Set memory limit to 96g\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nSophia II: Synergy Exp 2 - FWPCA-EtC Embedding (alpha=0.5) + SOTA BRBG Graph (lam=0.7)\nInitiating FWPCA-enhanced EtC Embedding Path (alpha_weight=0.5, embedding norm target_sum=1e-4, gamma_max_adapt=0.74)...\n  Applying FWPCA: Feature Weighting (alpha_weight=0.5) using Ridge R^2 per gene...\n  PCA on weighted HVGs embedding shape: (20000, 60)\n✓ FWPCA-enhanced EtC Embedding Path complete (FWPCA -> PCA -> Combat on PCs). Final embedding shape: (20000, 60)\nInitiating SOTA BRBG Graph Path with Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7, graph norm target_sum=1e4, gamma_max=0.74)...\n  Adaptive Residualization complete. Z_corr_graph shape: (20000,\
    \ 50)\n✓ BRBG Graph Path complete. Balanced kNN graph shape: (20000, 20000)\n✓ Sophia II: Aether II SOTA Replication pipeline complete (alpha=0.5).\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/cc2728fa-cd03-4603-be87-269cf481a039/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: cc2728fa-cd03-4603-be87-269cf481a039\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 4\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nThe creation of new knowledge from first principles is often necessary for a breakthrough. Endlessly grinding on recombination of existing components or hyperparameter tuning is not true research. Look beyond the primary score and goto Reflection Chamber to brainstorm novel ideas when you feel stuck.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Public Memory Room);\n2. `review 614` (in Research Counter);\n3. `review 533` (in Research Counter);\n4. `review 550` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n###\
