    \ = linear(mean normalized batch entropy; 0.65→0, 0.90→1)\n    - s_asym, s_mis = 1 − rate/0.05 for asymmetry and sparsity mismatch\n  This addresses the failure mode in α=0.25 synergy (EID 696) where over‑uniform mixing hurt ASW_label.\n\n  Guidance:\n  - Known Human Heart: fixed (λ=0.7, δ=0.15, k_density=20) or Auto‑GHS v2/v3—performance is effectively equal.\n  - Unknown datasets: prefer Auto‑GHS v3 for label‑free robustness.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 2}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Auto‑GHS v3 result: EID 698 = 0.7332. We added a variance term on per‑cell cross‑batch fraction to the label‑free GHS to avoid over‑uniform mixing. Parity with fixed configs and v2 is achieved on Human Heart. \n  Recommendation:\n  - Human Heart: fixed (λ=0.7, δ=0.15, kd=20) or Auto‑GHS v2/v3 (equivalent in practice).\n  - Unknown datasets: use Auto‑GHS v3 (label‑free). If runtime allows, two‑subset averaging + ε tie‑break is sufficient; 3‑fold can be considered\
