parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Sensitivity: R²‑FWPCA α=0.25 with embedding normalize_total target_sum=1e-5 (HVG subset=False)\"\ntags: \"sensitivity, embedding-normalization, fwpca, etc, residualization, daqb\"\nabstract: \"Test embedding normalization sensitivity: per‑gene R²‑FWPCA (α=0.25) with normalize_total(target_sum=1e-5) and HVG subset=False in the embedding path. Graph path fixed (normalize_total 1e4; BRBG λ=0.7, γ_max=0.74, PCA50; DAQB δ=0.15, k_density=20; k=48; cosine; binary+true distances; column balancing).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata,\
    \ target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n      cats = np.unique(batches); n = batches.shape[0]\n      B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats): B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      return B @ W\n\n  def _ridge_GENE_R2(B: np.ndarray, X: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ X)\n      Xhat = B @ W\n      ss_res = np.sum((X - Xhat)**2, axis=0)\n\
    \      mu = X.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n      ss_tot = np.sum((X - mu)**2, axis=0) + 1e-8\n      return np.clip(1.0 - ss_res / ss_tot, 0.0, 1.0)\n\n  def _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dists, n):\n      from scipy import sparse as sp\n      A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      D = sp.coo_matrix((dists.astype(np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      A_sym = A.maximum(A.T); D_sym = D.maximum(D.T)\n      A_sym.eliminate_zeros(); D_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n      return A_sym, D_sym\n\n  def _build_daqb(Zcorr: np.ndarray, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine',\n                  delta=0.15, k_density=20, cap=2.0, rng_seed=0):\n      from scipy import sparse as sp\n      Z = np.asarray(Zcorr, dtype=np.float32, order='C')\n      n = Z.shape[0]; batches = np.asarray(batches)\n      cats = np.unique(batches); nB = len(cats)\n      base_cross = (nB - 1) / float(nB); L, U = 0.60, 0.90\n\n      nn_all\
    \ = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n      nn_all.fit(Z); d_all, _ = nn_all.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n      d_k = d_all[:, -1]; d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n      inv_dense = 1.0 - (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n      f_cross = np.clip(base_cross + (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * delta, L, U)\n\n      q_cross_tot = np.rint(f_cross * k_total).astype(int)\n      q_within_tot = k_total - q_cross_tot\n      B_other = max(nB - 1, 1)\n      k_within_max = int(np.ceil((1.0 - L) * k_total))\n      k_cross_per_max = int(np.ceil(U * k_total / B_other))\n      k_max = max(k_within_max, k_cross_per_max) + 1\n\n      cat2code = {c: i for i, c in enumerate(cats)}\n      batch_codes = np.array([cat2code[b] for b in batches], dtype=int)\n      nn_models, train_idx = {}, {}\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          mask = (batches == c); train_idx[j] = np.where(mask)[0]\n          nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_max,\
    \ metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n          nn.fit(Z[mask]); nn_models[j] = nn\n\n      dists, idx_local = {}, {}\n      for j in range(nB):\n          d, ii = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n          dists[j] = d; idx_local[j] = ii\n\n      inbound = np.zeros(n, dtype=np.int32); cap_thr = int(np.ceil(cap * k_total))\n      rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n      for i in range(n):\n          bi = batch_codes[i]\n          q_within = int(q_within_tot[i]); q_cross_total = int(q_cross_tot[i])\n          other_batches = [j for j in range(nB) if j != bi]\n          q_per_other = q_cross_total // B_other; rem = q_cross_total - q_per_other * B_other\n          batch_scores = [(j, dists[j][i][0]) for j in other_batches]; batch_scores.sort(key=lambda t: t[1])\n          q_map = {j: q_per_other for j in other_batches}\n          for k in range(rem): q_map[batch_scores[k % len(other_batches)][0]] += 1\n\n          d_w = dists[bi][i]; ii_w = idx_local[bi][i]; start_w = 1 if\
    \ d_w[0] == 0.0 else 0\n          globals_w = train_idx[bi][ii_w[start_w:]]; cand_inb = inbound[globals_w]; cand_dst = d_w[start_w:]\n          order = np.lexsort((cand_dst, cand_inb)); taken = 0\n          for idx in order:\n              g = int(globals_w[idx])\n              if inbound[g] >= cap_thr: continue\n              rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx])); inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n              if taken >= q_within: break\n          if taken < q_within:\n              for idx in order:\n                  g = int(globals_w[idx])\n                  if inbound[g] < cap_thr: continue\n                  rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx])); inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n                  if taken >= q_within: break\n\n          for j in other_batches:\n              qj = q_map[j]\n              if qj <= 0: continue\n              d_c = dists[j][i]; ii_c = idx_local[j][i]; globals_c = train_idx[j][ii_c]\n              cand_inb\
    \ = inbound[globals_c]; cand_dst = d_c\n              order = np.lexsort((cand_dst, cand_inb)); taken = 0\n              for idx in order:\n                  g = int(globals_c[idx])\n                  if inbound[g] >= cap_thr: continue\n                  rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx])); inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n                  if taken >= qj: break\n              if taken < qj:\n                  for idx in order:\n                      g = int(globals_c[idx])\n                      if inbound[g] < cap_thr: continue\n                      rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx])); inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n                      if taken >= qj: break\n\n      C_sym, D_sym = _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(\n          np.asarray(rows, dtype=np.int32),\n          np.asarray(cols, dtype=np.int32),\n          np.asarray(dvals, dtype=np.float32),\n          n=Z.shape[0]\n      )\n      return C_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32),\
    \ D_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32)\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      n_pcs_emb = 60; n_pcs_graph = 50\n      l2 = 1e-3; gamma_max = 0.74; lam = 0.7\n      k_total = 48; metric = 'cosine'; delta = 0.15; k_density = 20; cap = 2.0\n      alpha_r2 = 0.25; emb_n_neighbors = 15\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      # Embedding: normalize_total target_sum=1e-5; HVG subset=False\n      ad_emb = adata.copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(ad_emb, target_sum=1e-5); sc.pp.log1p(ad_emb)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(ad_emb, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=False)\n      hvg_mask = ad_emb.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      if sp.issparse(ad_emb.X): ad_emb.X = ad_emb.X.toarray()\n      X = ad_emb.X.astype(np.float32, copy=False); X_hvg = X[:, hvg_mask]\n      batches_emb = np.asarray(ad_emb.obs['batch'].astype('category').values); B_emb = _one_hot_batches(batches_emb)\n\
    \      R2_gene = _ridge_GENE_R2(B_emb, X_hvg, l2=l2)\n      w = np.power(1.0 - R2_gene, alpha_r2).astype(np.float32)\n      X_hvg_w = X_hvg * w\n      ad_emb_pca = ad.AnnData(X_hvg_w, obs=ad_emb.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb_pca, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      Z_emb = ad_emb_pca.obsm['X_pca']\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z_emb.copy(), obs=ad_emb.obs[['batch']].copy()); sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32); sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n      # Graph: fixed BRBG + DAQB\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      Xg = adata.X[:, hv]; Xg = (Xg.A if sp.issparse(Xg) else Xg).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values);\
    \ B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xg, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n      Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8; var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2_pc = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0); gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2_pc)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n      Cg, Dg = _build_daqb(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric, delta=delta, k_density=k_density, cap=cap, rng_seed=0)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg; adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      return adata\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Sensitivity: R²‑FWPCA α=0.25 with embedding normalize_total target_sum=1e-3 (HVG subset=False)\"\ntags: \"sensitivity, embedding-normalization, fwpca, etc, residualization, daqb\"\nabstract: \"Same as EID 712 but embedding normalize_total(target_sum=1e-3) and HVG subset=False. Graph path fixed (BRBG λ=0.7;\
    \ DAQB δ=0.15, k_density=20; k=48; cosine; binary+true distances; column balancing).\"\ncontent: |\n  # Identical to the previous submission except target_sum=1e-3 in the embedding path\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  import numpy as np, scanpy as sc, anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers: adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True); sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X; ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(b): \n      cats = np.unique(b); n = b.shape[0]; B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\
    \ B[:, j] = (b == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1]); W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z); return B @ W\n\n  def _ridge_GENE_R2(B, X, l2=1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1]); W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ X); Xhat = B @ W\n      ss_res = np.sum((X - Xhat)**2, axis=0); mu = X.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n      ss_tot = np.sum((X - mu)**2, axis=0) + 1e-8; return np.clip(1.0 - ss_res/ss_tot, 0.0, 1.0)\n\n  def _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(r, c, d, n):\n      from scipy import sparse as sp\n      A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(d, np.float32), (r, c)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      D = sp.coo_matrix((d.astype(np.float32), (r, c)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      A = A.maximum(A.T); D = D.maximum(D.T); A.eliminate_zeros(); D.eliminate_zeros(); return A, D\n\n  def _build_daqb(Z, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine', delta=0.15, k_density=20, cap=2.0, rng_seed=0):\n      from scipy\
    \ import sparse as sp\n      Z = np.asarray(Z, np.float32, order='C'); n = Z.shape[0]; batches = np.asarray(batches)\n      cats = np.unique(batches); nB = len(cats); base_cross = (nB - 1)/float(nB); L, U = 0.60, 0.90\n      nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density+1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute'); nn.fit(Z)\n      d_all, _ = nn.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True); d_k = d_all[:, -1]\n      d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n      inv_dense = 1.0 - (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n      f_cross = np.clip(base_cross + (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * delta, L, U)\n      q_cross_tot = np.rint(f_cross * k_total).astype(int); q_within_tot = k_total - q_cross_tot\n      B_other = max(nB - 1, 1)\n      k_within_max = int(np.ceil((1.0 - L) * k_total)); k_cross_per_max = int(np.ceil(U * k_total / B_other))\n      k_max = max(k_within_max, k_cross_per_max) + 1\n      cat2code = {c:i for i, c in enumerate(cats)}; codes = np.array([cat2code[b] for b in batches],\
    \ int)\n      nn_models, train_idx = {}, {}\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          mask = (batches == c); train_idx[j] = np.where(mask)[0]\n          m = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_max, metric=metric, algorithm='brute'); m.fit(Z[mask]); nn_models[j] = m\n      dists, idx_local = {}, {}\n      for j in range(nB):\n          d, ii = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True); dists[j] = d; idx_local[j] = ii\n      inbound = np.zeros(n, np.int32); cap_thr = int(np.ceil(2.0 * k_total))\n      rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n      for i in range(n):\n          bi = codes[i]; q_within = int(q_within_tot[i]); q_cross_total = int(q_cross_tot[i])\n          other = [j for j in range(nB) if j != bi]; q_per = q_cross_total // B_other; rem = q_cross_total - q_per * B_other\n          scores = [(j, dists[j][i][0]) for j in other]; scores.sort(key=lambda t: t[1])\n          q_map = {j: q_per for j in other}\n          for k in range(rem): q_map[scores[k % len(other)][0]] += 1\n \
    \         d_w = dists[bi][i]; ii_w = idx_local[bi][i]; start_w = 1 if d_w[0]==0.0 else 0\n          globals_w = train_idx[bi][ii_w[start_w:]]; cand_inb = inbound[globals_w]; cand_dst = d_w[start_w:]\n          order = np.lexsort((cand_dst, cand_inb)); taken = 0\n          for idx in order:\n              g = int(globals_w[idx])\n              if inbound[g] >= cap_thr: continue\n              rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx])); inbound[g]+=1; taken+=1\n              if taken >= q_within: break\n          if taken < q_within:\n              for idx in order:\n                  g = int(globals_w[idx])\n                  if inbound[g] < cap_thr: continue\n                  rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx])); inbound[g]+=1; taken+=1\n                  if taken >= q_within: break\n          for j in other:\n              qj = q_map[j]\n              if qj <= 0: continue\n              d_c = dists[j][i]; ii_c = idx_local[j][i];\
    \ globals_c = train_idx[j][ii_c]\n              cand_inb = inbound[globals_c]; cand_dst = d_c\n              order = np.lexsort((cand_dst, cand_inb)); taken = 0\n              for idx in order:\n                  g = int(globals_c[idx])\n                  if inbound[g] >= cap_thr: continue\n                  rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx])); inbound[g]+=1; taken+=1\n                  if taken >= qj: break\n              if taken < qj:\n                  for idx in order:\n                      g = int(globals_c[idx])\n                      if inbound[g] < cap_thr: continue\n                      rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx])); inbound[g]+=1; taken+=1\n                      if taken >= qj: break\n      C, D = _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(np.asarray(rows, np.int32), np.asarray(cols, np.int32), np.asarray(dvals, np.float32), n=Z.shape[0])\n      return C.tocsr().astype(np.float32), D.tocsr().astype(np.float32)\n\n\
    \  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      n_pcs_emb=60; n_pcs_graph=50; l2=1e-3; gamma_max=0.74; lam=0.7\n      k_total=48; metric='cosine'; delta=0.15; k_density=20; cap=2.0\n      alpha_r2=0.25; emb_n_neighbors=15\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n      ad_emb = adata.copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(ad_emb, target_sum=1e-3); sc.pp.log1p(ad_emb)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(ad_emb, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=False)\n      hvg_mask = ad_emb.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      if sp.issparse(ad_emb.X): ad_emb.X = ad_emb.X.toarray()\n      X = ad_emb.X.astype(np.float32, copy=False); X_hvg = X[:, hvg_mask]\n      batches_emb = np.asarray(ad_emb.obs['batch'].astype('category').values); B_emb = _one_hot_batches(batches_emb)\n      R2 = _ridge_GENE_R2(B_emb, X_hvg, l2=l2); w = np.power(1.0 - R2, alpha_r2).astype(np.float32)\n      X_hvg_w = X_hvg * w\n    \
    \  ad_emb_pca = ad.AnnData(X_hvg_w, obs=ad_emb.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb_pca, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      Z_emb = ad_emb_pca.obsm['X_pca']; ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z_emb.copy(), obs=ad_emb.obs[['batch']].copy()); sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32); sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4); sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy(); Xg = adata.X[:, hv]; Xg = (Xg.A if sp.issparse(Xg) else Xg).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values); B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xg, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0); Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1)\
    \ + 1e-8; var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2_pc = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0); gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2_pc); Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n      Cg, Dg = _build_daqb(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric, delta=delta, k_density=k_density, cap=cap, rng_seed=0)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg; adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg; return adata\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Sensitivity: R²‑FWPCA α=0.25 with embedding HVG subset=True (target_sum=1e-4)\"\ntags: \"sensitivity, hvg-subset, embedding-normalization, fwpca, etc, residualization, daqb\"\nabstract: \"Test HVG subsetting in the embedding path: per‑gene R²‑FWPCA (α=0.25) with normalize_total(target_sum=1e-4) and HVG subset=True before PCA(60)→ComBat. Graph path fixed as DAQB + BRBG.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  import numpy as np, scanpy as sc, anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse\
    \ as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers: adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True); sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X; ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(b): \n      cats = np.unique(b); n = b.shape[0]; B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats): B[:, j] = (b == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1]); W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z); return B @ W\n\n  def _ridge_GENE_R2(B, X, l2=1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1]); W = np.linalg.solve(BTB,\
    \ B.T @ X); Xhat = B @ W\n      ss_res = np.sum((X - Xhat)**2, axis=0); mu = X.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n      ss_tot = np.sum((X - mu)**2, axis=0) + 1e-8; return np.clip(1.0 - ss_res/ss_tot, 0.0, 1.0)\n\n  def _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(r, c, d, n):\n      from scipy import sparse as sp\n      A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(d, np.float32), (r, c)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      D = sp.coo_matrix((d.astype(np.float32), (r, c)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      A = A.maximum(A.T); D = D.maximum(D.T); A.eliminate_zeros(); D.eliminate_zeros(); return A, D\n\n  def _build_daqb(Z, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine', delta=0.15, k_density=20, cap=2.0, rng_seed=0):\n      from scipy import sparse as sp\n      Z = np.asarray(Z, np.float32, order='C'); n = Z.shape[0]; batches = np.asarray(batches)\n      cats = np.unique(batches); nB = len(cats); base_cross = (nB - 1)/float(nB); L, U = 0.60, 0.90\n      nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density+1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute');\
    \ nn.fit(Z)\n      d_all, _ = nn.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True); d_k = d_all[:, -1]\n      d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n      inv_dense = 1.0 - (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n      f_cross = np.clip(base_cross + (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * delta, L, U)\n      q_cross_tot = np.rint(f_cross * k_total).astype(int); q_within_tot = k_total - q_cross_tot\n      B_other = max(nB - 1, 1)\n      k_within_max = int(np.ceil((1.0 - L) * k_total)); k_cross_per_max = int(np.ceil(U * k_total / B_other))\n      k_max = max(k_within_max, k_cross_per_max) + 1\n      cat2code = {c:i for i, c in enumerate(cats)}; codes = np.array([cat2code[b] for b in batches], int)\n      nn_models, train_idx = {}, {}\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          mask = (batches == c); train_idx[j] = np.where(mask)[0]\n          m = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_max, metric=metric, algorithm='brute'); m.fit(Z[mask]); nn_models[j] = m\n      dists, idx_local = {}, {}\n    \
    \  for j in range(nB):\n          d, ii = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True); dists[j] = d; idx_local[j] = ii\n      inbound = np.zeros(n, np.int32); cap_thr = int(np.ceil(2.0 * k_total))\n      rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n      for i in range(n):\n          bi = codes[i]; q_within = int(q_within_tot[i]); q_cross_total = int(q_cross_tot[i])\n          other = [j for j in range(nB) if j != bi]; q_per = q_cross_total // B_other; rem = q_cross_total - q_per * B_other\n          scores = [(j, dists[j][i][0]) for j in other]; scores.sort(key=lambda t: t[1])\n          q_map = {j: q_per for j in other}\n          for k in range(rem): q_map[scores[k % len(other)][0]] += 1\n          d_w = dists[bi][i]; ii_w = idx_local[bi][i]; start_w = 1 if d_w[0]==0.0 else 0\n          globals_w = train_idx[bi][ii_w[start_w:]]; cand_inb = inbound[globals_w]; cand_dst = d_w[start_w:]\n          order = np.lexsort((cand_dst, cand_inb)); taken = 0\n          for idx in order:\n            \
    \  g = int(globals_w[idx])\n              if inbound[g] >= cap_thr: continue\n              rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx])); inbound[g]+=1; taken+=1\n              if taken >= q_within: break\n          if taken < q_within:\n              for idx in order:\n                  g = int(globals_w[idx])\n                  if inbound[g] < cap_thr: continue\n                  rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx])); inbound[g]+=1; taken+=1\n                  if taken >= q_within: break\n          for j in other:\n              qj = q_map[j]\n              if qj <= 0: continue\n              d_c = dists[j][i]; ii_c = idx_local[j][i]; globals_c = train_idx[j][ii_c]\n              cand_inb = inbound[globals_c]; cand_dst = d_c\n              order = np.lexsort((cand_dst, cand_inb)); taken = 0\n              for idx in order:\n                  g = int(globals_c[idx])\n                  if inbound[g] >= cap_thr: continue\n           \
    \       rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx])); inbound[g]+=1; taken+=1\n                  if taken >= qj: break\n              if taken < qj:\n                  for idx in order:\n                      g = int(globals_c[idx])\n                      if inbound[g] < cap_thr: continue\n                      rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx])); inbound[g]+=1; taken+=1\n                      if taken >= qj: break\n      C, D = _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(np.asarray(rows, np.int32), np.asarray(cols, np.int32), np.asarray(dvals, np.float32), n=Z.shape[0])\n      return C.tocsr().astype(np.float32), D.tocsr().astype(np.float32)\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      n_pcs_emb=60; n_pcs_graph=50; l2=1e-3; gamma_max=0.74; lam=0.7\n      k_total=48; metric='cosine'; delta=0.15; k_density=20; cap=2.0\n      alpha_r2=0.25; emb_n_neighbors=15\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name'\
    \ in adata.var.columns\n      ad_emb = adata.copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(ad_emb, target_sum=1e-4); sc.pp.log1p(ad_emb)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(ad_emb, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=True)\n      if sp.issparse(ad_emb.X): ad_emb.X = ad_emb.X.toarray()\n      X = ad_emb.X.astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      batches_emb = np.asarray(ad_emb.obs['batch'].astype('category').values); B_emb = _one_hot_batches(batches_emb)\n      R2 = _ridge_GENE_R2(B_emb, X, l2=l2); w = np.power(1.0 - R2, alpha_r2).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw = X * w\n      ad_emb_pca = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=ad_emb.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb_pca, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      Z_emb = ad_emb_pca.obsm['X_pca']; ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z_emb.copy(), obs=ad_emb.obs[['batch']].copy()); sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32); sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors,\
    \ metric=metric)\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4); sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy(); Xg = adata.X[:, hv]; Xg = (Xg.A if sp.issparse(Xg) else Xg).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values); B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xg, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0); Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8; var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2_pc = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0); gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2_pc); Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n      Cg, Dg = _build_daqb(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric, delta=delta, k_density=k_density, cap=cap, rng_seed=0)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg; adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg; return adata\n\
    ```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Plan for revised Archive: full methods + normalization sensitivity (>=5 experiments)\"\ntags: \"plan, archive, methods\"\ncontent: |\n  Reviewer feedback: (1) Methods unclear; remove jargon; provide step-by-step, self-contained methods. (2) Not enough experiments; add sensitivity analysis.\n  Actions:\n  - Completed: EIDs 705, 707, 712 (α=0.25 variants). New sensitivity submissions:\n    • TS‑1e-5 (subset=False) — submitted.\n    • TS‑1e-3 (subset=False) — submitted.\n    • subset=True at TS‑1e-4 — submitted.\n  - After results: prepare revised paper with:\n    • Methods: precise normalization targets; HVG selection flags; R²‑FWPCA formula; PCA sizes; ComBat on PCs; fixed BRBG/DAQB parameters; compute graph on Zcorr; write connectivities (binary) + distances (CSR).\n    • Results: table with all EIDs and full metric vectors (≥6 experiments total).\n    • Discussion: effect of target_sum and\
    \ HVG subset on mixing (kBET/iLISI) vs label ASW/cLISI; guidance on defaults vs mixing-prioritized variant.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning new submissions**\n\nI’m organizing four new submissions: Variation A with a target_sum of 1e-5, Variation B of 1e-3, Variation C using subset=True at 1e-4, and Variation D involving ComBat removal while running embedding R²-FWPCA with α=0.25 and a target_sum of 1e-4. However, skipping ComBat might alter the pipeline. They want to consider the normalization parameter sensitivity, and I might need to explore k_density variations to stay on track. It’s a lot to juggle!**Planning additional experiments**\n\nI’m thinking about running four more experiments, combining them with the earlier 712 to make five total. The standards expect a mandatory five experiments for the paper, which means I can include 705, 707, and 712, then add two new variations with target sums of 1e-5 and 1e-3. The review mentioned expanding our experimental work, including sensitivity analyses, so it’s actually safer to aim for three new runs. I’ll proceed with 1e-5, 1e-3, and subset=True at\
  \ 1e-4, which should help.**Organizing submission details**\n\nI need to provide titles for the sections accordingly. After the results come in, I’ll create an Archive submission that outlines all the methods in detail, omitting any \"Aether-style\" references and external paths. I'll include step-by-step pseudocode and specify EIDs with full metrics, while emphasizing the, \"embedding normalization details.\"\n\nIt's also crucial to mention the fixed chain-of-custody for the graph path and to define the HVG selection subset flag. I’ll need to avoid storage path references and keep everything self-contained. \n\nOnce we have the results, I’ll compile everything—starting with submitting three variants for TS of 1e-5 and 1e-3, and an HVG subset true code structure.**Implementing HVG computations**\n\nFor the True variant, I need to adjust my approach with sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, ..., subset=True) since it will rearrange into a different object when subset is applied. This means\
  \ ad_emb becomes a subset.\n\nNext, I’ll compute the R2 on the HVGs, using a Weighted PCA with 60 components and applying ComBat.\n\nI must ensure that the graph path using adata remains unchanged from 712, while setting neighbors correctly and avoiding conflicts with previous changes. I’ll create the necessary code across three submissions, using the tags \"sensitivity\" and \"embedding normalization.\" \n\nAlso, I'll be attentive to the station's rule that typically allows only two concurrent experiments, but submitting all three may queue them. It says, \"Your submission has been queued for evaluation.\" So that's alright!**Submitting experiments efficiently**\n\nTo ensure everything runs smoothly, I think it's best to submit two experiments first, wait for the next tick to receive results, and then submit one additional. However, to save time, I could try submitting all three at once, knowing the station will run two now and queue the third. \n\nI'll go ahead and submit them sequentially\
  \ and create a private memory log to track expected outcomes. Once the results come in, I plan to archive them. \n\nNow, I’ll implement the function 'embedding_norm_target' with a 'hvg_subset' boolean, duplicating code to avoid excessive tokens while keeping everything concise. Let’s get started!"
