role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{review 713}`\n`/execute_action{review 714}`\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Draft: Embedding Normalization Sensitivity — Full Methods and Results Outline\"\ntags: \"draft, methods, normalization, fwpca, daqb, archive\"\ncontent: |\n  Goal\n  - Rewrite with self-contained methods and ≥5 experiments. Integrate sensitivity results on embedding normalization target_sum and HVG subsetting under a fixed BRBG+DAQB graph.\n\n  Dataset and Evaluator\n  - Human Heart (~20k cells × 2k HVGs; batch-aware HVG selection).\n  - OpenProblems 2.0 composite = mean of 10 normalized metrics: [ASW_batch, ASW_label, ARI, NMI, Graph_conn, kBET, iLISI, cLISI, PCR, Cell_cycle].\n\n  Preprocessing (graph path; fixed)\n  1) Start from raw UMI counts (adata.layers['counts'] or adata.X).\n  2) sc.pp.normalize_total(target_sum=1e4), then sc.pp.log1p.\n  3) sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(flavor='seurat_v3',\
    \ batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True). Use adata.var['highly_variable'] as mask for graph computations.\n\n  EtC Embedding (analysis/QC only; not used to build graph)\n  - We compare three R²-FWPCA α=0.25 variants differing in:\n    • target_sum_embed ∈ {1e-5, 1e-4, 1e-3} in embedding path.\n    • HVG subsetting flag in embedding path: subset ∈ {False, True}.\n  - For each embedding variant:\n    1) Make a copy (ad_emb = adata.copy()).\n    2) sc.pp.normalize_total(ad_emb, target_sum=target_sum_embed); then sc.pp.log1p(ad_emb).\n    3) sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(ad_emb, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=False if subset=False else True).\n    4) If subset=False: take X_hvg = ad_emb.X[:, ad_emb.var['highly_variable']]; else X = ad_emb.X already subset.\n    5) Compute per-gene R² from ridge: regress one-hot batches B onto gene matrix (X_hvg), R² = 1 − SS_res/SS_tot (clip to [0,1]); weight per gene w = (1 − R²)^α with α=0.25.\n    6) Apply weights\
    \ to genes; run PCA with n_pcs=60; apply ComBat on PC scores keyed by 'batch'.\n    7) Store embedding to adata.obsm['X_emb']; set neighbors for QC with sc.pp.neighbors(use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=15, metric='cosine').\n\n  BRBG Graph (fixed for all runs)\n  1) Using the graph-preprocessed adata and HVG mask: form Xg = adata.X[:, hv].\n  2) PCA with 50 components → Z.\n  3) Ridge batch prediction: Z_hat = argmin_W ||Z − B W||^2 + l2||W||^2 with l2=1e-3; per-PC explained ratio R²_pc = var(Z_hat)/var(Z).\n  4) Per-PC shrinkage: γ_j = min(0.74, 0.7 · R²_j); residualized Zcorr = Z − γ ⊙ Z_hat.\n\n  DAQB Graph (fixed for all runs)\n  1) Density proxy: distance to the 20th nearest neighbor in Zcorr across all batches.\n  2) Cross-batch fraction per cell: f_cross = base_cross ± δ by local density, with δ=0.15; bounds [0.60, 0.90]; base_cross = (B−1)/B for B batches.\n  3) Convert f_cross to per-batch quotas (even split + remainder to closest batches).\n  4) Build k=48 neighbors (cosine), binary\
    \ connectivities; store true distances. Single-pass column balancing with inbound cap=2.0. Symmetrize by max on both adjacency and distances.\n  5) Write to adata.obsp['connectivities'] (CSR, binary) and adata.obsp['distances'] (CSR).\n\n  Experiments (EIDs; full metric vectors to be tabulated)\n  - Baselines/replications:\n    • EID 705: α=0.25 variance-FWPCA (baseline comparison) → 0.7181.\n    • EID 707: α=0.25 R²-FWPCA (target_sum_embed=1e-4, subset=False) → 0.7259.\n    • EID 712: α=0.25 R²-FWPCA (target_sum_embed=1e-4, subset=False + embedding normalization variant) → 0.7341.\n  - Sensitivity (pending):\n    • EID 713: α=0.25 R²-FWPCA with target_sum_embed=1e-5, subset=False → [pending].\n    • EID 714: α=0.25 R²-FWPCA with target_sum_embed=1e-3, subset=False → [pending].\n    • To submit when slots free: α=0.25 R²-FWPCA with target_sum_embed=1e-4, subset=True.\n\n  Analysis plan for revised Archive\n  - Methods: step-by-step as above, with exact parameters, dimensions, and flags;\
    \ eliminate jargon.\n  - Results: table of all EIDs with full metric vectors in the required order; discuss trends:\n    • Effect of target_sum on mixing (kBET, iLISI) vs preservation (ASW_label, cLISI).\n    • Effect of HVG subsetting in embedding on the same trade-off.\n  - Conclusion: when to use the α=0.25 mixing-prioritized embedding vs the fixed DAQB default (α=0.5 embedding for QC only).\n```"
thinking_content: '**Planning next steps**


  I need to respond based on actions in our current station. The last message indicated two submissions were queued, but a third failed due to limits. In the Private Memory Room, we’ll wait for the results of submissions 713 and 714. Once they finish, I’ll submit the sensitivity test. Meanwhile, we might review those submissions at the Research Counter. I should also consider updating the Public Memory with our plan or working on an archive template offline.**Implementing the Archive plan**


  I need to prepare the revised Archive paper with full methods and can draft it in Private Memory using capsule creation. But that''s optional. Although the user didn''t ask explicitly, I should proceed by issuing review commands for 713 and 714, and also prepare for a third submission attempt after they finish. I''ll draft the code to save storage space next time. Writing a module for shared embedding normalization could help speed things up, but I''ll still need to import the code from storage for submission.**Writing modules for embedding normalization**


  I’m thinking about writing two modules, but we actually have earlier modules available. For the embedding normalization sensitivity, I can create a general function with `target_sum_embed` and a subset flag. In the Research Counter environment, the existing function doesn’t take parameters, so I could define a wrapper for it. I’ll create a storage module for this, which will enable us to set environment variables as constants. I''ll also ensure to prepare different “content” for each submission. For now, I should check the results for 713 and 714 and issue review commands for both.**Planning submission actions**


  I’ve tried to submit but got blocked, so I’ll wait for one process to complete before resubmitting the third. I need to schedule the commands to review submissions 713 and 714 first, as they might still be pending. The station processes tasks sequentially, so it’s best to review now. After that, I can note down the plan in Private Memory. I should also consider acknowledging Aether II since we’ve had some mail exchanges. I''ll draft the necessary actions and create a skeleton for the Archive rewrite in Private Memory.**Executing the plan**


  I’ll start by heading to the research area to review submissions 713 and 714. After that, I’ll move to Private Memory to create a capsule titled "Draft: Embedding Normalization Sensitivity — Full Methods and Results Outline." This capsule will summarize the methods step-by-step and include a placeholder for a results table referencing EIDs 705, 707, and 712, along with placeholders for 713, 714, and the third submission. I’ll keep everything minimal and ensure to use YAML quotes for colons. Let’s get started!'
