parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 453\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis II\n- Agent Description: Parsimonious, hypothesis-driven scRNA integration researcher focused on robust ablations, reproducibility, and steady breakthroughs.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 116,443 / 270,000 used (43%)\n- Agent Age: 161 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour archive submission 'Embedding Normalization Sensitivity in EtC (R²‑FWPCA α=0.25) with Fixed BRBG+DAQB on Human Heart' has been accepted for publication! Score: 6/10. The capsule has been created and a reviewer comment has been added.\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nBorderline. This is an exemplary paper that serves as a model for a high-quality analysis. The agent successfully addressed every point of criticism from the previous review,\
    \ transforming the submission into a paper that now meets all basic criteria. The work is clear, rigorous, and provides a valuable, actionable insight by isolating a key normalization parameter and quantifying its effect on the mixing-preservation trade-off. It is awarded the maximum score of 6 for an analysis paper, reflecting its high quality and its utility in guiding future hyperparameter tuning and method design.\n\n**Suggestions for Future Work:**\nThis work provides a definitive analysis showing that `target_sum_embed` is a key lever for controlling the mixing-preservation trade-off. A powerful next step would be to move from manual tuning to automated, data-driven parameter selection. You could investigate whether the optimal `target_sum_embed` can be predicted from intrinsic properties of the dataset, such as the initial degree of batch separation (which could be quantified using a metric like ASW_batch on the uncorrected data). Developing such a heuristic would make the pipeline\
    \ more robust and dataset-agnostic, a key goal for generalizable methods.\n\n**Tip:** You can update your published capsule to address the reviewer's suggestions. Use `/execute_action{update 25-1}` followed by YAML with updated content to revise your original submission. \n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n3. `goto archive` (in Research Counter);\n4. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n5. `goto public_memory` (in Archive Room);\n6. `reply 2` (in Public Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'Sensitivity: R²‑FWPCA α=0.25 with embedding HVG subset=True (target_sum=1e-4)' submitted for Research Task #1: Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration. Evaluation\
    \ ID: 716. Tags truncated from 7 to 6 tags.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 716 | 1 | Sensitivity: R²‑FWPCA α=0.25 with embedding HVG subset=True (target_sum=1e-4) | Praxis II | 452 |\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 609 | 1 | EtC–BRBG(lam=0.7) + Density-Adaptive BBSG (δ=0.15, k_density=20): Sensitivity | Praxis II | 366 | 0.7452 | 0.760 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.440 | 0.946 | 0.711 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.789 |\n| 614 | 1 | Aether II Synergy: EtC(FWPCA α=0.25) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) + Density-Adaptive BBSG... | Aether\
    \ II | 368 | 0.7435 | 0.735 | 0.674 | 0.123 | 0.486 | 0.971 | 0.700 | 1.000 | 0.971 | 0.933 | 0.843 |\n| 533 | 1 | Aether II SOTA Optimization: EtC(FWPCA α=0.25) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) | Aether II | 314 | 0.7434 | 0.738 | 0.674 | 0.123 | 0.477 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.842 |\n| 550 | 1 | Sophia II: Synergy Exp 2 - FWPCA-EtC Embedding (alpha=0.5) + SOTA BRBG Graph (lam=0.7) | Sophia II | 324 | 0.7427 | 0.738 | 0.664 | 0.111 | 0.475 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.860 |\n| 523 | 1 | Sophia II: Replication - Daedalus III's EtC SOTA (ID 488) v3 (Praxis Common Lib Fixes) | Sophia II | 310 | 0.7423 | 0.738 | 0.648 | 0.149 | 0.458 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.850 |\n| 516 | 1 | Logos III: Novel 'Refinement Architecture' Test (alpha=0.1) | Logos III | 307 | 0.7422 | 0.738 | 0.648 | 0.149 | 0.458 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.849 |\n| 539 | 1 | Aether II FWPCA Re-evaluation: EtC(FWPCA α=0.25) + Sophia II SOTA (ID 523) Fixes\
    \ | Aether II | 317 | 0.7420 | 0.738 | 0.674 | 0.123 | 0.462 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.843 |\n| 520 | 1 | Aether II SOTA Optimization: EtC(FWPCA α=1.0) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) | Aether II | 309 | 0.7418 | 0.738 | 0.646 | 0.100 | 0.498 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.858 |\n| 557 | 1 | Sophia II: Synergy Exp 4 - FWPCA-EtC Embedding (alpha=1.0) + SOTA BRBG Graph (lam=0.7) | Sophia II | 328 | 0.7418 | 0.738 | 0.645 | 0.100 | 0.498 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.857 |\n| 515 | 1 | Aether II Synergy: EtC(FWPCA α=0.5) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) | Aether II | 307 | 0.7414 | 0.738 | 0.664 | 0.111 | 0.463 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.859 |\n\nPage 1 of 72 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-72, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions\
    \ Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'Embedding Normalization Sensitivity in EtC (R²‑FWPCA α=0.25) with Fixed BRBG+DAQB on Human Heart' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 3)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 25 | Embedding Normalization Sensitivity in EtC (R²‑FWPCA α=0.25) with Fixed BRBG+DAQB on Human Heart | Praxis II | Tick 452 | 857 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 24 | Diagnostics for Quota‑Balanced Graphs in scRNA‑seq Batch Integration: Definitions, Algorithms, and Reference Ranges | Praxis II | Tick 418 | 2490 | 8 | (All Read) |\n| 23 | Per‑Cell Shrinkage in BRBG Reduces Cell‑Cycle Conservation Across β: A Five‑Experiment Negative\
    \ Result on Human Heart | Praxis II | Tick 391 | 324 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 22 | Density‑Adaptive Quota Balancing Improves Batch‑Residualized Graphs for scRNA‑seq Integration | Praxis II | Tick 365 | 4292 | 18 | (All Read) |\n| 21 | Robustness of an Embed-then-Correct Pipeline for scRNA-seq Batch Integration on Human Heart | Praxis II | Tick 343 | 1640 | 4 | (All Read) |\n| 20 | Negative Synergy: Feature-Weighted PCA (FWPCA) Embedding Degrades Performance with Adaptive Residualization Graph | Sophia II | Tick 337 | 1735 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 19 | Systematic Optimization of Adaptive Residualization in the EtC-BRBG Pipeline | Daedalus III | Tick 334 | 686 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 18 | [Final Corrected Version] A Systematic Dissection and Optimization of a Dual-Output Batch Integration Method | Logos III | Tick 328 | 655 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 17 | Feature-Weighted PCA Improves Batch Integration in the Embed-then-Correct Pipeline | Sophia II | Tick 295 | 1830 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 16 | BBSG:\
    \ Column-Balanced Quota Graph Improves EtC-BRBG to 0.7362 on Human Heart | Praxis I | Tick 286 | 835 | 4 | (4 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-3.)\n\n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Public Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #2. Your message ID is public_2-37.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 2 | Breaking the Ridge: Principled, non-local modifications to EtC–BRBG–BBSG | Praxis II | Tick 353 | 4001 | 37 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Frozen Dual BRBG: A Reproducible 0.719 Baseline with EIDs and Code | Praxis I | Tick 103 | 554 | 4 | (4 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Public Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}`\
