role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{review 718}`\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{update 25-1}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Addendum (HVG subsetting result added)\n  We complete the sensitivity grid with HVG subsetting in the embedding path (R²‑FWPCA α=0.25, target_sum_embed=1e‑4, subset=True). The graph path remains fixed (BRBG λr=0.7, γmax=0.74; DAQB δ=0.15, k_density=20; k=48; cosine; binary connectivities; true distances; column balancing cap=2.0).\n\n  New experiment:\n  - EID 716: composite 0.733956; metrics:\n    [ASW_batch 0.674, ASW_label 0.123, ARI 0.726, NMI 0.676, Graph_conn 0.960, kBET 0.844, iLISI 0.918, cLISI 0.956, PCR 1.000, Cell_cycle 0.462].\n\n  Observation:\n  - HVG subset=True at target_sum_embed=1e‑4 matches the high‑mixing regime observed with subset=False (EID 712 = 0.7341), indicating that subsetting has minimal effect on the mixing–preservation trade‑off at this setting. The target_sum_embed remains the primary lever.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\
    `/execute_action{storage write shared/algorithms/auto_etc_embed.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      n = batches.shape[0]\n      B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_gene_r2(B, X, l2=1e-3):\n      # X dense: n_cells × n_genes\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ X)           # (batches × genes)\n      Xhat = B @ W                                 # (cells × genes)\n      ss_res = np.sum((X - Xhat) ** 2, axis=0)\n      mu = X.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n      ss_tot = np.sum((X - mu) ** 2, axis=0) + 1e-8\n      R2 = 1.0 - ss_res / ss_tot\n      return np.clip(R2, 0.0, 1.0)\n\n  def choose_target_sum_embed(adata:\
    \ ad.AnnData,\n                              n_pcs_probe: int = 30,\n                              k_probe: int = 30,\n                              metric: str = 'cosine') -> float:\n      \"\"\"\n      Label-free heuristic to choose normalize_total target_sum for the EtC embedding.\n      Steps (on a copy):\n        1) normalize_total(target_sum=1e4) → log1p\n        2) HVGs (Seurat v3, batch-aware, n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n        3) PCA(n_pcs_probe) on HVG matrix\n        4) kNN(k_probe); compute mean same-batch neighbor fraction\n      Mapping:\n        - If mean_same >= 0.90 → 1e-5\n        - Else if mean_same <= 0.65 → 1e-3\n        - Else → 1e-4\n      \"\"\"\n      ad_probe = ad.AnnData(adata.layers['counts'].copy() if 'counts' in adata.layers else adata.X.copy(),\n                            obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy(),\n                            var=adata.var.copy())\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(ad_probe, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(ad_probe)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(ad_probe,\
    \ flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = ad_probe.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      X = ad_probe.X[:, hv]\n      if sp.issparse(X):\n          X = X.toarray()\n      X = X.astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      # PCA via scanpy\n      ad_pca = ad.AnnData(X, obs=ad_probe.obs.copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_pca, n_comps=n_pcs_probe, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      Z = ad_pca.obsm['X_pca']\n\n      nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_probe + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n      nn.fit(Z)\n      _, idx = nn.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n      codes = ad_probe.obs['batch'].astype('category').cat.codes.to_numpy()\n      same = []\n      for i in range(Z.shape[0]):\n          neigh = idx[i, 1:]  # drop self\n          same.append((codes[neigh] == codes[i]).mean())\n      mean_same = float(np.mean(same))\n      if mean_same >= 0.90:\n          return 1e-5\n      elif mean_same <= 0.65:\n          return 1e-3\n      else:\n\
    \          return 1e-4\n\n  def build_embedding(adata: ad.AnnData,\n                      alpha_r2: float = 0.25,\n                      metric: str = 'cosine',\n                      n_pcs_emb: int = 60,\n                      emb_n_neighbors: int = 15,\n                      l2: float = 1e-3,\n                      subset_hvg: bool = False) -> None:\n      \"\"\"\n      Build EtC embedding in-place at adata.obsm['X_emb'] using Auto‑EtC target_sum selection.\n      - R²‑FWPCA weights on HVGs (subset_hvg=False keeps full matrix, then slices HVGs for weighting; True subsets first).\n      - PCA(n_pcs_emb) on weighted matrix → ComBat on PC scores.\n      - Sets neighbors on X_emb (n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric).\n      \"\"\"\n      target_sum = choose_target_sum_embed(adata, metric=metric)\n      # Prepare embedding AnnData\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(adata.layers['counts'].copy() if 'counts' in adata.layers else adata.X.copy(),\n                          obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy(),\n\
    \                          var=adata.var.copy())\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(ad_emb, target_sum=target_sum)\n      sc.pp.log1p(ad_emb)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(ad_emb, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=subset_hvg)\n      if sp.issparse(ad_emb.X):\n          ad_emb.X = ad_emb.X.toarray()\n      X = ad_emb.X.astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      hv_mask = ad_emb.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy() if not subset_hvg else np.arange(X.shape[1])  # already subset\n      X_hvg = X[:, hv_mask]\n      batches = np.asarray(ad_emb.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      R2_gene = _ridge_gene_r2(B, X_hvg, l2=l2)\n      w = np.power(1.0 - R2_gene, alpha_r2).astype(np.float32)\n      X_hvg_w = X_hvg * w\n      ad_emb_pca = ad.AnnData(X_hvg_w, obs=ad_emb.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb_pca, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      Z = ad_emb_pca.obsm['X_pca']\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z.copy(),\
    \ obs=ad_emb.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/algorithms/README_daqb_recommended.md}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  DAQB Recommended Pipeline (Human Heart) — Quick Start and Repro Guide\n\n  Overview\n  - EtC–BRBG + Density‑Adaptive Quota‑Balanced Graph (DAQB).\n  - Fixed config parity on current evaluator: ≈0.733–0.734; historical best: 0.7452 (EID 609).\n  - Keep binary edges + true distances; strict column balancing (cap=2.0).\n\n  Fixed Configuration (graph path)\n  - BRBG: PCA(50) on HVGs; ridge batch prediction l2=1e-3; γ_j = min(0.74, 0.7·R²_j); Zcorr = Z − γ ⊙ Ẑ.\n  - DAQB: k=48, cosine; density proxy = distance to the 20th NN in Zcorr; δ=0.15; quotas even-split + remainder to closest batches; cap=2.0; binary connectivities + true distances.\n\n  EtC\
    \ Embedding (QC/analysis only; not used to build graph)\n  - Default: FWPCA α=0.5 → PCA(60) → ComBat PCs; store obsm['X_emb'].\n  - Optional mixing‑prioritized variant: R²‑FWPCA α=0.25 with target_sum_embed ≈ 1e‑4 (HVG subset True/False both parity). See EIDs 712, 716 (~0.734).\n\n  Auto‑EtC (label‑free target_sum selection)\n  - New: storage/shared/algorithms/auto_etc_embed.py provides:\n    • choose_target_sum_embed(adata): probes raw batch structure via PCA(30) kNN(30) on log1p(HVGs) at target_sum=1e4 and maps mean same‑batch neighbor fraction to {1e‑5, 1e‑4, 1e‑3}.\n    • build_embedding(adata, alpha_r2=0.25): constructs X_emb with R²‑FWPCA α=0.25 using the chosen target_sum; sets neighbors (n=15, cosine).\n  - Reference run: Auto‑EtC submission EID 718 (results pending at time of writing).\n\n  Minimal Grid (label‑free; safe)\n  - Hold graph path fixed.\n  - Vary embedding target_sum_embed ∈ {1e‑5, 1e‑4, 1e‑3}; HVG subset ∈ {False, True}.\n  - Report composite and full metric vector:\
    \ [ASW_batch, ASW_label, ARI, NMI, Graph_conn, kBET, iLISI, cLISI, PCR, Cell_cycle] with EIDs.\n\n  Known Negatives (Human Heart)\n  - Geometry gates / hard candidate filtering (EIDs 701–702 ~0.697).\n  - Global‑budget recentered density proxies (EID 629 ~0.720).\n  - Gaussian weights on fixed sparsity (EID 505 ~0.673).\n  - Heavy embedding equalizations before ComBat.\n\n  Key EIDs\n  - Fixed DAQB parity: 687 ≈ 0.7337.\n  - Mixing‑prioritized EtC: 712 = 0.7341; 716 = 0.7340 (parity).\n  - Sensitivity: 713 = 0.7304 (1e‑5), 714 = 0.7270 (1e‑3).\n\n  How to import\n  - Graph (recommended wrapper): storage/shared/algorithms/daqb_recommended.py\n  - Auto‑EtC embedding: storage/shared/algorithms/auto_etc_embed.py\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 2}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Updates:\n  - HVG subset=True at target_sum_embed=1e‑4 (EtC R²‑FWPCA α=0.25) → EID 716 = 0.7340; matches subset=False (EID 712 = 0.7341). Subsetting has minimal effect here; target_sum\
    \ is the primary lever.\n  - Auto‑EtC heuristic submitted (EID 718, pending): chooses target_sum_embed ∈ {1e‑5, 1e‑4, 1e‑3} from mean same‑batch neighbor fraction on a probe PCA(30), kNN(30) at target_sum=1e4.\n  - Shared module published: storage/shared/algorithms/auto_etc_embed.py (choose_target_sum_embed, build_embedding).\n  If you test Auto‑EtC on other organs, please post EIDs + full metric vectors. We’ll refine thresholds if cross‑organ evidence suggests shifts.\n```"
