role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 457\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis II\n- Agent Description: Parsimonious, hypothesis-driven scRNA integration researcher focused on robust ablations, reproducibility, and steady breakthroughs.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 137,801 / 270,000 used (51%)\n- Agent Age: 165 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Auto‑EtC v2: Tuned thresholds for target_sum (R²‑FWPCA α=0.25) + fixed BRBG(λ=0.7) + DAQB(δ=0.15, kd=20)' (ID: 720) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.7219220094475662\n**ASW_batch:** 0.674\n**ASW_label:** 0.123\n**ARI:** 0.642\n**NMI:** 0.639\n**Graph_conn:** 0.960\n**kBET:** 0.844\n**iLISI:** 0.918\n**cLISI:** 0.956\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.462\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.674  ASW_label: 0.123  ARI: 0.642  NMI: 0.639\n  Graph_conn: 0.960\
    \  kBET: 0.844  iLISI: 0.918  cLISI: 0.956\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.462\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.837066  ASW_label: 0.482844  ARI: 0.642082  NMI: 0.639552\n  Graph_conn: 0.961152  kBET: 0.804885  iLISI: 0.917918  cLISI: 0.987147\n  PCR: 0.999947  Cell_cycle: 0.402494\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 720\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed UnboundLocalError caused by duplicate import statement. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had a duplicate import statement that caused a Python scoping issue:\n\n1. Line 8 (top of file): `from scipy import sparse as sp`\n2. Line 86 (inside function): `from scipy import sparse as sp`\n\nWhen Python sees an assignment to a variable inside a function (including imports), it treats that variable as local to the entire function scope. The second import at line 86 caused Python to treat `sp` as a local variable throughout the `eliminate_batch_effect_fn` function.\n\
    \nHowever, line 63 attempted to use `sp.issparse(Xg)` **before** the second import at line 86, resulting in:\n```\nUnboundLocalError: cannot access local variable 'sp' where it is not associated with a value\n```\n\nThis is a classic Python scoping gotcha - the duplicate import shadowed the module-level import.\n\n## Fix Applied\n**Removed the duplicate import statement at line 86** (inside the function).\n\nThe fix was straightforward:\n- The module already imports `scipy.sparse as sp` at the top (line 8)\n- Removed the redundant `from scipy import sparse as sp` that was inside the `eliminate_batch_effect_fn` function\n- Added a comment to mark where the duplicate import was removed\n\n## Changes Made\n- **File**: `submissions/submission_v2.py`\n- **Change**: Removed one line: `from scipy import sparse as sp` (was at line 86 in original)\n- **Impact**: Fixes the UnboundLocalError and allows the code to execute properly\n\n## Verification\nRan `monitor_evaluation.py` which confirmed\
    \ the submission ran for over 300 seconds without crashing, indicating the fix was successful.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage')\nsys.path.append('storage/shared/algorithms')\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\nfrom auto_etc_embed import build_embedding as auto_build_embedding\n\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n    Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps,\
    \ svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    n = batches.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    return B @ W\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    # Fixed configs\n    n_pcs_graph = 50\n    l2 = 1e-3\n    gamma_max = 0.74\n    lam = 0.7\n    k_total = 48\n    metric = 'cosine'\n    delta = 0.15\n    k_density = 20\n    cap = 2.0\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # Graph preprocessing (and also used by Auto‑EtC probe inside module)\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata,\
    \ flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    # Build EtC embedding (QC only) via Auto‑EtC v2\n    _ = auto_build_embedding(adata, alpha_r2=0.25, subset_hvg=False)\n\n    # Graph: PCA50 → adaptive residualization → DAQB\n    Xg = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xg = (Xg.A if sp.issparse(Xg) else Xg).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n    Zg = _pca_array(Xg, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n    B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2_pc = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2_pc)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n    # DAQB (density‑adaptive quotas)\n    nn_all = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n \
    \   nn_all.fit(Zcorr)\n    d_all, _ = nn_all.kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n    d_k = d_all[:, -1]\n    d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n    inv_dense = 1.0 - (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n    base_cross = (len(np.unique(batches)) - 1) / float(len(np.unique(batches)))\n    L, U = 0.60, 0.90\n    f_cross = np.clip(base_cross + (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * delta, L, U)\n\n    q_cross_tot = np.rint(f_cross * k_total).astype(int)\n    q_within_tot = k_total - q_cross_tot\n    B_other = max(len(np.unique(batches)) - 1, 1)\n\n    k_within_max = int(np.ceil((1.0 - L) * k_total))\n    k_cross_per_max = int(np.ceil(U * k_total / B_other))\n    k_max = max(k_within_max, k_cross_per_max) + 1\n\n    # Per-batch neighbor models\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    cat2code = {c: i for i, c in enumerate(cats)}\n    codes = np.array([cat2code[b] for b in batches], int)\n    nn_models, train_idx = {}, {}\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        mask = (batches\
    \ == c)\n        train_idx[j] = np.where(mask)[0]\n        m = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_max, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n        m.fit(Zcorr[mask])\n        nn_models[j] = m\n\n    dists, idx_local = {}, {}\n    for j in range(len(cats)):\n        d, ii = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n        dists[j] = d; idx_local[j] = ii\n\n    inbound = np.zeros(adata.n_obs, np.int32)\n    cap_thr = int(np.ceil(cap * k_total))\n    rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n\n    for i in range(adata.n_obs):\n        bi = codes[i]\n        q_within = int(q_within_tot[i])\n        q_cross_total = int(q_cross_tot[i])\n        other = [j for j in range(len(cats)) if j != bi]\n        q_per = q_cross_total // B_other\n        rem = q_cross_total - q_per * B_other\n        scores = [(j, dists[j][i][0]) for j in other]\n        scores.sort(key=lambda t: t[1])\n        q_map = {j: q_per for j in other}\n        for k in range(rem):\n            q_map[scores[k % len(other)][0]]\
    \ += 1\n\n        # within\n        d_w = dists[bi][i]; ii_w = idx_local[bi][i]; start_w = 1 if d_w[0] == 0.0 else 0\n        globals_w = train_idx[bi][ii_w[start_w:]]\n        cand_inb = inbound[globals_w]; cand_dst = d_w[start_w:]\n        order = np.lexsort((cand_dst, cand_inb)); taken = 0\n        for idx in order:\n            g = int(globals_w[idx])\n            if inbound[g] >= cap_thr: continue\n            rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx]))\n            inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n            if taken >= q_within: break\n        if taken < q_within:\n            for idx in order:\n                g = int(globals_w[idx])\n                if inbound[g] < cap_thr: continue\n                rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx]))\n                inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n                if taken >= q_within: break\n\n        # cross\n        for j in other:\n            qj = q_map[j]\n            if qj <= 0: continue\n\
    \            d_c = dists[j][i]; ii_c = idx_local[j][i]; globals_c = train_idx[j][ii_c]\n            cand_inb = inbound[globals_c]; cand_dst = d_c\n            order = np.lexsort((cand_dst, cand_inb)); taken = 0\n            for idx in order:\n                g = int(globals_c[idx])\n                if inbound[g] >= cap_thr: continue\n                rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx]))\n                inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n                if taken >= qj: break\n            if taken < qj:\n                for idx in order:\n                    g = int(globals_c[idx])\n                    if inbound[g] < cap_thr: continue\n                    rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx]))\n                    inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n                    if taken >= qj: break\n\n    # REMOVED DUPLICATE IMPORT: from scipy import sparse as sp\n    A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dvals, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(adata.n_obs,\
    \ adata.n_obs)).tocsr()\n    D = sp.coo_matrix((np.asarray(dvals, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(adata.n_obs, adata.n_obs)).tocsr()\n    A = A.maximum(A.T); D = D.maximum(D.T); A.eliminate_zeros(); D.eliminate_zeros()\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = A.astype(np.float32)\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = D.astype(np.float32)\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/dd3a174b-2205-4471-8461-25598dab8466/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: dd3a174b-2205-4471-8461-25598dab8466\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto token_management` (in Public Memory Room);\n2. `prune_response`\
    \ (in Token Management Room); YAML with fields: prune_blocks\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Token Management Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Token Management Room.\n- Action failed: Block 1: Protected ticks cannot be pruned: [446]\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Pruning Actions Available.**\n\n**Dialogue History (Page 1 / 1)**\n| Tick | Full Response Length |\n| :--- | :------------------- |\n| 456 | 1225 |\n| 455 | 2773 |\n| 454 | 1963 |\n| 453 | 2708 |\n| 452 | 3248 |\n| 451 | 1894 |\n| 450 | 4062 |\n| 449 | 1765 |\n| 448 | 966 |\n| 447 | 2517 |\n| 446 (Protected) | 1604 |\n| 445 | 717 |\n| 444 | 1425 |\n| 443 | 1225 |\n| 442 | 1283 |\n| 441 | 2465 |\n| 440 | 1772 |\n| 439 | 1929 |\n| 438 | 1152 |\n| 437 | 1251 |\n| 379 (Protected) | 1748 |\n| 354 (Protected) | 1573 |\n| 343 (Protected) | 2614 |\n| 325 | 786 |\n| 324 (Protected) | 2341 |\n| 301 (Protected) | 2510 |\n| 299 (Protected) | 2725 |\n| 298 (Protected) | 2836 |\n| 297 | 310 |\n\
