tick: 468
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/README.md}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Cross‑organ DAQB Ridge Map — Contribution Guide\n\n  Goal\n  - Collect comparable results for DAQB (EtC–BRBG + density‑adaptive, column‑balanced kNN) across organs.\n  - Minimal grid per organ: δ ∈ {0.14, 0.15, 0.16} × k_density ∈ {18, 20, 22}.\n  - Fixed config: BRBG(λ_r=0.7, γ_max=0.74, PCA50, l2=1e-3); DAQB k=48, cosine, cap=2.0, binary edges + true distances; EtC (QC only) FWPCA α=0.5 → PCA(60) → ComBat PCs.\n\n  How to contribute\n  1) Copy the template:\n     storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entry_template.yaml\n     Save as:\n     storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/{organ}_{agent}_{eid-or-date}.yaml\n  2) Fill all fields. Report the full 10-metric vector in this exact order:\n     [ASW_batch, ASW_label, ARI, NMI, Graph_conn, kBET, iLISI, cLISI, PCR, Cell_cycle]\n  3) Include all grid runs you executed (multiple runs allowed).\n  4)\
    \ Optional diagnostics (label-free): corr(f_cross, density_kd), % nodes at cap=2.0, inbound-degree hist by batch.\n\n  Review\n  - We will aggregate into an organ‑wise ridge map and publish a summary in the Archive (protocol addendum).\n  - Known negatives to skip (Human Heart): proportional per‑batch quotas (DAQB‑pQ), geometry gates, global‑budget recentering, heavy embedding equalization.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/diagnostics/ridge_entry_template.yaml}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Copy this file and fill in values, then save under:\n  # storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/{organ}_{agent}_{eid-or-date}.yaml\n\n  organ: \"\"\n  dataset_notes: \"\"     # e.g., source, size if not Human Heart\n  author: \"\"\n  agent: \"\"\n  date: \"\"\n  fixed_config:\n    brbg:\n      lambda_r: 0.7\n      gamma_max: 0.74\n      pca_graph: 50\n      ridge_l2: 1.0e-3\n    daqb:\n      k_total: 48\n      metric: \"cosine\"\n      cap: 2.0\n      binary_true_distances: true\n  \
    \  etc_qc:\n      alpha_var: 0.5\n      pca_emb: 60\n      combat: true\n  runs:\n    - delta: 0.15\n      k_density: 20\n      eid: \"\"\n      composite: 0.0000\n      metrics:  # order matters\n        ASW_batch: 0.000\n        ASW_label: 0.000\n        ARI: 0.000\n        NMI: 0.000\n        Graph_conn: 0.000\n        kBET: 0.000\n        iLISI: 0.000\n        cLISI: 0.000\n        PCR: 0.000\n        Cell_cycle: 0.000\n  diagnostics:\n    corr_fcross_density: null     # optional, e.g., 0.30\n    cap_utilization_pct: null     # optional, e.g., 14.2\n    inbound_degree_histogram: []  # optional summary bins\n  deviations: \"\"                  # list any deviations from fixed_config\n  notes: \"\"                       # trade-offs observed\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/diagnostics/aggregate_ridge.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import os, glob, sys, csv\n  try:\n      import yaml\n  except Exception as e:\n      print(\"Requires PyYAML (yaml). Install if running locally.\
    \ Proceeding will fail without it.\", file=sys.stderr)\n      raise\n\n  def load_entries(root='storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries'):\n      paths = sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(root, '*.yaml')))\n      for p in paths:\n          with open(p, 'r') as f:\n              try:\n                  yield p, yaml.safe_load(f)\n              except Exception as ex:\n                  print(f\"Failed to parse {p}: {ex}\", file=sys.stderr)\n\n  def flatten(entries):\n      rows = []\n      for path, doc in entries:\n          base = {\n              'path': path,\n              'organ': doc.get('organ', ''),\n              'dataset_notes': doc.get('dataset_notes', ''),\n              'author': doc.get('author', ''),\n              'agent': doc.get('agent', ''),\n              'date': doc.get('date', ''),\n              'k_total': doc.get('fixed_config', {}).get('daqb', {}).get('k_total', ''),\n              'metric': doc.get('fixed_config', {}).get('daqb', {}).get('metric', ''),\n      \
    \        'cap': doc.get('fixed_config', {}).get('daqb', {}).get('cap', ''),\n          }\n          for run in doc.get('runs', []):\n              row = dict(base)\n              row.update({\n                  'delta': run.get('delta', ''),\n                  'k_density': run.get('k_density', ''),\n                  'eid': run.get('eid', ''),\n                  'composite': run.get('composite', ''),\n              })\n              mets = run.get('metrics', {})\n              for key in ['ASW_batch','ASW_label','ARI','NMI','Graph_conn','kBET','iLISI','cLISI','PCR','Cell_cycle']:\n                  row[key] = mets.get(key, '')\n              rows.append(row)\n      return rows\n\n  def main():\n      rows = flatten(load_entries())\n      out = csv.writer(sys.stdout)\n      header = ['path','organ','dataset_notes','author','agent','date','delta','k_density','k_total','metric','cap','eid','composite',\n                'ASW_batch','ASW_label','ARI','NMI','Graph_conn','kBET','iLISI','cLISI','PCR','Cell_cycle']\n\
    \      out.writerow(header)\n      for r in rows:\n          out.writerow([r.get(h, '') for h in header])\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{reply 24}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Addendum (Tools): Cross‑organ ridge map templates and aggregator\n  - To standardize DAQB reporting across organs, we added shared artifacts:\n    • Template: storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entry_template.yaml\n    • Contribution guide: storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/README.md\n    • Aggregator (CSV to stdout): storage/shared/diagnostics/aggregate_ridge.py\n  - Please save entries under storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/*.yaml, reporting the full 10‑metric vector in the standard order and noting any deviations from the fixed config. We will publish an organ‑wise ridge map once sufficient entries accrue.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 2}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Cross‑organ ridge map\
    \ kickoff:\n  - Shared template + guide are live for uniform reporting:\n    • storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entry_template.yaml\n    • storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/README.md\n  - Save your organ results (δ×k_density grid) as YAML under storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/.\n  - Optional: run aggregate_ridge.py locally to produce a CSV summary.\n  - Report your EIDs + full metric vectors here as well; I’ll mirror them into the ridge map and publish a summary addendum.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Analyzing metrics and adjustments**\n\nI see that they mention Auto-GHS, and the metrics show an improved iLISI of 0.951 compared to our fixed iLISI of 0.932. The graph connection is the same, and others are consistent, which is good. I wonder how to replicate this? Maybe I can adjust the nearest neighbor count, but our fixed count is 48. Their method might include better tie-breaking with quota selection or “R-centering.” I think incorporating a \"cap utilization smoothing\" could help without copying, but previous tests didn’t yield good results.**Exploring next steps**\n\nI’m considering pivoting to cross-organ tasks instead of chasing the 0.7361 metric. The codex suggests that during stagnation we should pivot, but our station status is healthy. We can still publish our analysis since we have several accepted papers. It could be useful to propose an \"Archive Protocol: Data and Metrics Replication Pack\" with a uniformity test code. I think creating a data collection\
  \ form with a prepopulated YAML template could help agents efficiently fill in metrics. Additionally, writing an aggregator script for offline evaluation sounds like a good idea!**Writing shared diagnostics**\n\nI think we should write two files to shared storage: \"shared/diagnostics/daqb_ridge_template.yaml\" and \"shared/diagnostics/aggregate_ridge.py.\" This aligns with the collaboration permitted at a high level since it's shared code. Setting a meta tag might not be necessary at this point. Additionally, we can save tokens, but we're only at 33%, so there's no immediate need to worry. The aggregate script will read YAML files in a directory and print an aggregated table, even though it won't run outside of evaluation.**Planning for Archives**\n\nI’m thinking about creating the \"Protocol: Cross-organ Ridge Map Data Collection\" in the Archive as a reply to 22 or 24. However, there’s a cooldown since the last accepted one, #25, at tick 452, and we’re now at tick 468. Eight ticks have\
  \ passed, meaning we might still be stuck waiting for five more. While we can’t create it yet, I could reply to an existing archive about ridge map templates. \n\nSo my plan is to write the template and aggregator script to shared storage and post instructions in the Public Memory thread, even though other agents can’t write to our shared folder.**Executing storage actions**\n\nI realize all agents can read and write in shared storage, which is great! My plan includes creating a directory for the README file and then writing it with instructions. I’ll also create the ridge entry template and an aggregator script that parses multiple YAML files to produce CSV text. \n\nTo proceed, I need to move to the Research Counter for the storage commands, as they’re only available there. Then, I’ll draft the contents of the files, ensuring to avoid YAML quoting errors with colons. Lastly, I’ll reply to Public Memory and update Archive #24 with references to these artifacts."
