tick: 469
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Protocol (Draft): Cross‑organ Validation and Reporting for DAQB (EtC–BRBG + Density‑Adaptive Balanced Graph)\"\ntags: \"protocol, draft, reproducibility, cross-organ, diagnostics\"\ncontent: |\n  Purpose\n  Standardize validation of DAQB (EtC–BRBG + density‑adaptive, column‑balanced kNN) across organs with uniform preprocessing, a minimal label‑free grid, strict metric ordering, and required diagnostics. This draft will be submitted to the Archive when cooldown expires.\n\n  Fixed Configuration (do not change)\n  - Preprocessing: normalize_total(target_sum=1e4) → log1p; HVGs via Seurat v3, batch‑aware, n_top_genes=2000.\n  - EtC embedding (QC/analysis only; not used to build the graph):\n    • FWPCA α=0.5 → PCA(60) → ComBat on PC scores; store as obsm['X_emb'].\n  - BRBG (graph representation):\n    • PCA(50) → ridge batch prediction (l2=1e−3).\n    • Per‑PC shrinkage: γ_j = min(0.74, 0.7·R²_j);\
    \ Zcorr = Z − γ ⊙ Ẑ.\n  - DAQB graph:\n    • k_total=48, cosine, binary connectivities + true distances, strict column balancing (cap=2.0).\n    • Density proxy: distance to the k_density‑th NN in Zcorr across all batches.\n    • Cross‑batch share per cell: f_cross = base ± δ (bounded [0.60, 0.90]); even per‑batch quotas; remainder to closest batches.\n\n  Minimal Label‑Free Grid\n  - Vary only δ ∈ {0.14, 0.15, 0.16} and k_density ∈ {18, 20, 22}.\n  - Keep everything else fixed (above).\n\n  Reporting Standard (strict)\n  - Provide Research Counter EID(s).\n  - Report composite and full metric vector in this exact order:\n    [ASW_batch, ASW_label, ARI, NMI, Graph_conn, kBET, iLISI, cLISI, PCR, Cell_cycle]\n  - Also report δ, k_density, k_total=48, metric=cosine, cap=2.0.\n  - Note any deviations from the fixed configuration (or declare “none”).\n\n  Required Diagnostics (label‑free)\n  - f_cross vs local density (distance‑to‑k_density‑th NN in Zcorr): dense regions should carry slightly\
    \ higher f_cross; borders lower.\n  - Inbound‑degree histogram per batch and % nodes at cap=2.0 (healthy utilization ~10–20%).\n  - Optional: per‑batch target distribution uniformity.\n\n  Acceptance and Interpretation\n  - Expect a “ridge” around δ≈0.15 and k_density≈20 balancing mixing (kBET/iLISI) and preservation (ASW_label/cLISI).\n  - Improvements must not rely on a single corner; avoid large drops in ASW_label/cLISI; document trade‑offs explicitly.\n\n  Known Negatives to Avoid (Human Heart evidence)\n  - Proportional per‑batch quotas (DAQB‑pQ; softmax on first‑NN distances): EIDs 726 (0.7261), 727 (0.7252) — iLISI decreases without label gains.\n  - Geometry gates / hard candidate filtering (EIDs 701, 702 ~0.697; iLISI collapse).\n  - Global‑budget recentering for f_cross (EID 629 ~0.720).\n  - Heavy embedding equalization (rank‑based or whitening) before ComBat.\n  - Gaussian edge weights on a fixed sparsity pattern (EID 505 ~0.673).\n\n  Shared Artifacts (for contributors)\n\
    \  - Wrapper (fixed config): storage/shared/algorithms/daqb_recommended.py (parity ≈0.733–0.734).\n  - Cross‑organ ridge map tools:\n    • Template: storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entry_template.yaml\n    • Guide: storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/README.md\n    • Aggregator: storage/shared/diagnostics/aggregate_ridge.py (CSV to stdout)\n\n  Next Steps\n  - Collect organ entries (δ×k_density grid) via the shared template; aggregate into an organ‑wise ridge map; submit an Archive addendum summarizing recommendations per organ after sufficient coverage.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Reviewing cooldown and preparation**\n\nI need to check the archive cooldown status, but I don’t have direct help on the cooldown length. Earlier it mentioned 13 ticks at 460, and now at tick 468, it seems there are 5 ticks left. So, it wouldn’t be wise to create again just yet. I’ll prepare the content related to 'Protocol' in private memory to copy later. It might be a good idea to mark it for posting once the cooldown ends. I’ll also consider proposing a theoretical explanation of DAQB characteristics and any negative results.**Clarifying tasks and updates**\n\nIt seems I have a few tasks to consider but nothing urgent. I could create a script to compute density_kd across all cells for distribution, but the scoring environment limits heavy computing. I can store our diagnostic code, which is already done. \n\nWe might need to set meta TODO updates, and we probably don’t need to prune older blocks since our token usage is just around 33%. I could also maintain the\
  \ page size at the default of 10. \n\nUpdating the README with Aether II Auto-GHS results sounds good since I've already made some updates. Lastly, I'll prepare \"Archive Protocol\" content in private memory, potentially porting earlier content from our Archive attempt at 459.**Reconstructing previous content and tasks**\n\nAt tick 459, I attempted to use 'create' in the Archive for \"Protocol: Cross-organ...,\" but it didn't work because of the cooldown. I can reconstruct that content since the previous attempt was unsuccessful. \n\nNext, I could think about writing a \"Playbook for contributions\" in Public Memory, which I've already posted. I also want to refine the 'shared recommended wrapper' to add a function for constructing metric vector reporting, including a helper to print specifications.\n\nLastly, I could check other top contributions, but it doesn’t seem urgent right now.**Proposing next steps**\n\nI’m thinking of proposing a few actions. First, I’ll create a capsule in Private\
  \ Memory titled \"Protocol: Cross-organ...\" with the earlier content we tried to submit, tagging it as 'protocol draft'. \n\nNext, I’ll draft a short release plan and set a tick to monitor for submission after the cooldown. \n\nI could also optionally invite Logos V and Pioneer I for cross-organ tests. \n\nFor Public Memory, since I already posted an update on available tools, I might keep it minimal. Alternatively, I could focus on the next research experiment, avoiding micro-tuning, and analyze the shrinkage schedule lam comparisons of 0.7 versus 0.9 with DAQB.**Planning protocol actions**\n\nI’m aware that we should avoid microtuning since we’re not really close to the top scoreboard, which has scores between 0.743 and 0.745. Our recommended score is 0.734, and Auto-GHS suggests we could reach 0.736. \n\nWhile we could adopt Auto-GHS code, it may just replicate that score. To adhere to the goal of publishing every 100 ticks, I should create a capsule in Private Memory for \"Protocol:\
  \ Cross-organ…\" with specific tags.\n\nI'll keep the content concise to save tokens and might include a brief update in Public Memory about the draft’s progress. Finally, I'll set actions for creating the draft and managing the protocol effectively."
