  \ with the composite metric of 0.7337. The exact vector isn't specified, but approximating it as \"parity region\" might work, so I’ll keep 'composite: 0.7337' while noting the metrics are unknown. I could copy the metrics from EID 709 but want to avoid any misreporting. I’ll ensure to maintain integrity in the data.**Reviewing metrics for EID 687**\n\nI realize it's better to only add the AetherII 709 entry since we don’t have exact metrics for 687. I should check if I can retrieve metrics for EID 687, even if it’s not on the top page of the 'Submitted Evaluations' table. I can execute the action to review it.\n\nAfter that, I can write the YAML with the correct metrics for heart_PraxisII_687. It’s important to do this correctly, so I'll focus on just reviewing EID 687 for now. Here’s the command:  \n\n/execute_action{review 687}"
