role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Auto‑GHS v4 (r_center=0.25): Label‑free DAQB (δ,kd) tuning with BRBG(λ=0.7)\"\ntags: \"auto-tuning, daqb, label-free, graph-health-score, residualization\"\nabstract: \"Label‑free grid selection of DAQB parameters on Human Heart using GHS v4 with r_center=0.25. Grid over δ∈{0.14,0.15,0.16} and k_density∈{18,20,22}; BRBG(λ=0.7, γ_max=0.74, PCA50). Graphs are binary + true distances with strict column balancing (cap=2.0); fixed remainder‑to‑closest split. EtC (FWPCA α=0.5, PCA60→ComBat) is QC‑only.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import pandas as pd\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    \
    \  sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      n = batches.shape[0]\n      B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      return B @ W\n\n  def _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dists, n):\n      A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      D = sp.coo_matrix((np.asarray(dists,\
    \ dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      A = A.maximum(A.T); D = D.maximum(D.T)\n      A.eliminate_zeros(); D.eliminate_zeros()\n      return A, D\n\n  def _zscore(x, eps=1e-8):\n      x = np.asarray(x, dtype=np.float32)\n      return (x - x.mean()) / (x.std() + eps)\n\n  def _gini(x, eps=1e-8):\n      x = np.asarray(x, dtype=np.float64)\n      if x.size == 0: return 0.0\n      mu = x.mean() + eps\n      diff = np.abs(x.reshape(-1,1) - x.reshape(1,-1))\n      return diff.mean() / (2.0 * mu)\n\n  def _build_daqb_fixed(Zcorr, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine', delta=0.15, k_density=20, cap=2.0, rng_seed=0):\n      Z = np.asarray(Zcorr, dtype=np.float32, order='C')\n      n = Z.shape[0]\n      batches = np.asarray(batches)\n      cats = np.unique(batches); nB = len(cats)\n      base_cross = (nB - 1) / float(nB); L, U = 0.60, 0.90\n\n      nn_all = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n      nn_all.fit(Z)\n      d_all, _\
    \ = nn_all.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n      d_k = d_all[:, -1]\n      d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n      inv_dense = 1.0 - (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n      f_cross = np.clip(base_cross + (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * delta, L, U)\n      q_cross_tot = np.rint(f_cross * k_total).astype(int)\n      q_within_tot = k_total - q_cross_tot\n      B_other = max(nB - 1, 1)\n\n      k_within_max = int(np.ceil((1.0 - L) * k_total))\n      k_cross_per_max = int(np.ceil(U * k_total / B_other))\n      k_max = max(k_within_max, k_cross_per_max) + 1\n\n      cat2code = {c: i for i, c in enumerate(cats)}\n      codes = np.array([cat2code[b] for b in batches], dtype=int)\n      nn_models, train_idx = {}, {}\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          mask = (batches == c)\n          train_idx[j] = np.where(mask)[0]\n          m = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_max, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n          m.fit(Z[mask])\n          nn_models[j]\
    \ = m\n\n      dists, idx_local = {}, {}\n      for j in range(nB):\n          d, ii = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n          dists[j] = d; idx_local[j] = ii\n\n      inbound = np.zeros(n, dtype=np.int32)\n      cap_thr = int(np.ceil(cap * k_total))\n      rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n\n      for i in range(n):\n          bi = codes[i]\n          q_within = int(q_within_tot[i])\n          q_cross_total = int(q_cross_tot[i])\n          other = [j for j in range(nB) if j != bi]\n\n          if q_cross_total > 0 and len(other) > 0:\n              q_per = q_cross_total // B_other\n              rem = q_cross_total - q_per * B_other\n              scores = [(j, dists[j][i][0]) for j in other]\n              scores.sort(key=lambda t: t[1])\n              q_map = {j: q_per for j in other}\n              for k in range(rem): q_map[scores[k % len(other)][0]] += 1\n          else:\n              q_map = {j: 0 for j in other}\n\n          d_w = dists[bi][i]; ii_w = idx_local[bi][i]\n\
    \          start_w = 1 if d_w[0] == 0.0 else 0\n          globals_w = train_idx[bi][ii_w[start_w:]]\n          cand_inb = inbound[globals_w]; cand_dst = d_w[start_w:]\n          order = np.lexsort((cand_dst, cand_inb))\n          taken = 0\n          for idx in order:\n              g = int(globals_w[idx])\n              if inbound[g] >= cap_thr: continue\n              rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx]))\n              inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n              if taken >= q_within: break\n          if taken < q_within:\n              for idx in order:\n                  g = int(globals_w[idx])\n                  if inbound[g] < cap_thr: continue\n                  rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx]))\n                  inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n                  if taken >= q_within: break\n\n          for j in other:\n              qj = q_map[j]\n              if qj <= 0: continue\n              d_c = dists[j][i]; ii_c\
    \ = idx_local[j][i]\n              globals_c = train_idx[j][ii_c]\n              cand_inb = inbound[globals_c]; cand_dst = d_c\n              order = np.lexsort((cand_dst, cand_inb))\n              taken = 0\n              for idx in order:\n                  g = int(globals_c[idx])\n                  if inbound[g] >= cap_thr: continue\n                  rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx]))\n                  inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n                  if taken >= qj: break\n              if taken < qj:\n                  for idx in order:\n                      g = int(globals_c[idx])\n                      if inbound[g] < cap_thr: continue\n                      rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx]))\n                      inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n                      if taken >= qj: break\n\n      C_sym, D_sym = _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(\n          np.asarray(rows, dtype=np.int32),\n          np.asarray(cols,\
    \ dtype=np.int32),\n          np.asarray(dvals, dtype=np.float32),\n          n\n      )\n      return C_sym.astype(np.float32), D_sym.astype(np.float32), f_cross, d_k\n\n  def _score_ghs(C: sp.csr_matrix, f_cross, d_k, batches, r_center=0.25, cap_util_target=0.15, cap_util_sigma=0.05,\n                 w_div=0.4, w_r=0.3, w_cap=0.2, w_inb=0.1):\n      n = C.shape[0]\n      def _z(x): return _zscore(x)\n      s = _z(-(d_k.astype(np.float32)))\n      r = float(np.corrcoef(f_cross.astype(np.float32), s)[0,1])\n      score_r = np.exp(-((r - r_center) ** 2) / (2.0 * (0.10 ** 2)))\n      inbound = np.asarray(C.sum(axis=0)).ravel().astype(np.int32)\n      k_total = int(np.asarray(C.sum(axis=1)).ravel().max())\n      cap_thr = int(np.ceil(2.0 * k_total))\n      cap_util = float((inbound >= cap_thr).mean())\n      score_cap = np.exp(-((cap_util - cap_util_target) ** 2) / (2.0 * (cap_util_sigma ** 2)))\n      indptr, indices = C.indptr, C.indices\n      batch_codes = pd.Categorical(batches).codes\n\
    \      B_other = max(len(np.unique(batch_codes)) - 1, 1)\n      div = np.zeros(n, dtype=np.float32)\n      for i in range(n):\n          nb = indices[indptr[i]:indptr[i+1]]\n          if nb.size == 0: continue\n          unique_other = np.unique(batch_codes[nb][batch_codes[nb] != batch_codes[i]]).size\n          div[i] = unique_other / float(B_other)\n      score_div = float(div.mean())\n      g = _gini(inbound.astype(np.float64))\n      score_inb = float(1.0 - g)\n      return (w_div*score_div + w_r*score_r + w_cap*score_cap + w_inb*score_inb)\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      n_pcs_emb, n_pcs_graph = 60, 50\n      l2, gamma_max, lam = 1e-3, 0.74, 0.7\n      k_total, metric, alpha_var, emb_n_neighbors, cap = 48, 'cosine', 0.5, 15, 2.0\n      deltas, kd_list = [0.14,0.15,0.16], [18,20,22]\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\
    \n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw = Xd * wv\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      Z_emb = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n\
    \      Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      best = None\n      for delta in deltas:\n          for kd in kd_list:\n              Cc, Dc, f_cross, d_k = _build_daqb_fixed(Zcorr, batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                                       delta=delta, k_density=kd, cap=cap, rng_seed=0)\n              ghs = _score_ghs(Cc, f_cross, d_k, batches, r_center=0.25)\n              if (best is None) or (ghs > best[0]):\n                  best = (ghs, delta, kd, Cc, Dc)\n      ghs, best_delta, best_kd, C_best, D_best = best\n      print(f\"[Auto-GHS r0.25] Selected delta={best_delta}, kd={best_kd}, GHS={ghs:.4f}\")\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C_best\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = D_best\n  \
    \    return adata\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Auto‑GHS v4 (weights r‑emphasis: w_div=0.30,w_r=0.40,w_cap=0.20,w_inb=0.10; r_center=0.30)\"\ntags: \"auto-tuning, daqb, label-free, graph-health-score, weighting, residualization\"\nabstract: \"Label‑free DAQB selection on Human Heart with GHS v4 that emphasizes density–mixing coupling: weights (w_div=0.30, w_r=0.40, w_cap=0.20, w_inb=0.10) and r_center=0.30. Grid δ∈{0.14,0.15,0.16}, k_density∈{18,20,22}; BRBG(λ=0.7, γ_max=0.74, PCA50); graphs are binary + true distances with strict column balancing.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import pandas as pd\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n  # (Same helpers as previous submission, trimmed here for brevity; duplicated inline for execution.)\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n\
    \      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      n = batches.shape[0]\n      B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats): B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      return B @ W\n  def _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dists, n):\n      A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dists, dtype=np.float32),\
    \ (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      D = sp.coo_matrix((np.asarray(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      A = A.maximum(A.T); D = D.maximum(D.T)\n      A.eliminate_zeros(); D.eliminate_zeros()\n      return A, D\n  def _zscore(x, eps=1e-8):\n      x = np.asarray(x, dtype=np.float32)\n      return (x - x.mean()) / (x.std() + eps)\n  def _gini(x, eps=1e-8):\n      x = np.asarray(x, dtype=np.float64)\n      if x.size == 0: return 0.0\n      mu = x.mean() + eps\n      diff = np.abs(x.reshape(-1,1) - x.reshape(1,-1))\n      return diff.mean() / (2.0 * mu)\n  def _build_daqb_fixed(Zcorr, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine', delta=0.15, k_density=20, cap=2.0, rng_seed=0):\n      Z = np.asarray(Zcorr, dtype=np.float32, order='C')\n      n = Z.shape[0]\n      batches = np.asarray(batches)\n      cats = np.unique(batches); nB = len(cats)\n      base_cross = (nB - 1) / float(nB); L, U = 0.60, 0.90\n      nn_all = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density +\
    \ 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n      nn_all.fit(Z)\n      d_all, _ = nn_all.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n      d_k = d_all[:, -1]\n      d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n      inv_dense = 1.0 - (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n      f_cross = np.clip(base_cross + (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * delta, L, U)\n      q_cross_tot = np.rint(f_cross * k_total).astype(int)\n      q_within_tot = k_total - q_cross_tot\n      B_other = max(nB - 1, 1)\n      k_within_max = int(np.ceil((1.0 - L) * k_total))\n      k_cross_per_max = int(np.ceil(U * k_total / B_other))\n      k_max = max(k_within_max, k_cross_per_max) + 1\n      cat2code = {c: i for i, c in enumerate(cats)}\n      codes = np.array([cat2code[b] for b in batches], dtype=int)\n      nn_models, train_idx = {}, {}\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          mask = (batches == c)\n          train_idx[j] = np.where(mask)[0]\n          m = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_max, metric=metric,\
    \ algorithm='brute')\n          m.fit(Z[mask])\n          nn_models[j] = m\n      dists, idx_local = {}, {}\n      for j in range(nB):\n          d, ii = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n          dists[j] = d; idx_local[j] = ii\n      inbound = np.zeros(n, dtype=np.int32)\n      cap_thr = int(np.ceil(2.0 * k_total))\n      rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n      for i in range(n):\n          bi = codes[i]\n          q_within = int(q_within_tot[i])\n          q_cross_total = int(q_cross_tot[i])\n          other = [j for j in range(nB) if j != bi]\n          if q_cross_total > 0 and len(other) > 0:\n              q_per = q_cross_total // B_other\n              rem = q_cross_total - q_per * B_other\n              scores = [(j, dists[j][i][0]) for j in other]\n              scores.sort(key=lambda t: t[1])\n              q_map = {j: q_per for j in other}\n              for k in range(rem): q_map[scores[k % len(other)][0]] += 1\n          else:\n              q_map = {j: 0\
    \ for j in other}\n          d_w = dists[bi][i]; ii_w = idx_local[bi][i]\n          start_w = 1 if d_w[0] == 0.0 else 0\n          globals_w = train_idx[bi][ii_w[start_w:]]\n          cand_inb = inbound[globals_w]; cand_dst = d_w[start_w:]\n          order = np.lexsort((cand_dst, cand_inb))\n          taken = 0\n          for idx in order:\n              g = int(globals_w[idx])\n              if inbound[g] >= cap_thr: continue\n              rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx]))\n              inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n              if taken >= q_within: break\n          if taken < q_within:\n              for idx in order:\n                  g = int(globals_w[idx])\n                  if inbound[g] < cap_thr: continue\n                  rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx]))\n                  inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n                  if taken >= q_within: break\n          for j in other:\n              qj = q_map[j]\n\
    \              if qj <= 0: continue\n              d_c = dists[j][i]; ii_c = idx_local[j][i]\n              globals_c = train_idx[j][ii_c]\n              cand_inb = inbound[globals_c]; cand_dst = d_c\n              order = np.lexsort((cand_dst, cand_inb))\n              taken = 0\n              for idx in order:\n                  g = int(globals_c[idx])\n                  if inbound[g] >= cap_thr: continue\n                  rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx]))\n                  inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n                  if taken >= qj: break\n              if taken < qj:\n                  for idx in order:\n                      g = int(globals_c[idx])\n                      if inbound[g] < cap_thr: continue\n                      rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx]))\n                      inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n                      if taken >= qj: break\n      C_sym, D_sym = _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(\n\
    \          np.asarray(rows, dtype=np.int32),\n          np.asarray(cols, dtype=np.int32),\n          np.asarray(dvals, dtype=np.float32),\n          n\n      )\n      return C_sym.astype(np.float32), D_sym.astype(np.float32), f_cross, d_k\n\n  def _score_ghs(C: sp.csr_matrix, f_cross, d_k, batches, r_center=0.30, cap_util_target=0.15, cap_util_sigma=0.05,\n                 w_div=0.30, w_r=0.40, w_cap=0.20, w_inb=0.10):\n      n = C.shape[0]\n      s = _zscore(-(d_k.astype(np.float32)))\n      r = float(np.corrcoef(f_cross.astype(np.float32), s)[0,1])\n      score_r = np.exp(-((r - r_center) ** 2) / (2.0 * (0.10 ** 2)))\n      inbound = np.asarray(C.sum(axis=0)).ravel().astype(np.int32)\n      k_total = int(np.asarray(C.sum(axis=1)).ravel().max())\n      cap_thr = int(np.ceil(2.0 * k_total))\n      cap_util = float((inbound >= cap_thr).mean())\n      score_cap = np.exp(-((cap_util - cap_util_target) ** 2) / (2.0 * (cap_util_sigma ** 2)))\n      indptr, indices = C.indptr, C.indices\n\
    \      batch_codes = pd.Categorical(batches).codes\n      B_other = max(len(np.unique(batch_codes)) - 1, 1)\n      div = np.zeros(n, dtype=np.float32)\n      for i in range(n):\n          nb = indices[indptr[i]:indptr[i+1]]\n          if nb.size == 0: continue\n          unique_other = np.unique(batch_codes[nb][batch_codes[nb] != batch_codes[i]]).size\n          div[i] = unique_other / float(B_other)\n      score_div = float(div.mean())\n      g = _gini(inbound.astype(np.float64))\n      score_inb = float(1.0 - g)\n      return (w_div*score_div + w_r*score_r + w_cap*score_cap + w_inb*score_inb)\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      n_pcs_emb, n_pcs_graph = 60, 50\n      l2, gamma_max, lam = 1e-3, 0.74, 0.7\n      k_total, metric, alpha_var, emb_n_neighbors, cap = 48, 'cosine', 0.5, 15, 2.0\n      deltas, kd_list = [0.14,0.15,0.16], [18,20,22]\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\
    \n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw = Xd * wv\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      Z_emb = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n\
    \      Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      best = None\n      for delta in deltas:\n          for kd in kd_list:\n              Cc, Dc, f_cross, d_k = _build_daqb_fixed(Zcorr, batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                                       delta=delta, k_density=kd, cap=cap, rng_seed=0)\n              ghs = _score_ghs(Cc, f_cross, d_k, batches, r_center=0.30,\n                               w_div=0.30, w_r=0.40, w_cap=0.20, w_inb=0.10)\n              if (best is None) or (ghs > best[0]):\n                  best = (ghs, delta, kd, Cc, Dc)\n      ghs, best_delta, best_kd, C_best, D_best = best\n      print(f\"[Auto-GHS weightsR] Selected delta={best_delta}, kd={best_kd}, GHS={ghs:.4f}\")\n      adata.obsp['connectivities']\
    \ = C_best\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = D_best\n      return adata\n```"
thinking_content: "**Addressing reviewer feedback**\n\nI need to respond to reviewer feedback by publishing an improved version of the negative paper, including the full math formula for GHS and adding at least five experiments. The inactivity message indicates we should resume our testing phase, which we recently started. Now, I need to run a series of experiments on GHS variations. We can explore different values for r_center and weightings for GHS components, ensuring we meet the five experiments requirement with different settings. Each evaluation will involve running tests and computing final scores through established metrics.**Producing Auto-GHS code**\n\nI’m focused on creating the code for the Auto-GHS variant using different inputs. First, I’ll set up a base template function to vary r_center and possibly adjust cap targets. I aim to submit five runs with the following r_center values: 0.20, 0.25, 0.30 (which I’ve done before), 0.35, and 0.40. Since we already have data for 0.30,\
  \ I’ll also ensure we include additional experiments for 0.25 and 0.35. To streamline submissions, I’ll utilize storage modules to minimize code duplication and add the necessary pandas import to fix a previous bug.**Analyzing Auto-GHS logs**\n\nI've noted that in the 734 logs, Auto-GHS selected delta=0.14 and kd=22 with a GHS score of 0.4704. It showed r near 1.0 and cap_util=0.0, which feels unnatural since using a target of r=0.30 should have led to better scoring. The huge gaussian penalty for being at 1.0 shouldn’t have been overlooked. It seems other components might’ve outweighed the penalties. I see that score_div is a crucial factor, so I plan to run at least four more experiments focused on r_center sweeps to adjust these weightings.**Preparing experiments and submissions**\n\nI need to improve the archive by providing the full formula for GHS, but first, I have to conduct experiments to fulfill the requirement for five submissions. Each variant will include r_center as a parameter,\
  \ along with additional weight variations. The weights I’m considering are w_div=0.30, w_r=0.40, w_cap=0.20, w_inb=0.10, and a second set of w_div=0.25, w_r=0.35, w_cap=0.25, w_inb=0.15. \n\nI’ll submit two runs concurrently, which keeps within the limits, and I plan to avoid rapid submissions to manage cooldown constraints. I'll carefully manage the submitting process, ensuring no more than two experiments run at once.**Staging experiment submissions**\n\nI’m planning to submit two experiments at a time and then wait for the results. Since the running limit is two, I'll go ahead with two submissions now: \n\nFirst, I'll submit Auto-GHS v4 with r_center=0.25 and default weights (0.4, 0.3, 0.2, 0.1). Next, I'll submit Auto-GHS v4 with modified weights (w_div=0.3, w_r=0.4, w_cap=0.2, w_inb=0.1) and r_center=0.30. \n\nTo keep everything organized, I’ll parameterize the code, copy from previous versions, and ensure to import pandas. I also want to acknowledge the archive rejection by signaling\
  \ our plan for restructuring. Finally, I’ll prepare to craft concise code, reusing functions as necessary while managing tokens effectively. Let’s get this done!"
