tick: 479
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Draft (Archive): Label‑Free Graph Tuning for DAQB on Human Heart — Methods (explicit formulas) and Results plan\"\ntags: \"draft, methods, ghs, label-free, daqb, residualization\"\ncontent: |\n  Objective\n  Provide a complete, self-contained Methods section with explicit formulas for label‑free DAQB tuning (GHS v4/v5), and enumerate the experiments to meet ≥5 requirement. This draft will be the source_private for the final Archive paper once EIDs 742/743 finish.\n\n  Dataset and Preprocessing\n  - Human Heart (~20k cells; 2k HVGs; 4 batches). Input: raw UMI counts (adata.X).\n  - Normalize + log: x̃ = log1p( normalize_total(x; target=1e4) ).\n  - HVGs: Seurat v3, batch-aware, n_top_genes=2000.\n\n  Embed-then-Correct (QC only; not used for graph)\n  - Feature-weighted PCA (FWPCA, α=0.5): per-gene variance var_g on HVGs; weight w_g = var_g^{-α/2}.\n  - PCA on weighted matrix, n_pcs_emb=60 → ComBat\
    \ on PC scores.\n  - Store adata.obsm['X_emb']; used only for neighbors() to set keys; NOT used for graph building.\n\n  BRBG (Graph Representation)\n  - PCA on HVGs: Z ∈ R^{n×50}.\n  - One-hot batch design B ∈ {0,1}^{n×B}.\n  - Ridge batch prediction: W = argmin_W ||Z − BW||_F^2 + λ||W||_F^2, λ=1e−3; Ẑ = BW.\n  - Per-PC shrinkage: For component j, R²_j = var(Ẑ_j)/var(Z_j), γ_j = min(γ_max, λ_r·R²_j), with γ_max=0.74 and λ_r=0.7.\n  - Residualization: Z_corr = Z − (Ẑ ⊙ γ), broadcasting γ over rows.\n\n  DAQB (Density‑Adaptive Quota‑Balanced kNN, fixed split)\n  - Inputs: Z_corr; k_total=48; metric=cosine; strict column balancing with inbound cap = ceil(cap·k_total), cap=2.0.\n  - Density proxy per cell i: d_k(i) = distance to k_density‑th NN in Z_corr (across all batches). Normalize s(i) = 1 − (d_k(i) − d_min)/(d_max − d_min).\n  - Cross-batch target fraction: f_cross(i) = clip( base_cross + 2·δ·(s(i) − 0.5), L, U ), with base_cross = (B−1)/B, L=0.60, U=0.90.\n  - Quotas per cell\
    \ i:\n    • q_cross_tot(i) = round( f_cross(i) · k_total ); q_within(i) = k_total − q_cross_tot(i).\n    • Distribute q_cross_tot evenly across other batches (floor), assign remainder to closest other batches by first‑NN distance.\n  - Selection (directed pass, then symmetrize):\n    • Within‑batch: choose q_within(i) targets by lexsort (inbound ascending, then distance ascending), honoring inbound cap first; fallback ignores cap if needed to fill degree.\n    • Per other batch j: choose q_j(i) similarly.\n    • Build directed edges (i→t) and track directed inbound counts; then symmetrize undirected adjacency by max; set connectivities binary and distances to true values.\n\n  GHS v4 (Label‑Free Graph Health Score; used in EIDs 734, 738, 739)\n  - Notation: C (undirected binary CSR); batches categorical; k_total as above.\n  - Components:\n    1) Cross‑batch diversity: For node i, div(i) = |{other batch codes among neighbors of i}| / (B−1); Score_div = mean_i div(i).\n    2) Density–mixing\
    \ coupling: z = zscore(−d_k); r = corr( f_cross, z ); Score_r = exp( −(r − r_center)^2 / (2·σ_r^2) ). Defaults: r_center=0.30, σ_r=0.10; variant: r_center=0.25.\n    3) Cap utilization (symmetric inbound in v4): inbound = degree(column sums of C); cap_thr = ceil(cap·k_total); cap_util = fraction(inbound ≥ cap_thr); Score_cap = exp( −(cap_util − cap_target)^2 / (2·σ_cap^2) ), cap_target=0.15, σ_cap=0.05.\n    4) Inbound uniformity: Score_inb = 1 − Gini(inbound).\n  - Aggregation: GHS_v4 = w_div·Score_div + w_r·Score_r + w_cap·Score_cap + w_inb·Score_inb.\n    • Default weights: (w_div, w_r, w_cap, w_inb) = (0.40, 0.30, 0.20, 0.10).\n    • r‑emphasis variant: (0.30, 0.40, 0.20, 0.10).\n\n  GHS v5 (Proposed; used in EIDs 742, 743)\n  - Fixes for v4 degeneration:\n    • Use DIRECTED inbound counts (pre‑symmetrization) for cap utilization.\n    • Replace density–mixing r‑term with target adherence to the realized cross‑batch fraction.\n  - Additional directed diagnostics from the DAQB builder:\n\
    \    • inbound_directed(t): inbound count for target t in directed selection.\n    • realized_cross(i) = (# directed cross‑batch edges out of i) / k_total.\n  - Components:\n    1) Diversity: as in v4 but computed on undirected C (Score_div).\n    2) Target adherence: MSE_target = mean_i ( realized_cross(i) − f_cross(i) )^2; Score_target = exp( − MSE_target / (2·σ_target^2) ), σ_target=0.05.\n    3) Cap utilization (directed): cap_thr = ceil(cap·k_total); cap_util = fraction(inbound_directed ≥ cap_thr); Score_cap = exp( −(cap_util − cap_target)^2 / (2·σ_cap^2) ), cap_target=0.15, σ_cap=0.05.\n    4) Inbound uniformity (directed): Score_inb = 1 − Gini(inbound_directed).\n  - Aggregation: GHS_v5 = w_div·Score_div + w_target·Score_target + w_cap·Score_cap + w_inb·Score_inb.\n    • Default weights: (0.35, 0.35, 0.20, 0.10).\n    • Target‑heavy: (0.25, 0.45, 0.20, 0.10).\n\n  Experiments (≥5; all Human Heart; BRBG and DAQB fixed as above; graphs binary + true distances; cosine; cap=2.0)\n\
    \  - v4‑A (EID 734): r_center=0.30; default weights (0.40,0.30,0.20,0.10) — RESULT: 0.7261; picks (δ=0.14, kd=22).\n  - v4‑B (EID 738): r_center=0.25; default weights — RESULT: 0.7236; picks (δ=0.14, kd=22).\n  - v4‑C (EID 739): r‑emphasis weights (0.30,0.40,0.20,0.10); r_center=0.30 — RESULT: 0.7239; picks (δ=0.14, kd=22).\n  - v5‑A (EID 742): default v5 weights (0.35,0.35,0.20,0.10); σ_target=0.05; cap_target=0.15 — PENDING.\n  - v5‑B (EID 743): target‑heavy v5 weights (0.25,0.45,0.20,0.10) — PENDING.\n  References:\n  - Fixed DAQB ridge (reference): EID 687 = 0.7337 (δ=0.15, kd=20).\n  - Published label‑free tuning (Auto‑GHS): EIDs 693, 699 ≈ 0.7361.\n\n  Planned Results Section (to fill once 742/743 finish)\n  - Table: method variant → (δ, kd) chosen, composite, full metric vector [ASW_batch, ASW_label, ARI, NMI, Graph_conn, kBET, iLISI, cLISI, PCR, Cell_cycle].\n  - Analysis:\n    • Show that v4 consistently chooses δ=0.14, kd=22 and underperforms ridge/baselines.\n    • Evaluate\
    \ whether v5 shifts choices back toward ridge region (δ≈0.15, kd≈20); analyze component contributions (diversity, target adherence, cap utilization, uniformity).\n\n  Conclusion (anticipated)\n  - On Human Heart, both v4 and v5 automatic label‑free selection are negative or parity−; fixed DAQB ridge remains recommended. We provide full formulas and ablations to satisfy reproducibility and generalization criteria.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Organizing research tasks**\n\nI need to respond with appropriate actions. I've submitted two jobs, 742 and 743, and now I should wait for their evaluation or shift focus to other tasks, like writing Private Memory notes and preparing the Archive paper. The reviewer asked for five or more experiments, and I have currently listed experiments 734, 738, 739, 742, and 743, which total five. Once I receive results for 742 and 743, I can finalize the paper.**Planning research publication**\n\nI've had previous rejections for the protocol paper, so it’s best to hold back on further commentary. Now, I plan to publish the negative results paper once I complete jobs 742 and 743, which will include five or more experiments. I might create a Private Memory outline to capture mathematical formulas and experimental designs. Once the results come in, I can submit them to Archive. I'll also keep track of token management, as we're currently at 53%, which is manageable.**Preparing for\
  \ v5 adjustments**\n\nFor v5, I need to replace the r term with target adherence, which is calculated as S_target = exp(-MSE(realized_cross - f_cross)/(2 sigma_target^2)). I'll also compute capacity utilization using directed inbound and cap_thr = ceil(cap*k_total), providing the necessary parameter values. While I’d like to pre-create Archive content, it's best to hold off until I have the results. I could prepare a draft in Private Memory and consolidate everything once the results come in. We could also consider additional experiments if needed, though we already have five.**Organizing memory and updates**\n\nI can update our meta, but it’s not strictly necessary. I might want to store the ghs_v5 code in storage, and I’ve done that already. I plan to create a Private Memory capsule called \"Draft: Label-Free Graph Tuning Negative Result (GHS v4/v5),\" which will include methods with explicit formulas and a planned results table along with placeholders for EIDs. I could also draft an\
  \ update to Archive #24 regarding the GHS v5 addition, but it's wise to hold off until results are complete. In the meantime, I can focus on writing!**Creating Private Memory capsule**\n\nI'm going to create a Private Memory capsule with explicit mathematical details. I’ll also prepare a saved \"archive draft content\" using source_private later. First, I’ll check Research Counter, knowing that results might not be immediate this time. \n\nIn the capsule, I'll define important formulas and components like Zcorr, f_cross, quota rounding, and GHS structures. I’ll include weights for both GHS v4 and v5, as well as placeholders for EIDs 742 and 743. Once I have the results, I can plan to submit to Archive. For now, I’ll just focus on this implementation!"
