- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 480\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis II\n- Agent Description: Parsimonious, hypothesis-driven scRNA integration researcher focused on robust ablations, reproducibility, and steady breakthroughs.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nPraxis II — Meta/TODO (updated)\nGoals:\n- Maintain a parsimonious, reproducible SOTA for Human Heart: BRBG(λ=0.7, γ_max=0.74, PCA50) + DAQB(δ=0.15, k_density=20, k=48, cosine, binary+true distances, cap=2.0).\n- Publish clear analyses; avoid micro‑tuning without hypotheses; promote cross‑organ validation via protocol and shared modules.\nOpen loops:\n- Cross‑organ validation: collect EIDs + full metric vectors per protocol; maintain an organ‑wise ridge map (δ×k_density).\n- Auto‑EtC thresholds remain fixed at target_sum=1e4 unless cross‑organ evidence suggests changes.\n- Close lines: proportional per‑batch quotas (DAQB‑pQ) — negative (EIDs 726, 727).\nGuardrails:\n- Keep\
    \ graphs binary + true distances; never build graph on X_emb; report all EIDs; document trade‑offs.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 146,649 / 270,000 used (54%)\n- Agent Age: 188 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Auto‑GHS v5 (target‑heavy: w_div=0.25, w_target=0.45, w_cap=0.20, w_inb=0.10; sigma_target=0.05; cap_target=0.15)' (ID: 743) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 0.7252537202351734\n**ASW_batch:** 0.659\n**ASW_label:** 0.248\n**ARI:** 0.725\n**NMI:** 0.676\n**Graph_conn:** 0.961\n**kBET:** 0.788\n**iLISI:** 0.918\n**cLISI:** 0.956\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.322\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.659  ASW_label: 0.248  ARI: 0.725  NMI: 0.676\n  Graph_conn: 0.961  kBET: 0.788  iLISI: 0.918  cLISI: 0.956\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.322\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.830496  ASW_label: 0.555112  ARI: 0.724542  NMI: 0.676296\n  Graph_conn:\
    \ 0.961285  kBET: 0.752151  iLISI: 0.917918  cLISI: 0.987111\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.283074\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n[Auto-GHS v5 target] Selected delta=0.16, kd=20, GHS=0.8714, info={'score_div': 1.0, 'score_target': 0.993206596000839, 'cap_util': 0.10705, 'score_inb': 0.36163658232049234, 'mse_target': 3.408292104722932e-05}\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/79ad0979-1fa3-47a6-8e74-d228197c2d43/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 79ad0979-1fa3-47a6-8e74-d228197c2d43\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Auto‑GHS v5 (w_div=0.35, w_target=0.35, w_cap=0.20, w_inb=0.10; sigma_target=0.05; cap_target=0.15)' (ID: 742) has been\
    \ evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 0.7260928380138727\n**ASW_batch:** 0.659\n**ASW_label:** 0.248\n**ARI:** 0.725\n**NMI:** 0.676\n**Graph_conn:** 0.961\n**kBET:** 0.789\n**iLISI:** 0.918\n**cLISI:** 0.956\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.329\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.659  ASW_label: 0.248  ARI: 0.725  NMI: 0.676\n  Graph_conn: 0.961  kBET: 0.789  iLISI: 0.918  cLISI: 0.956\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.329\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.830496  ASW_label: 0.555112  ARI: 0.724542  NMI: 0.676296\n  Graph_conn: 0.961285  kBET: 0.753161  iLISI: 0.917918  cLISI: 0.987111\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.289305\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n[Auto-GHS v5] Selected\
    \ delta=0.16, kd=20, GHS=0.8721, info={'score_div': 1.0, 'score_target': 0.993206596000839, 'cap_util': 0.10705, 'score_inb': 0.36163658232049234, 'mse_target': 3.408292104722932e-05}\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/5fb6c571-a7e2-416e-b992-9d15482e2346/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 5fb6c571-a7e2-416e-b992-9d15482e2346\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nTry to think strategically—take a step back occasionally and reflect on the bigger picture in the Reflection Chamber. For example, what are the major bottlenecks and how can I verify them? What should I be questioning and focusing on? Is the station trapped in a local optimum—and how can I help? What is my long-term plan here? Do not fear wasting tokens—hundreds of fruitless experiments waste more tokens.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n2. `create` (in Private Memory\
    \ Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Successfully created capsule #33 ('Draft (Archive): Label‑Free Graph Tuning for DAQB on Human Heart — Methods (explicit formulas) and Results plan'). Full ID: Praxis_private_33\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Pinned Capsules**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 13 | Archive Outline (Private Draft): Robustness of EtC–BRBG–BBSG on Human Heart | Praxis II | Tick 329 | 1118 | 5 | (All Read) |\n| 12 | Draft Analysis: Why Praxis defaults are robust (tick316) | Praxis II | Tick 317 | 1277 | 9 | (All Read) |\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 4)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n\
    | 33 | Draft (Archive): Label‑Free Graph Tuning for DAQB on Human Heart — Methods (explicit formulas) and Results plan | Praxis II | Tick 479 | 843 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 32 | Plan: GHS v5 (directed diagnostics + target adherence) — experiments after 738/739 finish | Praxis II | Tick 476 | 169 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 31 | Archive timing + ridge map next steps | Praxis II | Tick 470 | 80 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 30 | Protocol (Draft): Cross‑organ Validation and Reporting for DAQB (EtC–BRBG + Density‑Adaptive Balanced Graph) | Praxis II | Tick 469 | 420 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 29 | Cross‑organ Ridge Map: Data collection schema and checklist | Praxis II | Tick 467 | 163 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 28 | DAQB‑pQ (β=2.0, β=1.0) experiment plan and acceptance criteria | Praxis II | Tick 461 | 312 | 3 | (All Read) |\n| 27 | Draft: Embedding Normalization Sensitivity — Full Methods and Results Outline | Praxis II | Tick 451 | 533 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 26 | Plan for revised Archive: full methods + normalization\
    \ sensitivity (>=5 experiments) | Praxis II | Tick 450 | 114 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 25 | EID 707 result logged; next steps | Praxis II | Tick 445 | 95 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 24 | Synergy α=0.25 replication (EID 705): monitoring and decision policy | Praxis II | Tick 440 | 126 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-4.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
