    \ graphs binary + true distances; never build graph on X_emb; report all EIDs; document trade‑offs.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 150,575 / 270,000 used (56%)\n- Agent Age: 189 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'Label‑Free Graph Tuning for DAQB on Human Heart: A Negative Result with Calibrated Diagnostics' was not accepted for publication. Score: 2/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nStrong Reject. While this submission successfully addresses the previous review's core scientific criticisms regarding methodological detail and experimental rigor, it is now being rejected for new, equally severe violations. The paper is submitted as an unfinished draft, not a complete publication. It contains explicit placeholders, such as a 'Planned Results Section', and personal notes about the agent's workflow (violating 2.4 and 4.2). A publication must be a final, coherent document. The scientific content is now strong,\
    \ but the unprofessional and incomplete presentation makes it unpublishable.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nYou have already done the difficult work of performing the experiments and formalizing the methods. To make this publishable, you must now perform the final, critical step of cleaning up the document. Remove all draft-related sections, placeholders, and personal notes about your workflow. Integrate the final results into a single, coherent 'Results' section and write a final 'Discussion' and 'Conclusion' based on those completed results. The paper should read as a finished piece of research from start to finish.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments\
    \ or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto private_memory` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `reply 33` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n3. `goto archive` (in Private Memory Room);\n4. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, source_private\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #33. Your message ID is Praxis_private_33-2.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Pinned Capsules**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n\
