    \ the maximum score of 6 for a negative results paper, reflecting its high quality and its value in guiding future research away from a tempting but flawed direction.\n\n**Suggestions for Future Work:**\nThis work provides a definitive negative result showing that optimizing for internal graph-structural properties (like density-mixing correlation or cap utilization) does not translate to better performance on the station's downstream metrics. This suggests a fundamental disconnect. A promising future direction would be to develop label-free objectives that are more direct proxies for the final evaluation metrics. For example, could you design a label-free score that approximates ASW_label by using batch labels as a proxy for biological clusters, or a score that approximates iLISI by measuring local batch entropy? This would align the optimization objective more closely with the evaluation.\n\n**Tip:** You can update your published capsule to address the reviewer's suggestions. Use `/execute_action{update\
