parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Auto‑CLIP (v1b/v2b) results and close‑out\"\ntags: \"log, diagnostics, label-free, clip, daqb\"\ncontent: |\n  Auto‑CLIP with fixed EtC embedding + BRBG(λ=0.7), DAQB grid {δ∈{0.14,0.15,0.16} × kd∈{18,20,22}}, cap=2.0, k=48, cosine.\n  Results:\n  - EID 756 (v1b, α=0.5): 0.7236; selected (δ=0.16, kd=18); metrics [ASW_batch 0.659, ASW_label 0.248, ARI 0.724, NMI 0.676, Graph_conn 0.961, kBET 0.791, iLISI 0.918, cLISI 0.956, PCR 1.000, Cell_cycle 0.303].\n  - EID 757 (v2b, α=0.7): 0.7251; selected (δ=0.16, kd=18); metrics [0.659, 0.248, 0.724, 0.676, 0.961, 0.791, 0.918, 0.956, 1.000, 0.318].\n  Interpretation: Both < fixed DAQB ridge (~0.733–0.734); iLISI not improved; no label gains.\n  Decision: Close CLIP line as negative on Heart. Keep fixed DAQB (δ=0.15, kd=20) with BRBG(λ=0.7) as recommended; continue cross‑organ ridge map per protocol.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{reply\
    \ 26}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Addendum (CLIP label‑free proxy): Negative on Human Heart\n  We evaluated CLIP (Leiden‑silhouette × batch‑entropy) for label‑free DAQB tuning with fixed EtC embedding and BRBG(λ=0.7). Grid {δ∈{0.14,0.15,0.16}, k_density∈{18,20,22}}; DAQB k=48, cosine; binary + true distances; cap=2.0.\n  - Auto‑CLIP v1b (α=0.5): EID 756 = 0.7236; selected (δ=0.16, kd=18).\n  - Auto‑CLIP v2b (α=0.7): EID 757 = 0.7251; selected (δ=0.16, kd=18).\n  Both are below the fixed DAQB ridge (~0.733–0.734) with no label‑structure gains. Conclusion: CLIP is a negative direction on Heart under this setup. Recommendation remains unchanged: fixed DAQB (δ=0.15, kd=20) with BRBG(λ=0.7).\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 2}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Auto‑CLIP (label‑free DAQB tuner) — negative on Heart:\n  - v1b (α=0.5): EID 756 = 0.7236; picked (δ=0.16, kd=18).\n  - v2b (α=0.7): EID 757 = 0.7251; picked (δ=0.16, kd=18).\n  Neither improves iLISI nor\
    \ label metrics; both < fixed ridge (~0.733–0.734). Closing CLIP line on Heart.\n  Recommendation unchanged: BRBG(λ=0.7, γ_max=0.74, PCA50) + DAQB(δ=0.15, kd=20, k=48, cosine, binary+true distances, cap=2.0).\n  Cross‑organ validation continues; please contribute entries via the shared ridge template + post EIDs here.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/algorithms/README_daqb_recommended.md}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  DAQB Recommended Pipeline (Human Heart) — Quick Start and Repro Guide\n  (Updated: add Auto‑CLIP negative control)\n\n  Overview\n  - Parsimonious EtC–BRBG + Density‑Adaptive Quota‑Balanced Graph (DAQB).\n  - Parity on current evaluator: ≈0.733–0.734 (e.g., EIDs 687, 709).\n  - Keep binary edges + true distances and strict column balancing (cap=2.0).\n\n  Recommended Configuration (fixed)\n  - EtC embedding (QC only; not for graph): normalize_total(1e4) → log1p; HVGs (Seurat v3, n=2000, batch‑aware); FWPCA α=0.5 → PCA(60) → ComBat\
    \ PCs → obsm['X_emb'].\n  - BRBG: PCA(50) → ridge batch prediction (l2=1e‑3); γ_j = min(0.74, 0.7·R²_j); Zcorr = Z − γ ⊙ Ẑ.\n  - DAQB: k_total=48, cosine, binary connectivities + true distances, cap=2.0; density proxy = distance to 20th NN in Zcorr; f_cross = base ± δ with δ=0.15; even per‑batch quotas; remainder to closest.\n\n  Import\n    import sys; sys.path.append('storage/shared/algorithms')\n    from daqb_recommended import eliminate_batch_effect_fn\n\n  Minimal Label‑Free Grid\n  - Hold: λ_r=0.7, γ_max=0.74; k=48; cosine; FWPCA α=0.5; PCA(60)/PCA(50).\n  - Vary: δ ∈ {0.14, 0.15, 0.16}, k_density ∈ {18, 20, 22}.\n  - Report composite + full vector [ASW_batch, ASW_label, ARI, NMI, Graph_conn, kBET, iLISI, cLISI, PCR, Cell_cycle] + EIDs.\n\n  Diagnostics (label‑free)\n  - f_cross vs local density (distance‑to‑k_density NN in Zcorr); inbound‑degree per batch; cap utilization (cap=2.0 ~10–20% typical).\n  - See storage/shared/diagnostics/{daqb_diagnostics.py, daqb_auto_heuristics.py}.\n\
    \n  Negative Controls (Human Heart)\n  - Proportional per‑batch quotas (DAQB‑pQ; softmax on first‑NN distances):\n    • β=2.0 → EID 726 = 0.7261; iLISI 0.842 (↓), ASW_label 0.248 (no gain).\n    • β=1.0 → EID 727 = 0.7252; iLISI 0.896 (↓), ASW_label 0.248.\n  - Auto‑CLIP (Leiden‑silhouette × batch‑entropy) label‑free tuning:\n    • v1b α=0.5 → EID 756 = 0.7236 (picked δ=0.16, kd=18).\n    • v2b α=0.7 → EID 757 = 0.7251 (picked δ=0.16, kd=18).\n    Conclusion: reduces or fails to improve mixing/preservation; below ridge; not recommended.\n  - Geometry gates / hard candidate filtering (EIDs 701, 702 ~0.697); global‑budget recentering (EID 629 ~0.720); heavy embedding equalizations; Gaussian edge weights (EID 505 ~0.673).\n\n  Key EIDs\n  - Fixed: 687 ≈ 0.7337; replication 709 ≈ 0.7339. Label‑free Auto‑GHS: 693/699 ≈ 0.7361. Negatives: 505, 629, 701/702, 726/727, 756/757.\n\n  Contribute Cross‑Organ Results\n  - Use the template + guide:\n    • storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entry_template.yaml\n\
    \    • storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/README.md\n  - Save entries under storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/ and post EIDs + full vectors in Public Memory (#2). We will aggregate and publish an organ‑wise ridge map.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Protocol: Cross‑organ Validation and Reporting for DAQB (EtC–BRBG + Density‑Adaptive Balanced Graph)\"\ntags: \"protocol, reproducibility, single-cell, batch integration, graph, diagnostics\"\nabstract: |\n  This protocol standardizes validation of the DAQB pipeline across organs. It fixes preprocessing and graph configurations, defines a minimal label‑free grid over (δ, k_density), specifies strict reporting order for the 10 metrics, and lists required diagnostics. Shared templates and an aggregator script enable uniform submissions and a compiled ridge map.\nsource_private: 30\n```"
