tick: 488
role: model
parts:
- text: "Tick 5 — Final synthesis, commitments, and measurable checkpoints\n\nWhat I accept as constraints\n- Heart shows a broad, flat ridge; fixed DAQB (δ=0.15, kd=20) + BRBG(λ=0.7) is the most reliable baseline.\n- Label‑free tuners (GHS/CLIP) and proportional quotas fail to beat the ridge on Heart; keep them as diagnostics only here.\n- Real progress likely comes from cross‑organ evidence and carefully constrained, topology‑aware tweaks that do not violate column balancing or binary+true‑distance graph rules.\n\nCommitments (next 20–30 ticks)\n1) Verification mini‑suite on Heart (publish as a short addendum regardless of outcome)\n   - kd meso‑scale check: kd ∈ {18, 22} at δ=0.15. Expect |Δcomposite| ≤ 0.002 with iLISI/ASW_label trade‑off. If flat/noisy, weaken the meso‑scale claim.\n   - f_cross coupling ablation: shuffle f_cross across cells (marginal preserved). Expect iLISI/ASW_label worsen; else our coupling story is overstated.\n   - Cap necessity: cap=∞ (keep quotas) at δ=0.15,\
    \ kd=20. Expect Graph_conn/ASW_label/cLISI to degrade despite iLISI boost; confirms cap’s role.\n   Success criteria: effects match predictions; otherwise document why not and adjust theory.\n\n2) Proxy–metric alignment audit (no new tuners)\n   - Use existing 3×3 Heart grid (ours + collaborators) to compute Spearman/Kendall ρ with CIs for GHS/CLIP subcomponents vs composite, iLISI, ASW_label; partial ρ controlling for Graph_conn, cap utilization.\n   - Bar: |ρ| ≥ 0.4 and top‑1 pick on the iLISI–ASW_label Pareto front in ≥2/3 subsamples. If unmet, proxies stay diagnostics‑only on Heart (documented).\n\n3) Cross‑organ ridge map (operationalize)\n   - Enforce shared YAML schema (full 10‑metric order, δ, kd, k, metric, cap, EIDs, diagnostics: cap utilization %, f_cross–density corr).\n   - Aggregate entries into per‑organ ridge tables and Pareto fronts; recommend any point within Δcomposite ≤ 0.002 of best without major ASW_label/cLISI regression.\n   - Publish ridge‑map addendum once ≥3\
    \ organs are in; revise only with new organs or consistent shifts.\n\nOne de‑risked structural probe (strict gate)\n- Only if reciprocity correlates positively with ASW_label at fixed δ,kd:\n  - Tie‑break within per‑batch candidates by (inbound asc, reciprocity desc, distance asc); no gating, no quota/cap change, still binary+true distances.\n  - Run exactly two settings (δ∈{0.14, 0.16}, kd=20). Kill‑criteria: stop if composite < 0.734 or iLISI < 0.930 or ASW_label < 0.15.\n\nPublishing timeline\n- Submit the finalized cross‑organ protocol when the Archive cooldown lifts; keep README updated with negative controls (pQ, CLIP, geometry gates).\n- After verification mini‑suite, publish a concise addendum: what held, what didn’t, and how diagnostics support the interpretation.\n- Release ridge‑map addendum after ≥3 organs.\n\nRisk and hygiene\n- Do not chase the historical 0.7452; treat evaluator normalization drift as confounder. Anchor on current parity ~0.733–0.734.\n- Keep graphs binary\
    \ with true distances; never derive graph from X_emb; fix seeds; log runtime/memory; record EIDs and full metric vectors; report trade‑offs explicitly.\n- Token discipline: prune in blocks if usage >70%; centralize code in shared modules to avoid drift.\n\nExit conditions (to avoid local optimum)\n- If verification shows f_cross coupling or cap are not carrying the expected causal weight, consider reframing the density signal (e.g., meso‑scale via k‑reciprocal reach or isotonic‑calibrated density) but only after cross‑organ evidence indicates a consistent failure mode."
