parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Verification: f_cross shuffle ablation (δ=0.15, kd=20) + BRBG(λ=0.7)\"\ntags: \"verification, daqb, coupling-ablation, residualization, single-cell\"\nabstract: \"Test whether density coupling drives performance: compute f_cross as usual for δ=0.15, kd=20, then randomly permute it across cells (preserving marginal). Expect iLISI and/or ASW_label to worsen if coupling is causal. BRBG fixed (λ=0.7, γ_max=0.74, PCA50); graph binary with true distances; k=48, cosine; quotas preserved; cap=2.0.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n  # --- Utilities ---\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum,\
    \ inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      n = batches.shape[0]\n      B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      return B @ W\n\n  def _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dists, n):\n      from scipy import sparse as sp\n      A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      D = sp.coo_matrix((np.asarray(dists,\
    \ dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      A = A.maximum(A.T); D = D.maximum(D.T)\n      A.eliminate_zeros(); D.eliminate_zeros()\n      return A, D\n\n  # --- DAQB builder with f_cross shuffle (preserve marginal) ---\n  def _build_daqb_shuffle(Zcorr: np.ndarray, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine',\n                          delta=0.15, k_density=20, cap=2.0, rng_seed=0):\n      from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n      Z = np.asarray(Zcorr, dtype=np.float32, order='C')\n      n = Z.shape[0]\n      batches = np.asarray(batches)\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      nB = len(cats)\n      base_cross = (nB - 1) / float(nB)\n      L, U = 0.60, 0.90\n      rng = np.random.default_rng(rng_seed)\n\n      # Density proxy and original f_cross\n      nn_all = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n      nn_all.fit(Z)\n      d_all, _ = nn_all.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n      d_k = d_all[:, -1]\n      d_min,\
    \ d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n      inv_dense = 1.0 - (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n      f_cross = np.clip(base_cross + (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * delta, L, U)\n\n      # Shuffle f_cross across cells (preserve marginal distribution)\n      idx = rng.permutation(n)\n      f_cross_shuf = f_cross[idx]\n\n      q_cross_tot = np.rint(f_cross_shuf * k_total).astype(int)\n      q_within_tot = k_total - q_cross_tot\n      B_other = max(nB - 1, 1)\n\n      # Neighbor list sizes\n      k_within_max = int(np.ceil((1.0 - L) * k_total))\n      k_cross_per_max = int(np.ceil(U * k_total / B_other))\n      k_max = max(k_within_max, k_cross_per_max) + 1\n\n      # Per-batch neighbor models\n      cat2code = {c: i for i, c in enumerate(cats)}\n      codes = np.array([cat2code[b] for b in batches], dtype=int)\n      nn_models, train_idx = {}, {}\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          mask = (batches == c)\n          train_idx[j] = np.where(mask)[0]\n       \
    \   m = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_max, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n          m.fit(Z[mask])\n          nn_models[j] = m\n\n      dists, idx_local = {}, {}\n      for j in range(nB):\n          d, ii = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n          dists[j] = d; idx_local[j] = ii\n\n      inbound = np.zeros(n, dtype=np.int32)\n      cap_thr = int(np.ceil(cap * k_total))\n      rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n\n      for i in range(n):\n          bi = codes[i]\n          q_within = int(q_within_tot[i])\n          q_cross_total = int(q_cross_tot[i])\n          other = [j for j in range(nB) if j != bi]\n\n          if q_cross_total > 0 and len(other) > 0:\n              scores = np.array([dists[j][i][0] for j in other], dtype=np.float32)\n              order_batches = np.argsort(scores)\n              q_per = q_cross_total // len(other)\n              rem = q_cross_total - q_per * len(other)\n              q_map = {j: q_per for j in other}\n              for k in\
    \ range(rem):\n                  q_map[other[order_batches[k % len(other)]]] += 1\n          else:\n              q_map = {j: 0 for j in other}\n\n          # Within-batch\n          d_w = dists[bi][i]; ii_w = idx_local[bi][i]\n          start_w = 1 if d_w[0] == 0.0 else 0\n          globals_w = train_idx[bi][ii_w[start_w:]]\n          cand_inb = inbound[globals_w]; cand_dst = d_w[start_w:]\n          order = np.lexsort((cand_dst, cand_inb))\n          taken = 0\n          for idx2 in order:\n              g = int(globals_w[idx2])\n              if inbound[g] >= cap_thr: continue\n              rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx2]))\n              inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n              if taken >= q_within: break\n          if taken < q_within:\n              for idx2 in order:\n                  g = int(globals_w[idx2])\n                  if inbound[g] < cap_thr: continue\n                  rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx2]))\n\
    \                  inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n                  if taken >= q_within: break\n\n          # Cross-batch\n          for j in other:\n              qj = q_map[j]\n              if qj <= 0: continue\n              d_c = dists[j][i]; ii_c = idx_local[j][i]\n              globals_c = train_idx[j][ii_c]\n              cand_inb = inbound[globals_c]; cand_dst = d_c\n              order = np.lexsort((cand_dst, cand_inb))\n              taken = 0\n              for idx2 in order:\n                  g = int(globals_c[idx2])\n                  if inbound[g] >= cap_thr: continue\n                  rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx2]))\n                  inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n                  if taken >= qj: break\n              if taken < qj:\n                  for idx2 in order:\n                      g = int(globals_c[idx2])\n                      if inbound[g] < cap_thr: continue\n                      rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx2]))\n\
    \                      inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n                      if taken >= qj: break\n\n      A_sym, D_sym = _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(\n          np.array(rows, np.int32), np.array(cols, np.int32), np.array(dvals, np.float32), n\n      )\n      return A_sym.astype(np.float32), D_sym.astype(np.float32)\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Config (reference δ,kd; shuffle ablation only)\n      n_pcs_emb = 60\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma_max = 0.74\n      lam = 0.7\n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      delta = 0.15\n      k_density = 20\n      cap = 2.0\n      alpha_var = 0.5\n      emb_n_neighbors = 15\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n\
    \      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      # EtC embedding (QC only)\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw = Xd * wv\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      Z_emb = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n      # Graph path\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0,\
    \ ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      Cg, Dg = _build_daqb_shuffle(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                   k_total=k_total, metric=metric, delta=delta, k_density=k_density, cap=cap, rng_seed=0)\n      print(f\"[Ablation f_cross shuffle] delta={delta}, k_density={k_density}, cap={cap}\")\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      return adata\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Verification: No inbound cap (cap→∞) at δ=0.15, kd=20 + BRBG(λ=0.7)\"\ntags: \"verification, daqb, column-balancing, residualization, single-cell\"\nabstract: \"Test column-balancing cap necessity: use δ=0.15, kd=20, but disable inbound cap (simulate cap→∞) while preserving per-cell quotas and even per-batch split. Expect iLISI to rise\
    \ but Graph_conn and ASW_label/cLISI to degrade if cap guards against over-hub formation.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      n = batches.shape[0]\n      B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n\
    \          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      return B @ W\n\n  def _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dists, n):\n      A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      D = sp.coo_matrix((np.asarray(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      A = A.maximum(A.T); D = D.maximum(D.T)\n      A.eliminate_zeros(); D.eliminate_zeros()\n      return A, D\n\n  def _build_daqb_no_cap(Zcorr: np.ndarray, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine',\n                         delta=0.15, k_density=20, rng_seed=0):\n      Z = np.asarray(Zcorr, dtype=np.float32, order='C')\n      n = Z.shape[0]\n      batches = np.asarray(batches)\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      nB = len(cats)\n      base_cross = (nB -\
    \ 1) / float(nB)\n      L, U = 0.60, 0.90\n\n      nn_all = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n      nn_all.fit(Z)\n      d_all, _ = nn_all.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n      d_k = d_all[:, -1]\n      d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n      inv_dense = 1.0 - (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n      f_cross = np.clip(base_cross + (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * delta, L, U)\n\n      q_cross_tot = np.rint(f_cross * k_total).astype(int)\n      q_within_tot = k_total - q_cross_tot\n      B_other = max(nB - 1, 1)\n\n      k_within_max = int(np.ceil((1.0 - L) * k_total))\n      k_cross_per_max = int(np.ceil(U * k_total / B_other))\n      k_max = max(k_within_max, k_cross_per_max) + 1\n\n      cat2code = {c: i for i, c in enumerate(cats)}\n      codes = np.array([cat2code[b] for b in batches], dtype=int)\n      nn_models, train_idx = {}, {}\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          mask = (batches == c)\n  \
    \        train_idx[j] = np.where(mask)[0]\n          m = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_max, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n          m.fit(Z[mask])\n          nn_models[j] = m\n\n      dists, idx_local = {}, {}\n      for j in range(nB):\n          d, ii = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n          dists[j] = d; idx_local[j] = ii\n\n      inbound = np.zeros(n, dtype=np.int32)\n      rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n\n      for i in range(n):\n          bi = codes[i]\n          q_within = int(q_within_tot[i])\n          q_cross_total = int(q_cross_tot[i])\n          other = [j for j in range(nB) if j != bi]\n\n          if q_cross_total > 0 and len(other) > 0:\n              scores = np.array([dists[j][i][0] for j in other], dtype=np.float32)\n              order_batches = np.argsort(scores)\n              q_per = q_cross_total // len(other)\n              rem = q_cross_total - q_per * len(other)\n              q_map = {j: q_per for j in other}\n              for\
    \ k in range(rem):\n                  q_map[other[order_batches[k % len(other)]]] += 1\n          else:\n              q_map = {j: 0 for j in other}\n\n          # Within-batch (no cap check)\n          d_w = dists[bi][i]; ii_w = idx_local[bi][i]\n          start_w = 1 if d_w[0] == 0.0 else 0\n          globals_w = train_idx[bi][ii_w[start_w:]]\n          cand_dst = d_w[start_w:]\n          order = np.argsort(cand_dst)\n          taken = 0\n          for idx2 in order:\n              g = int(globals_w[idx2])\n              rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx2]))\n              inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n              if taken >= q_within: break\n\n          # Cross-batch per other batch (no cap check)\n          for j in other:\n              qj = q_map[j]\n              if qj <= 0: continue\n              d_c = dists[j][i]; ii_c = idx_local[j][i]\n              globals_c = train_idx[j][ii_c]\n              cand_dst = d_c\n              order = np.argsort(cand_dst)\n\
    \              taken = 0\n              for idx2 in order:\n                  g = int(globals_c[idx2])\n                  rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx2]))\n                  inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n                  if taken >= qj: break\n\n      A_sym, D_sym = _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(\n          np.array(rows, np.int32), np.array(cols, np.int32), np.array(dvals, np.float32), Z.shape[0]\n      )\n      return A_sym.astype(np.float32), D_sym.astype(np.float32)\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Config (reference δ,kd; cap removed)\n      n_pcs_emb = 60\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma_max = 0.74\n      lam = 0.7\n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      delta = 0.15\n      k_density = 20\n      alpha_var = 0.5\n      emb_n_neighbors = 15\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n\
    \      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      # EtC embedding (QC only)\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw = Xd * wv\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      Z_emb = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n      # Graph path\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xd,\
    \ n_comps=50, random_state=0)\n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=1e-3)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma = np.minimum(0.74, 0.7 * R2)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      Cg, Dg = _build_daqb_no_cap(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                  k_total=k_total, metric=metric, delta=delta, k_density=k_density, rng_seed=0)\n      print(f\"[Ablation no-cap] delta={delta}, k_density={k_density}, cap=None (disabled)\")\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      return adata\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Verification mini‑suite: kd sweep, f_cross shuffle, and cap removal — acceptance & logging\"\ntags: \"plan, verification, diagnostics\"\ncontent: |\n  Verification\
    \ runs (Heart; BRBG λ=0.7, γ_max=0.74, PCA50; DAQB k=48, cosine; binary+true distances):\n  - kd sweep: kd=18 (EID 765), kd=22 (EID 766) at δ=0.15. Expect |Δcomposite| ≤ 0.002 vs kd=20; iLISI/ASW_label trade-off.\n  - f_cross shuffle at δ=0.15, kd=20 (submitted): Expect iLISI and/or ASW_label to worsen if density coupling is causal.\n  - No inbound cap at δ=0.15, kd=20 (submitted): Expect iLISI↑ but Graph_conn and ASW_label/cLISI degrade.\n  Acceptance:\n  - Record full metric vectors and interpret diagnostic expectations explicitly; publish short addendum regardless of outcome.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Ensuring code accuracy**\n\nI want to ensure the code replicates baseline enforcements and safe modifications. I’m planning to compute the Spearman correlation of proxies versus metrics, but the station doesn’t easily provide access to metrics for arbitrary grid runs. I think analyzing previously computed EIDs and metrics might work, though the code can’t access evaluation results. So, I’ll aim to write a shared script to aggregate EIDs versus metrics. For now, I'll proceed with experiments while defining acceptance criteria. I'll also submit evaluation codes and create a logging entry for next steps.**Preparing verification code**\n\nI need to craft code for \"Verification: f_cross shuffle coupling ablation (δ=0.15, kd=20),\" ensuring the builder computes f_cross as usual and randomly permutes across cells. I’ll print the chosen experiment settings as I go. For the \"Verification: cap removal,\" I'll set cap_thr to a very large value to avoid checking inbound connections.\
  \ I must check that the code compiles in the environment and follows the same import pattern as before. \n\nI'll also maintain consistency in using the function to build neighbor models and include prints to STDOUT. Let's prepare two submissions with appropriate titles and code!**Adjusting test parameters**\n\nFor the second test, I need to ensure the inbound cap is effectively disabled. I’ll modify the selection loops to skip the inbound cap check, so it doesn’t restrict how high the inbound value can go. That’s intended, but I’ll keep the fallback loops just in case. I’m also wondering if we should adjust the acceptance criteria since iLISI might increase. In my earlier predictions, cap removal showed an increase in iLISI, but some other metrics degraded. I'll include minimal comments in the code and produce the two submissions while aiming to reduce runtime by using 'algorithm=brute'. Let's create the entries for submission!"
