parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 491\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis II\n- Agent Description: Parsimonious, hypothesis-driven scRNA integration researcher focused on robust ablations, reproducibility, and steady breakthroughs.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nPraxis II — Meta/TODO (updated)\nGoals:\n- Maintain a parsimonious, reproducible SOTA for Human Heart: BRBG(λ=0.7, γ_max=0.74, PCA50) + DAQB(δ=0.15, k_density=20, k=48, cosine, binary+true distances, cap=2.0).\n- Publish clear analyses; avoid micro‑tuning without hypotheses; promote cross‑organ validation via protocol and shared modules.\nOpen loops:\n- Cross‑organ validation: collect EIDs + full metric vectors per protocol; maintain an organ‑wise ridge map (δ×k_density).\n- Auto‑EtC thresholds remain fixed at target_sum=1e4 unless cross‑organ evidence suggests changes.\n- Close lines: proportional per‑batch quotas (DAQB‑pQ) — negative (EIDs 726, 727).\nGuardrails:\n- Keep\
    \ graphs binary + true distances; never build graph on X_emb; report all EIDs; document trade‑offs.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 130,036 / 270,000 used (48%)\n- Agent Age: 199 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Verification: DAQB kd=22 (δ=0.15) + BRBG(λ=0.7) — meso-scale check' (ID: 766) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 0.7147844905866315\n**ASW_batch:** 0.659\n**ASW_label:** 0.248\n**ARI:** 0.642\n**NMI:** 0.640\n**Graph_conn:** 0.961\n**kBET:** 0.789\n**iLISI:** 0.918\n**cLISI:** 0.956\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.335\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.659  ASW_label: 0.248  ARI: 0.642  NMI: 0.640\n  Graph_conn: 0.961  kBET: 0.789  iLISI: 0.918  cLISI: 0.956\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.335\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.830496  ASW_label: 0.555112  ARI: 0.642303  NMI: 0.639765\n  Graph_conn: 0.961218  kBET: 0.752392  iLISI: 0.917918\
    \  cLISI: 0.987148\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.294795\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n[Verification kd-sweep] delta=0.15, k_density=22, cap=2.0\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/62587143-ef26-4c48-b7b5-631ce1f4a826/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 62587143-ef26-4c48-b7b5-631ce1f4a826\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Verification: DAQB kd=18 (δ=0.15) + BRBG(λ=0.7) — meso-scale check' (ID: 765) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 0.7241577629667539\n**ASW_batch:** 0.659\n**ASW_label:** 0.248\n**ARI:** 0.725\n**NMI:** 0.676\n**Graph_conn:** 0.961\n**kBET:** 0.790\n**iLISI:** 0.918\n**cLISI:** 0.956\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:**\
    \ 0.309\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.659  ASW_label: 0.248  ARI: 0.725  NMI: 0.676\n  Graph_conn: 0.961  kBET: 0.790  iLISI: 0.918  cLISI: 0.956\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.309\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.830496  ASW_label: 0.555112  ARI: 0.724990  NMI: 0.676213\n  Graph_conn: 0.961218  kBET: 0.753592  iLISI: 0.917918  cLISI: 0.987116\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.272166\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n[Verification kd-sweep] delta=0.15, k_density=18, cap=2.0\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/51b1adc0-0840-4b7c-b2e5-2f0fd44210a8/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 51b1adc0-0840-4b7c-b2e5-2f0fd44210a8\n\
    \n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n3. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n4. `create` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Submission failed: You have reached the maximum limit of 2 concurrent pending evaluations. Your current pending/running evaluations are: 765, 766. Please wait for these to complete before submitting new ones.\n- Submission failed: You have reached the maximum limit of 2 concurrent pending evaluations. Your current pending/running evaluations are: 765, 766. Please wait for these to complete before submitting new ones.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq\
    \ Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 609 | 1 | EtC–BRBG(lam=0.7) + Density-Adaptive BBSG (δ=0.15, k_density=20): Sensitivity | Praxis II | 366 | 0.7452 | 0.760 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.440 | 0.946 | 0.711 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.789 |\n| 614 | 1 | Aether II Synergy: EtC(FWPCA α=0.25) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) + Density-Adaptive BBSG... | Aether II | 368 | 0.7435 | 0.735 | 0.674 | 0.123 | 0.486 | 0.971 | 0.700 | 1.000 | 0.971 | 0.933 | 0.843 |\n| 533 | 1 | Aether II SOTA Optimization: EtC(FWPCA α=0.25) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) | Aether II | 314 | 0.7434 | 0.738 | 0.674 | 0.123 | 0.477 | 0.972 | 0.701\
    \ | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.842 |\n| 550 | 1 | Sophia II: Synergy Exp 2 - FWPCA-EtC Embedding (alpha=0.5) + SOTA BRBG Graph (lam=0.7) | Sophia II | 324 | 0.7427 | 0.738 | 0.664 | 0.111 | 0.475 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.860 |\n| 523 | 1 | Sophia II: Replication - Daedalus III's EtC SOTA (ID 488) v3 (Praxis Common Lib Fixes) | Sophia II | 310 | 0.7423 | 0.738 | 0.648 | 0.149 | 0.458 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.850 |\n| 516 | 1 | Logos III: Novel 'Refinement Architecture' Test (alpha=0.1) | Logos III | 307 | 0.7422 | 0.738 | 0.648 | 0.149 | 0.458 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.849 |\n| 539 | 1 | Aether II FWPCA Re-evaluation: EtC(FWPCA α=0.25) + Sophia II SOTA (ID 523) Fixes | Aether II | 317 | 0.7420 | 0.738 | 0.674 | 0.123 | 0.462 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.843 |\n| 520 | 1 | Aether II SOTA Optimization: EtC(FWPCA α=1.0) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) | Aether II | 309 | 0.7418 | 0.738 | 0.646 | 0.100 | 0.498 | 0.972\
    \ | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.858 |\n| 557 | 1 | Sophia II: Synergy Exp 4 - FWPCA-EtC Embedding (alpha=1.0) + SOTA BRBG Graph (lam=0.7) | Sophia II | 328 | 0.7418 | 0.738 | 0.645 | 0.100 | 0.498 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.857 |\n| 515 | 1 | Aether II Synergy: EtC(FWPCA α=0.5) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) | Aether II | 307 | 0.7414 | 0.738 | 0.664 | 0.111 | 0.463 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.859 |\n\nPage 1 of 77 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-77, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Successfully created capsule #35 ('Verification mini‑suite: kd sweep, f_cross shuffle, and cap removal — acceptance & logging'). Full ID: Praxis_private_35\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Pinned Capsules**\n\
    | ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 13 | Archive Outline (Private Draft): Robustness of EtC–BRBG–BBSG on Human Heart | Praxis II | Tick 329 | 1118 | 5 | (All Read) |\n| 12 | Draft Analysis: Why Praxis defaults are robust (tick316) | Praxis II | Tick 317 | 1277 | 9 | (All Read) |\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 4)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 35 | Verification mini‑suite: kd sweep, f_cross shuffle, and cap removal — acceptance & logging | Praxis II | Tick 490 | 81 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 34 | Auto‑CLIP (v1b/v2b) results and close‑out | Praxis II | Tick 487 | 102 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 33 | Draft (Archive): Label‑Free Graph Tuning for DAQB on Human Heart — Methods (explicit formulas) and Results plan | Praxis II | Tick 479 | 1177 | 2 | (All\
    \ Read) |\n| 32 | Plan: GHS v5 (directed diagnostics + target adherence) — experiments after 738/739 finish | Praxis II | Tick 476 | 169 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 31 | Archive timing + ridge map next steps | Praxis II | Tick 470 | 80 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 30 | Protocol (Draft): Cross‑organ Validation and Reporting for DAQB (EtC–BRBG + Density‑Adaptive Balanced Graph) | Praxis II | Tick 469 | 420 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 29 | Cross‑organ Ridge Map: Data collection schema and checklist | Praxis II | Tick 467 | 163 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 28 | DAQB‑pQ (β=2.0, β=1.0) experiment plan and acceptance criteria | Praxis II | Tick 461 | 312 | 3 | (All Read) |\n| 27 | Draft: Embedding Normalization Sensitivity — Full Methods and Results Outline | Praxis II | Tick 451 | 533 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 26 | Plan for revised Archive: full methods + normalization sensitivity (>=5 experiments) | Praxis II | Tick 450 | 114 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-4.)\n\n\n---\n\
    \n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
