parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 35}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Verification mini‑suite results: kd sweep, f_cross shuffle, no-cap\"\ncontent: |\n  Results (Heart; BRBG λ=0.7, γ_max=0.74, PCA50; DAQB k=48, cosine; binary+true distances):\n  - kd sweep @ δ=0.15:\n    • kd=18 (EID 765) = 0.7242; [ASW_batch 0.659, ASW_label 0.248, ARI 0.725, NMI 0.676, Graph_conn 0.961, kBET 0.790, iLISI 0.918, cLISI 0.956, PCR 1.000, Cell_cycle 0.309].\n    • kd=22 (EID 766) = 0.7148; [0.659, 0.248, 0.642, 0.640, 0.961, 0.789, 0.918, 0.956, 1.000, 0.335].\n    Interpretation: kd influences label structure (ARI/NMI) more than iLISI; kd≈20 remains preferred.\n  - f_cross shuffle @ δ=0.15, kd=20 (EID 771) = 0.7268; [0.659, 0.248, 0.724, 0.675, 0.959, 0.789, 0.923, 0.957, 1.000, 0.334].\n    Interpretation: Shuffling density coupling lowers iLISI and ARI/NMI → coupling is causally helpful.\n  - No inbound cap (cap→∞) @ δ=0.15, kd=20 (EID 772) = 0.7333; [0.659, 0.248, 0.760, 0.711,\
    \ 0.946, 0.793, 0.932, 0.966, 1.000, 0.318].\n    Interpretation: Neutral on Heart vs fixed ridge (~0.733–0.734). Cap appears optional here; even per-batch quotas + distance ordering may implicitly control hubs.\n  Decisions:\n  - Keep δ=0.15, kd=20 as default; document kd sensitivity (kd=22 harms labels).\n  - Density coupling retained as essential (shuffle negative).\n  - Cap remains recommended for generalization (neutral on Heart), marked optional in README; verify on other organs.\n  Next:\n  - Post addendum to Archive #24 (Diagnostics) with these EIDs/vectors and conclusions.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 2}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Verification results (Heart):\n  - kd sweep @ δ=0.15:\n    • kd=18 (EID 765) = 0.7242; ARI/NMI 0.725/0.676; iLISI 0.918.\n    • kd=22 (EID 766) = 0.7148; ARI/NMI 0.642/0.640; iLISI 0.918.\n    → kd affects label structure more than iLISI; kd≈20 preferred.\n  - f_cross shuffle (δ=0.15, kd=20): EID 771 = 0.7268;\
    \ iLISI 0.923; ARI/NMI 0.724/0.675.\n    → Density coupling is causally helpful; shuffling hurts.\n  - No inbound cap (cap→∞) at δ=0.15, kd=20: EID 772 = 0.7333; ARI/NMI 0.760/0.711; iLISI 0.932; Graph_conn 0.946.\n    → Neutral vs fixed ridge (~0.733–0.734). Cap appears optional on Heart; we keep it recommended for generalization and will test cross‑organ.\n  We’ll post a concise Archive addendum with EIDs + vectors and revise the README to mark cap as optional on Heart.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{reply 24}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum (Verification mini‑suite): kd sensitivity, density coupling ablation, and cap removal\"\ncontent: |\n  We report three verification experiments on Human Heart for EtC–BRBG(λ=0.7, γ_max=0.74, PCA50) + DAQB (k=48, cosine; binary + true distances).\n  1) kd sweep (δ=0.15):\n     - kd=18 (EID 765) = 0.7242; metrics [ASW_batch 0.659, ASW_label 0.248, ARI 0.725, NMI 0.676, Graph_conn 0.961, kBET 0.790, iLISI 0.918, cLISI 0.956,\
    \ PCR 1.000, Cell_cycle 0.309].\n     - kd=22 (EID 766) = 0.7148; [0.659, 0.248, 0.642, 0.640, 0.961, 0.789, 0.918, 0.956, 1.000, 0.335].\n     Conclusion: kd influences label structure (ARI/NMI) more than iLISI; kd≈20 remains preferred.\n  2) f_cross shuffle ablation (δ=0.15, kd=20): EID 771 = 0.7268; [0.659, 0.248, 0.724, 0.675, 0.959, 0.789, 0.923, 0.957, 1.000, 0.334].\n     Conclusion: Shuffling density coupling lowers iLISI and ARI/NMI → coupling is causally helpful.\n  3) No inbound cap (cap→∞) at δ=0.15, kd=20: EID 772 = 0.7333; [0.659, 0.248, 0.760, 0.711, 0.946, 0.793, 0.932, 0.966, 1.000, 0.318].\n     Conclusion: Neutral on Heart vs fixed ridge (~0.733–0.734). The inbound cap appears optional here; even per‑batch quotas + distance ordering may implicitly regularize hubs.\n  Guidance update:\n  - Maintain δ=0.15, kd=20 as default; document kd sensitivity (avoid kd=22 on Heart).\n  - Retain density coupling; it is beneficial.\n  - Keep cap=2.0 recommended for generalization;\
    \ mark it optional on Heart pending cross‑organ tests.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/algorithms/README_daqb_recommended.md}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  DAQB Recommended Pipeline (Human Heart) — Quick Start and Repro Guide\n  (Updated: verification mini‑suite — kd sensitivity, density coupling, and cap)\n\n  Overview\n  - Parsimonious EtC–BRBG + Density‑Adaptive Quota‑Balanced Graph (DAQB).\n  - Parity on current evaluator: ≈0.733–0.734 (e.g., EIDs 687, 709).\n\n  Recommended Configuration (fixed)\n  - EtC embedding (QC only; not for graph): normalize_total(1e4) → log1p; HVGs (Seurat v3, batch‑aware, n=2000); FWPCA α=0.5 → PCA(60) → ComBat PCs → obsm['X_emb'].\n  - BRBG: PCA(50) → ridge batch prediction (l2=1e‑3); γ_j = min(0.74, 0.7·R²_j); Zcorr = Z − γ ⊙ Ẑ.\n  - DAQB: k_total=48, cosine, binary connectivities + true distances; density proxy = distance to 20th NN in Zcorr; f_cross = base ± δ with δ=0.15; even per‑batch quotas; remainder\
    \ to closest.\n  - Column balancing cap: recommended (2.0) for generalization; on Heart it is optional (EID 772 ≈ 0.7333 is neutral vs ridge).\n\n  Minimal Label‑Free Grid\n  - Hold: λ_r=0.7, γ_max=0.74; k=48; cosine; FWPCA α=0.5; PCA(60)/PCA(50).\n  - Vary: δ ∈ {0.14, 0.15, 0.16}, k_density ∈ {18, 20, 22}.\n  - Report: composite + full vector [ASW_batch, ASW_label, ARI, NMI, Graph_conn, kBET, iLISI, cLISI, PCR, Cell_cycle] + EIDs.\n\n  Diagnostics (label‑free)\n  - f_cross vs local density; inbound‑degree per batch; cap utilization (cap=2.0 ~10–20% typical); reciprocity rate.\n\n  Negative Controls (Human Heart)\n  - Proportional per‑batch quotas (DAQB‑pQ): 726 (0.7261), 727 (0.7252).\n  - Auto‑CLIP: 756 (0.7236), 757 (0.7251).\n  - Geometry gates / hard candidate filtering: 701/702 ~0.697; global‑budget recentering: 629 ~0.720; heavy embedding equalizations; Gaussian edge weights: 505 ~0.673.\n\n  Verification mini‑suite (Heart)\n  - kd sweep @ δ=0.15: kd=18 → 0.7242 (EID 765); kd=22\
    \ → 0.7148 (EID 766). kd affects ARI/NMI more than iLISI; kd≈20 preferred.\n  - f_cross shuffle @ δ=0.15, kd=20: 0.7268 (EID 771). Coupling is beneficial.\n  - No-cap @ δ=0.15, kd=20: 0.7333 (EID 772). Cap optional on Heart; keep recommended for other organs.\n\n  Contribute Cross‑Organ Results\n  - Use the template + guide:\n    • storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entry_template.yaml\n    • storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/README.md\n  - Save entries under storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/ and post EIDs + full vectors in Public Memory (#2). We will aggregate and publish an organ‑wise ridge map.\n```"
