parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/diagnostics/reciprocity_probe.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys, numpy as np\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from scipy.stats import spearmanr\n\n  def _csr_reciprocity(A: sp.csr_matrix):\n      # returns per-node reciprocity rate: |{j: A[i,j]=A[j,i]=1}| / outdeg(i)\n      A = A.tocsr().astype(np.int8)\n      AT = A.T.tocsr()\n      # logical AND via multiplication on {0,1} is not trivial; instead use min on coo overlap\n      # Build symmetric min: M = min(A, AT)\n      M = A.minimum(AT)\n      outdeg = np.asarray(A.sum(axis=1)).ravel()\n      mutual = np.asarray(M.sum(axis=1)).ravel()\n      recip = np.zeros_like(outdeg, dtype=np.float32)\n      mask = outdeg > 0\n      recip[mask] = (mutual[mask] / outdeg[mask]).astype(np.float32)\n      return recip, outdeg\n\n  def _median_neighbor_distance(D: sp.csr_matrix):\n      # median of nonzero distances per row as a label-free\
    \ density proxy (smaller = denser)\n      D = D.tocsr().astype(np.float32)\n      med = np.zeros(D.shape[0], dtype=np.float32)\n      indptr, data = D.indptr, D.data\n      for i in range(D.shape[0]):\n          s, e = indptr[i], indptr[i+1]\n          if e > s:\n              med[i] = np.median(data[s:e]).astype(np.float32)\n      return med\n\n  def _cross_batch_fraction(A: sp.csr_matrix, batches):\n      # per-node fraction of neighbors from a different batch (label-free; uses batch labels)\n      A = A.tocsr()\n      n = A.shape[0]\n      frac = np.zeros(n, dtype=np.float32)\n      indptr, indices = A.indptr, A.indices\n      for i in range(n):\n          s, e = indptr[i], indptr[i+1]\n          if e <= s: \n              frac[i] = 0.0\n              continue\n          nb = indices[s:e]\n          denom = e - s\n          frac[i] = np.sum(batches[nb] != batches[i]) / float(denom)\n      return frac\n\n  def analyze(h5ad_path: str):\n      adata = ad.read_h5ad(h5ad_path)\n      A\
    \ = adata.obsp.get('connectivities', None)\n      D = adata.obsp.get('distances', None)\n      if A is None or D is None:\n          print(f\"[reciprocity_probe] Missing graph in {h5ad_path}\", flush=True); return\n      if 'batch' not in adata.obs:\n          print(f\"[reciprocity_probe] Missing batch labels in {h5ad_path}\", flush=True); return\n      batches = adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').cat.codes.to_numpy()\n\n      recip, outdeg = _csr_reciprocity(A)\n      dens = _median_neighbor_distance(D)  # smaller = denser\n      cbf = _cross_batch_fraction(A, batches)\n\n      # Normalize density so larger = denser for monotone intuition\n      dens_inv = (dens.max() - dens) / (dens.max() - dens.min() + 1e-8)\n\n      # Correlations (Spearman)\n      r_recip_cbf, _ = spearmanr(recip, cbf)\n      r_recip_dens, _ = spearmanr(recip, dens_inv)\n      r_cbf_dens, _  = spearmanr(cbf, dens_inv)\n\n      print(f\"[reciprocity_probe] File: {h5ad_path}\")\n      print(f\"  mean_recip={recip.mean():.4f},\
    \ mean_outdeg={outdeg.mean():.2f}, mean_cbf={cbf.mean():.4f}\")\n      print(f\"  spearman(recip, cross_batch_frac) = {r_recip_cbf:.3f}\")\n      print(f\"  spearman(recip, density_inv)      = {r_recip_dens:.3f}\")\n      print(f\"  spearman(cross_batch_frac, density_inv) = {r_cbf_dens:.3f}\")\n      print(\"  Note: density_inv derived from median neighbor distance; larger = denser.\")\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      if len(sys.argv) < 2:\n          print(\"Usage: python reciprocity_probe.py storage/shared/tmp/<UUID>/result_human.h5ad [more_paths...]\", file=sys.stderr)\n          sys.exit(1)\n      for p in sys.argv[1:]:\n          analyze(p)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/heart_PraxisII_ablation.yaml}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  organ: \"Human Heart\"\n  dataset_notes: \"CELLxGENE Census; ~20k cells × 2k HVGs; 4 batches\"\n  author: \"Praxis II\"\n  agent: \"Praxis II\"\n  date: \"tick 493\"\n  fixed_config:\n    brbg:\n      lambda_r:\
    \ 0.7\n      gamma_max: 0.74\n      pca_graph: 50\n      ridge_l2: 1.0e-3\n    daqb:\n      k_total: 48\n      metric: \"cosine\"\n      cap: 2.0\n      binary_true_distances: true\n    etc_qc:\n      alpha_var: 0.5\n      pca_emb: 60\n      combat: true\n  runs:\n    - delta: 0.15\n      k_density: 20\n      eid: \"771\"\n      composite: 0.7268\n      metrics:\n        ASW_batch: 0.659\n        ASW_label: 0.248\n        ARI: 0.724\n        NMI: 0.675\n        Graph_conn: 0.959\n        kBET: 0.789\n        iLISI: 0.923\n        cLISI: 0.957\n        PCR: 1.000\n        Cell_cycle: 0.334\n      deviations: \"f_cross shuffled across cells (marginal preserved)\"\n    - delta: 0.15\n      k_density: 20\n      eid: \"772\"\n      composite: 0.7333\n      metrics:\n        ASW_batch: 0.659\n        ASW_label: 0.248\n        ARI: 0.760\n        NMI: 0.711\n        Graph_conn: 0.946\n        kBET: 0.793\n        iLISI: 0.932\n        cLISI: 0.966\n        PCR: 1.000\n        Cell_cycle: 0.318\n\
    \      deviations: \"inbound cap disabled (cap→∞); per-batch quotas retained\"\n  diagnostics:\n    corr_fcross_density: null\n    cap_utilization_pct: null\n    inbound_degree_histogram: []\n  deviations: \"see per-run deviations\"\n  notes: \"Density coupling is beneficial (shuffle hurts); cap is optional on Heart but kept recommended for generalization.\"\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 2}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tools + ridge entries:\n  - Added reciprocity_probe to shared diagnostics:\n      storage/shared/diagnostics/reciprocity_probe.py\n    Usage: python reciprocity_probe.py storage/shared/tmp/<UUID>/result_human.h5ad [more...]\n    Reports per-node reciprocity, cross-batch neighbor fraction, and correlations to a label-free density proxy.\n  - Logged Heart ablations to ridge map:\n      storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/heart_PraxisII_ablation.yaml\n    • f_cross shuffle (EID 771) = 0.7268 (hurts iLISI/ARI/NMI) → density coupling\
    \ matters.\n    • no-cap (EID 772) = 0.7333 (neutral vs ridge) → cap optional on Heart; keep recommended for other organs.\n  Cross-organ ask:\n  - Please run kd∈{18,20,22} at δ=0.15 and the no-cap variant once per organ, add YAML entries under ridge_entries/, and post EIDs + full vectors here. If you can, also run reciprocity_probe on your result files and paste the summary.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n\n```yaml\nrecipients: Sophia III\ntitle: \"Quick validation asks: kd sweep + no-cap + reciprocity probe (your organ)\"\ncontent: |\n  Hi Sophia III, thanks for the Auto‑GHS replications. Could you run 4 quick checks on any non‑Heart organ you’re working on (fixed EtC/BRBG; DAQB k=48, cosine; δ=0.15; binary+true distances)?\n  1) kd sweep: k_density ∈ {18, 20, 22}.\n  2) No‑cap variant at kd=20 (disable inbound cap but keep per‑batch quotas).\n  3) Add entries via the shared YAML template:\n       storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/README.md\n\
    \  4) Optional: run reciprocity_probe on your result_human.h5ad (path printed in evaluator logs) and paste the summary.\n  Please post EIDs + full vectors in Public (#2) as well. I’ll aggregate into the ridge map and update the protocol with organ‑wise recommendations.\n```\n\n"
thinking_content: '**Evaluating next steps**


  I think we should consider our actions moving forward, like pushing the archive addendum, updating the README, and logging ridge entries. The user hasn''t asked a clear question; it''s more narrative. I see some results for verification, with various kd values. They’ve already posted an addendum and updated the README. For next steps, we might coordinate with others to run cap ablation, and maybe implement a diagnostic script to check mutual-edge rate, though that might not be necessary.**Proposing diagnostics and protocols**


  I’m considering implementing a small function to compute the reciprocity rate and correlation, possibly adding a test function to print diagnostics. While it’s allowed to override evaluations, it''s generating NaN, which isn’t necessary. I can write a script for shared diagnostics instead. They might also publish a cross-organ protocol to the Archive, but it seems there’s a cooldown preventing that. Back at tick 488, they faced a cooldown issue that needs further investigation. It’s odd to see differing tick counts on cooldown.**Planning next steps**


  I think we should avoid trying to create the Archive again to prevent failure, and instead focus on the cross-organ ridge map script while requesting contributions. We''re still fine with token usage, at 149k out of 270k. We could also submit a small reciprocal tie-break test if we find a correlation signal, although we haven’t computed that yet. Instead of making new structural modifications, I propose creating a diagnostics tool to analyze reciprocity versus ASW_label correlation using previously stored results.**Developing a diagnostic plan**


  I’m thinking about writing a shared diagnostic script to load AnnData files and compute adjacency reciprocals and family metrics, but I’m unsure of the UUID paths, so we could incorporate that as a parameter. Another option is to update the ridge entries by adding ablation entries for shuffle and no-cap, possibly as a separate document in an "ablation" directory. I might also propose emailing Sophia III about testing "cap optional" on other organs. The token usage is currently at 55%, so it doesn''t need pruning right now.**Drafting the reciprocity probe**


  I’m considering posting the EIDs to Public Memory and calling for cross-organ cap ablation to verify if it’s optional. I can implement a script named ''reciprocity_probe.py'' to compute reciprocity rates and Spearman correlation with ASW_label. However, accessing metrics from storage seems tricky since we can’t use cell_type info for integration. It''s safer to lean towards label-free measures. I’ll write the script to load adjacency and compute these metrics, then propose a series of actions including creating diagnostic tools and ridge entries.'
