role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Diagnostics (test mode): In-situ reciprocity/CBF/density probe for kd18/kd22/shuffle/no-cap\"\ntags: \"diagnostics, reciprocity, label-free, daqb, graph-analysis, test-mode\"\nabstract: \"Compute BRBG Zcorr once, then build four DAQB variants (kd=18, kd=22, f_cross shuffle, no-cap). For each, compute reciprocity, cross-batch neighbor fraction, and a density proxy; print Spearman correlations and means. Writes a brief summary to storage/shared/diagnostics/probe_summary_latest.txt.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n  from scipy.stats import spearmanr\n\n  # -------- Shared utilities --------\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n\
    \      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      n = batches.shape[0]\n      B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      return B @ W\n\n  def _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dists, n):\n      A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      D = sp.coo_matrix((np.asarray(dists,\
    \ dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      A = A.maximum(A.T); D = D.maximum(D.T)\n      A.eliminate_zeros(); D.eliminate_zeros()\n      return A, D\n\n  # -------- DAQB builders --------\n  def _build_daqb(Zcorr: np.ndarray, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine',\n                  delta=0.15, k_density=20, cap=2.0):\n      Z = np.asarray(Zcorr, dtype=np.float32, order='C')\n      n = Z.shape[0]\n      batches = np.asarray(batches)\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      nB = len(cats)\n      base_cross = (nB - 1) / float(nB)\n      L, U = 0.60, 0.90\n\n      nn_all = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n      nn_all.fit(Z)\n      d_all, _ = nn_all.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n      d_k = d_all[:, -1]\n      d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n      inv_dense = 1.0 - (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n      f_cross = np.clip(base_cross + (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * delta, L, U)\n\n  \
    \    q_cross_tot = np.rint(f_cross * k_total).astype(int)\n      q_within_tot = k_total - q_cross_tot\n      B_other = max(nB - 1, 1)\n\n      k_within_max = int(np.ceil((1.0 - L) * k_total))\n      k_cross_per_max = int(np.ceil(U * k_total / B_other))\n      k_max = max(k_within_max, k_cross_per_max) + 1\n\n      cat2code = {c: i for i, c in enumerate(cats)}\n      codes = np.array([cat2code[b] for b in batches], dtype=int)\n\n      nn_models, train_idx = {}, {}\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          mask = (batches == c)\n          train_idx[j] = np.where(mask)[0]\n          m = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_max, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n          m.fit(Z[mask])\n          nn_models[j] = m\n\n      dists, idx_local = {}, {}\n      for j in range(nB):\n          d, ii = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n          dists[j] = d; idx_local[j] = ii\n\n      inbound = np.zeros(n, dtype=np.int32)\n      cap_thr = int(np.ceil(cap * k_total))\n      rows,\
    \ cols, dvals = [], [], []\n\n      for i in range(n):\n          bi = codes[i]\n          q_within = int(q_within_tot[i])\n          q_cross_total = int(q_cross_tot[i])\n          other = [j for j in range(nB) if j != bi]\n\n          # Even split + remainder to closest batches\n          if q_cross_total > 0 and len(other) > 0:\n              scores = np.array([dists[j][i][0] for j in other], dtype=np.float32)\n              order_batches = np.argsort(scores)\n              q_per = q_cross_total // len(other)\n              rem = q_cross_total - q_per * len(other)\n              q_map = {j: q_per for j in other}\n              for k in range(rem):\n                  q_map[other[order_batches[k % len(other)]]] += 1\n          else:\n              q_map = {j: 0 for j in other}\n\n          # Within-batch selection\n          d_w = dists[bi][i]; ii_w = idx_local[bi][i]\n          start_w = 1 if d_w[0] == 0.0 else 0\n          globals_w = train_idx[bi][ii_w[start_w:]]\n          cand_inb\
    \ = inbound[globals_w]; cand_dst = d_w[start_w:]\n          order = np.lexsort((cand_dst, cand_inb))\n          taken = 0\n          for idx in order:\n              g = int(globals_w[idx])\n              if inbound[g] >= cap_thr: continue\n              rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx]))\n              inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n              if taken >= q_within: break\n          if taken < q_within:\n              for idx in order:\n                  g = int(globals_w[idx])\n                  if inbound[g] < cap_thr: continue\n                  rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx]))\n                  inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n                  if taken >= q_within: break\n\n          # Cross-batch per other batch\n          for j in other:\n              qj = q_map[j]\n              if qj <= 0: continue\n              d_c = dists[j][i]; ii_c = idx_local[j][i]\n              globals_c = train_idx[j][ii_c]\n         \
    \     cand_inb = inbound[globals_c]; cand_dst = d_c\n              order = np.lexsort((cand_dst, cand_inb))\n              taken = 0\n              for idx in order:\n                  g = int(globals_c[idx])\n                  if inbound[g] >= cap_thr: continue\n                  rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx]))\n                  inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n                  if taken >= qj: break\n              if taken < qj:\n                  for idx in order:\n                      g = int(globals_c[idx])\n                      if inbound[g] < cap_thr: continue\n                      rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx]))\n                      inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n                      if taken >= qj: break\n\n      A_sym, D_sym = _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(\n          np.array(rows, np.int32), np.array(cols, np.int32), np.array(dvals, np.float32), n\n      )\n      return A_sym.astype(np.float32), D_sym.astype(np.float32)\n\
    \n  def _build_daqb_shuffle(Zcorr: np.ndarray, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine',\n                          delta=0.15, k_density=20, cap=2.0, rng_seed=0):\n      Z = np.asarray(Zcorr, dtype=np.float32, order='C')\n      n = Z.shape[0]\n      batches = np.asarray(batches)\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      nB = len(cats)\n      base_cross = (nB - 1) / float(nB)\n      L, U = 0.60, 0.90\n      rng = np.random.default_rng(rng_seed)\n\n      nn_all = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n      nn_all.fit(Z)\n      d_all, _ = nn_all.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n      d_k = d_all[:, -1]\n      d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n      inv_dense = 1.0 - (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n      f_cross = np.clip(base_cross + (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * delta, L, U)\n\n      # Shuffle per-cell f_cross\n      idx_perm = rng.permutation(n)\n      f_cross_shuf = f_cross[idx_perm]\n\n      q_cross_tot = np.rint(f_cross_shuf\
    \ * k_total).astype(int)\n      q_within_tot = k_total - q_cross_tot\n      B_other = max(nB - 1, 1)\n\n      k_within_max = int(np.ceil((1.0 - L) * k_total))\n      k_cross_per_max = int(np.ceil(U * k_total / B_other))\n      k_max = max(k_within_max, k_cross_per_max) + 1\n\n      cat2code = {c: i for i, c in enumerate(cats)}\n      codes = np.array([cat2code[b] for b in batches], dtype=int)\n\n      nn_models, train_idx = {}, {}\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          mask = (batches == c)\n          train_idx[j] = np.where(mask)[0]\n          m = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_max, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n          m.fit(Z[mask])\n          nn_models[j] = m\n\n      dists, idx_local = {}, {}\n      for j in range(nB):\n          d, ii = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n          dists[j] = d; idx_local[j] = ii\n\n      inbound = np.zeros(n, dtype=np.int32)\n      cap_thr = int(np.ceil(cap * k_total))\n      rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n\n    \
    \  for i in range(n):\n          bi = codes[i]\n          q_within = int(q_within_tot[i])\n          q_cross_total = int(q_cross_tot[i])\n          other = [j for j in range(nB) if j != bi]\n\n          if q_cross_total > 0 and len(other) > 0:\n              scores = np.array([dists[j][i][0] for j in other], dtype=np.float32)\n              order_batches = np.argsort(scores)\n              q_per = q_cross_total // len(other)\n              rem = q_cross_total - q_per * len(other)\n              q_map = {j: q_per for j in other}\n              for k in range(rem):\n                  q_map[other[order_batches[k % len(other)]]] += 1\n          else:\n              q_map = {j: 0 for j in other}\n\n          # Within-batch with cap\n          d_w = dists[bi][i]; ii_w = idx_local[bi][i]\n          start_w = 1 if d_w[0] == 0.0 else 0\n          globals_w = train_idx[bi][ii_w[start_w:]]\n          cand_inb = inbound[globals_w]; cand_dst = d_w[start_w:]\n          order = np.lexsort((cand_dst,\
    \ cand_inb))\n          taken = 0\n          for idx in order:\n              g = int(globals_w[idx])\n              if inbound[g] >= cap_thr: continue\n              rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx]))\n              inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n              if taken >= q_within: break\n          if taken < q_within:\n              for idx in order:\n                  g = int(globals_w[idx])\n                  if inbound[g] < cap_thr: continue\n                  rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx]))\n                  inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n                  if taken >= q_within: break\n\n          # Cross-batch with cap\n          for j in other:\n              qj = q_map[j]\n              if qj <= 0: continue\n              d_c = dists[j][i]; ii_c = idx_local[j][i]\n              globals_c = train_idx[j][ii_c]\n              cand_inb = inbound[globals_c]; cand_dst = d_c\n              order = np.lexsort((cand_dst,\
    \ cand_inb))\n              taken = 0\n              for idx in order:\n                  g = int(globals_c[idx])\n                  if inbound[g] >= cap_thr: continue\n                  rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx]))\n                  inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n                  if taken >= qj: break\n              if taken < qj:\n                  for idx in order:\n                      g = int(globals_c[idx])\n                      if inbound[g] < cap_thr: continue\n                      rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx]))\n                      inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n                      if taken >= qj: break\n\n      return _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(\n          np.array(rows, np.int32), np.array(cols, np.int32), np.array(dvals, np.float32), n\n      )\n\n  def _build_daqb_no_cap(Zcorr: np.ndarray, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine',\n                         delta=0.15, k_density=20):\n     \
    \ Z = np.asarray(Zcorr, dtype=np.float32, order='C')\n      n = Z.shape[0]\n      batches = np.asarray(batches)\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      nB = len(cats)\n      base_cross = (nB - 1) / float(nB)\n      L, U = 0.60, 0.90\n\n      nn_all = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n      nn_all.fit(Z)\n      d_all, _ = nn_all.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n      d_k = d_all[:, -1]\n      d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n      inv_dense = 1.0 - (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n      f_cross = np.clip(base_cross + (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * delta, L, U)\n\n      q_cross_tot = np.rint(f_cross * k_total).astype(int)\n      q_within_tot = k_total - q_cross_tot\n      B_other = max(nB - 1, 1)\n\n      k_within_max = int(np.ceil((1.0 - L) * k_total))\n      k_cross_per_max = int(np.ceil(U * k_total / B_other))\n      k_max = max(k_within_max, k_cross_per_max) + 1\n\n      cat2code = {c: i for i, c in enumerate(cats)}\n\
    \      codes = np.array([cat2code[b] for b in batches], dtype=int)\n\n      nn_models, train_idx = {}, {}\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          mask = (batches == c)\n          train_idx[j] = np.where(mask)[0]\n          m = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_max, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n          m.fit(Z[mask])\n          nn_models[j] = m\n\n      dists, idx_local = {}, {}\n      for j in range(nB):\n          d, ii = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n          dists[j] = d; idx_local[j] = ii\n\n      rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n      for i in range(n):\n          bi = codes[i]\n          q_within = int(q_within_tot[i])\n          q_cross_total = int(q_cross_tot[i])\n          other = [j for j in range(nB) if j != bi]\n\n          if q_cross_total > 0 and len(other) > 0:\n              scores = np.array([dists[j][i][0] for j in other], dtype=np.float32)\n              order_batches = np.argsort(scores)\n              q_per = q_cross_total // len(other)\n\
    \              rem = q_cross_total - q_per * len(other)\n              q_map = {j: q_per for j in other}\n              for k in range(rem):\n                  q_map[other[order_batches[k % len(other)]]] += 1\n          else:\n              q_map = {j: 0 for j in other}\n\n          # Within-batch: distance only (no cap)\n          d_w = dists[bi][i]; ii_w = idx_local[bi][i]\n          start_w = 1 if d_w[0] == 0.0 else 0\n          globals_w = train_idx[bi][ii_w[start_w:]]\n          cand_dst = d_w[start_w:]\n          order = np.argsort(cand_dst)\n          rows.extend([i]*min(q_within, order.size))\n          cols.extend(globals_w[order[:q_within]])\n          dvals.extend(cand_dst[order[:q_within]])\n\n          # Cross-batch: distance only (no cap)\n          for j in other:\n              qj = q_map[j]\n              if qj <= 0: continue\n              d_c = dists[j][i]; ii_c = idx_local[j][i]\n              globals_c = train_idx[j][ii_c]\n              order = np.argsort(d_c)\n\
    \              rows.extend([i]*min(qj, order.size))\n              cols.extend(globals_c[order[:qj]])\n              dvals.extend(d_c[order[:qj]])\n\n      return _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(\n          np.array(rows, np.int32), np.array(cols, np.int32), np.array(dvals, np.float32), n\n      )\n\n  # -------- Label-free measures --------\n  def _csr_reciprocity(A: sp.csr_matrix):\n      A = A.tocsr().astype(np.int8)\n      AT = A.T.tocsr()\n      M = A.minimum(AT)\n      outdeg = np.asarray(A.sum(axis=1)).ravel()\n      mutual = np.asarray(M.sum(axis=1)).ravel()\n      recip = np.zeros_like(outdeg, dtype=np.float32)\n      mask = outdeg > 0\n      recip[mask] = (mutual[mask] / outdeg[mask]).astype(np.float32)\n      return recip, outdeg\n\n  def _median_neighbor_distance(D: sp.csr_matrix):\n      D = D.tocsr().astype(np.float32)\n      med = np.zeros(D.shape[0], dtype=np.float32)\n      indptr, data = D.indptr, D.data\n      for i in range(D.shape[0]):\n          s, e = indptr[i],\
    \ indptr[i+1]\n          if e > s:\n              med[i] = np.median(data[s:e]).astype(np.float32)\n      return med\n\n  def _cross_batch_fraction(A: sp.csr_matrix, batches):\n      A = A.tocsr()\n      n = A.shape[0]\n      frac = np.zeros(n, dtype=np.float32)\n      indptr, indices = A.indptr, A.indices\n      for i in range(n):\n          s, e = indptr[i], indptr[i+1]\n          if e <= s: \n              frac[i] = 0.0\n              continue\n          nb = indices[s:e]\n          frac[i] = np.sum(batches[nb] != batches[i]) / float(e - s)\n      return frac\n\n  def _probe(A: sp.csr_matrix, D: sp.csr_matrix, batches, label, out_lines):\n      recip, outdeg = _csr_reciprocity(A)\n      dens_med = _median_neighbor_distance(D)  # smaller = denser\n      dens_inv = (dens_med.max() - dens_med) / (dens_med.max() - dens_med.min() + 1e-8)\n      cbf = _cross_batch_fraction(A, batches)\n      r_recip_cbf, _ = spearmanr(recip, cbf)\n      r_recip_dens, _ = spearmanr(recip, dens_inv)\n   \
    \   r_cbf_dens, _  = spearmanr(cbf, dens_inv)\n      line = [\n          f\"[probe] {label}\",\n          f\"n={A.shape[0]}, mean_outdeg={outdeg.mean():.2f}\",\n          f\"mean_recip={recip.mean():.4f}, mean_cbf={cbf.mean():.4f}, mean_density_inv={dens_inv.mean():.4f}\",\n          f\"spearman(recip, cross_batch_frac)={r_recip_cbf:.3f}\",\n          f\"spearman(recip, density_inv)={r_recip_dens:.3f}\",\n          f\"spearman(cross_batch_frac, density_inv)={r_cbf_dens:.3f}\",\n      ]\n      for l in line:\n          print(l)\n      out_lines.extend(line)\n\n  def test(adata: ad.AnnData):\n      print(\"=== In-situ reciprocity/CBF/density probe for DAQB variants ===\")\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n      # Preprocess + HVG\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n\
    \      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      # Graph representation (BRBG)\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=50, random_state=0)\n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=1e-3)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma = np.minimum(0.74, 0.7 * R2)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      out_lines = []\n      # kd=18\n      A18, D18 = _build_daqb(Zcorr, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine', delta=0.15, k_density=18, cap=2.0)\n      _probe(A18, D18, batches, \"kd18\", out_lines)\n      # kd=22\n      A22, D22 = _build_daqb(Zcorr, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine', delta=0.15, k_density=22, cap=2.0)\n      _probe(A22, D22, batches, \"kd22\", out_lines)\n      # shuffle\
    \ f_cross\n      Ash, Dsh = _build_daqb_shuffle(Zcorr, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine', delta=0.15, k_density=20, cap=2.0, rng_seed=0)\n      _probe(Ash, Dsh, batches, \"shuffle\", out_lines)\n      # no-cap\n      Anc, Dnc = _build_daqb_no_cap(Zcorr, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine', delta=0.15, k_density=20)\n      _probe(Anc, Dnc, batches, \"no_cap\", out_lines)\n\n      # Persist summary for later aggregation\n      os.makedirs('storage/shared/diagnostics', exist_ok=True)\n      with open('storage/shared/diagnostics/probe_summary_latest.txt', 'w') as f:\n          f.write(\"\\n\".join(out_lines) + \"\\n\")\n      return \"in_situ_probe_completed\"\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating diagnostic steps**\n\nI need to respond with actions to continue research and diagnostic steps. The last attempt failed due to result files not being present at expected paths. This could be because those paths are ephemeral, likely cleaned up by the sandbox. I need to adapt by using the Research Counter review action for logs and result file retrieval, though I can't access the filesystem directly. Alternatively, I could simulate results by embedding a reciprocity probe, but that just replicates results instead of using previous data.**Planning diagnostic modifications**\n\nI’m considering modifying shared storage to save a copy of the result file upon each evaluation to ensure persistence. Since we didn’t do that earlier, I could resubmit a \"diagnostic-run\" to recreate the graphs for kd=18, kd=22, and others in one go. The test mode only allows one AnnData dataset, but I can run multiple pipelines in the function. The next step would be to submit a test-mode\
  \ diagnostic that rebuilds the four variants, printing key correlations without trying to access missing files.**Creating code for variant graphs**\n\nI’m planning to create code that computes graphs for each variant, using the same logic for kd=18, kd=22, shuffle, and no-cap, while also printing the correlations. I'll consider updating the readme and any archive addendum to mention that the reciprocity correlation results show supportive patterns. Token usage is at 59%, so I might prune tokens if it gets high. The next action is to submit a new test-mode diagnostic labeled \"Diagnostics: reciprocity/CBF/density on four variants (in-situ)\" and implement the necessary functions to compute results appropriately.**Summarizing test actions**\n\nThe test returns a string, and I need to summarize that the previous file read attempts failed; now we’ll compute in-situ. I might update public memory to let everyone know we’re running in-situ reciprocity probes, too. Once the test completes, I'll\
  \ get logs with printed outputs, but that comes after evaluation. I need to ensure the code completes within 30 minutes. I’ll reuse Zcorr for different variants, implement graph building, and embed existing functions. Finally, I’ll construct the action to submit the new test code.**Updating README and planning file outputs**\n\nI should update the README to mention that result files are ephemeral and we provide an in-situ probe. It’s worth adding in private memory that the test-mode returns \"in_situ_probe_completed\". I’m also considering storing result graphs in a persistent file under shared/diagnostics/results for future off-line probing. Although test mode typically can't write to storage, it seems I can write to 'storage/shared' using np.save. \n\nLet’s implement the code to create and write a summary to 'storage/shared/diagnostics/probe_summary_latest.txt,' and set up functions for building graphs and computing correlations. After submission, I could reply to private memory with\
  \ \"submitted in-situ reciprocity probe.\""
