role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/diagnostics/reciprocity_probe_in_situ.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import os, sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n  from scipy.stats import spearmanr\n\n  # Utilities\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      n = batches.shape[0]\n      B\
    \ = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      return B @ W\n\n  # Build DAQB and return DIRECTED graph (no symmetrization), plus distances\n  def _build_daqb_directed(Zcorr: np.ndarray, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine',\n                           delta=0.15, k_density=20, cap=2.0, shuffle=False, rng_seed=0):\n      Z = np.asarray(Zcorr, dtype=np.float32, order='C')\n      n = Z.shape[0]\n      batches = np.asarray(batches)\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      nB = len(cats)\n      base_cross = (nB - 1) / float(nB)\n      L, U = 0.60, 0.90\n      rng = np.random.default_rng(rng_seed)\n\n      # Density proxy and f_cross\n      nn_all = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric,\
    \ algorithm='brute')\n      nn_all.fit(Z)\n      d_all, _ = nn_all.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n      d_k = d_all[:, -1]\n      d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n      inv_dense = 1.0 - (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n      f_cross = np.clip(base_cross + (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * delta, L, U)\n      if shuffle:\n          idx_perm = rng.permutation(n)\n          f_cross = f_cross[idx_perm]\n\n      q_cross_tot = np.rint(f_cross * k_total).astype(int)\n      q_within_tot = k_total - q_cross_tot\n      B_other = max(nB - 1, 1)\n\n      k_within_max = int(np.ceil((1.0 - L) * k_total))\n      k_cross_per_max = int(np.ceil(U * k_total / B_other))\n      k_max = max(k_within_max, k_cross_per_max) + 1\n\n      # Per-batch models\n      cat2code = {c: i for i, c in enumerate(cats)}\n      codes = np.array([cat2code[b] for b in batches], dtype=int)\n      nn_models, train_idx = {}, {}\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          mask = (batches ==\
    \ c)\n          train_idx[j] = np.where(mask)[0]\n          m = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_max, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n          m.fit(Z[mask])\n          nn_models[j] = m\n\n      dists, idx_local = {}, {}\n      for j in range(nB):\n          d, ii = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n          dists[j] = d; idx_local[j] = ii\n\n      inbound = np.zeros(n, dtype=np.int32)\n      cap_thr = None if cap is None else int(np.ceil(cap * k_total))\n      rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n\n      for i in range(n):\n          bi = codes[i]\n          q_within = int(q_within_tot[i])\n          q_cross_total = int(q_cross_tot[i])\n          other = [j for j in range(nB) if j != bi]\n\n          # Even split + remainder to closest\n          if q_cross_total > 0 and len(other) > 0:\n              scores = np.array([dists[j][i][0] for j in other], dtype=np.float32)\n              order_batches = np.argsort(scores)\n              q_per = q_cross_total // len(other)\n\
    \              rem = q_cross_total - q_per * len(other)\n              q_map = {j: q_per for j in other}\n              for k in range(rem):\n                  q_map[other[order_batches[k % len(other)]]] += 1\n          else:\n              q_map = {j: 0 for j in other}\n\n          # Within-batch selection\n          d_w = dists[bi][i]; ii_w = idx_local[bi][i]\n          start_w = 1 if d_w[0] == 0.0 else 0\n          globals_w = train_idx[bi][ii_w[start_w:]]\n          cand_inb = inbound[globals_w]\n          cand_dst = d_w[start_w:]\n          order = np.lexsort((cand_dst, cand_inb)) if cap is not None else np.argsort(cand_dst)\n          taken = 0\n          for idx2 in order:\n              g = int(globals_w[idx2])\n              if cap is not None and inbound[g] >= cap_thr: continue\n              rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx2]))\n              inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n              if taken >= q_within: break\n\n          # Cross-batch selection\n\
    \          for j in other:\n              qj = q_map[j]\n              if qj <= 0: continue\n              d_c = dists[j][i]; ii_c = idx_local[j][i]\n              globals_c = train_idx[j][ii_c]\n              cand_inb = inbound[globals_c]\n              cand_dst = d_c\n              order = np.lexsort((cand_dst, cand_inb)) if cap is not None else np.argsort(cand_dst)\n              taken = 0\n              for idx2 in order:\n                  g = int(globals_c[idx2])\n                  if cap is not None and inbound[g] >= cap_thr: continue\n                  rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx2]))\n                  inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n                  if taken >= qj: break\n\n      A_dir = sp.csr_matrix((np.ones(len(rows), dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n))\n      D_dir = sp.csr_matrix((np.array(dvals, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n))\n      return A_dir, D_dir\n\n  # Label-free measures on DIRECTED graph\n  def _directed_reciprocity(A_dir:\
    \ sp.csr_matrix):\n      A = A_dir.tocsr().astype(np.int8)\n      AT = A.T\n      M = A.minimum(AT)  # mutual edges present\n      outdeg = np.asarray(A.sum(axis=1)).ravel().astype(np.float32)\n      mutual = np.asarray(M.sum(axis=1)).ravel().astype(np.float32)\n      recip = np.zeros_like(outdeg, dtype=np.float32)\n      mask = outdeg > 0\n      recip[mask] = mutual[mask] / outdeg[mask]\n      return recip, outdeg\n\n  def _median_neighbor_distance_dir(D_dir: sp.csr_matrix):\n      D = D_dir.tocsr().astype(np.float32)\n      med = np.zeros(D.shape[0], dtype=np.float32)\n      indptr, data = D.indptr, D.data\n      for i in range(D.shape[0]):\n          s, e = indptr[i], indptr[i+1]\n          if e > s:\n              med[i] = np.median(data[s:e]).astype(np.float32)\n      return med\n\n  def _cross_batch_fraction_dir(A_dir: sp.csr_matrix, batches):\n      A = A_dir.tocsr()\n      n = A.shape[0]\n      frac = np.zeros(n, dtype=np.float32)\n      indptr, indices = A.indptr, A.indices\n\
    \      for i in range(n):\n          s, e = indptr[i], indptr[i+1]\n          if e <= s: \n              frac[i] = 0.0\n              continue\n          nb = indices[s:e]\n          frac[i] = np.sum(batches[nb] != batches[i]) / float(e - s)\n      return frac\n\n  def probe_variants(adata: ad.AnnData, out_path: str):\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n      # Preprocess\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      # BRBG Zcorr\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=50, random_state=0)\n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=1e-3)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0,\
    \ ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma = np.minimum(0.74, 0.7 * R2)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      variants = [\n          (\"kd18\", dict(delta=0.15, k_density=18, cap=2.0, shuffle=False)),\n          (\"kd22\", dict(delta=0.15, k_density=22, cap=2.0, shuffle=False)),\n          (\"shuffle\", dict(delta=0.15, k_density=20, cap=2.0, shuffle=True)),\n          (\"no_cap\", dict(delta=0.15, k_density=20, cap=None, shuffle=False)),\n      ]\n      lines = []\n      for name, cfg in variants:\n          A_dir, D_dir = _build_daqb_directed(Zcorr, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine', **cfg)\n          recip, outdeg = _directed_reciprocity(A_dir)\n          dens_med = _median_neighbor_distance_dir(D_dir)  # smaller = denser\n          dens_inv = (dens_med.max() - dens_med) / (dens_med.max() - dens_med.min() + 1e-8)\n          cbf = _cross_batch_fraction_dir(A_dir, batches)\n\
    \          r1, _ = spearmanr(recip, cbf)\n          r2, _ = spearmanr(recip, dens_inv)\n          r3, _ = spearmanr(cbf, dens_inv)\n          lines.extend([\n              f\"[directed_probe] {name}\",\n              f\"  n={A_dir.shape[0]}, mean_outdeg={outdeg.mean():.2f}\",\n              f\"  mean_recip={recip.mean():.4f}, mean_cbf={cbf.mean():.4f}, mean_density_inv={dens_inv.mean():.4f}\",\n              f\"  spearman(recip, cross_batch_frac)={r1:.3f}\",\n              f\"  spearman(recip, density_inv)={r2:.3f}\",\n              f\"  spearman(cross_batch_frac, density_inv)={r3:.3f}\",\n          ])\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(out_path), exist_ok=True)\n      with open(out_path, 'w') as f:\n          f.write(\"\\n\".join(lines) + \"\\n\")\n      for l in lines:\n          print(l)\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      out = \"storage/shared/diagnostics/probe_directed_summary.txt\"\n      adata = sc.read_h5ad(\"storage/system/human_heart.h5ad\") if os.path.exists(\"storage/system/human_heart.h5ad\"\
    ) else None\n      if adata is None:\n          print(\"Missing system dataset; run via evaluator test() to access adata.\", file=sys.stderr)\n          sys.exit(1)\n      probe_variants(adata, out)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Diagnostics (test mode): Directed reciprocity probe (kd18/kd22/shuffle/no-cap)\"\ntags: \"diagnostics, reciprocity, label-free, daqb, graph-analysis, test-mode\"\nabstract: \"Fix reciprocity artifact (symmetrization makes reciprocity=1). Build four DAQB variants in-situ and compute reciprocity on the DIRECTED graph before symmetrization; report correlations with cross-batch fraction and a density proxy. Persist summary to shared storage.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  from shared.diagnostics.reciprocity_probe_in_situ import probe_variants\n\n  def test(adata: ad.AnnData):\n      print(\"=== Directed reciprocity probe (in-situ) ===\")\n      out = \"storage/shared/diagnostics/probe_directed_summary.txt\"\
    \n      probe_variants(adata, out)\n      print(f\"[directed_probe] summary saved to {out}\")\n      return \"directed_reciprocity_probe_completed\"\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Reciprocity probe: fix and expectations\"\ntags: \"diagnostics, reciprocity, plan\"\ncontent: |\n  Issue: reciprocity on symmetrized graphs was 1.0 (degenerate), yielding NaN correlations (EID 782 logs).\n  Fix: run directed reciprocity probe on the directed graph before symmetrization via shared/diagnostics/reciprocity_probe_in_situ.py; submission queued (Directed probe).\n  Expectations:\n  - kd18 vs kd22: slight changes in mean cross-batch fraction; reciprocity should correlate mildly with density proxy in kd18/22 if denser regions have more mutual edges.\n  - shuffle: decouple f_cross from density; expect weaker/misaligned correlations.\n  - no-cap: possible drop in reciprocity if hubs increase unilateral edges; correlations may weaken.\n \
    \ Actions:\n  - Post directed probe summary to Public and Archive diagnostics addendum after results print; update README notes accordingly.\n```"
