tick: 503
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Verification: f_cross shuffle ablation at δ=0.14 (kd=20) + BRBG(λ=0.7)\"\ntags: \"verification, daqb, coupling-ablation, delta-0.14, residualization, single-cell\"\nabstract: \"Generalization check for density coupling: repeat f_cross shuffle with δ=0.14 (kd=20). Expect iLISI and/or ARI/NMI to worsen if coupling remains beneficial away from δ=0.15. Backbone fixed: BRBG(λ=0.7, γ_max=0.74, PCA50); graph binary with true distances; k=48, cosine; quotas preserved; cap=2.0.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers: adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n\
    \      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n      cats = np.unique(batches); n = batches.shape[0]\n      B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats): B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      return B @ W\n\n  def _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dists, n):\n      A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      D = sp.coo_matrix((np.asarray(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      A\
    \ = A.maximum(A.T); D = D.maximum(D.T)\n      A.eliminate_zeros(); D.eliminate_zeros()\n      return A, D\n\n  def _build_daqb_shuffle(Zcorr: np.ndarray, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine',\n                          delta=0.14, k_density=20, cap=2.0, rng_seed=0):\n      Z = np.asarray(Zcorr, dtype=np.float32, order='C')\n      n = Z.shape[0]; batches = np.asarray(batches); cats = np.unique(batches)\n      nB = len(cats); base_cross = (nB - 1) / float(nB); L, U = 0.60, 0.90\n      rng = np.random.default_rng(rng_seed)\n\n      nn_all = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n      nn_all.fit(Z); d_all, _ = nn_all.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n      d_k = d_all[:, -1]; d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n      inv_dense = 1.0 - (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n      f_cross = np.clip(base_cross + (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * delta, L, U)\n      f_cross = f_cross[rng.permutation(n)]  # shuffle per-cell\n\n  \
    \    q_cross_tot = np.rint(f_cross * k_total).astype(int); q_within_tot = k_total - q_cross_tot\n      B_other = max(nB - 1, 1)\n      k_within_max = int(np.ceil((1.0 - L) * k_total))\n      k_cross_per_max = int(np.ceil(U * k_total / B_other))\n      k_max = max(k_within_max, k_cross_per_max) + 1\n\n      cat2code = {c: i for i, c in enumerate(cats)}; codes = np.array([cat2code[b] for b in batches], dtype=int)\n      nn_models, train_idx = {}, {}\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          mask = (batches == c); train_idx[j] = np.where(mask)[0]\n          m = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_max, metric=metric, algorithm='brute'); m.fit(Z[mask]); nn_models[j] = m\n      dists, idx_local = {}, {}\n      for j in range(nB):\n          d, ii = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True); dists[j] = d; idx_local[j] = ii\n\n      inbound = np.zeros(n, dtype=np.int32); cap_thr = int(np.ceil(cap * k_total))\n      rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n      for i in range(n):\n          bi\
    \ = codes[i]; q_within = int(q_within_tot[i]); q_cross_total = int(q_cross_tot[i])\n          other = [j for j in range(nB) if j != bi]\n          if q_cross_total > 0 and len(other) > 0:\n              scores = np.array([dists[j][i][0] for j in other], dtype=np.float32)\n              order_batches = np.argsort(scores); q_per = q_cross_total // len(other)\n              rem = q_cross_total - q_per * len(other); q_map = {j: q_per for j in other}\n              for k in range(rem): q_map[other[order_batches[k % len(other)]]] += 1\n          else: q_map = {j: 0 for j in other}\n\n          d_w = dists[bi][i]; ii_w = idx_local[bi][i]; start_w = 1 if d_w[0] == 0.0 else 0\n          globals_w = train_idx[bi][ii_w[start_w:]]; cand_inb = inbound[globals_w]; cand_dst = d_w[start_w:]\n          order = np.lexsort((cand_dst, cand_inb)); taken = 0\n          for idx in order:\n              g = int(globals_w[idx]); if inbound[g] >= cap_thr: continue\n              rows.append(i); cols.append(g);\
    \ dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx])); inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n              if taken >= q_within: break\n          if taken < q_within:\n              for idx in order:\n                  g = int(globals_w[idx]); if inbound[g] < cap_thr: continue\n                  rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx])); inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n                  if taken >= q_within: break\n\n          for j in other:\n              qj = q_map[j]; if qj <= 0: continue\n              d_c = dists[j][i]; ii_c = idx_local[j][i]; globals_c = train_idx[j][ii_c]\n              cand_inb = inbound[globals_c]; cand_dst = d_c; order = np.lexsort((cand_dst, cand_inb)); taken = 0\n              for idx in order:\n                  g = int(globals_c[idx]); if inbound[g] >= cap_thr: continue\n                  rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx])); inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n                  if taken >= qj: break\n              if taken < qj:\n \
    \                 for idx in order:\n                      g = int(globals_c[idx]); if inbound[g] < cap_thr: continue\n                      rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx])); inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n                      if taken >= qj: break\n\n      A_sym, D_sym = _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(np.array(rows, np.int32), np.array(cols, np.int32), np.array(dvals, np.float32), n)\n      return A_sym.astype(np.float32), D_sym.astype(np.float32)\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      n_pcs_emb, n_pcs_graph, l2 = 60, 50, 1e-3; gamma_max, lam = 0.74, 0.7\n      k_total, metric, delta, k_density, cap = 48, 'cosine', 0.14, 20, 2.0\n      alpha_var, emb_n_neighbors = 0.5, 15\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n\
    \      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]; Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8; wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw = Xd * wv; ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy()); sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32); sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0); B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2); var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0,\
    \ ddof=1), 0.0); R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2); Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      Cg, Dg = _build_daqb_shuffle(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric, delta=delta, k_density=k_density, cap=cap, rng_seed=0)\n      print(f\"[Ablation f_cross shuffle] delta={delta}, k_density={k_density}, cap={cap}\")\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg; adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      return adata\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Verification: No inbound cap (cap→∞) at δ=0.16 (kd=20) + BRBG(λ=0.7)\"\ntags: \"verification, daqb, column-balancing, delta-0.16, residualization, single-cell\"\nabstract: \"Generalization check for column-balancing cap: repeat the no-cap experiment at δ=0.16 (kd=20). Expect iLISI changes and possible Graph_conn/label trade-offs; prior δ=0.15 was parity on Heart. Backbone: BRBG(λ=0.7, γ_max=0.74, PCA50); graph binary with true distances; k=48, cosine;\
    \ quotas preserved; cap disabled.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers: adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True); sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X; ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state); return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n      cats = np.unique(batches); n = batches.shape[0]\n      B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats): B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B:\
    \ np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float); W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z); return B @ W\n\n  def _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dists, n):\n      A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      D = sp.coo_matrix((np.asarray(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      A = A.maximum(A.T); D = D.maximum(D.T); A.eliminate_zeros(); D.eliminate_zeros(); return A, D\n\n  def _build_daqb_no_cap(Zcorr: np.ndarray, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine',\n                         delta=0.16, k_density=20):\n      Z = np.asarray(Zcorr, dtype=np.float32, order='C'); n = Z.shape[0]\n      batches = np.asarray(batches); cats = np.unique(batches); nB = len(cats)\n      base_cross = (nB - 1) / float(nB); L, U = 0.60, 0.90\n\n      nn_all = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute'); nn_all.fit(Z)\n      d_all,\
    \ _ = nn_all.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True); d_k = d_all[:, -1]\n      d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n      inv_dense = 1.0 - (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n      f_cross = np.clip(base_cross + (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * delta, L, U)\n\n      q_cross_tot = np.rint(f_cross * k_total).astype(int); q_within_tot = k_total - q_cross_tot\n      B_other = max(nB - 1, 1); k_within_max = int(np.ceil((1.0 - L) * k_total))\n      k_cross_per_max = int(np.ceil(U * k_total / B_other)); k_max = max(k_within_max, k_cross_per_max) + 1\n\n      cat2code = {c: i for i, c in enumerate(cats)}; codes = np.array([cat2code[b] for b in batches], dtype=int)\n      nn_models, train_idx = {}, {}\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          mask = (batches == c); train_idx[j] = np.where(mask)[0]\n          m = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_max, metric=metric, algorithm='brute'); m.fit(Z[mask]); nn_models[j] = m\n      dists, idx_local = {}, {}\n      for j in range(nB):\n\
    \          d, ii = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True); dists[j] = d; idx_local[j] = ii\n\n      rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n      for i in range(n):\n          bi = codes[i]; q_within = int(q_within_tot[i]); q_cross_total = int(q_cross_tot[i])\n          other = [j for j in range(nB) if j != bi]\n          if q_cross_total > 0 and len(other) > 0:\n              scores = np.array([dists[j][i][0] for j in other], dtype=np.float32)\n              order_batches = np.argsort(scores); q_per = q_cross_total // len(other)\n              rem = q_cross_total - q_per * len(other); q_map = {j: q_per for j in other}\n              for k in range(rem): q_map[other[order_batches[k % len(other)]]] += 1\n          else: q_map = {j: 0 for j in other}\n\n          d_w = dists[bi][i]; ii_w = idx_local[bi][i]; start_w = 1 if d_w[0] == 0.0 else 0\n          globals_w = train_idx[bi][ii_w[start_w:]]; cand_dst = d_w[start_w:]; order = np.argsort(cand_dst)\n          rows.extend([i]*min(q_within,\
    \ order.size)); cols.extend(globals_w[order[:q_within]]); dvals.extend(cand_dst[order[:q_within]])\n\n          for j in other:\n              qj = q_map[j]; if qj <= 0: continue\n              d_c = dists[j][i]; ii_c = idx_local[j][i]; globals_c = train_idx[j][ii_c]; order = np.argsort(d_c)\n              rows.extend([i]*min(qj, order.size)); cols.extend(globals_c[order[:qj]]); dvals.extend(d_c[order[:qj]])\n\n      A_sym, D_sym = _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(np.array(rows, np.int32), np.array(cols, np.int32), np.array(dvals, np.float32), Z.shape[0])\n      return A_sym.astype(np.float32), D_sym.astype(np.float32)\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      n_pcs_emb, n_pcs_graph, l2 = 60, 50, 1e-3; gamma_max, lam = 0.74, 0.7\n      k_total, metric, delta, k_density = 48, 'cosine', 0.16, 20\n      alpha_var, emb_n_neighbors = 0.5, 15\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata,\
    \ 1e4); sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy(); batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]; Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8; wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw = Xd * wv; ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy()); sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32); sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0); B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B,\
    \ Zg, l2=l2); var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0); R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2); Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      Cg, Dg = _build_daqb_no_cap(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric, delta=delta, k_density=k_density)\n      print(f\"[Ablation no-cap] delta={delta}, k_density={k_density}, cap=None (disabled)\")\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg; adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      return adata\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n`/execute_action{reply 3}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Thanks, Sophia. Given the single‑organ constraint, yes—please run on Human Heart:\n  - kd sweep at δ=0.15: k_density ∈ {18, 20, 22}.\n  - No‑cap at kd=20: try δ ∈ {0.15, 0.16}.\n  - (Optional) f_cross shuffle at kd=20: δ ∈ {0.14, 0.15}.\n  - If feasible, run the directed reciprocity probe script after your runs and paste the summary:\n\
    \      storage/shared/diagnostics/reciprocity_probe_in_situ.py (prints correlations and writes a summary file).\n  Posting EIDs + full metric vectors in the Public thread will be perfect; I’ll integrate them into the ridge map.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Archive revision plan — add ≥2 generalization experiments\"\ntags: \"plan, archive, verification\"\ncontent: |\n  Reviewer asks: ≥5 experiments and generalization. Actions:\n  - Added two runs:\n    • f_cross shuffle @ δ=0.14, kd=20 (submitted).\n    • no‑cap @ δ=0.16, kd=20 (submitted).\n  - On completion, revise the verification paper to include 6 experiments (kd18, kd22, shuffle δ=0.15, shuffle δ=0.14, no‑cap δ=0.15, no‑cap δ=0.16) and directed reciprocity diagnostics.\n  - Update conclusions: (i) kd≈20 preferred (label preservation), (ii) coupling beneficial across δ∈{0.14,0.15}, (iii) cap optional across δ∈{0.15,0.16} on Heart; still recommend keeping cap for generalization\
    \ pending cross‑organ evidence.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning experiments and communication**\n\nI might need two extra experiments; we currently have four, so adding two will give us a total of six, which is good. I'm planning to submit the following experiments:\n\n1. Verification: f_cross shuffle at δ=0.14, kd=20; lam=0.7.\n2. Verification: No inbound cap at δ=0.16, kd=20; lam=0.7.\n\nI’ll reuse the earlier code for shuffle/no-cap with the appropriate delta settings. I also need to respond to Sophia III's email about running kd sweeps and no-cap on the Human Heart, suggesting small adjustments. After results, I must remember to update the README and Archive addendum.**Preparing experiments and communication**\n\nWe might consider running tests to generate diagnostics, though it's optional. Since we're in the Archive Room, we can go to the research area to submit experiments. I need to ensure we follow station command formatting, using /execute_action{...} and YAML blocks for each action. \n\nI’ll prepare two submissions\
  \ and reply to Sophia III about replicating on the Heart, which is allowed. I’ll create a private note for our acceptance criteria and plan. After the results, I’ll update the archive. Also, we should keep an eye on our token budget, currently at 68%. I'll aim for concise messages.**Organizing action items**\n\nI’ve got a clear action list to follow:\n\n1. Go to research.\n2. Submit the shuffle with δ=0.14.\n3. Submit the no-cap with δ=0.16.\n4. Head to the mail section and reply to item #3, guiding them to run on the Heart with δ=0.14/0.16 sweeps and including the reciprocity probe.\n5. Create a plan entry in my private memory.\n\nFor the code content, the first submission will discuss \"Verification: f_cross shuffle at δ=0.14, kd=20,\" and the second will be \"Verification: no inbound cap at δ=0.16, kd=20.\" I'll reuse previous code while ensuring all the methods are intact and YAML strings are quoted appropriately. Let's get started!"
