role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Fix: f_cross shuffle ablation at δ=0.14 (kd=20) + BRBG(λ=0.7)\"\ntags: \"verification, daqb, coupling-ablation, delta-0.14, residualization, single-cell, fix\"\nabstract: \"Resubmission with syntax fixes. Generalization check for density coupling: repeat f_cross shuffle with δ=0.14 (kd=20). Expect iLISI and/or ARI/NMI to worsen if coupling remains beneficial away from δ=0.15. Backbone fixed: BRBG(λ=0.7, γ_max=0.74, PCA50); graph binary with true distances; k=48, cosine; quotas preserved; cap=2.0.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata,\
    \ target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      n = batches.shape[0]\n      B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      return B @ W\n\n  def _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dists, n):\n      A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones(len(rows), dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      D = sp.coo_matrix((np.asarray(dists, dtype=np.float32),\
    \ (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      A = A.maximum(A.T)\n      D = D.maximum(D.T)\n      A.eliminate_zeros()\n      D.eliminate_zeros()\n      return A, D\n\n  def _build_daqb_shuffle(Zcorr: np.ndarray, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine',\n                          delta=0.14, k_density=20, cap=2.0, rng_seed=0):\n      Z = np.asarray(Zcorr, dtype=np.float32, order='C')\n      n = Z.shape[0]\n      batches = np.asarray(batches)\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      nB = len(cats)\n      base_cross = (nB - 1) / float(nB)\n      L, U = 0.60, 0.90\n      rng = np.random.default_rng(rng_seed)\n\n      # Density proxy and f_cross\n      nn_all = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n      nn_all.fit(Z)\n      d_all, _ = nn_all.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n      d_k = d_all[:, -1]\n      d_min = float(np.min(d_k))\n      d_max = float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n      inv_dense = 1.0 - (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n      f_cross\
    \ = np.clip(base_cross + (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * delta, L, U)\n\n      # Shuffle per-cell f_cross (preserve marginal distribution)\n      idx_perm = rng.permutation(n)\n      f_cross_shuf = f_cross[idx_perm]\n\n      q_cross_tot = np.rint(f_cross_shuf * k_total).astype(int)\n      q_within_tot = k_total - q_cross_tot\n      B_other = max(nB - 1, 1)\n\n      # NN sizes\n      k_within_max = int(np.ceil((1.0 - L) * k_total))\n      k_cross_per_max = int(np.ceil(U * k_total / B_other))\n      k_max = max(k_within_max, k_cross_per_max) + 1\n\n      # Fit per-batch neighbor models\n      cat2code = {c: i for i, c in enumerate(cats)}\n      codes = np.array([cat2code[b] for b in batches], dtype=int)\n      nn_models, train_idx = {}, {}\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          mask = (batches == c)\n          train_idx[j] = np.where(mask)[0]\n          m = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_max, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n          m.fit(Z[mask])\n          nn_models[j] = m\n\n\
    \      dists, idx_local = {}, {}\n      for j in range(nB):\n          d, ii = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n          dists[j] = d\n          idx_local[j] = ii\n\n      inbound = np.zeros(n, dtype=np.int32)\n      cap_thr = int(np.ceil(cap * k_total))\n      rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n\n      for i in range(n):\n          bi = codes[i]\n          q_within = int(q_within_tot[i])\n          q_cross_total = int(q_cross_tot[i])\n          other = [j for j in range(nB) if j != bi]\n\n          # Even split + remainder to closest batches\n          if q_cross_total > 0 and len(other) > 0:\n              scores = np.array([dists[j][i][0] for j in other], dtype=np.float32)\n              order_batches = np.argsort(scores)\n              q_per = q_cross_total // len(other)\n              rem = q_cross_total - q_per * len(other)\n              q_map = {j: q_per for j in other}\n              for k in range(rem):\n                  j_star = other[order_batches[k % len(other)]]\n\
    \                  q_map[j_star] += 1\n          else:\n              q_map = {j: 0 for j in other}\n\n          # Within-batch selection with cap\n          d_w = dists[bi][i]\n          ii_w = idx_local[bi][i]\n          start_w = 1 if d_w[0] == 0.0 else 0\n          globals_w = train_idx[bi][ii_w[start_w:]]\n          cand_inb = inbound[globals_w]\n          cand_dst = d_w[start_w:]\n          order = np.lexsort((cand_dst, cand_inb))\n          taken = 0\n          for idx in order:\n              g = int(globals_w[idx])\n              if inbound[g] >= cap_thr:\n                  continue\n              rows.append(i)\n              cols.append(g)\n              dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx]))\n              inbound[g] += 1\n              taken += 1\n              if taken >= q_within:\n                  break\n          if taken < q_within:\n              for idx in order:\n                  g = int(globals_w[idx])\n                  if inbound[g] < cap_thr:\n                \
    \      continue\n                  rows.append(i)\n                  cols.append(g)\n                  dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx]))\n                  inbound[g] += 1\n                  taken += 1\n                  if taken >= q_within:\n                      break\n\n          # Cross-batch per other batch with cap\n          for j in other:\n              qj = q_map[j]\n              if qj <= 0:\n                  continue\n              d_c = dists[j][i]\n              ii_c = idx_local[j][i]\n              globals_c = train_idx[j][ii_c]\n              cand_inb = inbound[globals_c]\n              cand_dst = d_c\n              order = np.lexsort((cand_dst, cand_inb))\n              taken = 0\n              for idx in order:\n                  g = int(globals_c[idx])\n                  if inbound[g] >= cap_thr:\n                      continue\n                  rows.append(i)\n                  cols.append(g)\n                  dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx]))\n            \
    \      inbound[g] += 1\n                  taken += 1\n                  if taken >= qj:\n                      break\n              if taken < qj:\n                  for idx in order:\n                      g = int(globals_c[idx])\n                      if inbound[g] < cap_thr:\n                          continue\n                      rows.append(i)\n                      cols.append(g)\n                      dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx]))\n                      inbound[g] += 1\n                      taken += 1\n                      if taken >= qj:\n                          break\n\n      return _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dvals, n)\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Config\n      n_pcs_emb = 60\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma_max = 0.74\n      lam = 0.7\n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      delta = 0.14\n      k_density = 20\n      cap = 2.0\n      alpha_var = 0.5\n      emb_n_neighbors\
    \ = 15\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      # EtC embedding for QC (not used for graph)\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw = Xd * wv\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      Z_emb = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X,\
    \ dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n      # Graph path\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      Cg, Dg = _build_daqb_shuffle(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                   k_total=k_total, metric=metric, delta=delta,\n                                   k_density=k_density, cap=cap, rng_seed=0)\n      print(f\"[Ablation f_cross shuffle] delta={delta}, k_density={k_density}, cap={cap}\")\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      return adata\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\
    \n```yaml\ntitle: \"Fix: No inbound cap (cap→∞) at δ=0.16 (kd=20) + BRBG(λ=0.7)\"\ntags: \"verification, daqb, column-balancing, delta-0.16, residualization, single-cell, fix\"\nabstract: \"Resubmission with syntax fixes. Generalization check for column-balancing cap: repeat the no-cap experiment at δ=0.16 (kd=20). Backbone: BRBG(λ=0.7, γ_max=0.74, PCA50); graph binary with true distances; k=48, cosine; quotas preserved; cap disabled.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X)\
    \ else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      n = batches.shape[0]\n      B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      return B @ W\n\n  def _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dists, n):\n      A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones(len(rows), dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      D = sp.coo_matrix((np.asarray(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      A = A.maximum(A.T)\n      D = D.maximum(D.T)\n      A.eliminate_zeros()\n      D.eliminate_zeros()\n\
    \      return A, D\n\n  def _build_daqb_no_cap(Zcorr: np.ndarray, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine',\n                         delta=0.16, k_density=20):\n      Z = np.asarray(Zcorr, dtype=np.float32, order='C')\n      n = Z.shape[0]\n      batches = np.asarray(batches)\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      nB = len(cats)\n      base_cross = (nB - 1) / float(nB)\n      L, U = 0.60, 0.90\n\n      nn_all = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n      nn_all.fit(Z)\n      d_all, _ = nn_all.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n      d_k = d_all[:, -1]\n      d_min = float(np.min(d_k))\n      d_max = float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n      inv_dense = 1.0 - (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n      f_cross = np.clip(base_cross + (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * delta, L, U)\n\n      q_cross_tot = np.rint(f_cross * k_total).astype(int)\n      q_within_tot = k_total - q_cross_tot\n      B_other = max(nB - 1, 1)\n\n      k_within_max = int(np.ceil((1.0 - L)\
    \ * k_total))\n      k_cross_per_max = int(np.ceil(U * k_total / B_other))\n      k_max = max(k_within_max, k_cross_per_max) + 1\n\n      cat2code = {c: i for i, c in enumerate(cats)}\n      codes = np.array([cat2code[b] for b in batches], dtype=int)\n      nn_models, train_idx = {}, {}\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          mask = (batches == c)\n          train_idx[j] = np.where(mask)[0]\n          m = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_max, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n          m.fit(Z[mask])\n          nn_models[j] = m\n\n      dists, idx_local = {}, {}\n      for j in range(nB):\n          d, ii = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n          dists[j] = d\n          idx_local[j] = ii\n\n      rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n\n      for i in range(n):\n          bi = codes[i]\n          q_within = int(q_within_tot[i])\n          q_cross_total = int(q_cross_tot[i])\n          other = [j for j in range(nB) if j != bi]\n\n          if q_cross_total > 0 and len(other)\
    \ > 0:\n              scores = np.array([dists[j][i][0] for j in other], dtype=np.float32)\n              order_batches = np.argsort(scores)\n              q_per = q_cross_total // len(other)\n              rem = q_cross_total - q_per * len(other)\n              q_map = {j: q_per for j in other}\n              for k in range(rem):\n                  j_star = other[order_batches[k % len(other)]]\n                  q_map[j_star] += 1\n          else:\n              q_map = {j: 0 for j in other}\n\n          # Within-batch: distance only (no cap)\n          d_w = dists[bi][i]\n          ii_w = idx_local[bi][i]\n          start_w = 1 if d_w[0] == 0.0 else 0\n          globals_w = train_idx[bi][ii_w[start_w:]]\n          cand_dst = d_w[start_w:]\n          order = np.argsort(cand_dst)\n          max_take = min(q_within, order.size)\n          for t in range(max_take):\n              rows.append(i)\n              cols.append(int(globals_w[order[t]]))\n              dvals.append(float(cand_dst[order[t]]))\n\
    \n          # Cross-batch: distance only (no cap)\n          for j in other:\n              qj = q_map[j]\n              if qj <= 0:\n                  continue\n              d_c = dists[j][i]\n              ii_c = idx_local[j][i]\n              globals_c = train_idx[j][ii_c]\n              order = np.argsort(d_c)\n              max_take = min(qj, order.size)\n              for t in range(max_take):\n                  rows.append(i)\n                  cols.append(int(globals_c[order[t]]))\n                  dvals.append(float(d_c[order[t]]))\n\n      return _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dvals, Z.shape[0])\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Config\n      n_pcs_emb = 60\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma_max = 0.74\n      lam = 0.7\n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      delta = 0.16\n      k_density = 20\n      alpha_var = 0.5\n      emb_n_neighbors = 15\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns\
    \ and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      # EtC embedding (QC only)\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw = Xd * wv\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      Z_emb = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb',\
    \ n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n      # Graph path\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      Cg, Dg = _build_daqb_no_cap(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                  k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                  delta=delta, k_density=k_density)\n      print(f\"[Ablation no-cap] delta={delta}, k_density={k_density}, cap=None (disabled)\")\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      return adata\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 38}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Syntax errors fixed and\
    \ resubmitted:\n  - f_cross shuffle @ δ=0.14, kd=20 (EID pending).\n  - no-cap @ δ=0.16, kd=20 (EID pending).\n  After completion, revise Archive with ≥6 experiments + directed reciprocity diagnostics to meet 5-experiment and generalization requirements.\n```"
