tick: 509
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{read 27}`\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replication: DAQB(δ=0.10, kd=20) + BRBG(λ=0.5, γ_max=0.74) — Logos V #27 params\"\ntags: \"replication, daqb, residualization, parameter-sweep, single-cell\"\nabstract: \"Replicate Logos V #27 claim: BRBG shrinkage λ=0.5 and DAQB δ=0.10 (k_density=20) exceed prior ridge. Keep k=48, cosine, binary+true distances, cap=2.0; EtC for QC only; PCA50 graph path. Test on Heart.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers: adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def\
    \ _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n      cats = np.unique(batches); n = batches.shape[0]\n      B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats): B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      return B @ W\n\n  def _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dists, n):\n      A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n,n)).tocsr()\n      D = sp.coo_matrix((np.asarray(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n,n)).tocsr()\n      A = A.maximum(A.T); D = D.maximum(D.T);\
    \ A.eliminate_zeros(); D.eliminate_zeros()\n      return A, D\n\n  def _build_daqb(Zcorr: np.ndarray, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine',\n                  delta=0.10, k_density=20, cap=2.0):\n      Z = np.asarray(Zcorr, dtype=np.float32, order='C'); n = Z.shape[0]\n      batches = np.asarray(batches); cats = np.unique(batches); nB = len(cats)\n      base_cross = (nB - 1) / float(nB); L, U = 0.60, 0.90\n\n      nn_all = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute').fit(Z)\n      d_all, _ = nn_all.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n      d_k = d_all[:, -1]; d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n      inv_dense = 1.0 - (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n      f_cross = np.clip(base_cross + (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * delta, L, U)\n\n      q_cross_tot = np.rint(f_cross * k_total).astype(int)\n      q_within_tot = k_total - q_cross_tot\n      B_other = max(nB - 1, 1)\n\n      k_within_max = int(np.ceil((1.0 - L) * k_total))\n\
    \      k_cross_per_max = int(np.ceil(U * k_total / B_other))\n      k_max = max(k_within_max, k_cross_per_max) + 1\n\n      cat2code = {c: i for i, c in enumerate(cats)}\n      codes = np.array([cat2code[b] for b in batches], dtype=int)\n      nn_models, train_idx = {}, {}\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          mask = (batches == c); train_idx[j] = np.where(mask)[0]\n          nn_models[j] = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_max, metric=metric, algorithm='brute').fit(Z[mask])\n\n      dists, idx_local = {}, {}\n      for j in range(nB):\n          d, ii = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n          dists[j], idx_local[j] = d, ii\n\n      inbound = np.zeros(n, dtype=np.int32); cap_thr = int(np.ceil(cap * k_total))\n      rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n\n      for i in range(n):\n          bi = codes[i]; q_within = int(q_within_tot[i]); q_cross_total = int(q_cross_tot[i])\n          other = [j for j in range(nB) if j != bi]\n\n          if q_cross_total > 0 and other:\n\
    \              scores = np.array([dists[j][i][0] for j in other], dtype=np.float32)\n              order_batches = np.argsort(scores)\n              q_per = q_cross_total // len(other); rem = q_cross_total - q_per * len(other)\n              q_map = {j: q_per for j in other}\n              for k in range(rem): q_map[other[order_batches[k % len(other)]]] += 1\n          else:\n              q_map = {j: 0 for j in other}\n\n          d_w, ii_w = dists[bi][i], idx_local[bi][i]\n          start_w = 1 if d_w[0] == 0.0 else 0\n          globals_w = train_idx[bi][ii_w[start_w:]]\n          cand_inb, cand_dst = inbound[globals_w], d_w[start_w:]\n          order = np.lexsort((cand_dst, cand_inb)); taken = 0\n          for idx in order:\n              g = int(globals_w[idx])\n              if inbound[g] >= cap_thr: continue\n              rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx]))\n              inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n              if taken >= q_within: break\n  \
    \        if taken < q_within:\n              for idx in order:\n                  g = int(globals_w[idx])\n                  if inbound[g] < cap_thr: continue\n                  rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx]))\n                  inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n                  if taken >= q_within: break\n\n          for j in other:\n              qj = q_map[j]\n              if qj <= 0: continue\n              d_c, ii_c = dists[j][i], idx_local[j][i]\n              globals_c = train_idx[j][ii_c]\n              cand_inb, cand_dst = inbound[globals_c], d_c\n              order = np.lexsort((cand_dst, cand_inb)); taken = 0\n              for idx in order:\n                  g = int(globals_c[idx])\n                  if inbound[g] >= cap_thr: continue\n                  rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx]))\n                  inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n                  if taken >= qj: break\n              if taken < qj:\n\
    \                  for idx in order:\n                      g = int(globals_c[idx])\n                      if inbound[g] < cap_thr: continue\n                      rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx]))\n                      inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n                      if taken >= qj: break\n\n      A_sym, D_sym = _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(np.array(rows, np.int32),\n                                                       np.array(cols, np.int32),\n                                                       np.array(dvals, np.float32), n)\n      return A_sym.astype(np.float32), D_sym.astype(np.float32)\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      n_pcs_emb, n_pcs_graph = 60, 50\n      l2 = 1e-3; gamma_max = 0.74; lam = 0.5\n      k_total = 48; metric = 'cosine'\n      delta = 0.10; k_density = 20; cap = 2.0\n      alpha_var = 0.5; emb_n_neighbors = 15\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in\
    \ adata.var.columns\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8; wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw = Xd * wv; ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy()); sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph,\
    \ random_state=0)\n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches); Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8; var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0); gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      Cg, Dg = _build_daqb(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                           delta=delta, k_density=k_density, cap=cap)\n      print(f\"[Replication LogosV] lam={lam}, delta={delta}, kd={k_density}, cap={cap}\")\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg; adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      return adata\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replication: DAQB(δ=0.10, kd=18) + BRBG(λ=0.5) — sensitivity near Logos V #27\"\ntags: \"replication, daqb, parameter-sweep, residualization, single-cell\"\nabstract: \"Sensitivity around Logos V settings: δ=0.10 with kd=18 (vs kd=20) under BRBG λ=0.5.\
    \ All else fixed (k=48, cosine, cap=2.0; binary+true distances; PCA50 graph).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n  # Reuse identical helpers; only change k_density=18 and keep lam=0.5, delta=0.10\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers: adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True); sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X; ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n      cats = np.unique(batches); n = batches.shape[0]; B = np.zeros((n, cats.size),\
    \ dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats): B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float); return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float); W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z); return B @ W\n\n  def _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dists, n):\n      A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n,n)).tocsr()\n      D = sp.coo_matrix((np.asarray(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n,n)).tocsr()\n      A = A.maximum(A.T); D = D.maximum(D.T); A.eliminate_zeros(); D.eliminate_zeros(); return A, D\n\n  def _build_daqb(Zcorr: np.ndarray, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine', delta=0.10, k_density=18, cap=2.0):\n      Z = np.asarray(Zcorr, dtype=np.float32, order='C'); n = Z.shape[0]\n      batches = np.asarray(batches); cats = np.unique(batches); nB = len(cats)\n      base_cross = (nB - 1) / float(nB); L, U = 0.60, 0.90\n      nn_all\
    \ = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute').fit(Z)\n      d_all, _ = nn_all.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n      d_k = d_all[:, -1]; d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n      inv_dense = 1.0 - (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n      f_cross = np.clip(base_cross + (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * delta, L, U)\n      q_cross_tot = np.rint(f_cross * k_total).astype(int); q_within_tot = k_total - q_cross_tot\n      B_other = max(nB - 1, 1)\n      k_within_max = int(np.ceil((1.0 - L) * k_total)); k_cross_per_max = int(np.ceil(U * k_total / B_other))\n      k_max = max(k_within_max, k_cross_per_max) + 1\n      cat2code = {c: i for i, c in enumerate(cats)}; codes = np.array([cat2code[b] for b in batches], dtype=int)\n      nn_models, train_idx = {}, {}\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          mask = (batches == c); train_idx[j] = np.where(mask)[0]\n          nn_models[j] = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_max, metric=metric,\
    \ algorithm='brute').fit(Z[mask])\n      dists, idx_local = {}, {}\n      for j in range(nB):\n          d, ii = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True); dists[j], idx_local[j] = d, ii\n      inbound = np.zeros(n, dtype=np.int32); cap_thr = int(np.ceil(cap * k_total))\n      rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n      for i in range(n):\n          bi = codes[i]; q_within = int(q_within_tot[i]); q_cross_total = int(q_cross_tot[i])\n          other = [j for j in range(nB) if j != bi]\n          if q_cross_total > 0 and other:\n              scores = np.array([dists[j][i][0] for j in other], dtype=np.float32)\n              order_batches = np.argsort(scores); q_per = q_cross_total // len(other)\n              rem = q_cross_total - q_per * len(other); q_map = {j: q_per for j in other}\n              for k in range(rem): q_map[other[order_batches[k % len(other)]]] += 1\n          else: q_map = {j: 0 for j in other}\n          d_w, ii_w = dists[bi][i], idx_local[bi][i]; start_w = 1 if d_w[0]\
    \ == 0.0 else 0\n          globals_w = train_idx[bi][ii_w[start_w:]]; cand_inb, cand_dst = inbound[globals_w], d_w[start_w:]\n          order = np.lexsort((cand_dst, cand_inb)); taken = 0\n          for idx in order:\n              g = int(globals_w[idx]); if inbound[g] >= cap_thr: continue\n              rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx])); inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n              if taken >= q_within: break\n          if taken < q_within:\n              for idx in order:\n                  g = int(globals_w[idx]); if inbound[g] < cap_thr: continue\n                  rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx])); inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n                  if taken >= q_within: break\n          for j in other:\n              qj = q_map[j]; if qj <= 0: continue\n              d_c, ii_c = dists[j][i], idx_local[j][i]; globals_c = train_idx[j][ii_c]\n              cand_inb, cand_dst = inbound[globals_c], d_c; order = np.lexsort((cand_dst,\
    \ cand_inb)); taken = 0\n              for idx in order:\n                  g = int(globals_c[idx]); if inbound[g] >= cap_thr: continue\n                  rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx])); inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n                  if taken >= qj: break\n              if taken < qj:\n                  for idx in order:\n                      g = int(globals_c[idx]); if inbound[g] < cap_thr: continue\n                      rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx])); inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n                      if taken >= qj: break\n      A_sym, D_sym = _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(np.array(rows, np.int32),\n                                                       np.array(cols, np.int32),\n                                                       np.array(dvals, np.float32), Z.shape[0])\n      return A_sym.astype(np.float32), D_sym.astype(np.float32)\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n\
    \      n_pcs_emb, n_pcs_graph = 60, 50\n      l2 = 1e-3; gamma_max = 0.74; lam = 0.5\n      k_total = 48; metric = 'cosine'; delta = 0.10; k_density = 18; cap = 2.0\n      alpha_var = 0.5; emb_n_neighbors = 15\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]; Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8; wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw = Xd * wv; ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy());\
    \ sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32); sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches); Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8; var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0); gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      Cg, Dg = _build_daqb(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                           delta=delta, k_density=k_density, cap=cap)\n      print(f\"[Replication LogosV] lam={lam}, delta={delta}, kd={k_density}, cap={cap}\")\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg; adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      return adata\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 2}`\n\
    \n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Replication plan for Logos V #27:\n  - Running Heart replications with BRBG λ=0.5 and DAQB δ=0.10:\n    • kd=20 (cap=2.0) and kd=18 (cap=2.0). EIDs pending.\n  - All else fixed (EtC for QC only; PCA50 graph; k=48, cosine; binary + true distances).\n  - If results surpass the current ridge, we’ll update the README and ridge map; otherwise we’ll document as a neutral/negative replication. Will post EIDs + full vectors.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Investigating Praxis II Research**


  I need to continue examining actions related to Praxis II''s research. They previewed Logos V #27, claiming an optimal lam of 0.5 and delta of 0.1, achieving a SOTA of 0.7362. This conflicts with our findings where lam=0.7 and delta=0.15 showed robustness. Some agents found a similar SOTA of 0.743 before, but current parity is around 0.733-0.734. I''ll read through the entire #27 capsule to explore their methodology and run a replication with lam=0.5 and delta=0.1 to better understand the situation.**Adjusting Parameters for BRBG**


  I''m working on submitting research code with an adjusted lam parameter in the BRBG shrink schedule. Previously, we used lam at 0.7, but now I''ll try lam=0.5 with delta=0.1 and kd=20 while keeping other parameters the same. I''ll also test a small grid around that to see how delta and kd affect results. We can submit two experiments, as token usage is at 62%. I could also reach out to Logos V for more details, and finally, I’ll pre-register an ablation experiment with those parameters.**Updating README and Submitting Replicates**


  I should update the README with information on a new candidate, but I''ll wait until we have results. First, I want to check the full content of capsule 27 for EIDs and other details. I’ve only seen the abstract, so I’ll focus on "read 27" to access the full text. Then, I’ll plan to submit replicates based on our earlier work. The code will use a shared algorithm wrapper, which needs adjustments for lam and delta, ensuring everything aligns with our earlier standards. I''ll write the eliminate_batch_effect_fn with lam=0.5, delta=0.1, and kd=20.**Planning Submissions and Code Updates**


  I might consider a second submission with "lam=0.5, delta=0.1, kd=18" to assess kd sensitivity. However, since we can only have two pending submissions, I could go with kd=20 and kd=22. It seems reasonable to stick with kd=20 and 18. I also want to update Public Memory about the replication attempt while keeping token usage low by providing minimal code. For BRBG work, I need to ensure we''re using the _build_bbsg function. Since the previous SOTA used DAQB, I need to be mindful that our DAQB code employs custom quotas that differ from the expectations of _build_bbsg.**Preparing Replicate Submissions**


  For our replicate of the Logos V parameter optimization using DAQB, I''ll stick with our custom building code. We''ll use the DAQB builder with the k_density parameter, and keep lam for BRBG and delta for density-adaptive purposes. I need to include the builder code for replicability, condensing it where possible. Here''s the plan for the first replicate: normalize data, compute HVGs, perform PCA, and batch predictions with lam=0.5 and delta=0.1 at kd=20. The second replicate will use kd=18. Finally, I’ll log our settings and publish our actions. Let''s get started!'
