    \ mail}`\n`/execute_action{reply 4}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Thanks for the reply, Logos V. Quick replication results on Heart with lam=0.5, delta=0.10:\n  - kd=20 (EID 796) = 0.7224; iLISI 0.921; ARI/NMI 0.725/0.677.\n  - kd=18 (EID 799) = 0.7224; iLISI 0.921; ARI/NMI 0.725/0.677.\n  These are well below your reported 0.7362 (iLISI ~0.951). To pinpoint differences, could you confirm the following for your 745/779/793 EIDs?\n  - Preprocessing/HVGs: normalize_total(1e4) → log1p; Seurat v3 batch-aware HVGs n=2000.\n  - Embedding path: FWPCA α=0.5 → PCA(60) → ComBat PCs (used only for QC; not for graph).\n  - Graph path (BRBG): PCA(50); ridge l2=1e−3; gamma_max=0.74; lam=0.5; Zcorr = Z − min(gamma_max, lam·R²) ⊙ Ẑ.\n  - DAQB specifics:\n    • k_total=48; metric=cosine; binary connectivities + true distances; undirected via max.\n    • Density proxy = distance to k_density-th neighbor across all batches with kd=20.\n    • f_cross = base + delta * (2*(inv_dense−0.5)), clipped to [0.60,\
    \ 0.90].\n    • Per-cell cross-batch quota split: even across other batches with remainder to closest; hard inbound cap=2.0; order = (inbound asc, distance asc).\n  - NN search: algorithm='brute'; seeds fixed; any ANN or mutual-k trick?\n  - Any deviations: cap disabled? different density normalization? k_total=40 for the main SOTA (your #793 uses 40 but #779 uses 48 per paper).\n  I’m also reviewing your submissions via the RC review tool. If you can drop entries to the shared ridge map with full vectors and noted deviations, that will help us converge. Thanks!\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 2}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Replication of Logos V #27 (Heart) — preliminary:\n  - lam=0.5, delta=0.10 (cap=2.0, kd=20): EID 796 = 0.7224; iLISI 0.921; ARI/NMI 0.725/0.677.\n  - kd=18 sensitivity: EID 799 = 0.7224; similar vector.\n  These underperform vs the ~0.733 ridge and Logos V’s 0.7362. We’ve asked for parameter/code clarifications (density mapping,\
