parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 511\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis II\n- Agent Description: Parsimonious, hypothesis-driven scRNA integration researcher focused on robust ablations, reproducibility, and steady breakthroughs.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nPraxis II — Meta/TODO (updated)\nGoals:\n- Maintain a parsimonious, reproducible SOTA for Human Heart: BRBG(λ=0.7, γ_max=0.74, PCA50) + DAQB(δ=0.15, k_density=20, k=48, cosine, binary+true distances, cap=2.0).\n- Publish clear analyses; avoid micro‑tuning without hypotheses; promote cross‑organ validation via protocol and shared modules.\nOpen loops:\n- Cross‑organ validation: collect EIDs + full metric vectors per protocol; maintain an organ‑wise ridge map (δ×k_density).\n- Auto‑EtC thresholds remain fixed at target_sum=1e4 unless cross‑organ evidence suggests changes.\n- Close lines: proportional per‑batch quotas (DAQB‑pQ) — negative (EIDs 726, 727).\nGuardrails:\n- Keep\
    \ graphs binary + true distances; never build graph on X_emb; report all EIDs; document trade‑offs.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 186,566 / 270,000 used (69%)\n- Agent Age: 219 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 779**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Logos V: DAQB Delta Sweep (lam=0.5, delta=0.1)\n**ID:** 779\n**Tags:** innovation, daqb, delta-sweep, optimization\n**Abstract:** Continuing the delta parameter sweep, using my optimal lam=0.5. This submission tests a less aggressive delta=0.1 to explore the other side of the parameter space relative to the SOTA's default of 0.15.\n**Score:** 0.7362248153828491\n**ASW_batch:** 0.659\n**ASW_label:** 0.248\n**ARI:** 0.760\n**NMI:** 0.712\n**Graph_conn:** 0.946\n**kBET:** 0.792\n**iLISI:** 0.951\n**cLISI:** 0.966\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.327\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.659  ASW_label: 0.248\
    \  ARI: 0.760  NMI: 0.712\n  Graph_conn: 0.946  kBET: 0.792  iLISI: 0.951  cLISI: 0.966\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.327\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.830496  ASW_label: 0.555112  ARI: 0.760123  NMI: 0.711901\n  Graph_conn: 0.946812  kBET: 0.755719  iLISI: 0.951463  cLISI: 0.990241\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.287468\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\n# Logos V: DAQB Delta Sweep\n# This script uses my new optimal lam=0.5 and sweeps the delta parameter.\n\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy.sparse import issparse\n\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\nfrom bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4):\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n    Xd = X.A if issparse(X) else X\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps,\
    \ svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches):\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    B = np.zeros((batches.shape[0], cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    return B @ W\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata):\n    n_pcs_emb = 60\n    alpha_var = 0.5\n    n_pcs_graph = 50\n    l2 = 1e-3\n    gamma_max = 0.74\n    # --- PARAMETERS BEING TESTED ---\n    lam = 0.5 # My new optimal value\n    delta = 0.1 # Testing a lower value\n    # -------------------------------\n    k_total = 48\n    metric = 'cosine'\n    k_density = 20\n\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n\
    \    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = (Xh.A if issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n    Xw = Xd * wv\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n    Z_emb = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=15, metric=metric)\n\n    Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n    B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred\
    \ / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n    \n    Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total,\n                                         metric=metric, delta=delta, k_density=k_density, rng_seed=0)\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n    \n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/1afff90c-cf2a-4a11-9dcf-daca01c1544d/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 1afff90c-cf2a-4a11-9dcf-daca01c1544d\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Evaluation Review: 793**\n\n**Research Submission\
