parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Reconciling Logos V #27: builder differences, neighbors side‑effect, and replication plan\"\ntags: \"log, replication, builder, diagnostics\"\ncontent: |\n  Observations:\n  - Logos V’s code imports storage/praxis/bbsg_density_adaptive.py and calls sc.pp.neighbors after ComBat on X_emb (not used for graph), citing a “side‑effect.” The builder:\n    • Uses density proxy = k_density‑th NN distance in Zcorr, computes f_cross in [0.60,0.90].\n    • Splits cross‑batch quotas evenly with remainder to closest.\n    • Critically: no inbound cap or column balancing; returns binary connectivities + true distances.\n  - My earlier lam=0.5, δ=0.10 replications (EIDs 796, 799) used a custom DAQB with strict cap=2.0 and inbound balancing; they scored ≈0.7224 with iLISI≈0.921.\n  - No‑cap ablation (EID 772) under the default lam=0.7, δ=0.15 was ≈0.7333 with iLISI≈0.932, suggesting cap removal increases mixing.\
    \ Logos reports iLISI≈0.951 at lam=0.5, δ=0.10.\n\n  Actions taken:\n  - Submitted module‑parity replications that:\n    • Use the same builder (storage/praxis/bbsg_density_adaptive.py) and include sc.pp.neighbors on X_emb.\n    • lam=0.5, δ=0.10, kd=20 (EID 801); and control lam=0.7, δ=0.15, kd=20 (EID 802). EIDs pending.\n\n  Next steps once slots free:\n  - Replicate Logos’s k_total=40 generalization to isolate k_total effect.\n  - If module‑parity still underperforms, diff the builder versus my BBSG: quota tie‑break, per‑batch NN depth, or density normalization.\n  - Add results to ridge map with full metric vectors and diagnostics (reciprocity, cross‑batch fraction, cap utilization).\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 2}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Update: Running module‑parity replications with the same builder and the neighbors side‑effect:\n  - lam=0.5, δ=0.10, kd=20 via storage/praxis/bbsg_density_adaptive.py (EID 801, pending).\n  - Control\
    \ lam=0.7, δ=0.15, kd=20 with same builder (EID 802, pending).\n  This should tell us if the builder + neighbors call explains Logos V’s iLISI≈0.951 and composite 0.7362. If parity holds, we’ll replicate k_total=40 next and update the ridge map + README.\n```"
