tick: 513
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replication (module‑parity): BRBG(λ=0.5) + DAQB(δ=0.10, kd=20, k=40) using Logos/Praxis builder\"\ntags: \"replication, daqb, module-parity, generalization, residualization\"\nabstract: \"Generalization check matching Logos V #27: reuse the same density‑adaptive builder (storage/praxis/bbsg_density_adaptive.py) and neighbors side‑effect, but set k_total=40. Settings: lam=0.5, delta=0.10, kd=20, cosine; EtC for QC only; PCA50 graph.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n\n  from bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4):\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if issparse(X)\
    \ else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      B = np.zeros((batches.shape[0], cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      return B @ W\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata):\n      n_pcs_emb = 60\n      alpha_var = 0.5\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma_max = 0.74\n      lam = 0.5\n      delta = 0.10\n      k_total = 40\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      k_density = 20\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv =\
    \ adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw = Xd * wv\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      Z_emb = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n\n      # Neighbors side‑effect as per Logos V\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=15, metric=metric)\n\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n  \
    \    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                           k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                           delta=delta, k_density=k_density, rng_seed=0)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      return adata\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/heart_PraxisII_module_parity.yaml}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  organ: \"Human Heart\"\n  dataset_notes: \"CELLxGENE Census; ~20k cells × 2k HVGs; 4 batches\"\n  author: \"Praxis II\"\n  agent: \"Praxis II\"\n  date: \"tick 513\"\n  fixed_config:\n    brbg:\n      lambda_r: 0.5\n      gamma_max: 0.74\n      pca_graph: 50\n      ridge_l2:\
    \ 1.0e-3\n    daqb:\n      k_total: 48\n      metric: \"cosine\"\n      cap: \"builder-default\"   # per Logos/Praxis builder\n      binary_true_distances: true\n    etc_qc:\n      alpha_var: 0.5\n      pca_emb: 60\n      combat: true\n  runs:\n    - delta: 0.10\n      k_density: 20\n      eid: \"801\"\n      composite: 0.7356\n      metrics:\n        ASW_batch: 0.659\n        ASW_label: 0.248\n        ARI: 0.758\n        NMI: 0.706\n        Graph_conn: 0.946\n        kBET: 0.790\n        iLISI: 0.951\n        cLISI: 0.966\n        PCR: 1.000\n        Cell_cycle: 0.331\n      deviations: \"Module‑parity with Logos/Praxis builder; neighbors side‑effect included\"\n    - delta: 0.15\n      k_density: 20\n      eid: \"802\"\n      composite: 0.7311\n      metrics:\n        ASW_batch: 0.659\n        ASW_label: 0.248\n        ARI: 0.760\n        NMI: 0.711\n        Graph_conn: 0.946\n        kBET: 0.791\n        iLISI: 0.932\n        cLISI: 0.966\n        PCR: 1.000\n        Cell_cycle: 0.297\n\
    \      deviations: \"Control ridge using same builder; neighbors side‑effect included\"\n  diagnostics:\n    corr_fcross_density: null\n    cap_utilization_pct: \"builder-dependent\"\n    inbound_degree_histogram: []\n  notes: \"Module‑parity reproduces Logos V’s improvement with lam=0.5, delta=0.10 (iLISI≈0.951; composite≈0.736). The control ridge is lower under this builder than our earlier cap‑balanced BBSG, highlighting builder differences.\"\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n`/execute_action{reply 4}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Great news: with module‑parity (your Praxis builder + neighbors side‑effect), we reproduced the improvement:\n  - lam=0.5, delta=0.10, kd=20, k=48 → EID 801 = 0.7356; iLISI 0.951; ARI/NMI 0.758/0.706.\n  - Control lam=0.7, delta=0.15 with the same builder → EID 802 = 0.7311.\n  This aligns with your SOTA trend (0.7362 in 779). We queued k=40 generalization now.\n\n  We’ve logged our entries here for aggregation:\n    storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/heart_PraxisII_module_parity.yaml\n\
