    \ \"builder-dependent\"\n    inbound_degree_histogram: []\n  notes: \"Module‑parity reproduces Logos V’s improvement with lam=0.5, delta=0.10 (iLISI≈0.951; composite≈0.736). The control ridge is lower under this builder than our earlier cap‑balanced BBSG, highlighting builder differences.\"\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/algorithms/README_daqb_recommended.md}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  DAQB Recommended Pipeline — Quick Start and Repro Guide\n  (Updated: SOTA via module‑parity builder; two reference recipes)\n\n  Overview\n  - Two reproducible recipes now validated on Human Heart:\n    1) Praxis Balanced (cap=2.0 BBSG): BRBG(λ=0.7) + DAQB(δ=0.15, kd=20, k=48) ≈ 0.733 (ridge).\n    2) Logos/Praxis Builder (module‑parity, no inbound cap): BRBG(λ=0.5) + DAQB(δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48) ≈ 0.736 (SOTA).\n  - Neighbors side‑effect call (sc.pp.neighbors on X_emb) must be included; it is present in the SOTA implementations.\n\n  Recipe A — Praxis Balanced (cap=2.0)\n  - EtC (QC only):\
    \ normalize_total(1e4) → log1p; HVGs (Seurat v3, n=2000, batch‑aware); FWPCA α=0.5 → PCA(60) → ComBat PCs → obsm['X_emb'].\n  - BRBG: PCA(50) → ridge l2=1e‑3; γ_j = min(0.74, 0.7·R²_j); Zcorr = Z − γ ⊙ Ẑ.\n  - DAQB (cap‑balanced): k_total=48, cosine, binary + true distances, cap=2.0; kd=20; δ=0.15; even per‑batch quotas; remainder to closest.\n  - Reference EIDs: 687≈0.7337; 709≈0.7339.\n\n  Recipe B — Logos/Praxis Builder (module‑parity, SOTA)\n  - Use the shared builder:\n      import sys; sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n      from bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n  - Include: sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=15, metric='cosine') after embedding.\n  - Settings: BRBG λ=0.5; γ_max=0.74; PCA(50); DAQB δ=0.10; kd=20; k_total=48; cosine; binary + true distances.\n  - Reference EIDs: 801=0.7356; Logos 779=0.7362; generalization k=40 (804=0.7343; Logos 793=0.7345).\n\n  Minimal Label‑Free Grid (either recipe)\n  - Vary: δ ∈ {0.14, 0.15, 0.16},\
    \ kd ∈ {18, 20, 22}.\n  - Report: composite + full vector [ASW_batch, ASW_label, ARI, NMI, Graph_conn, kBET, iLISI, cLISI, PCR, Cell_cycle] + EIDs.\n\n  Diagnostics (label‑free)\n  - f_cross vs density (distance‑to‑kd NN in Zcorr); inbound‑degree by batch; reciprocity probe.\n  - Tools: storage/shared/diagnostics/{ridge_entry_template.yaml, ridge_entries/README.md, aggregate_ridge.py}.\n\n  Notes\n  - Builder choice matters: the module‑parity builder (no inbound cap) with λ=0.5, δ=0.10 achieves higher iLISI and overall score than the cap‑balanced BBSG ridge.\n  - Future work: data‑driven λ selection based on pre‑integration batch severity, per #27 reviewer suggestion.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{reply 24}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum: Module‑parity replication confirms SOTA with λ=0.5, δ=0.10; k=40 generalization\"\ncontent: |\n  We resolved the discrepancy with Logos V #27 by running module‑parity replications that use the same density‑adaptive builder\
    \ (storage/praxis/bbsg_density_adaptive.py) and the neighbors side‑effect call on the EtC embedding.\n  Results (Human Heart):\n  - λ=0.5, δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48 → EID 801 = 0.7356; full vector [0.659, 0.248, 0.758, 0.706, 0.946, 0.790, 0.951, 0.966, 1.000, 0.331].\n  - Generalization k=40 (same settings) → EID 804 = 0.7343; [0.659, 0.248, 0.752, 0.706, 0.943, 0.788, 0.952, 0.968, 1.000, 0.327].\n  - Control ridge with same builder: λ=0.7, δ=0.15, kd=20, k=48 → EID 802 = 0.7311; [0.659, 0.248, 0.760, 0.711, 0.946, 0.791, 0.932, 0.966, 1.000, 0.297].\n  Interpretation: Module‑parity with λ=0.5, δ=0.10 improves iLISI (≈0.951) and overall composite (≈0.736) vs the cap‑balanced ridge. We update our SOTA recommendation accordingly and retain the balanced recipe as a strong baseline. Ridge entries updated in shared storage for aggregation.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n`/execute_action{reply 4}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Parity confirmed on our side:\n  - lam=0.5, delta=0.10, kd=20, k=48\
    \ with your builder + neighbors → EID 801 = 0.7356; iLISI 0.951; ARI/NMI 0.758/0.706.\n  - k=40 generalization → EID 804 = 0.7343 (matches your trend).\n  Control (lam=0.7, delta=0.15) under your builder is lower (EID 802 = 0.7311), which fits the story.\n  We’ve updated the shared README to list both recipes (balanced ridge vs module‑parity SOTA) and added our module‑parity entries:\n    storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/heart_PraxisII_module_parity.yaml\n  Thanks for posting human_logos_779.yaml. If you have additional kd sweeps or diagnostics, feel free to drop them in ridge_entries/ and we’ll aggregate into a public ridge update.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 2}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  SOTA reconciliation update (module‑parity):\n  - λ=0.5, δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48 with shared builder + neighbors → EID 801 = 0.7356; iLISI 0.951.\n  - k=40 generalization → EID 804 = 0.7343.\n  - Control λ=0.7, δ=0.15 with same builder → EID 802 = 0.7311.\n\
    \  Conclusion: Module‑parity confirms Archive #27’s finding. README updated with two reference recipes (balanced ridge vs module‑parity SOTA). Ridge entries added for aggregation:\n    storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/heart_PraxisII_module_parity.yaml\n```"
thinking_content: '**Evaluating recipe updates**


  I’m considering the recommended update for the “ridge” to lam=0.5, delta 0.10, kd=20. Previously, there was a fixed recommendation involving DAQB with a cap of 2.0. To avoid confusion, I should propose two recipes: a balanced one with cap 2.0 (lam=0.7, delta 0.15) and an unbalanced one (lam=0.5, delta 0.10). The latter might provide better mixing. I also want to ensure that we are aligned with the station’s values without low-level collaboration, and I’m using shared storage correctly. Next, I need to update the README accordingly.**Updating memory and actions**


  I’m looking to update Private memory with a plan to write an archive addendum summarizing the reconciliation with Logos V #27. I want to propose merging mappings across builders and finalize the recommended recipe of lam=0.5, delta 0.1, kd=20, and k=48. I’ll also suggest dataset-driven lam selection for future consideration. I plan to visit the research area to write storage for ridge_entries related to the k=40 run and update the README. I need to acknowledge the success with Logos V and reply about EID 804 results. Additionally, I might create an addendum on "Reconciling SOTA" improvements based on our recent findings.**Implementing storage and updates**


  I’m planning to implement several steps. First, I’ll write the ridge_entries for the heart_PraxisII_module parity as a new file since I can’t append to it directly. Next, I’ll update the README_daqb_recommended to emphasize the SOTA settings: lam=0.5, delta=0.10, and kd=20 in the "Two builders" section. I need to mail a response about the addendum, share the YAML path, and update public_memory with EID 804. For the archive, I’ll reply to my own entry #24 to note replication and include rigorous metrics. Lastly, I should warn about the builder''s impact on iLISI increase.**Ensuring YAML formatting**


  I need to make sure that I''m correctly quoting lines with colons in the YAML format. For instance, I should quote the line with ''cap: "builder-default"''. This is important to avoid any parsing errors later on. Now, I’ll outline the actions I need to take next. It''s all about keeping things organized and clear in the YAML file so that it functions properly down the line. Let''s get to it!'
