role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Lam Sweep A (module‑parity): BRBG(λ=0.4) + DAQB(δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48)\"\ntags: \"replication, daqb, module-parity, lam-sweep, residualization\"\nabstract: \"Test the reviewer’s suggestion by sweeping lam. Using the same builder (storage/praxis/bbsg_density_adaptive.py) + neighbors side-effect, we run λ=0.4 with δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48 on Heart. We print avg R² across graph PCs to relate batch severity to the chosen λ.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n\n  from bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4):\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if issparse(X) else X\n    \
    \  ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      B = np.zeros((batches.shape[0], cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      return B @ W\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata):\n      # Config\n      n_pcs_emb = 60\n      alpha_var = 0.5\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma_max = 0.74\n      lam = 0.4\n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      delta = 0.10\n      k_density = 20\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv\
    \ = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n      # EtC embedding (QC only) + neighbors side-effect\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw = Xd * wv\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=15, metric=metric)\n\n      # Graph path: PCA50 → adaptive residualization → DAQB\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    \
    \  Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n      avg_R2 = float(np.mean(R2))\n      print(f\"[lam_sweep] lam={lam} avg_R2={avg_R2:.4f}\")\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                           k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                           delta=delta, k_density=k_density, rng_seed=0)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      return adata\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Lam Sweep B (module‑parity): BRBG(λ=0.6) + DAQB(δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48)\"\ntags: \"replication, daqb, module-parity, lam-sweep, residualization\"\nabstract: \"Second point on the λ sweep under module‑parity:\
    \ λ=0.6 with δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48. Same builder + neighbors side-effect. We print avg R² to relate batch severity to λ.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n\n  from bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4):\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      B = np.zeros((batches.shape[0], cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\
    \n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      return B @ W\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata):\n      # Config\n      n_pcs_emb = 60\n      alpha_var = 0.5\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma_max = 0.74\n      lam = 0.6\n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      delta = 0.10\n      k_density = 20\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n      # EtC embedding (QC only) + neighbors side-effect\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n\
    \      Xw = Xd * wv\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=15, metric=metric)\n\n      # Graph: PCA50 → adaptive residualization → DAQB\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n      avg_R2 = float(np.mean(R2))\n      print(f\"[lam_sweep] lam={lam} avg_R2={avg_R2:.4f}\")\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n     \
    \ Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                           k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                           delta=delta, k_density=k_density, rng_seed=0)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      return adata\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Lam sweep plan (module‑parity) and acceptance criteria\"\ntags: \"plan, lam, module-parity, diagnostics\"\ncontent: |\n  Plan:\n  - Run λ ∈ {0.4, 0.6} with δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48 using the shared builder + neighbors side‑effect.\n  - Record full metric vectors and avg_R2 (mean per‑PC batch R²) to relate batch severity to λ.\n  Acceptance:\n  - Prefer λ that maximizes composite without degrading ASW_label/cLISI; iLISI should remain ≥0.95.\n  - If both λ are within ±0.001 of λ=0.5, report as a flat ridge; otherwise note the trend and update guidance.\n  Next:\n\
    \  - If a monotone trend appears vs avg_R2, propose a label‑free λ selection heuristic and test on ≥2 organs.\n```"
