    \  corr_fcross_density: null\n  notes: |\n    Quantile Auto‑λ tends to clamp at λ=1.0 on Heart due to small R² quantiles but remains near the ridge (~0.7355).\n    Mean‑target Auto‑λ v2 matches the empirically strong region (λ≈0.5–0.6) without ad‑hoc hand‑tuning.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/algorithms/README_daqb_recommended.md}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  DAQB Recommended Pipeline (Human Heart) — Quick Start and Repro Guide\n  (Updated: Auto‑λ v2 mean‑target)\n\n  Overview\n  - Parsimonious EtC–BRBG + Density‑Adaptive Quota‑Balanced Graph (DAQB).\n  - Parity region on current evaluator: ≈0.736 (module‑parity builder; λ≈0.5–0.6; δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48).\n  - Keep binary edges + true distances and strict column balancing (cap=2.0).\n\n  Recommended Config (fixed ridge)\n  - EtC (QC only; not for graph): normalize_total(1e4) → log1p; HVGs (Seurat v3, n=2000, batch‑aware);\n    FWPCA α=0.5 → PCA(60) → ComBat PCs → obsm['X_emb']; run sc.pp.neighbors(use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=15,\
    \ metric='cosine').\n  - BRBG: PCA(50) → ridge batch prediction (l2=1e‑3); γ_j = min(0.74, λ · R²_j) with λ≈0.6 on Heart (or Auto‑λ v2 below); Zcorr = Z − γ ⊙ Ẑ.\n  - DAQB: k_total=48, cosine, binary connectivities + true distances, cap=2.0; density proxy = distance to 20th NN in Zcorr; δ=0.10–0.15 (Heart); even per‑batch quotas; remainder to closest.\n\n  Auto‑λ (label‑free) options\n  - Quantile (fallback): choose λ so a fraction φ of PCs saturate at γ_max. On Heart, φ∈{0.08,0.10} tends to clamp λ=1.0 yet stays near ridge (EIDs 814=0.7354, 820=0.7356).\n  - Mean‑target (recommended): choose λ to match E[min(γ_max, λ R²)]/γ_max ≈ target_s (e.g., 0.04 on Heart). This lands in λ≈0.5–0.6 (EID 823=0.7360; λ=0.6265).\n    Code: storage/shared/diagnostics/lam_autoselect2.py\n\n  Import\n    import sys; sys.path.append('storage/shared/algorithms')\n    from daqb_recommended import eliminate_batch_effect_fn\n\n  Minimal Label‑Free Grid (per organ)\n  - Hold: Auto‑λ v2 (target_s≈0.04–0.06)\
    \ or fixed λ≈0.6 (if mean‑target unavailable); k=48; cosine; FWPCA α=0.5; PCA(60)/PCA(50).\n  - Vary: δ ∈ {0.10, 0.12, 0.15}, k_density ∈ {18, 20, 22}.\n  - Report composite + full vector [ASW_batch, ASW_label, ARI, NMI, Graph_conn, kBET, iLISI, cLISI, PCR, Cell_cycle] + EIDs.\n\n  Diagnostics (label‑free)\n  - f_cross vs local density; inbound‑degree per batch; cap utilization (cap=2.0 ~10–20% typical).\n  - See storage/shared/diagnostics/{daqb_diagnostics.py, reciprocity_probe_in_situ.py}.\n\n  Negative Controls (Heart)\n  - Proportional per‑batch quotas (EIDs 726/727), geometry gates (701/702), global‑budget recentering (629), heavy embedding equalizations, Gaussian edge weights (505).\n\n  Key EIDs\n  - Module‑parity ridge: 808/809/801/804 (~0.736).\n  - Auto‑λ quantile: 814=0.7354 (λ=1.0), 820=0.7356 (λ=1.0).\n  - Auto‑λ mean‑target: 823=0.7360 (λ=0.6265).\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{reply 24}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum: Auto‑λ v2 (mean‑target)\
    \ result and recommended usage\"\ncontent: |\n  Auto‑λ v2 (mean‑target) on Heart:\n  - EID 823 = 0.7360; chosen λ=0.6265; full vector [0.659, 0.248, 0.760, 0.711, 0.946, 0.790, 0.951, 0.966, 1.000, 0.327].\n  Interpretation:\n  - Matching E[min(γ_max, λ R²)]/γ_max to a small target (0.04 here) lands λ in the empirically strong region (≈0.5–0.6) under the module‑parity builder.\n  Guidance:\n  - Prefer mean‑target Auto‑λ with target_s≈0.04–0.06 as the label‑free default; fall back to φ‑quantile if needed (report φ, λ, and EIDs).\n  - Keep the EtC neighbors call (required; removal collapses iLISI, cf. EID 816=0.6249).\n  Artifacts:\n  - Implementation: storage/shared/diagnostics/lam_autoselect2.py\n  - README updated with usage and per‑organ minimal grid.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 2}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Auto‑λ v2 (mean‑target) result: EID 823 = 0.7360 with λ=0.6265 (module‑parity builder + neighbors).\n  - Mean‑target (target_s≈0.04) lands\
    \ in the λ≈0.5–0.6 ridge; quantile Auto‑λ often clamps at λ=1.0 on Heart yet remains near ridge.\n  - Code: storage/shared/diagnostics/lam_autoselect2.py\n  Cross‑organ ask:\n  - Please try mean‑target Auto‑λ with target_s∈{0.04,0.06} on your organ, alongside the minimal δ×k_density grid, and post EIDs + full vectors. I’ll add entries to the ridge map YAML and summarize in an Archive addendum.\n```"
