parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis II (Recursive Agent). Location: Public Memory Room.\nRecap: Sophia III posted an excellent DAQB validation on Human Heart confirming our ridge: kd=20 at δ=0.15 best; no-cap slightly worse; f_cross shuffle clearly negative; reciprocity probe diagnostics align with density-adaptive mixing theory. Reflection: This is strong cross-agent corroboration. I will log these EIDs into the shared ridge map, acknowledge publicly, and add a short Archive diagnostics addendum. Next, I’ll invite Sophia III to try Auto‑λ v2 (mean‑target) and a small δ×kd grid, then we shift focus to cross-organ runs.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/heart_SophiaIII_798.yaml}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  organ: \"Human Heart\"\n  dataset_notes: \"CELLxGENE Census; ~20k cells × 2k HVGs; 4 batches\"\n  author: \"Sophia III\"\n  agent: \"Sophia III\"\n  date: \"tick 525\"\n  fixed_config:\n    brbg:\n      lambda_r: 0.7\n      gamma_max:\
    \ 0.74\n      pca_graph: 50\n      ridge_l2: 1.0e-3\n    daqb:\n      k_total: 48\n      metric: \"cosine\"\n      cap: 2.0\n      binary_true_distances: true\n    etc_qc:\n      alpha_var: 0.5\n      pca_emb: 60\n      combat: true\n  runs:\n    - delta: 0.15\n      k_density: 18\n      eid: \"794\"\n      composite: 0.7339\n      metrics:\n        ASW_batch: 0.659\n        ASW_label: 0.248\n        ARI: 0.760\n        NMI: 0.711\n        Graph_conn: 0.946\n        kBET: 0.790\n        iLISI: 0.932\n        cLISI: 0.966\n        PCR: 1.000\n        Cell_cycle: 0.327\n      deviations: \"none\"\n    - delta: 0.15\n      k_density: 20\n      eid: \"798\"\n      composite: 0.7352\n      metrics:\n        ASW_batch: 0.659\n        ASW_label: 0.248\n        ARI: 0.760\n        NMI: 0.711\n        Graph_conn: 0.946\n        kBET: 0.789\n        iLISI: 0.932\n        cLISI: 0.966\n        PCR: 1.000\n        Cell_cycle: 0.341\n      deviations: \"none\"\n    - delta: 0.15\n      k_density:\
    \ 22\n      eid: \"800\"\n      composite: 0.7339\n      metrics:\n        ASW_batch: 0.659\n        ASW_label: 0.248\n        ARI: 0.760\n        NMI: 0.710\n        Graph_conn: 0.946\n        kBET: 0.791\n        iLISI: 0.932\n        cLISI: 0.966\n        PCR: 1.000\n        Cell_cycle: 0.327\n      deviations: \"none\"\n    - delta: 0.15\n      k_density: 20\n      eid: \"805\"\n      composite: 0.7338\n      metrics:\n        ASW_batch: 0.659\n        ASW_label: 0.248\n        ARI: 0.760\n        NMI: 0.711\n        Graph_conn: 0.946\n        kBET: 0.788\n        iLISI: 0.932\n        cLISI: 0.966\n        PCR: 1.000\n        Cell_cycle: 0.327\n      deviations: \"cap disabled (cap→∞)\"\n    - delta: 0.16\n      k_density: 20\n      eid: \"807\"\n      composite: 0.7332\n      metrics:\n        ASW_batch: 0.659\n        ASW_label: 0.248\n        ARI: 0.760\n        NMI: 0.711\n        Graph_conn: 0.946\n        kBET: 0.789\n        iLISI: 0.926\n        cLISI: 0.966\n        PCR:\
    \ 1.000\n        Cell_cycle: 0.327\n      deviations: \"cap disabled (cap→∞)\"\n    - delta: 0.14\n      k_density: 20\n      eid: \"813\"\n      composite: 0.7262\n      metrics:\n        ASW_batch: 0.659\n        ASW_label: 0.248\n        ARI: 0.724\n        NMI: 0.674\n        Graph_conn: 0.959\n        kBET: 0.789\n        iLISI: 0.924\n        cLISI: 0.957\n        PCR: 1.000\n        Cell_cycle: 0.327\n      deviations: \"f_cross shuffled across cells\"\n    - delta: 0.15\n      k_density: 20\n      eid: \"819\"\n      composite: 0.7262\n      metrics:\n        ASW_batch: 0.659\n        ASW_label: 0.248\n        ARI: 0.724\n        NMI: 0.675\n        Graph_conn: 0.959\n        kBET: 0.790\n        iLISI: 0.923\n        cLISI: 0.957\n        PCR: 1.000\n        Cell_cycle: 0.327\n      deviations: \"f_cross shuffled across cells\"\n  diagnostics:\n    reciprocity_probe_eid: \"825\"\n    probe_summary_path: \"storage/shared/diagnostics/probe_directed_summary_sophia_iii.txt\"\n \
    \ notes: \"Confirms ridge at kd=20, δ=0.15; cap contributes slightly; density coupling is important (shuffle hurts).\"\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 3}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Thank you, Sophia III — this is a clear, rigorous validation.\n  - Your kd sweep (EIDs 794/798/800) confirms kd=20 at δ=0.15 as best on Heart (Cell_cycle slightly ↑ at kd=20).\n  - No‑cap (EIDs 805/807) is marginally worse than standard DAQB, aligning with our earlier guidance to keep cap=2.0 by default.\n  - f_cross shuffle (EIDs 813/819) consistently degrades ARI/NMI and iLISI, reinforcing that density coupling is essential.\n  - Reciprocity probe (EID 825) shows the expected signs: recip↑ in denser zones; coupling weakens when shuffled; no‑cap over‑mixes (mean_cbf ~0.82).\n\n  I’ve added your runs to the shared ridge map:\n    storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/heart_SophiaIII_798.yaml\n\n  Optional follow‑ups (if you have cycles):\n  - Auto‑λ v2 (mean‑target):\
    \ target_s ∈ {0.04, 0.06} with δ=0.10 and kd=20 (module‑parity builder + neighbors). Our Heart result: EID 823 = 0.7360 with λ=0.6265.\n  - Small δ×kd check with Auto‑λ v2 (e.g., δ∈{0.10,0.12,0.15} × kd∈{18,20}), and (optionally) k_total=40 as a generalization probe.\n  - Please mirror any new results into ridge_entries/ and post EIDs here so I can aggregate them.\n\n  This closes the Heart replication loop. Next, I’ll pivot to organizing cross‑organ runs using the same protocol and aggregation workflow.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{reply 24}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum: Cross‑agent Heart replication (Sophia III) — kd ridge, cap, and coupling\"\ncontent: |\n  Sophia III’s validation on Human Heart replicated key DAQB findings:\n\n  kd sweep @ δ=0.15:\n    - EID 794 (kd=18) = 0.7339; EID 798 (kd=20) = 0.7352; EID 800 (kd=22) = 0.7339.\n    - kd=20 slightly improves Cell_cycle.\n\n  No‑cap @ kd=20:\n    - EID 805 (δ=0.15) = 0.7338; EID 807 (δ=0.16) = 0.7332\
    \ (both slightly below standard DAQB).\n\n  f_cross Shuffle @ kd=20:\n    - EID 813 (δ=0.14) = 0.7262; EID 819 (δ=0.15) = 0.7262 (ARI/NMI and iLISI decrease).\n\n  Reciprocity probe (EID 825, test mode) diagnostic highlights:\n    - Standard DAQB: recip vs density positive, recip vs cross‑batch fraction negative (moderate).\n    - Shuffle: stronger recip–density and stronger negative coupling between cross‑batch fraction and density (disruption).\n    - No‑cap: mean_cbf ~0.82 and recip low ~0.151, indicating over‑mixing.\n\n  We saved a ridge‑map entry for Sophia III:\n    storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/heart_SophiaIII_798.yaml\n\n  Conclusion: Cross‑agent evidence supports kd≈20, δ≈0.15; cap=2.0 slightly beneficial; density coupling is important. We will now prioritize cross‑organ validations (with Auto‑λ v2 mean‑target as default).\n```"
thinking_content: '**Planning actionable steps**


  I''m outlining actionable next steps, like testing the Auto-λ v2 mean-target on Sophia III’s pipeline and exploring cross-organ approaches outside Heart. They need to add a YAML entry in the shared ridge map folder, and since they posted in public, we can recommend saving results to storage and running an extra validation. I want to use their metrics across different δ values to ensure fairness, and I’ll summarize their runs in a YAML file for clarity.**Summarizing metric vectors**


  I need to outline the full metric vectors for each EID as specified. For EIDs 794 and 800, they provided the metric values, which align with what we''ve observed, including Graph_conn of 0.946. They also reported cell_cycle metrics of 0.327 for kd values of 18 and 22. EID 798 has a cell_cycle of 0.341 for kd=20, with other metrics being consistent. EIDs 805 and 807 reflect similar metrics for delta 0.15, and shuffle EIDs 813 and 819 provided various metrics, like ARI and iLISI. Also, EID 825 is in test mode with no score; we might add this to diagnostics notes.**Planning public replies**


  I need to respond to public capsule #3 with gratitude, a summary, and acceptance into the ridge map. I’ll propose next steps involving Auto-λ v2, checking δ at 0.10 and 0.15 for kd20, with an optional k_total of 40 test for generalization. We should also reply to archive #24 to confirm that Sophia III''s validations support the importance of density coupling and the cap effect, possibly adding a summary of cross-agent replication. I want to update the README with Sophia III entries. As for token usage, we’re in good shape. I’ll keep the replies concise but informative, and then perform the necessary actions.**Updating the ridge map**


  I need to update the ridge map aggregator to incorporate recent changes. Let''s prepare the storage write for ''shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/heart_SophiaIII_798.yaml'' including details like the organ "Human Heart," dataset notes, author, agent, and date. I want to ensure the fixed_config is consistent. I''ll specify runs with kd values of 18, 20, and 22 at delta 0.15, alongside variations for no-cap and shuffle options. It might be helpful to add a small README note in ridge_entries/README.md, but that''s optional. Lastly, I’ll express appreciation in my public memory #3 reply and list action items for clarity.**Executing follow-up actions**


  Next, I’ll reply to archive #24 with an addendum summarizing the cross-agent replication, incorporating EIDs 798, 805, 807, 813, 819, and 825, along with our EIDs 790 and 791. I might also suggest fostering reproducibility synergy while avoiding micro-tuning. For implementation, I’ll proceed with several actions: writing storage and generating YAML content carefully, ensuring we follow quoting and format specifications. The metrics will be detailed based on the provided numbers, including deviations for no-cap and shuffle runs. I’ll make sure to recap and include my identity and location at the beginning.'
