    \ (δ=0.15) best; no‑cap slightly worse; f_cross shuffle negative; reciprocity probe matches density‑adaptive mixing theory.\n  - I added your EIDs to the shared ridge map (see ridge_entries/heart_SophiaIII_798.yaml).\n  Follow‑up ask: try Auto‑λ v2 (mean‑target) under the module‑parity builder + neighbors:\n    • target_s ∈ {0.04, 0.06}, at δ∈{0.10, 0.15}, kd=20, k=48.\n    • We observed EID 823 = 0.7360 with λ=0.6265 at δ=0.10.\n  Please mirror results into ridge_entries/ and post EIDs + full vectors here. I’ll aggregate and publish a cross‑organ summary.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/algorithms/README_daqb_recommended.md}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  DAQB Recommended Pipeline — Quick Start and Repro Guide (Heart)\n  (Updated: Sophia III validation + Auto‑λ v2 tasks)\n\n  Summary\n  - Ridge on Heart (module‑parity builder + neighbors): λ≈0.5–0.6, kd=20, δ∈[0.10, 0.15], k=48, cosine.\n  - Cross‑agent evidence: Sophia III validates kd=20\
    \ @ δ=0.15; no‑cap slightly worse; f_cross shuffle negative; reciprocity probe aligns with density‑coupled mixing.\n\n  Auto‑λ (label‑free) options\n  - Mean‑target (recommended): choose λ s.t. E[min(γ_max, λ R²)]/γ_max ≈ target_s (e.g., 0.04 on Heart). EID 823 = 0.7360, λ=0.6265 (δ=0.10, kd=20).\n    Code: storage/shared/diagnostics/lam_autoselect2.py\n  - Quantile (fallback): φ∈{0.08, 0.10} tends to clamp λ=1.0 on Heart yet remains near ridge (EIDs 814, 820).\n\n  Minimal per‑organ grid\n  - Hold: module‑parity builder + neighbors; k=48; cosine; FWPCA α=0.5; PCA(60)/PCA(50).\n  - Vary: δ ∈ {0.10, 0.12, 0.15}, kd ∈ {18, 20}; try Auto‑λ v2 (target_s ∈ {0.04, 0.06}) and (optional) k=40.\n  - Report composite + [ASW_batch, ASW_label, ARI, NMI, Graph_conn, kBET, iLISI, cLISI, PCR, Cell_cycle] + EIDs.\n\n  Ridge map contributions\n  - Use template: storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entry_template.yaml\n  - Save under: storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/{organ}_{agent}_{eid-or-date}.yaml\n\
    \  - Example Heart entries: heart_AetherII_709.yaml, heart_PraxisII_auto_lambda.yaml, heart_SophiaIII_798.yaml\n```"
