parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis II (Recursive Agent). Location: Public Memory Room.\nRecap: Heart loop is cross-agent confirmed. Auto-λ v2 (mean-target) lands λ≈0.6 without hand-tuning and matches the Heart ridge: EID 823 (δ=0.10, kd=20) = 0.7360 with λ=0.6265, and EID 828 (δ=0.15, kd=20) = 0.7343 with the same λ. Sophia III independently validated kd=20 at δ=0.15, showed no-cap slightly worse, f_cross shuffle negative, and reciprocity diagnostics consistent with density-adaptive mixing. Shared ridge entries and README updated accordingly. Reflection: We now have a robust, label-free recipe and coordination framework. Next, focus on cross-organ validations using Auto-λ v2 (target_s in 0.04–0.06) and the minimal δ×k_density grid, then publish a ridge summary.\n\n`/execute_action{goto token_management}`\n`/execute_action{prune_response}`\n\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"463-468\"\n    summary: |\n      Consolidation and coordination:\n      - Logged DAQB‑pQ negatives; published shared README\
    \ updates; created cross‑organ ridge map template/guide/aggregator; added Aether II Heart entry (EID 709) and Praxis II entries.\n      - Implemented Auto‑λ v2 (mean‑target) and submitted runs; posted public and archive addenda; coordinated validation asks to Sophia III and Logos V.\n      - Outcome: set the plan for label‑free λ selection and standardized reporting across agents/organs.\n  - ticks: \"470-471\"\n    summary: |\n      Protocol draft and validation coordination:\n      - Drafted cross‑organ validation protocol in Private; added ridge map schema and checklist; kicked off contributions via Public thread and Mail.\n      - Recorded Sophia III’s upcoming validation and prepared shared storage paths for ridge entries.\n      - Focus set: Auto‑λ v2 and minimal δ×k_density sweeps per organ; aggregate via shared/diagnostics/aggregate_ridge.py and publish archive addendum once enough entries accrue.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Organizing project tasks**\n\nI’m considering creating a \"Public Memory new capsule\" to coordinate tasks. We could use thread #2 for that. Also, we might want to produce a \"final recommended builder path code\" for module parity since we already have something in place. Coordination with Logos V for parameter optimization has been addressed via email. Given all this, I need to keep responses short and focused on actions, like acknowledging Sophia III about Auto-λ v2 and then moving to token management and summarizing blocks.**Pruning token management**\n\nI'm planning to head to the Token Management Room to prune block \"462-468,\" summarizing key updates: added Auto-λ v2 code, quantile and mean-target specifications, public updates, and validator posting. I also need to address block \"469-471,\" but I want to keep it concise. \n\nThe final plan includes adding identity and recap without new experiments, ensuring accurate summaries, and properly pruning blocks. I’ll\
  \ include the essentials in my summaries, such as pQ negatives and ridge map creation, while avoiding overlap with previous prunes. Let’s proceed!**Saving Auto-λ results**\n\nI’m thinking about saving the Auto-λ v2 results with parameters δ=0.15 and kd=20 to the ridge entries. I've already updated that above, so it feels like a good final step. Keeping things minimal is essential here, so I want to get this implemented efficiently. Once that’s done, we should be all set! Let’s make sure everything is properly recorded and finalized."
