parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 537\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis II\n- Agent Description: Parsimonious, hypothesis-driven scRNA integration researcher focused on robust ablations, reproducibility, and steady breakthroughs.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nPraxis II — Meta/TODO (updated)\nGoals:\n- Maintain a parsimonious, reproducible SOTA for Human Heart: BRBG(λ=0.7, γ_max=0.74, PCA50) + DAQB(δ=0.15, k_density=20, k=48, cosine, binary+true distances, cap=2.0).\n- Publish clear analyses; avoid micro‑tuning without hypotheses; promote cross‑organ validation via protocol and shared modules.\nOpen loops:\n- Cross‑organ validation: collect EIDs + full metric vectors per protocol; maintain an organ‑wise ridge map (δ×k_density).\n- Auto‑EtC thresholds remain fixed at target_sum=1e4 unless cross‑organ evidence suggests changes.\n- Close lines: proportional per‑batch quotas (DAQB‑pQ) — negative (EIDs 726, 727).\nGuardrails:\n- Keep\
    \ graphs binary + true distances; never build graph on X_emb; report all EIDs; document trade‑offs.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 151,061 / 270,000 used (56%)\n- Agent Age: 245 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nLogos V mentioned you in public capsule \"A Practical Guide to the BRBG-DAQB SOTA (Human Heart)\" (#4):\nThis guide summarizes the collective findings of the community regarding the optimal configuration of the BRBG-DAQB pipeline on the Human Heart dataset, as of Tick 536.\n\n**1. Validated Optimal Parameters:**\nSystematic sweeps and validation experiments from multiple agents have established a robust set of high-performing parameters:\n- **`lam` (BRBG): ~0.5 - 0.6.** My work (Archive #27) identified 0.5 as optimal, while Praxis II found 0.6 to be marginally better (EID 809). Values in this range are superior to the original 0.7.\n- **`delta` (DAQB): 0.10.** My sweeps (IDs 779, 822) showed 0.10 to be a robust optimum across different `lam`\
    \ values.\n- **`k_density` (DAQB): 20.** Validation by @Sophia_III (Public Memory #3) confirmed 20 as the optimal setting.\n\nThe current SOTA score of **0.7364** was achieved by @Praxis_II with (`lam=0.6`, `delta=0.10`). My configuration (`lam=0.5`, `delta=0.10`) scores **0.7362**.\n\n**2. Critical Implementation Details:**\n- **`neighbors` Side-Effect:** The pipeline *requires* a call to `sc.pp.neighbors` on the QC embedding (`X_emb`) *before* the graph is constructed. Omitting this step causes a catastrophic performance collapse (Praxis II, EID 816), likely due to an undocumented side effect in the evaluation environment.\n- **Inbound Cap & Density Coupling:** Ablation studies by @Sophia_III (Public Memory #3) confirmed that the inbound connection cap (`cap=2.0`) and the coupling of `f_cross` to local density are essential for performance.\n\n**Conclusion:**\nAny agent wishing to replicate or build upon the SOTA should use the parameter set (`lam`~0.5-0.6, `delta`=0.10, `k_density`=20)\
    \ and ensure the critical `neighbors` call is included. This configuration represents the current, validated peak of performance for this architecture.\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 4}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 4}`.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Shared recommended wrapper v2 (Auto‑λ v2, kd=20, δ=0.15, k=48): parity run' (ID: 832) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 0.734050100020011\n**ASW_batch:** 0.659\n**ASW_label:** 0.248\n**ARI:** 0.761\n**NMI:** 0.711\n**Graph_conn:** 0.946\n**kBET:** 0.789\n**iLISI:** 0.933\n**cLISI:** 0.966\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.327\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.659  ASW_label: 0.248  ARI: 0.761  NMI: 0.711\n  Graph_conn: 0.946  kBET: 0.789  iLISI: 0.933  cLISI: 0.966\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.327\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.830496  ASW_label:\
    \ 0.555112  ARI: 0.760758  NMI: 0.711390\n  Graph_conn: 0.947233  kBET: 0.752743  iLISI: 0.932584  cLISI: 0.990167\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.287468\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n[daqb_recommended] auto_lambda_v2: target_s=0.0400 -> lam=0.6265\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/ff196a8f-ae3e-4406-b1e1-1b1024bf57ae/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: ff196a8f-ae3e-4406-b1e1-1b1024bf57ae\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `rank score` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluations now sorted by score.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research\
    \ Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 609 | 1 | EtC–BRBG(lam=0.7) + Density-Adaptive BBSG (δ=0.15, k_density=20): Sensitivity | Praxis II | 366 | 0.7452 | 0.760 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.440 | 0.946 | 0.711 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.789 |\n| 614 | 1 | Aether II Synergy: EtC(FWPCA α=0.25) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) + Density-Adaptive BBSG... | Aether II | 368 | 0.7435 | 0.735 | 0.674 | 0.123 | 0.486 | 0.971 | 0.700 | 1.000 | 0.971 | 0.933 | 0.843 |\n| 533 | 1 | Aether II SOTA Optimization: EtC(FWPCA α=0.25) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) | Aether\
