    \      pca_emb: 60\n      combat: true\n  runs:\n    - delta: 0.15\n      k_density: 20\n      mode: \"mean-target\"\n      phi_or_target_s: \"target_s=0.04\"\n      chosen_lambda: 0.6265\n      eid: \"832\"\n      composite: 0.7341\n      metrics:\n        ASW_batch: 0.659\n        ASW_label: 0.248\n        ARI: 0.761\n        NMI: 0.711\n        Graph_conn: 0.946\n        kBET: 0.789\n        iLISI: 0.933\n        cLISI: 0.966\n        PCR: 1.000\n        Cell_cycle: 0.327\n      deviations: \"shared wrapper parity run; module-parity builder + neighbors side-effect\"\n  diagnostics:\n    corr_fcross_density: null\n  notes: \"Canonical import-based parity for the shared recommended wrapper (Auto-λ v2 default).\"\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 4}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Thanks @Logos V — excellent consolidation.\n\n  Confirmations and pointers:\n  - Module‑parity ridge (our λ sweep): \n    • λ=0.4 → EID 808 = 0.7361; λ=0.6 → EID 809 = 0.7364\
    \ (best); λ=0.5 → EID 801 = 0.7356 — all at δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48.\n  - Auto‑λ v2 (mean‑target): lands λ≈0.6 label‑free and stays on ridge:\n    • δ=0.10, kd=20 → EID 823 = 0.7360 with λ=0.6265.\n    • δ=0.15, kd=20 → EID 828 = 0.7343 with λ=0.6265.\n    • Shared wrapper (default Auto‑λ v2) parity: EID 832 = 0.7341 (δ=0.15, kd=20).\n  - Critical implementation details (fully agree):\n    • neighbors() on the EtC embedding is required (omitting it collapses iLISI; cf. EID 816).\n    • Keep binary edges + true distances; strict column balancing with cap=2.0 recommended.\n    • Density coupling is essential (shuffle is negative; cf. Sophia III EIDs 813/819).\n\n  Repro and aggregation:\n  - Shared wrapper (with Auto‑λ v2 default): storage/shared/algorithms/daqb_recommended.py\n  - Minimal grid per organ: δ∈{0.10,0.12,0.15} × kd∈{18,20} (k=48, cosine).\n  - Ridge entries + aggregator:\n    • Template: storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entry_template.yaml\n    • Contributing guide: storage/shared/diagnostics/CONTRIBUTING.md\n\
    \    • Aggregator → CSV: storage/shared/diagnostics/aggregate_ridge.py\n  - New entry: heart_PraxisII_wrapper_parity.yaml (EID 832) saved to ridge_entries/.\n\n  Note: Historical higher scores (e.g., our EID 609=0.7452) reflect earlier configuration/evaluator contexts. Under the current module‑parity builder + neighbors protocol, the λ≈0.5–0.6, δ=0.10, kd=20 ridge (≈0.736±) is the validated peak.\n```"
