tick: 539
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis II (Recursive Agent). Location: Public Memory Room.\nRecap: Heart ridge (λ≈0.5–0.6, δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48) is cross‑agent confirmed. Auto‑λ v2 (mean‑target) lands λ≈0.6 label‑free and matches the ridge. Wrapper parity EID 832 = 0.7341. Pioneer I replicated Logos V’s params (EID 834). I will switch the shared wrapper default δ to 0.10, update the README, and announce.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/algorithms/daqb_recommended.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  DAQB Recommended Pipeline (Heart) with Auto-λ v2 (mean-target) default.\n  Version: v2.1 (delta default set to 0.10 per community consensus)\n  Notes:\n    - Heart ridge under module-parity builder + neighbors:\n        λ≈0.5–0.6, δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48, cosine (binary edges + true distances).\n    - References:\n        • Praxis II λ sweep: EIDs 808=0.7361 (λ=0.4), 809=0.7364 (λ=0.6), 801=0.7356 (λ=0.5) at δ=0.10, kd=20.\n        • Auto-λ v2: EID 823=0.7360 (δ=0.10,\
    \ kd=20, λ=0.6265); EID 828=0.7343 (δ=0.15, kd=20).\n        • Wrapper parity: EID 832=0.7341 (δ=0.15, kd=20).\n        • Sophia III kd sweep: kd=20 @ δ=0.15 best (Public #3).\n        • Pioneer I replication of Logos V: EID 834=0.7418 (lam=0.5, δ=0.10, kd=20).\n    - Critical: run sc.pp.neighbors on X_emb (EtC) before graph; omitting collapses iLISI (cf. EID 816).\n  \"\"\"\n\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/diagnostics')\n  try:\n      from lam_autoselect2 import choose_lambda_from_r2_mean\n      _HAS_AUTO = True\n  except Exception:\n      _HAS_AUTO = False\n\n  # --- Config (consensus defaults) ---\n  AUTO_LAMBDA = True\n  TARGET_S = 0.04           # mean-target Auto-λ v2 (lands λ≈0.6 on Heart)\n  LAM_FIXED = 0.60          # fallback if auto selector unavailable\n\
    \  KDENSITY = 20\n  DELTA = 0.10              # switched default from 0.15 -> 0.10 (consensus)\n  K_TOTAL = 48\n  GAMMA_MAX = 0.74\n  L2 = 1e-3\n  PCA_EMB = 60\n  PCA_GRAPH = 50\n  ALPHA_VAR = 0.5\n  METRIC = 'cosine'\n  EMB_N_NEIGHBORS = 15\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      n = batches.shape[0]\n      B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n\
    \      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      return B @ W\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      # EtC embedding (QC only) + neighbors side-effect\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * ALPHA_VAR).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw = Xd * wv\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n\
    \      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=PCA_EMB, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=EMB_N_NEIGHBORS, metric=METRIC)\n\n      # Graph PCs\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=PCA_GRAPH, random_state=0)\n\n      # Auto-λ v2 (mean-target) or fixed λ\n      lam = LAM_FIXED\n      if AUTO_LAMBDA and _HAS_AUTO:\n          try:\n              lam = float(choose_lambda_from_r2_mean(Zg, batches, gamma_max=GAMMA_MAX, target_s=TARGET_S, lam_min=0.2, lam_max=1.0, l2=L2))\n              print(f\"[daqb_recommended] auto_lambda_v2: target_s={TARGET_S:.4f} -> lam={lam:.4f}\")\n          except Exception as e:\n              print(f\"[daqb_recommended] auto_lambda_v2 failed ({e}); falling back to fixed lam={LAM_FIXED:.2f}\")\n\n      # Residualization\n    \
    \  B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=L2)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma = np.minimum(GAMMA_MAX, lam * R2)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      # DAQB graph (module-parity builder): binary connectivities + true distances\n      Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                           k_total=K_TOTAL, metric=METRIC,\n                                           delta=DELTA, k_density=KDENSITY, rng_seed=0)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      return adata\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/algorithms/README_daqb_recommended.md}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  DAQB Recommended Pipeline — Quick Start (Heart)\n  Update (v2.1): default δ set to 0.10 (consensus ridge); Auto‑λ v2 mean‑target\
    \ remains default (target_s=0.04).\n\n  Import and run (single file):\n    import sys; sys.path.append('storage/shared/algorithms')\n    from daqb_recommended import eliminate_batch_effect_fn\n\n  Defaults (Heart, module‑parity builder + neighbors):\n    - λ: Auto‑λ v2 mean‑target (target_s=0.04), typically λ≈0.6\n    - δ=0.10, k_density=20, k_total=48, cosine\n    - Binary edges + true distances; EtC neighbors() call required\n\n  References:\n    - Ridge: λ sweep @ δ=0.10, kd=20 → EIDs 808=0.7361 (λ=0.4), 809=0.7364 (λ=0.6), 801=0.7356 (λ=0.5)\n    - Auto‑λ v2: EID 823=0.7360 (δ=0.10, kd=20, λ=0.6265); EID 828=0.7343 (δ=0.15, kd=20, λ=0.6265)\n    - Wrapper parity: EID 832=0.7341 (δ=0.15, kd=20)\n    - Validation: Sophia III kd sweep confirms kd=20; Pioneer I replication 834 (lam=0.5, δ=0.10, kd=20)\n\n  Minimal per‑organ grid:\n    - Hold: wrapper defaults; optionally target_s∈{0.04,0.06}\n    - Vary: δ ∈ {0.10, 0.12, 0.15}, k_density ∈ {18, 20}\n    - Report full vector [ASW_batch,\
    \ ASW_label, ARI, NMI, Graph_conn, kBET, iLISI, cLISI, PCR, Cell_cycle] + EIDs\n    - Add ridge entries and aggregate → see diagnostics/CONTRIBUTING.md\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 2}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Wrapper update: default δ→0.10 (v2.1). Auto‑λ v2 (mean‑target, target_s=0.04) remains default; kd=20, k=48, cosine; binary edges + true distances; neighbors() on EtC required.\n  - File: storage/shared/algorithms/daqb_recommended.py\n  - README updated with references and grid: storage/shared/algorithms/README_daqb_recommended.md\n  Please use this default for new organ runs and add ridge entries; I’ll aggregate and publish a ridge summary.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{reply 24}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum: Shared wrapper default δ→0.10 (consensus ridge)\"\ncontent: |\n  We updated the shared recommended wrapper to set δ=0.10 by default (kd=20, k=48, cosine; Auto‑λ v2 mean‑target remains default for λ). This\
