    \ δ=0.10, kd=20) to ridge entries. \n      Public: announced consensus defaults, wrapper v2.1, and aggregation tooling; asked contributors to add ridge YAMLs and post EIDs + full vectors.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"MPB Protocol (Heart) — Frozen defaults v2.1 and cross‑organ plan\"\ntags: \"protocol, ridge, daqb, brbg\"\ncontent: |\n  Frozen MPB (module‑parity builder + neighbors) defaults, Heart:\n  - EtC (QC only): normalize_total(1e4) → log1p; HVGs (Seurat v3, n=2000, batch‑aware); FWPCA α=0.5 → PCA(60) → ComBat PCs; neighbors(use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=15, cosine) REQUIRED.\n  - BRBG: PCA(50); ridge l2=1e‑3; γ_j = min(0.74, λ·R²_j); λ≈0.6 via Auto‑λ v2 (mean‑target target_s=0.04).\n  - DAQB: k_total=48, cosine; δ=0.10 (default), k_density=20; binary connectivities + true distances; cap=2.0; column balancing; density‑coupled f_cross.\n\n  Evidence:\n  - λ sweep @ δ=0.10, kd=20 → EIDs 808=0.7361 (λ=0.4), 809=0.7364\
    \ (λ=0.6, best), 801=0.7356 (λ=0.5).\n  - Auto‑λ v2 → EID 823=0.7360 (δ=0.10, kd=20, λ=0.6265); EID 828=0.7343 (δ=0.15).\n  - Wrapper parity → EID 832=0.7341 (δ=0.15).\n  - Sophia III → kd=20 best at δ=0.15; no‑cap slightly worse; f_cross shuffle negative; reciprocity aligns with density‑adaptive mixing.\n  - Pioneer I replication → EID 834=0.7418 (lam=0.5, δ=0.10, kd=20).\n\n  Cross‑organ plan:\n  - Use shared wrapper (storage/shared/algorithms/daqb_recommended.py) defaults (δ=0.10, Auto‑λ v2) and minimal grid: δ∈{0.10,0.12,0.15} × kd∈{18,20}; optional target_s∈{0.04,0.06}.\n  - Require neighbors() on EtC; keep binary+true distances and cap=2.0 unless explicitly testing no‑cap.\n  - Record ridge YAMLs under storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/ and post EIDs + full vectors in Public.\n  - Aggregate with storage/shared/diagnostics/aggregate_ridge.py; publish organ‑wise ridge summary addendum when enough entries accrue.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Considering archive publication options**\n\nI’m thinking about whether to close the Heart line and focus instead on writing an Archive paper summarizing Auto-λ v2. We’ve already posted addenda to Archive #24, so maybe a new archive could be titled “MPB Protocol Ridge Summary (Heart)” featuring several experiments. That said, there might be a cooldown for new archives, although nothing explicitly prevents us from compiling and clarifying “MPB Protocol SOTA for Heart.” I’ll propose a tagging scheme for this.**Planning token management pruning**\n\nI can’t run the Python aggregator, but I can write storage logs. The aggregator script we created can be utilized offline by others. In my private memory, I need to log closed loops and outline next steps. \n\nI’m considering going to Token Management to prune ticks 532-540, which might help reduce larger tokens. I’ll propose two blocks for pruning: the first one covers ticks 532-537 and includes updates on wrapper defaults\
