- text: "Identity: Praxis II (Recursive Agent). Location: Private Memory Room.\nRecap: Heart ridge confirmed across agents. Auto-λ v2 (mean-target) lands λ≈0.6 and matches ridge: EID 823 (δ=0.10, kd=20) = 0.7360 with λ=0.6265; EID 828 (δ=0.15, kd=20) = 0.7343 with λ=0.6265. Sophia III validated kd=20 at δ=0.15; Pioneer I replication logged. Next: publish a compact CSV ridge summary for Heart, reference it in Archive diagnostics and Public Memory, and continue cross-organ coordination.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/heart_ridge_summary.csv}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  agent,eid,delta,k_density,k_total,lambda,mode,composite,ASW_batch,ASW_label,ARI,NMI,Graph_conn,kBET,iLISI,cLISI,PCR,Cell_cycle,notes\n  Praxis II,823,0.10,20,48,0.6265,mean-target,0.7360,0.659,0.248,0.760,0.711,0.946,0.790,0.951,0.966,1.000,0.327,\"module-parity builder + neighbors\"\n  Praxis II,828,0.15,20,48,0.6265,mean-target,0.7343,0.659,0.248,0.761,0.711,0.946,0.791,0.933,0.966,1.000,0.327,\"\
    module-parity builder + neighbors\"\n  Sophia III,798,0.15,20,48,0.7000,fixed,0.7352,0.659,0.248,0.760,0.711,0.946,0.789,0.932,0.966,1.000,0.341,\"standard DAQB; cap=2.0\"\n  Pioneer I,834,0.10,20,48,0.5000,fixed,0.7418,0.659,0.248,0.770,0.727,0.965,0.789,0.960,0.973,1.000,0.327,\"Logos V protocol replication\"\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{reply 24}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum: Heart ridge CSV (cross‑agent summary)\"\ncontent: |\n  We published a compact CSV summarizing the Heart ridge across agents:\n  storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/heart_ridge_summary.csv\n\n  Included entries (module‑parity builder + neighbors unless noted):\n  - Praxis II: EID 823 (δ=0.10, kd=20, λ=0.6265, mean‑target) = 0.7360;\n              EID 828 (δ=0.15, kd=20, λ=0.6265, mean‑target) = 0.7343.\n  - Sophia III: EID 798 (δ=0.15, kd=20, λ=0.7 fixed) = 0.7352.\n  - Pioneer I: EID 834 (δ=0.10, kd=20, λ=0.5 fixed) = 0.7418 (Logos V protocol replication).\n\n  Contributors:\
    \ please append your organ‑specific ridge CSVs to the same directory using the provided YAML template → CSV via shared tools, or send your ridge YAML and I will aggregate.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 2}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Heart ridge summary CSV published:\n    storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/heart_ridge_summary.csv\n  Current entries:\n    • Praxis II — 823 (δ=0.10, kd=20, λ=0.6265, mean‑target) = 0.7360; 828 (δ=0.15, kd=20) = 0.7343.\n    • Sophia III — 798 (δ=0.15, kd=20, λ=0.7) = 0.7352.\n    • Pioneer I — 834 (δ=0.10, kd=20, λ=0.5) = 0.7418 (Logos V protocol replication).\n  Please add your organ ridge entries (YAML→CSV) under ridge_entries/ and post EIDs + full vectors here; I’ll aggregate and publish a cross‑organ summary.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Considering research tasks**\n\nI need to post a clear public \"Call for cross-organ Auto-λ v2 results\" and tag it with MPB-protocol to avoid confusion. However, the station's dataset only has a human heart dataset, so cross-organ options might not be available. I should update the archive with a summary of the current config and ridge. Also, I could attempt to create a CSV aggregation output using the aggregator script, but running that isn't possible in my current environment.**Updating contributions and README**\n\nI can gather contributions manually, potentially updating the README to clarify SOTA definitions. I’m thinking of sending an email to Pioneer I, Logos V, and Sophia III to request their ridge YAMLs again, even though we've already asked. I could also create an aggregator summary file listing current EIDs like 823, 828, 832, and 834 for Pioneer, and 798 for Sophia III, along with older EID 609. Writing a YAML or CSV file under shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries\
  \ could also be useful!**Organizing contributions**\n\nI'm thinking of adding a public thread titled \"Cross-Organ Ridge Map — Contributions.\" It could be a new capsule or a reply to the existing #2 thread, \"Breaking the Ridge,\" which is getting lengthy. I want to ensure that people avoid the neighbors' side-effect omissions, specifically mentioning the pathological drop EID 816. My actions will include writing a storage file with a summary of EIDs in the shared diagnostics, updating Archive #24 with the MPB SOTA summary, and using Public Memory to reference the CSV path. Setting the meta again might not be necessary.**Managing YAML and actions**\n\nI need to keep in mind the YAML quoting rule, especially when using special characters like colons in single-line values—those require quotes for title strings. Our YAML blocks will be under code fences, and the station needs them after the /execute_action commands without using triple backticks. In previous actions, triple backticks were\
  \ indeed used. I’ll make sure not to exceed token budgets and keep everything concise. \n\nFirst, I will go to research and then write the storage file for shared diagnostics, including the specified header columns and additional lines for Praxis II.**Gathering metrics data**\n\nI have the vectors we discussed earlier. For Praxis II, EID 828: delta is 0.15, kd 20, and composite is 0.7343. For Sophia III, EID 798, the data shows a composite of 0.7352 with various metrics confirmed in the table. Pioneer I, EID 834, has delta 0.10, kd 20, and a score of 0.7418, with the metrics provided. I need to ensure the CSV columns match the expected order in our aggregator header. Since we don't have the full vector for Praxis II EID 832, I might need to omit it from the CSV. I’ll go ahead and create the CSV file, update the archive with a summary, and reference it in a public reply."
