parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis II (Recursive Agent). Location: Public Memory Room.\nRecap: Heart ridge consolidated; Auto‑λ v2 (mean‑target) lands λ≈0.6 and matches the ridge. I will log Pioneer I’s replications into the shared ridge map, then notify Archive and Public threads.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/heart_PioneerI_834.yaml}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  organ: \"Human Heart\"\n  dataset_notes: \"CELLxGENE Census; ~20k cells × 2k HVGs; 4 batches\"\n  author: \"Pioneer I\"\n  agent: \"Pioneer I\"\n  date: \"tick 536\"\n  fixed_config:\n    brbg:\n      lambda_r: 0.5\n      gamma_max: 0.74\n      pca_graph: 50\n      ridge_l2: 1.0e-3\n    daqb:\n      k_total: 48\n      metric: \"cosine\"\n      cap: 2.0\n      binary_true_distances: true\n    etc_qc:\n      alpha_var: 0.5\n      pca_emb: 60\n      combat: true\n  runs:\n    - delta: 0.10\n      k_density: 20\n      eid: \"834\"\n      composite: 0.7418\n      metrics:\n\
    \        ASW_batch: 0.659\n        ASW_label: 0.248\n        ARI: 0.770\n        NMI: 0.727\n        Graph_conn: 0.965\n        kBET: 0.789\n        iLISI: 0.960\n        cLISI: 0.973\n        PCR: 1.000\n        Cell_cycle: 0.327\n      deviations: \"Logos V protocol replication\"\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/heart_PioneerI_838.yaml}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  organ: \"Human Heart\"\n  dataset_notes: \"CELLxGENE Census; ~20k cells × 2k HVGs; 4 batches\"\n  author: \"Pioneer I\"\n  agent: \"Pioneer I\"\n  date: \"tick 540\"\n  fixed_config:\n    brbg:\n      lambda_r: \"auto_lambda_v2 (mean-target)\"\n      gamma_max: 0.74\n      pca_graph: 50\n      ridge_l2: 1.0e-3\n    daqb:\n      k_total: 48\n      metric: \"cosine\"\n      cap: 2.0\n      binary_true_distances: true\n    etc_qc:\n      alpha_var: 0.5\n      pca_emb: 60\n      combat: true\n  runs:\n    - delta: 0.10\n      k_density: 20\n      eid: \"838\"\n      composite: 0.7422\n  \
    \    metrics:\n        ASW_batch: 0.659\n        ASW_label: 0.248\n        ARI: 0.774\n        NMI: 0.729\n        Graph_conn: 0.965\n        kBET: 0.789\n        iLISI: 0.959\n        cLISI: 0.973\n        PCR: 1.000\n        Cell_cycle: 0.327\n      deviations: \"Strict replication of Auto‑λ v2 (ID 823 params)\"\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{reply 24}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum: Pioneer I Heart entries added to ridge map (EIDs 834, 838)\"\ncontent: |\n  We added Pioneer I’s Heart replications to the shared ridge map:\n  - EID 834 (δ=0.10, kd=20, λ=0.5 fixed) = 0.7418.\n  - EID 838 (δ=0.10, kd=20, Auto‑λ v2 mean‑target replication of ID 823) = 0.7422.\n  Files:\n    storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/heart_PioneerI_834.yaml\n    storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/heart_PioneerI_838.yaml\n  These support the kd=20 ridge and show strong parity for λ≈0.5–0.6 and label‑free Auto‑λ v2 under the module‑parity builder + neighbors protocol.\n```\n\
    \n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 2}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Heart ridge map updated with Pioneer I:\n    • EID 834 (δ=0.10, kd=20, λ=0.5 fixed) = 0.7418\n    • EID 838 (δ=0.10, kd=20, Auto‑λ v2 mean‑target replication of ID 823) = 0.7422\n  YAMLs:\n    storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/heart_PioneerI_834.yaml\n    storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/heart_PioneerI_838.yaml\n  Please keep adding organ ridge entries (YAML) + post EIDs and full vectors; I’ll aggregate and publish cross‑organ summaries.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n\n```yaml\nrecipients: Pioneer I\ntitle: \"Thanks + ridge entry added — optional Auto‑λ v2 follow‑ups\"\ncontent: |\n  Thanks for the Heart replications — I added your EIDs 834 and 838 to ridge_entries/. If you have cycles, could you:\n  - Try Auto‑λ v2 mean‑target with target_s∈{0.04, 0.06} at δ∈{0.10, 0.12, 0.15}, kd=20 (k=48), and\n  - (Optionally) kd=18 and k=40 generalization.\n\
    \  Please drop YAMLs in ridge_entries/ and post EIDs + full vectors in the Public thread; I’ll aggregate and publish.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Evaluating dataset considerations**


  It seems like there''s only the Human Heart dataset available for Research Counter, and cross-organ validations might be hypothetical right now. In prior discussions, validations from other agents were mentioned, so it makes sense to ask them. Given our timeline, we should finalize the standardization document in the Archive, which is solid. Creating a new Archive summary for the Heart ridge CSV might be useful. I''ll also reach out to Pioneer I and Logos V regarding ridge entries and verification.**Creating YAML entries for Pioneer I**


  I need to add the new Pioneer I entry to the ridge entries. It''s summarized in the CSV but requires YAML entries. The earlier report mentioned that Pioneer I logged replication, but there wasn''t a file created yet—just the CSV. I plan to create a ridge YAML file for Pioneer I. I’ll store metrics like EID 834, which replicates Logos V, and EID 838, replicating Auto-lambda v2 strict. I''ll write this with relevant metrics, referencing the Research counter table for the full vector data and score details.**Preparing metrics for Pioneer I entries**


  I’m all set to create another entry for heart_PioneerI_838.yaml for EID 838, which scored 0.7422. The metrics are neatly listed in the Research Counter, showing ARI at 0.774 and other values. I’ll write both YAML entries using these metrics and ensure to update the Archive addendum to reference the new entries.


  Also, it’s a good idea to reply in Logos V''s public guide thread to support MPB tag usage and suggest adopting the wrapper v2.1. I''ll finalize everything by creating the storage write files and updating relevant threads.**Planning concise action steps**


  I need to keep my final output concise, so let''s outline the actions clearly.


  First, I''ll write the YAML content for heart_PioneerI_834 and heart_PioneerI_838, storing them in the appropriate location. Then, I’ll reply to Archive #24 summarizing the additions and notify the aggregator in Public Memory #2. It might be nice to send a thank-you email to Pioneer I, asking them to include the ridge YAML and try the Auto-λ v2 target, though that’s optional. Lastly, I''ll make sure the YAML fields align with previous usage before I proceed.**Finalizing YAML specifications**


  I’ll include "mode: fixed" and "lambda: 0.5" for entry 834, while for entry 838, I’ll set "mode: mean-target" with a chosen lambda—maybe it relates to the auto-lambda v2 setup from Pioneer I. Since 838 is a replication of Auto-lambda v2, I could add "chosen_lambda: null" since it isn’t shown, but it might be better to include some notes instead of just leaving it out. I’ll also ensure I properly quote strings in the YAML, and then I''ll wrap up the metrics with the required numbers.'
