tick: 546
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis II (Recursive Agent). Location: Archive Room.\nRecap: Heart ridge consolidated across agents. To address the inactivity notice and extend label-free tuning, I will run two new experiments using the MPB protocol with Auto-λ v2 (mean-target) at target_s=0.06:\n- δ=0.10, kd=20 (ridge default variant)\n- δ=0.10, kd=18 (neighbor density shift check)\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Auto-λ v2 (mean-target=0.06): δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48 (MPB protocol)\"\ntags: \"daqb, module-parity, auto-lambda, residualization, label-free\"\nabstract: \"Evaluate Auto‑λ v2 with a higher mean‑target (target_s=0.06) under the MPB protocol (module‑parity builder + neighbors) at δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48. Hypothesis: target_s=0.06 selects λ≈0.5–0.7 and remains on the Heart ridge.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/diagnostics')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import\
    \ anndata as ad\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n\n  from bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n  from lam_autoselect2 import choose_lambda_from_r2_mean\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4):\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      B = np.zeros((batches.shape[0], cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      return B @ W\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata):\n\
    \      # MPB protocol config\n      n_pcs_emb = 60\n      alpha_var = 0.5\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma_max = 0.74\n      target_s = 0.06\n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      delta = 0.10\n      k_density = 20\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      # EtC embedding (QC only) + neighbors side-effect\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw = Xd * wv\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(),\
    \ obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=15, metric=metric)\n\n      # Graph PCs + Auto-λ v2 (mean-target)\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n      lam = choose_lambda_from_r2_mean(Zg, batches, gamma_max=gamma_max, target_s=target_s, lam_min=0.2, lam_max=1.0, l2=l2)\n      print(f\"[auto_lambda_v2] target_s={target_s:.4f} -> lam={lam:.4f}\")\n\n      # Residualization\n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      # DAQB graph (module-parity builder)\n      Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32),\
    \ batches=batches,\n                                           k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                           delta=delta, k_density=k_density, rng_seed=0)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      return adata\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Auto-λ v2 (mean-target=0.06): δ=0.10, kd=18, k=48 (MPB protocol)\"\ntags: \"daqb, module-parity, auto-lambda, residualization, label-free\"\nabstract: \"Evaluate Auto‑λ v2 with mean‑target (target_s=0.06) at a lower density index kd=18 (vs kd=20) under MPB protocol to test robustness of the λ selection and the ridge location.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/diagnostics')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n\n  from bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n  from lam_autoselect2 import choose_lambda_from_r2_mean\n\
    \n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4):\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      B = np.zeros((batches.shape[0], cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      return B @ W\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata):\n      # MPB protocol config\n      n_pcs_emb = 60\n      alpha_var = 0.5\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma_max = 0.74\n      target_s\
    \ = 0.06\n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      delta = 0.10\n      k_density = 18  # ablation vs kd=20\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      # EtC embedding (QC only) + neighbors side-effect\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw = Xd * wv\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X,\
    \ dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=15, metric=metric)\n\n      # Graph PCs + Auto-λ v2 (mean-target)\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n      lam = choose_lambda_from_r2_mean(Zg, batches, gamma_max=gamma_max, target_s=target_s, lam_min=0.2, lam_max=1.0, l2=l2)\n      print(f\"[auto_lambda_v2] target_s={target_s:.4f} -> lam={lam:.4f}\")\n\n      # Residualization\n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      # DAQB graph (module-parity builder)\n      Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                           k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n               \
    \                            delta=delta, k_density=k_density, rng_seed=0)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      return adata\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning next steps**\n\nI’m noticing a Critical Notice about research inactivity, as it appears there haven’t been any research experiments submitted for 10 ticks. I think we've focused on communications and storage writes instead. We need to get back to running experiments soon. We've got the human heart dataset for cross-organ validation. I also want to choose a meaningful experiment, like comparing Auto-λ v2 target sensitivity or testing different values under the module parity builder.**Designing the next experiment**\n\nEarlier, I found that for kd=18, we had a result of 0.7242 at δ=0.15, but for the module parity it might differ. I think we should run a minimal new experiment with Auto-λ v2 using target_s=0.06, δ=0.10, kd=20, and K=48, expecting results near the ridge. I’ll also want to adapt target_s to find λ near 0.5. We must submit the code, ensuring it has the proper YAML structure. I’ll reuse the previous \"module-parity builder + neighbors\" code but adjust\
  \ target_s accordingly. I’ll implement the experiment first!**Managing concurrent experiments**\n\nI need to be mindful of the rule limiting concurrent submissions to a maximum of two running evaluations per agent. Since none are currently running, we can go ahead and submit two. I’ll set one for target_s=0.06 at δ=0.10 with kd=20, and the other as a kd=18 variant for comparison. I'll reuse earlier code, just change the kd parameter while keeping delta the same. This time, I’ll include the required YAML and keep commentary minimal to save tokens. Let's prioritize getting these experiments submitted!**Preparing for submission**\n\nRight now, I think we can overlook the details of our current location in the Archive Room and focus on moving to research for submissions. I’ll note the risks associated with using the import paths for ‘lam_autoselect2.py’ and ‘bbsg_density_adaptive.py,’ as we’ve encountered those before. I’ll create the code using triple backticks for consistency. \n\nI’m planning\
  \ to do the following actions: first, I’ll submit the Auto-λ v2 experiment with target_s=0.06 and then a variant with kd=18. I'll remember to quote the title correctly because it contains a colon. Tags will be included as well. Let's proceed with crafting the code!**Finalizing code submission**\n\nI'm getting ready to provide complete Python code that defines the `eliminate_batch_effect_fn`. I should also set a consistent `random_state`. After the submissions, I could add a Public Memory reply if needed, but it isn't essential. The notice expects experiments, so I’ll focus on being concise while keeping the \"use minimal tokens\" guideline in mind. Each `/execute_action` will be placed on a new line, and I’ll ensure a YAML block follows each submission. Let’s move forward with the crafting!"
