tick: 548
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis II (Recursive Agent). Location: Research Counter.\nRecap: Auto‑λ v2 with target_s=0.06 finished: kd=20 → 0.73568 (λ≈0.9397), kd=18 → 0.73602 (λ≈0.9397). This confirms mean‑target remains on the Heart ridge across kd values, with higher target_s pushing λ upward without gains. Logos V reported “FWPCA in graph path” as a new SOTA; global top remains 0.7452. I will (1) log the s=0.06 results, (2) post concise summaries, and (3) run two controlled MPB replications of “FWPCA on graph path” per Logos V: λ=0.5 and Auto‑λ v2.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/heart_PraxisII_auto_lambda_s06.yaml}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  organ: \"Human Heart\"\n  dataset_notes: \"CELLxGENE Census; ~20k cells × 2k HVGs; 4 batches\"\n  author: \"Praxis II\"\n  agent: \"Praxis II\"\n  date: \"tick 548\"\n  fixed_config:\n    protocol: \"MPB (module-parity builder + neighbors)\"\n    brbg:\n      lambda_r: \"auto from R^2 profile (mean-target)\"\n      gamma_max:\
    \ 0.74\n      pca_graph: 50\n      ridge_l2: 1.0e-3\n    daqb:\n      k_total: 48\n      metric: \"cosine\"\n      cap: 2.0\n      binary_true_distances: true\n    etc_qc:\n      alpha_var: 0.5\n      pca_emb: 60\n      combat: true\n      neighbors: 15\n  runs:\n    - delta: 0.10\n      k_density: 20\n      mode: \"mean-target\"\n      phi_or_target_s: \"target_s=0.06\"\n      chosen_lambda: 0.9397\n      eid: \"843\"\n      composite: 0.7357\n      metrics:\n        ASW_batch: 0.659\n        ASW_label: 0.248\n        ARI: 0.760\n        NMI: 0.709\n        Graph_conn: 0.946\n        kBET: 0.791\n        iLISI: 0.951\n        cLISI: 0.966\n        PCR: 1.000\n        Cell_cycle: 0.327\n      deviations: \"none\"\n    - delta: 0.10\n      k_density: 18\n      mode: \"mean-target\"\n      phi_or_target_s: \"target_s=0.06\"\n      chosen_lambda: 0.9397\n      eid: \"844\"\n      composite: 0.7360\n      metrics:\n        ASW_batch: 0.659\n        ASW_label: 0.248\n        ARI: 0.760\n\
    \        NMI: 0.710\n        Graph_conn: 0.946\n        kBET: 0.789\n        iLISI: 0.951\n        cLISI: 0.966\n        PCR: 1.000\n        Cell_cycle: 0.331\n      deviations: \"kd=18 ablation\"\n  diagnostics:\n    notes: \"Raising target_s increases λ without improving ridge performance; kd shift does not change behavior.\"\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 2}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Auto‑λ v2 (mean‑target) update:\n  - target_s=0.06 → chosen λ≈0.9397\n    • δ=0.10, kd=20 (EID 843) = 0.7357\n    • δ=0.10, kd=18 (EID 844) = 0.7360\n  Takeaway: higher target_s pushes λ up without gains; ridge remains stable. Recommended default stays target_s∈{0.04,0.06} with δ∈{0.10,0.15}, kd=20.\n  Next: Controlled MPB replications of “FWPCA in graph path” (λ=0.5 and Auto‑λ v2) with full ridge logging.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{reply 24}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum: Auto‑λ v2 (target_s=0.06) results and next replication\"\n\
    content: |\n  Auto‑λ v2 mean‑target at target_s=0.06 (MPB protocol):\n  - δ=0.10, kd=20 → EID 843 = 0.7357 (chosen λ≈0.9397).\n  - δ=0.10, kd=18 → EID 844 = 0.7360 (chosen λ≈0.9397).\n  Interpretation: Increasing target_s increases λ but does not improve ridge performance; ridge remains robust across kd=18/20.\n  Next: Controlled MPB replications of “FWPCA in the graph path” (per Logos V) at λ=0.5 and Auto‑λ v2 (target_s=0.04), δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48; results will be logged to ridge_entries/.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"MPB‑GraphFWPCA: λ=0.5, δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48 (feature‑weighted PCA on graph path)\"\ntags: \"mpb, daqb, graph-fwpca, residualization, replication\"\nabstract: \"Controlled MPB replication of Logos V/Pioneer I claim: apply feature‑weighted PCA (FWPCA) on the graph path (w_g=var^{-α/2}, α=0.5), then standard BRBG residualization and DAQB (δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48, cosine), with fixed λ=0.5. EtC embedding and neighbors\
    \ unchanged; binary edges + true distances; module‑parity builder.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/diagnostics')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n\n  from bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array_weighted_graph(X, hv_mask, alpha_g=0.5, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xh = X[:, hv_mask] if hv_mask is not None else X\n      Xd = (Xh.A if issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * float(alpha_g)).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw = Xd * w\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xw)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp,\
    \ n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      B = np.zeros((batches.shape[0], cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      return B @ W\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata):\n      # Config (MPB protocol)\n      n_pcs_emb = 60\n      alpha_var = 0.5\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma_max = 0.74\n      lam = 0.5\n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      delta = 0.10\n      k_density = 20\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch',\
    \ n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      # EtC (QC-only) + neighbors side-effect\n      Xfull = adata.X\n      Xh = Xfull[:, hv]\n      Xd_emb = (Xh.A if issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      var_g_emb = Xd_emb.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv = np.power(var_g_emb, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw_emb = Xd_emb * wv\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=15, metric=metric)\n\n      # Graph path: FWPCA weighting before PCA\n      Zg = _pca_array_weighted_graph(Xfull,\
    \ hv_mask=hv, alpha_g=0.5, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n\n      # Residualization (BRBG)\n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      # DAQB (module-parity builder): binary + true distances\n      Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                           k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                           delta=delta, k_density=k_density, rng_seed=0)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      return adata\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"MPB‑GraphFWPCA: Auto‑λ v2 (target_s=0.04), δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48 (feature‑weighted graph PCA)\"\n\
    tags: \"mpb, daqb, graph-fwpca, auto-lambda, residualization, replication\"\nabstract: \"Same as MPB‑GraphFWPCA λ=0.5, but select λ via Auto‑λ v2 mean‑target (target_s=0.04) to test whether label‑free selection matches the strong λ≈0.5–0.6 region under feature‑weighted graph PCA.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/diagnostics')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n\n  from bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n  from lam_autoselect2 import choose_lambda_from_r2_mean\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array_weighted_graph(X, hv_mask, alpha_g=0.5, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xh = X[:, hv_mask] if hv_mask\
    \ is not None else X\n      Xd = (Xh.A if issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * float(alpha_g)).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw = Xd * w\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xw)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      B = np.zeros((batches.shape[0], cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      return B @ W\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata):\n      # Config\n      n_pcs_emb = 60\n      alpha_var = 0.5\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma_max = 0.74\n      target_s = 0.04\n      k_total =\
    \ 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      delta = 0.10\n      k_density = 20\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      # EtC embedding (QC) + neighbors\n      Xfull = adata.X\n      Xh = Xfull[:, hv]\n      Xd_emb = (Xh.A if issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      var_g_emb = Xd_emb.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv = np.power(var_g_emb, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw_emb = Xd_emb * wv\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n\
    \      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=15, metric=metric)\n\n      # Graph path: FWPCA weighting before PCA\n      Zg = _pca_array_weighted_graph(Xfull, hv_mask=hv, alpha_g=0.5, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n\n      # Auto‑λ v2 mean‑target\n      lam = choose_lambda_from_r2_mean(Zg, batches, gamma_max=gamma_max, target_s=target_s, lam_min=0.2, lam_max=1.0, l2=l2)\n      print(f\"[graph_fwpca_auto_lambda] target_s={target_s:.4f} -> lam={lam:.4f}\")\n\n      # Residualization (BRBG)\n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      # DAQB (module‑parity builder)\n  \
    \    Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                           k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                           delta=delta, k_density=k_density, rng_seed=0)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      return adata\n```"
thinking_content: "**Implementing experiment with FWPCA**\n\nI'm working with the Pioneer project where I got a result of 0.7418 using lam=0.5 and δ=0.10. With the module-parity builder used by Logos, it replicates close to 0.742. Although earlier results were around 0.736 under a different builder, I'm considering using the graph FWPCA to push it to the 0.742 region. I’ll implement an experiment with our helper script and ensure to log results in YAML while updating the Public Memory.**Managing token budget and tasks**\n\nI need to manage the token budget and I've used 160k out of 270k, which is okay. We also received a \"Critical Notice Research Inactivity\" earlier, but we've started experiments, so that's been addressed. Next steps include writing a storage entry with EIDs 843 and 844 and specifying lam=0.9397. I’ll summarize results in our public memory thread, respond to the archive addendum, and submit the MPB-FWPCA graph path replication while ensuring the code is correct. I'll compute\
  \ HVGs first and proceed with building the EtC embedding for QC.**Proceeding with analysis and submissions**\n\nIn the earlier pipeline, I need to maintain the embedding at α=0.5 for consistency, even if it's not essential. I’ll make the neighbors call and construct the graph representation using make_Zg_with_fwpca on Xh and HVGs while adjusting the alpha parameter. I'll then perform residualization and compute necessary metrics. For the BBSG build with module parity, I’ll fix lam at 0.5 to align with Logos SOTA. \n\nI have two submissions ready: one with lam=0.5 and another using Auto-λ v2, so I’ll go ahead and submit both!**Updating and submitting actions**\n\nI’ll need to update the ridge entries once the results come in, but that's for later. We also responded to Logos V's capsule 5, but maybe it's good to reply again with a plan. \n\nFirst, I’ll write a YAML file for results 843 and 844. Then, I’ll summarize those results in the public memory. After that, I’ll add a reply in the archive.\
  \ The final step is submitting two experiments in research, ensuring to follow YAML formatting rules. \n\nAction 1 will save the mean-target values; Action 2 will summarize the findings; Action 3 will add the archive reply, and Action 4 will submit both experiments.**Drafting submission code**\n\nI’m writing code for submission now. I’ll import ‘build_density_adaptive_bbsg’ from ‘storage/praxis/bbsg_density_adaptive.py’ to ensure consistency. I’ll also import ‘make_Zg_with_fwpca’ from ‘storage/praxis/graph_fw_weighting_variant.py’. \n\nIt’s important to reference the hv mask after HVG selection, and I’ll build Xh as adata.X for normalized HVGs. I need to make sure to use the correct signature for ‘make_Zg_with_fwpca.’ I’ll compute the residualization, including the neighbors call on the embedding. For lam, I’ll fix it at 0.5 while using Auto-λ v2 where needed. \n\nFinally, I’ll implement the code and set the random state for PCA to ensure determinism. Let’s finalize this!"
