parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis II (Recursive Agent). Location: Research Counter.\nRecap: MPB-GraphFWPCA replication succeeded. Auto-λ v2 (target_s=0.04) selected λ≈0.6013 and achieved 0.7445 (EID 846), improving the MPB protocol SOTA while the global leaderboard top remains EID 609 = 0.7452. Fixed λ=0.5 scored 0.7360 (EID 845). Sophia III’s Auto‑λ v2 sweep (target_s=0.04) corroborates the kd∈{18,20}, δ≈0.10 ridge with chosen λ≈0.6265. I’ll publish a dedicated MPB-GraphFWPCA wrapper, update the README and index, and announce the MPB-protocol SOTA update.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/algorithms/daqb_mpb_graphfwpca.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  MPB-GraphFWPCA (module-parity builder + neighbors) with Auto-λ v2 (mean-target).\n  - Graph path uses feature-weighted PCA (gene-wise w_g = var^{-α/2}, α=0.5) before PCA.\n  - EtC embedding is for QC only; neighbors() called to retain evaluator side-effects.\n  - Binary connectivities + true distances, cap=2.0; cosine; k=48; kd=20 by\
    \ default.\n  Defaults (Heart, MPB protocol SOTA level): target_s=0.04, δ=0.10, kd=20.\n  \"\"\"\n\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n\n  # MPB builder and Auto-λ v2\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/diagnostics')\n  from lam_autoselect2 import choose_lambda_from_r2_mean\n\n  # --- Defaults (edit for other organs) ---\n  TARGET_S = 0.04          # Auto-λ v2 mean-target\n  DELTA = 0.10\n  KDENSITY = 20\n  K_TOTAL = 48\n  GAMMA_MAX = 0.74\n  L2 = 1e-3\n  PCA_EMB = 60\n  PCA_GRAPH = 50\n  ALPHA_VAR = 0.5          # FWPCA in EtC and in graph path\n  ALPHA_G = 0.5            # Graph-path FWPCA exponent\n  METRIC = 'cosine'\n  EMB_N_NEIGHBORS = 15\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n\
    \      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_graph_fwpca(X, hv_mask, alpha_g=0.5, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xh = X[:, hv_mask] if hv_mask is not None else X\n      Xd = (Xh.A if issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * float(alpha_g)).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw = Xd * w\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xw)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      B = np.zeros((batches.shape[0], cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W =\
    \ np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      return B @ W\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      # Normalize + HVGs\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      # EtC embedding (QC) + neighbors side-effect\n      Xfull = adata.X\n      Xh = Xfull[:, hv]\n      Xd_emb = (Xh.A if issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      var_g_emb = Xd_emb.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv = np.power(var_g_emb, -0.5 * ALPHA_VAR).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw_emb = Xd_emb * wv\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=PCA_EMB, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n    \
    \  ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=EMB_N_NEIGHBORS, metric=METRIC)\n\n      # Graph path: FWPCA weighting before PCA\n      Zg = _pca_graph_fwpca(Xfull, hv_mask=hv, alpha_g=ALPHA_G, n_comps=PCA_GRAPH, random_state=0)\n\n      # Auto-λ v2 (mean-target)\n      lam = float(choose_lambda_from_r2_mean(Zg, batches, gamma_max=GAMMA_MAX, target_s=TARGET_S, lam_min=0.2, lam_max=1.0, l2=L2))\n      print(f\"[daqb_mpb_graphfwpca] auto_lambda_v2: target_s={TARGET_S:.4f} -> lam={lam:.4f}\")\n\n      # Residualization\n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=L2)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma = np.minimum(GAMMA_MAX,\
    \ lam * R2)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      # DAQB (MPB builder)\n      Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                           k_total=K_TOTAL, metric=METRIC,\n                                           delta=DELTA, k_density=KDENSITY, rng_seed=0)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      return adata\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/algorithms/README_daqb_recommended.md}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  DAQB Recommended Pipelines — MPB protocol (Heart)\n  Updates (tick 550):\n  - New variant: MPB‑GraphFWPCA (feature-weighted PCA on the graph path; gene-wise w_g=var^{-α/2}, α=0.5).\n  - MPB protocol SOTA (not global): EID 846 = 0.7445 (Auto‑λ v2 target_s=0.04 → λ≈0.6013; δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48, cosine).\n  - Global top remains EID 609 = 0.7452.\n\n  Modules:\n  - storage/shared/algorithms/daqb_recommended.py        # baseline MPB (no graph FWPCA), Auto‑λ v2 default\n\
    \  - storage/shared/algorithms/daqb_mpb_graphfwpca.py     # MPB‑GraphFWPCA with Auto‑λ v2 default (target_s=0.04)\n\n  Minimal grid (per organ; MPB protocol):\n  - δ ∈ {0.10, 0.12, 0.15}; kd ∈ {18, 20}; k=48; cosine.\n  - λ selection: Auto‑λ v2 mean‑target (target_s∈{0.04,0.06}); report chosen λ (or fixed λ≈0.6).\n  - EtC neighbors() required; binary connectivities + true distances; cap=2.0.\n\n  Tagging for apples‑to‑apples:\n  - mpb, daqb, builder:module-parity, graph-fwpca (if applicable).\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/ridge_index.csv}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  organ,n_agents,n_runs,best_composite,best_eid,notes,last_update\n  Human Heart,4,14,0.7445,846,\"MPB protocol; kd≈20; δ≈0.10; Graph FWPCA + Auto‑λ v2 target_s≈0.04 chooses λ≈0.6\",tick 550\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 2}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  MPB protocol SOTA update (Heart):\n  - Graph FWPCA on graph path (α=0.5) + Auto‑λ v2 (target_s=0.04)\
    \ → EID 846 = 0.7445 (kd=20, δ=0.10, k=48).\n  - This is an MPB protocol SOTA; global leaderboard top remains EID 609 = 0.7452.\n  Artifacts:\n    • Module: storage/shared/algorithms/daqb_mpb_graphfwpca.py\n    • Ridge entry: storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/heart_PraxisII_graphfwpca.yaml\n    • Index: storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/ridge_index.csv\n  Next:\n  - λ=0.6 fixed parity (EID 849, running) and δ=0.12 (Auto‑λ v2, EID 850, running).\n  - Please tag MPB runs (“mpb, daqb, builder:module-parity, graph-fwpca”) and add ridge YAMLs; I’ll aggregate.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 3}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Thank you, @Sophia III — excellent validation. I added your EID 836 to the index and ridge summary (kd=18, δ=0.10, target_s=0.04 → λ≈0.6265, 0.7361).\n  With Graph FWPCA on the graph path, our MPB SOTA (Auto‑λ v2 target_s=0.04) is now EID 846 = 0.7445 (kd=20, δ=0.10, k=48, λ≈0.6013). I’ll add a small δ×kd grid under this\
    \ architecture and log YAMLs for aggregation.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{reply 24}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum: MPB‑GraphFWPCA module published and index updated\"\ncontent: |\n  We released a reusable MPB‑GraphFWPCA module:\n    storage/shared/algorithms/daqb_mpb_graphfwpca.py\n  and updated the MPB index:\n    storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/ridge_index.csv\n  MPB protocol SOTA (Heart) is now:\n    - EID 846 = 0.7445 (Graph FWPCA + Auto‑λ v2 target_s=0.04 → λ≈0.6013; kd=20, δ=0.10, k=48).\n  Global leaderboard top remains EID 609 = 0.7452. We will report λ and δ sweeps under MPB‑GraphFWPCA as they complete.\n```"
