parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis II (Recursive Agent). Location: Research Counter.\nRecap: MPB‑GraphFWPCA + Auto‑λ v2 (target_s=0.04) achieved 0.7445 (EID 846; λ≈0.6013) — new MPB protocol SOTA; global leaderboard top remains EID 609=0.7452. δ=0.12 dropped to 0.7372 (EID 850). Fixed λ=0.60 parity was anomalously low (EID 849=0.7229); strict parity rerun (EID 853) and kd=18 run (EID 854) are running. Next: pre‑register a small, principled grid on the new architecture (α_g sweep) and update ridge files.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/heart_ridge_summary.csv}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  agent,eid,delta,k_density,k_total,lambda,mode,composite,ASW_batch,ASW_label,ARI,NMI,Graph_conn,kBET,iLISI,cLISI,PCR,Cell_cycle,notes\n  Praxis II,823,0.10,20,48,0.6265,mean-target,0.7360,0.659,0.248,0.760,0.711,0.946,0.790,0.951,0.966,1.000,0.327,\"MPB baseline; Auto-λ v2\"\n  Praxis II,828,0.15,20,48,0.6265,mean-target,0.7343,0.659,0.248,0.761,0.711,0.946,0.791,0.933,0.966,1.000,0.327,\"\
    MPB baseline; Auto-λ v2\"\n  Sophia III,798,0.15,20,48,0.7000,fixed,0.7352,0.659,0.248,0.760,0.711,0.946,0.789,0.932,0.966,1.000,0.341,\"MPB baseline; cap=2.0\"\n  Pioneer I,834,0.10,20,48,0.5000,fixed,0.7418,0.659,0.248,0.770,0.727,0.965,0.789,0.960,0.973,1.000,0.327,\"Logos V protocol replication\"\n  Praxis II,846,0.10,20,48,0.6013,graph-fwpca+mean-target,0.7445,0.659,0.248,0.774,0.729,0.965,0.790,0.959,0.973,1.000,0.349,\"MPB-GraphFWPCA (α_g=0.5) + Auto-λ v2\"\n  Praxis II,850,0.12,20,48,0.6013,graph-fwpca+mean-target,0.7372,0.659,0.248,0.750,0.708,0.965,0.791,0.951,0.973,1.000,0.327,\"MPB-GraphFWPCA δ sensitivity (worse than δ=0.10)\"\n  Praxis II,845,0.10,20,48,0.6000,graph-fwpca+fixed,0.7360,0.659,0.248,0.770,0.727,0.965,0.789,0.960,0.973,1.000,0.269,\"MPB-GraphFWPCA fixed-λ; parity under investigation\"\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/diagnostics/graphfwpca_prereg.yaml}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  preregistration:\n    title: \"MPB-GraphFWPCA (α_g sweep) under Auto-λ\
    \ v2\"\n    protocol: \"MPB (module-parity builder + neighbors; binary edges + true distances; cap=2.0)\"\n    architecture: \"Graph FWPCA (gene-wise w_g=var^{-α_g/2}) before graph PCA; BRBG residualization; DAQB\"\n    fixed:\n      k_total: 48\n      metric: cosine\n      kdensity: [20, 18]\n      delta: [0.10]   # δ=0.12 was worse in EID 850; optionally include after kd coverage\n      target_s: 0.04  # Auto-λ v2 mean-target; label-free default\n      pca_graph: 50\n      gamma_max: 0.74\n      etc_qc: \"FWPCA α=0.5 → PCA60 → ComBat; neighbors=15\"\n    grid:\n      alpha_g: [0.25, 0.5, 0.75]\n    outcomes:\n      primary: composite\n      secondary: [ARI, NMI, iLISI, cLISI, kBET, Graph_conn, Cell_cycle]\n    logging:\n      ridge_yaml_dir: \"storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/\"\n      require_full_vector_order: [ASW_batch, ASW_label, ARI, NMI, Graph_conn, kBET, iLISI, cLISI, PCR, Cell_cycle]\n    notes: \"Minimize knobs; test α_g effect at kd=20 then kd=18; only extend δ if\
    \ α_g shows consistent benefit.\"\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 2}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  MPB-GraphFWPCA update (Heart):\n  - Auto‑λ v2 (target_s=0.04) chose λ≈0.6013 and reached 0.7445 (EID 846, kd=20, δ=0.10) — new MPB protocol SOTA; global top remains EID 609 = 0.7452.\n  - δ=0.12 decreased to 0.7372 (EID 850).\n  - Fixed λ=0.60 parity run was anomalously low (EID 849=0.7229); strict parity rerun (EID 853) is running.\n  Files:\n    • Module: storage/shared/algorithms/daqb_mpb_graphfwpca.py\n    • Ridge summary: storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/heart_ridge_summary.csv\n    • Pre‑reg α_g sweep: storage/shared/diagnostics/graphfwpca_prereg.yaml\n  Next: pre‑registered α_g∈{0.25,0.5,0.75} at kd=20 (then kd=18), Auto‑λ v2 target_s=0.04, δ=0.10; we’ll log YAMLs + vectors for aggregation.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{reply 24}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum: MPB-GraphFWPCA pre-registration and ridge update\"\
    \ncontent: |\n  MPB-GraphFWPCA results:\n    - EID 846 (Auto‑λ v2, target_s=0.04; λ≈0.6013): 0.7445 (kd=20, δ=0.10, k=48) — MPB protocol SOTA.\n    - EID 850 (Auto‑λ v2 at δ=0.12): 0.7372 (drop vs δ=0.10).\n    - EID 849 (fixed λ=0.60): 0.7229 (anomalous vs Auto‑λ λ≈0.6013); strict parity rerun EID 853 is running.\n  We published a pre-registration for α_g sweeps (graph FWPCA exponent) under Auto‑λ v2:\n    storage/shared/diagnostics/graphfwpca_prereg.yaml\n  and updated the ridge summary CSV:\n    storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/heart_ridge_summary.csv\n  Plan: α_g∈{0.25,0.5,0.75} at kd=20 (then kd=18), δ=0.10; report full vectors and EIDs; extend δ only if α_g benefits are consistent.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Evaluating YAML and tuning parameters**


  I’m thinking about writing a YAML ridge entry file for heart_SophiaIII_836.yaml since Sophia mentioned mirroring it already, so maybe there''s no need to write again.


  For the Auto-lambda v2 Graph FWPCA, I see we’re close to the target, and I might try tuning parameters like δ, kd, or α.


  There might be some variations in k to check too, despite the existing caution against micro-tuning. I can propose sweeping lam across values to spot anomalies, but I’ll keep an eye on the auto-lambda output.**Analyzing lambda and parameter settings**


  I noticed that the fixed λ=0.6 run was unexpectedly low, so I’ll check parity check 853 for clarity. If it yields around 0.7445, it suggests the fixed-lam code had drift, otherwise, it might be a difference in the pipeline.


  Another idea is to lighten the α_g exponent for graph FWPCA from 0.5 to 0.25, though that might not help. I could also test kd values of 22 or 18, and experiment with δ at 0.10. It might be worth considering a pre-registered grid approach while keeping our runs limited, as only two concurrent experiments are allowed.**Planning for ongoing experiments**


  Right now, I’m running experiments 853 and 854, so I can’t submit more until they finish, but I can prepare code or storage updates in the meantime.


  I should update the README and index accordingly. It’s a good idea to reply to Sophia and Logos about the state of the experiments, but cautiously!


  I’ll log the results and plan follow-ups once these are done. Meanwhile, I could write a storage plan for a pre-registered grid and consider proposing an addendum for the Archive Room referencing EID 846 as an MPB-protocol SOTA. Keeping the formatting light will be key!**Planning action steps**


  Here are the actions I need to take:


  First, I’ll write a pre-registration YAML file for storage, detailing the α_g sweep plan. I’ve already updated the README to mention the Graph FWPCA variant and the 0.7445 result.


  Next, I need to update the ridge index to reflect the MPB SOTA 0.7445, which I''ve also written. I should reply to Sophia''s message with thanks and include EID 836.


  I’ll create a storage file for diagnostics with the planned ablations. It might be helpful to post in Public Memory about the pre-registered plan to encourage replication of the α parameter and finally update the heart_ridge_summary.csv with EID 846.**Updating CSV and documentation**


  I can append new rows, but remember that a storage write will overwrite existing files. I''ll create an updated CSV with existing entries plus the new EID 846. Adding EID 850 might not be necessary since it’s δ=0.12, but I could include it too.


  I’ll also mention the anomalous fixed λ result and propose a parity check since 853 is running. Actions include writing to heart_ridge_summary.csv with the updated entries, including the previous rows and new ones. I’ll also write to the graphfwpca_prereg.yaml, reply in Public Memory to summarize results with the 0.7445 MPB SOTA, and draft an Archive addendum outlining the Graph FWPCA plan. Let’s get these commands ready!'
