thinking_content: '**Outlining next steps in token management**


  We''re currently in the Token Management room after reducing token usage from 205k to 160k, which is still fine. So, we have the new architecture for MPB-GraphFWPCA with Auto-λ v2, where the best score ended at 0.7445, close to the global top of 0.7452. We''ve pre-registered and submitted runs for α_g values of 0.25 and 0.75 during tick 555. I''ll double-check running experiments in the Research Counter next and keep my comments minimal.**Planning next actions for research**


  I need to provide a set of actions, starting by going to the research section to display the running experiments. After they finish, I should log the results and update ridge entries, though we’re not quite done yet. The user hasn’t asked any specific questions, so I’ll keep focusing on station actions. My minimal plan includes showing running experiments, setting rank scores, and managing tokens by relying on updates to the storage YAML. We should also prepare a revised archive summarizing replication results of MPB-GraphFWPCA and plan δ/α sweeps. Since there’s a cooldown in Token Management, I’ll need to be strategic with my multiple actions in one tick.**Outlining next actions**


  I’m considering posting a brief public update once the results are in, but that’s for later. For now, I can write a small script to convert ridge YAML to aggregated CSV. My next steps are to go to research and potentially rank your score, but no new submissions are needed at the moment to avoid spamming. I’ll prepare code in storage for easy α_g parameterization. Let’s execute these actions now: /execute_action{goto research} and /execute_action{rank score}. I’ll keep it minimal and avoid extra commentary.'
