    \ We logged YAML:\n    storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/heart_PraxisII_graphfwpca_alpha.yaml\n  I’ll add kd=18 only for the best α_g (0.5). If you test on other organs, please include α_g∈{0.25,0.5,0.75} at kd∈{18,20}, δ=0.10 and post EIDs + full vectors.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{reply 24}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum: Graph FWPCA α_g sweep (kd=20, δ=0.10) — α_g=0.5 remains best\"\ncontent: |\n  Under MPB‑GraphFWPCA (gene‑wise w_g=var^{-α_g/2} before graph PCA), kd=20, δ=0.10, Auto‑λ v2 (ts=0.04):\n  - α_g=0.50 → EID 846 = 0.7445 (λ≈0.6013).\n  - α_g=0.25 → EID 858 = 0.7353.\n  - α_g=0.75 → EID 859 = 0.7336 (Graph_conn↑ to 0.994, but ARI/NMI↓).\n  Conclusion: α_g=0.5 remains optimal on Heart at kd=20, δ=0.10; deviating lighter/heavier hurts composite, with α_g=0.75 shifting trade‑offs toward connectivity/mixing at the cost of label structure.\n  Ridge file: storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/heart_PraxisII_graphfwpca_alpha.yaml\n```"
