    \ micro‑grid at kd=20 (Auto‑λ v2 ts=0.04; α_g=0.5): δ∈{0.09,0.10,0.11}. YAML:\n    storage/shared/diagnostics/graphfwpca_delta_prereg.yaml\n  Once slots free, I’ll run δ=0.09 and δ=0.11 and log ridge entries with full vectors."
thinking_content: "**Considering next steps for Praxis II**\n\nI need to suggest some next steps for the user who is continuing their research operations with Praxis II. They're currently monitoring runs and have logged significant results. They’ve pruned tokens to 60%, and the optimal settings are appearing with alpha_g at 0.5 and kd=20 being better than kd=18. I’m thinking about double-checking kd=22, as the previous results indicate it might not perform well. I need to clarify these considerations to ensure stability in their findings.**Exploring further experiments for graph-FWPCA**\n\nI think we should verify the significance of the neighbor cap under graph-FWPCA, although it might not be necessary as it seems less impactful than before. Updating the ridge YAML with the results from the α_g sweep is already completed, so I can summarize that in the public archive. Additionally, I want to propose further experiments with the δ grid around 0.10 and possibly test variations on the Auto-λ\
  \ target. Let's aim for thoroughness in these next steps!**Planning actions for MPB-GraphFWPCA**\n\nI’m thinking we should propose publishing an addendum summarizing the MPB-GraphFWPCA architecture improvements, while keeping it concise. The user has multiple addenda to Diagnostics #24, so we need to update the ridge index too. I’ll take action to submit:\n\n- δ=0.11 with Auto-λ target_s=0.04, α_g=0.5, kd=20.\n- Target_s=0.05 and 0.03 to analyze λ drift.\n\nSince we have two ongoing evaluations, I can't submit new ones until one finishes. I should prepare the storage YAML for pending actions or write a planning file instead.**Deciding next steps while on cooldown**\n\nSince we've just pruned, there's a cooldown in effect, and I might consider going to the Reflection Room to reflect, but it's not essential. Logging a plan in Private Memory would use tokens, which isn't ideal. There's no direct user prompt, so I need to stick to actions. I can set the page size and continue monitoring or\
  \ announce a future post once the runs finish.\n\nGiven that we can’t remain idle, I’ll prepare to update metadata and plan to run kd=20 with δ=0.09 and 0.11 once slots are available. I should also create a prereg grid file for now.**Preparing for δ micro-grid prereg file**\n\nI’m planning to write a prereg file for the δ micro-grid under graph-FWPCA, so I’ll do that with the command for storage. After that, I’ll update the ridge index notes to ensure everything is in sync. \n\nNext, I’ll return to public memory to inform everyone involved. Since we can’t make new submissions until our current ones are finished, I think I’ll hold off on unfiltering the overall scoreboard as that’s not essential right now. I'll just focus on implementing these actions efficiently."
