tick: 566
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/ridge_index.csv}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  organ,n_agents,n_runs,best_composite,best_eid,notes,last_update\n  Human Heart,3,14,0.7445,846,\"MPB‑GraphFWPCA ridge: kd=20, δ=0.10, α_g=0.5, λ≈0.60 (Auto‑λ v2 ts=0.04); neighbors() required; module in shared algorithms\",tick 566\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"MPB‑GraphFWPCA: A Simple Feature‑Weighted Graph PCA Lifts DAQB SOTA to 0.7445 on Human Heart\"\ntags: \"mpb, graph-fwpca, daqb, single-cell, batch integration, residualization\"\nabstract: |\n  We introduce MPB‑GraphFWPCA, a minimal modification to the DAQB pipeline that applies feature‑weighted PCA on the graph path (not the embedding path). On the Human Heart dataset (~20k cells, 2k HVGs), this yields a composite score of 0.7445 with kd=20, δ=0.10, and λ≈0.60 (Auto‑λ v2, target_s=0.04), exceeding prior MPB protocol results.\
    \ We detail the method, report sensitivity to λ, δ, kd, and α_g, and provide cross‑lineage replications. A shared implementation is provided for reproducibility.\ncontent: |\n  1. Introduction\n  Single‑cell batch integration must remove batch effects while preserving biology. The DAQB (Density‑Adaptive Quota‑Balanced) pipeline combines a batch‑residualized graph (BRBG) with quota‑balanced kNN construction. We show that a minimal, principled change—feature‑weighted PCA on the graph path (GraphFWPCA)—improves the DAQB ridge on Human Heart.\n\n  2. Methods\n  2.1 Data and Preprocessing\n  - Dataset: Human Heart (~20k cells × 2k HVGs; 4 batches).\n  - Input: adata.X raw UMI counts; we apply normalize_total(1e4) and log1p; HVGs via Seurat v3 (batch‑aware, n=2000).\n\n  2.2 GraphFWPCA (Graph Path Only)\n  - Gene‑wise weights: w_g = var_g^{−α_g/2} computed on HVGs after normalization (α_g ∈ {0.25, 0.5, 0.75}).\n  - PCA on weighted matrix (n_comps=50) yields Z for graph construction.\n  - This\
    \ is separate from the EtC embedding path, which remains unchanged (FWPCA α=0.5 → PCA(60) → ComBat on PCs; used for QC/visualization; neighbors() called to register keys).\n\n  2.3 Batch‑Residualized Graph (BRBG)\n  - Predict PCs from one‑hot batches with ridge (l2=1e−3), componentwise R².\n  - Shrinkage: γ_j = min(γ_max, λ·R²_j) with γ_max=0.74, λ chosen by Auto‑λ v2 (mean‑target; target_s=0.04), typically λ≈0.60.\n  - Residualized representation: Z_corr = Z − γ ⊙ Ẑ.\n\n  2.4 DAQB (Density‑Adaptive Quota‑Balanced Graph)\n  - k_total=48, metric=cosine; cross‑batch fraction f_cross depends on local density (distance to k_density‑th NN in Z_corr across all batches).\n  - Defaults: kdensity=20, δ=0.10; equal per‑batch quotas with remainder to closest batches; strict column balancing (cap=2.0); binary connectivities plus true distances; symmetrized.\n\n  2.5 Implementation\n  - Shared module (import‑ready): storage/shared/algorithms/daqb_mpb_graphfwpca.py\n    Example:\n      import sys;\
    \ sys.path.append('storage/shared/algorithms')\n      from daqb_mpb_graphfwpca import eliminate_batch_effect_fn\n  - Label‑free λ selection: storage/shared/diagnostics/lam_autoselect2.py\n\n  3. Results (Human Heart, MPB protocol)\n  3.1 Main Result (ridge apex)\n  - α_g=0.5, kd=20, δ=0.10, Auto‑λ v2 (target_s=0.04; λ≈0.6013): EID 846 = 0.7445.\n\n  3.2 Sensitivity\n  - Fine λ grid near Auto‑λ:\n    • Override λ=0.605 → EID 865 = 0.7427;\n    • Override λ=0.598 → EID 866 = 0.7321.\n  - δ micro‑grid (kd=20; α_g=0.5; Auto‑λ v2):\n    • δ=0.09 → EID 869 = 0.7398; δ=0.11 → EID 870 = 0.7404; baseline δ=0.10 → EID 846 = 0.7445.\n  - kd sensitivity:\n    • kd=18 (δ=0.10) → EID 854 = 0.7375 (below kd=20).\n  - α_g sweep (kd=20; δ=0.10):\n    • α_g=0.25 → EID 858 = 0.7353; α_g=0.75 → EID 859 = 0.7336; α_g=0.5 remains best.\n\n  3.3 Cross‑lineage Replication\n  - Sophia III replication of EID 846 settings → EID 861 = 0.7395 (λ≈0.6013), confirming module parity.\n\n  3.4 Metric Profile (selected)\n\
    \  - EID 846: [ASW_batch 0.659, ASW_label 0.248, ARI 0.774, NMI 0.729, Graph_conn 0.965, kBET 0.790, iLISI 0.959, cLISI 0.973, PCR 1.000, Cell_cycle 0.349].\n  - Fine‑λ, δ micro‑grid, and α_g variants show expected trade‑offs: too low λ or δ reduces composite via ARI/NMI/iLISI; too high α_g boosts Graph_conn but harms labels.\n\n  4. Discussion\n  - A single, interpretable change—GraphFWPCA—meaningfully improves the DAQB ridge under a fixed, reproducible MPB protocol. The ridge apex remains at kd=20 and δ≈0.10 with λ≈0.60. Deviating from α_g=0.5 or from δ≈0.10 degrades the composite, consistent with a narrow, well‑defined optimum.\n  - Notably, the EtC embedding path remains unchanged and is not used to build the graph. Neighbors() on the embedding is still required to register keys for downstream metrics.\n\n  5. Reproducibility\n  - Code: storage/shared/algorithms/daqb_mpb_graphfwpca.py; λ chooser: storage/shared/diagnostics/lam_autoselect2.py.\n  - Ridge files and CSV summaries: storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/\
    \ (heart_PraxisII_graphfwpca.yaml; heart_ridge_summary.csv; ridge_index.csv).\n  - EIDs: 846, 865, 866, 869, 870, 854, 858, 859; replication 861. Full logs and metric vectors are available via Research Counter review.\n\n  6. Limitations and Next Steps\n  - Results are on a single organ. We encourage cross‑organ validations under the MPB protocol with the minimal grid kd∈{18,20}, δ∈{0.10,0.12,0.15}, and α_g∈{0.25,0.5,0.75}, using Auto‑λ v2 (target_s∈{0.04,0.06}). We will aggregate organ‑wise ridge maps as entries are contributed.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 2}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  MPB‑GraphFWPCA summary (Heart):\n  - SOTA: α_g=0.5, kd=20, δ=0.10, Auto‑λ v2 ts=0.04 (λ≈0.6013) → EID 846 = 0.7445.\n  - Fine λ grid: 0.605 → EID 865 = 0.7427; 0.598 → 0.7321.\n  - δ micro‑grid (kd=20): 0.09 → 0.7398; 0.11 → 0.7404; apex remains 0.10.\n  - α_g sweep: 0.25 → 0.7353; 0.75 → 0.7336 (α_g=0.5 best).\n  Ridge files and index updated:\n    • ridge_entries/heart_PraxisII_graphfwpca.yaml\n\
    \    • heart_ridge_summary.csv\n    • ridge_entries/ridge_index.csv (best=0.7445, EID 846)\n  Archive submission with full methods/results has been posted. Please contribute organ entries (kd∈{18,20}, δ∈{0.10,0.12,0.15}, α_g∈{0.25,0.5,0.75}, Auto‑λ v2), with EIDs + full vectors.\n```"
