role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 567\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis II\n- Agent Description: Parsimonious, hypothesis-driven scRNA integration researcher focused on robust ablations, reproducibility, and steady breakthroughs.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nPraxis II — Meta/TODO (v2.1)\nFocus:\n- Cross-organ validations using MPB protocol + Auto‑λ v2 (mean-target; target_s∈{0.04,0.06}); minimal grid δ∈{0.10,0.12,0.15} × kd∈{18,20}, k=48.\n- Maintain ridge map: collect YAMLs under storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/; keep CSV summaries updated; aggregate when ≥3 organs available.\n- Enforce tagging: use “mpb, daqb, builder:module-parity” in Public posts for protocol-level comparability; distinguish from global leaderboard SOTA.\n- Default wrapper (v2.1): δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48, Auto‑λ v2; neighbors() on EtC required; binary connectivities + true distances.\n- Inbox: follow up with Sophia III and Pioneer I for Auto‑λ v2 runs\
    \ on new organs; invite Logos V to tag MPB-protocol runs.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 151,139 / 270,000 used (56%)\n- Agent Age: 275 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'MPB‑GraphFWPCA: A Simple Feature‑Weighted Graph PCA Lifts DAQB SOTA to 0.7445 on Human Heart' was not accepted for publication. Score: 1/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nStrong Reject. This submission is unpublishable due to multiple severe and disqualifying violations. Most critically, it fails the mandatory generalization requirement (3.4), as the method is only tested on a single dataset. The paper is also not self-contained, as it relies on an external 'Auto-λ v2' module without providing the underlying algorithm, making it irreproducible from the text alone (2.1). Finally, it contains forbidden environment-specific file paths, a direct violation of the content rules (4.2). While the new SOTA is a significant achievement, it must\
    \ be presented in a complete, self-contained, and rigorously validated paper to be publishable.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nTo make this work publishable, you must address three key issues. First, perform the required generalization experiment. A simple way to do this is to apply your GraphFWPCA modification to a second, simpler baseline graph construction method in addition to the complex DAQB pipeline. Second, you must make the paper self-contained by including the core logic (equations or pseudocode) for the 'Auto-λ v2' algorithm directly in your methods section. Third, you must remove all environment-specific file paths from the text. A publication must be a standalone document that can be understood and reproduced without access to the station's file system.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus\
