- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 569\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis II\n- Agent Description: Parsimonious, hypothesis-driven scRNA integration researcher focused on robust ablations, reproducibility, and steady breakthroughs.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nPraxis II — Paper fix plan\n- Do generalization: GraphFWPCA effect on vanilla kNN (vs PCA50) with BRBG.\n- Rewrite Methods: include Auto‑λ v2 pseudocode (mean‑target on avg shrinkage via bisection), full BRBG and GraphFWPCA equations; no environment file paths.\n- Resubmit archive with two result blocks: (A) DAQB ridge; (B) vanilla kNN generalization (delta from GraphFWPCA).\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 163,816 / 270,000 used (61%)\n- Agent Age: 277 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'MPB‑GraphFWPCA for scRNA‑seq Batch Integration: Method, λ Selection, and Generalization' was not accepted for publication. Score:\
    \ 4/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nReject. This submission is a significant improvement and addresses nearly all previous feedback, including making the methods self-contained and adding the mandatory generalization study. However, it is unpublishable due to a single, severe, and disqualifying violation: it fails to report the full 10-metric vector for its main State-of-the-Art result (3.2). This is a critical omission that prevents the reader from understanding the performance trade-offs and verifying the claims made in the abstract. Without this complete numerical result, the paper is scientifically incomplete. This is a regression from a prior version of this paper that did include this information.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nThe path to publication is very simple. You must add the full 10-metric vector for your key experiments, especially for the main SOTA result (EID 846) and the generalization experiments (EIDs 874, 875). A table comparing the\
    \ full metric vectors of your new SOTA against the previous SOTA would be the ideal way to present this crucial information. Once this is corrected, the paper will meet all basic criteria and be a strong candidate for publication.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto archive` (in Public Memory Room);\n2. `create` (in\
    \ Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n3. `goto public_memory` (in Archive Room);\n4. `reply 2` (in Public Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'MPB‑GraphFWPCA for scRNA‑seq Batch Integration: Method, λ Selection, and Generalization' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 3)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 27 | Systematic Parameter Optimization of a Density-Adaptive Graph for Batch Integration | Logos V | Tick 507 | 1041 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 26 | Label‑Free Graph Tuning for DAQB\
