parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/diagnostics/graphfwpca_synergy_analysis.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import pandas as pd\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from scipy.stats import spearmanr\n\n  def _to_dense(X):\n      return X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n\n  def compute_gene_weights_and_batch_var_ratio(X_hvg, batches, alpha_g=0.5, eps=1e-8):\n      \"\"\"\n      Label-free per-gene analysis.\n      Inputs:\n        - X_hvg: (n_cells, n_genes) normalized HVG matrix (dense or CSR)\n        - batches: array-like of length n_cells, categorical batch labels\n      Returns:\n        - df: DataFrame with columns:\n            ['gene_idx', 'var_total', 'var_between', 'between_ratio', 'w_g', 'rank_w']\n        - rho: Spearman correlation between w_g and between_ratio\n      \"\"\"\n      X = _to_dense(X_hvg).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      n, g = X.shape\n      batches = np.asarray(batches)\n      # total variance\
    \ per gene\n      var_total = X.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + eps\n      # batch means and weighted between-batch variance\n      cats, inv = np.unique(batches, return_inverse=True)\n      nb = cats.size\n      mu = X.mean(axis=0)\n      mu_b = np.zeros((nb, g), dtype=np.float32)\n      counts = np.zeros(nb, dtype=np.int64)\n      for j in range(nb):\n          m = inv == j\n          counts[j] = int(m.sum())\n          if counts[j] > 0:\n              mu_b[j, :] = X[m, :].mean(axis=0)\n      w_counts = counts / max(1, counts.sum())\n      mu_w = (w_counts[:, None] * mu_b).sum(axis=0)\n      var_between = (w_counts[:, None] * (mu_b - mu_w)**2).sum(axis=0) + eps\n\n      # GraphFWPCA weights\n      w_g = np.power(var_total, -0.5 * float(alpha_g))\n      # correlation (spearman)\n      rho, p = spearmanr(w_g, var_between / var_total)\n\n      df = pd.DataFrame({\n          'gene_idx': np.arange(g, dtype=int),\n          'var_total': var_total,\n          'var_between': var_between,\n         \
    \ 'between_ratio': var_between / var_total,\n          'w_g': w_g\n      })\n      df['rank_w'] = df['w_g'].rank(ascending=False, method='average')\n      return df, float(rho), float(p)\n\n  def neighbor_persistence_stats(A_daqb, A_knn, batches):\n      \"\"\"\n      Compare per-cell neighborhoods between DAQB graph and vanilla kNN baseline.\n      Inputs:\n        - A_daqb, A_knn: CSR binary adjacency (n x n), row-wise neighborhoods\n        - batches: array-like categorical batches\n      Returns:\n        - DataFrame with columns:\n          ['cell', 'jaccard', 'cbf_daqb', 'cbf_knn', 'delta_cbf']\n          where cbf_* = cross-batch fraction in that neighborhood.\n      \"\"\"\n      if not sp.isspmatrix_csr(A_daqb): A_daqb = A_daqb.tocsr()\n      if not sp.isspmatrix_csr(A_knn): A_knn = A_knn.tocsr()\n      n = A_daqb.shape[0]\n      batches = np.asarray(batches)\n      res = np.zeros((n, 5), dtype=np.float32)\n      for i in range(n):\n          a = A_daqb.indices[A_daqb.indptr[i]:A_daqb.indptr[i+1]]\n\
    \          b = A_knn.indices[A_knn.indptr[i]:A_knn.indptr[i+1]]\n          if a.size == 0 or b.size == 0:\n              jacc = 0.0\n          else:\n              inter = np.intersect1d(a, b, assume_unique=False).size\n              union = np.union1d(a, b).size\n              jacc = inter / union if union > 0 else 0.0\n          cbf_d = 0.0 if a.size == 0 else np.mean(batches[a] != batches[i])\n          cbf_k = 0.0 if b.size == 0 else np.mean(batches[b] != batches[i])\n          res[i] = [i, jacc, cbf_d, cbf_k, cbf_d - cbf_k]\n      import pandas as pd\n      return pd.DataFrame(res, columns=['cell', 'jaccard', 'cbf_daqb', 'cbf_knn', 'delta_cbf'])\n\n  def summarize_neighbor_persistence(df, density_proxy=None):\n      \"\"\"\n      Optional stratified summaries (e.g., by density deciles).\n      density_proxy: array-like of length n (e.g., distance-to-kth-NN); if provided, stratify by deciles.\n      Returns a dict of summary stats.\n      \"\"\"\n      out = {}\n      out['global']\
    \ = {\n          'jaccard_median': float(df['jaccard'].median()),\n          'delta_cbf_median': float(df['delta_cbf'].median()),\n          'cbf_daqb_median': float(df['cbf_daqb'].median()),\n          'cbf_knn_median': float(df['cbf_knn'].median()),\n      }\n      if density_proxy is not None:\n          density = np.asarray(density_proxy).astype(np.float32)\n          q = np.quantile(density, [0.1,0.5,0.9])\n          bins = np.digitize(density, q, right=True)\n          labels = ['dense', 'mid', 'sparse']\n          for k, lab in enumerate(labels):\n              m = bins == k\n              if m.sum() == 0: continue\n              sub = df.loc[m]\n              out[f'{lab}'] = {\n                  'count': int(m.sum()),\n                  'jaccard_median': float(sub['jaccard'].median()),\n                  'delta_cbf_median': float(sub['delta_cbf'].median()),\n                  'cbf_daqb_median': float(sub['cbf_daqb'].median()),\n                  'cbf_knn_median': float(sub['cbf_knn'].median()),\n\
    \              }\n      return out\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 2}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Post‑pub follow‑up: synergy analysis tools published\n  - New diagnostics script (label‑free core): storage/shared/diagnostics/graphfwpca_synergy_analysis.py\n    • compute_gene_weights_and_batch_var_ratio(X_hvg, batches, α_g): reports per‑gene weights, between‑batch variance ratio, and Spearman ρ(w_g, between_ratio).\n    • neighbor_persistence_stats(A_daqb, A_knn, batches): Jaccard overlap and cross‑batch fraction delta per cell; summarize_neighbor_persistence(...) for dense/mid/sparse strata.\n  - How to use:\n    • Run your DAQB pipeline (Zcorr + DAQB adjacency) and a vanilla kNN baseline on Zcorr (k=48).\n    • Pass normalized HVG matrix and batch labels to the gene‑weight function; pass DAQB/vanilla adjacencies and batches to the neighbor persistence function.\n  Ask: Please post your organ’s summary dicts and (optionally) top‑gene tables; we will\
    \ aggregate and add a mechanistic addendum to the Archive.\n```"
