tick: 572
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Synergy diagnostics (test): GraphFWPCA gene-weight vs batch-variance and DAQB vs vanilla kNN neighbor persistence\"\ntags: \"graph-fwpca, diagnostics, daqb, knn, residualization, batch-variance, neighbor-persistence\"\nabstract: \"Label-free analysis (test mode) to probe why GraphFWPCA synergizes with DAQB. We compute: (1) Spearman correlation between GraphFWPCA gene weights and between-batch variance ratios; (2) per-cell neighbor persistence and cross-batch fraction deltas between DAQB and vanilla kNN graphs on Zcorr. Outputs are printed as JSON summaries.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json\n  import numpy as np\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n  from scipy.stats import spearmanr\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\n  def _to_dense(X):\n\
    \      return X.A if sp.isspmatrix(X) else X\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum=1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_graph_fwpca(X, hv_mask, alpha_g=0.5, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xh = X[:, hv_mask] if hv_mask is not None else X\n      Xd = _to_dense(Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * float(alpha_g)).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw = Xd * w\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xw)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca'], w, var_g\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      B = np.zeros((batches.shape[0], cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n\
    \      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      return B @ W\n\n  def _choose_lambda_from_r2_mean(Z, batches, gamma_max=0.74, s_target=0.04, l2=1e-3, lam_min=0.2, lam_max=1.0, iters=32, tol=1e-4):\n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Z.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      lo, hi = lam_min, lam_max\n      for _ in range(iters):\n          mid = 0.5 * (lo + hi)\n          gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, mid * R2)\n          s_bar = float(gamma.mean() / gamma_max)\n          if abs(s_bar - s_target) <= tol:\n              return mid\n          if s_bar < s_target:\n              lo = mid\n          else:\n              hi = mid\n      return 0.5 * (lo + hi)\n\n  def _neighbor_persistence(A_daqb,\
    \ A_knn, batches):\n      if not sp.isspmatrix_csr(A_daqb): A_daqb = A_daqb.tocsr()\n      if not sp.isspmatrix_csr(A_knn): A_knn = A_knn.tocsr()\n      n = A_daqb.shape[0]\n      batches = np.asarray(batches)\n      jacc = np.zeros(n, dtype=np.float32)\n      cbf_d = np.zeros(n, dtype=np.float32)\n      cbf_k = np.zeros(n, dtype=np.float32)\n      for i in range(n):\n          ai = A_daqb.indices[A_daqb.indptr[i]:A_daqb.indptr[i+1]]\n          bi = A_knn.indices[A_knn.indptr[i]:A_knn.indptr[i+1]]\n          if ai.size == 0 or bi.size == 0:\n              jacc[i] = 0.0\n          else:\n              inter = np.intersect1d(ai, bi, assume_unique=False).size\n              union = np.union1d(ai, bi).size\n              jacc[i] = inter / union if union > 0 else 0.0\n          cbf_d[i] = 0.0 if ai.size == 0 else np.mean(batches[ai] != batches[i])\n          cbf_k[i] = 0.0 if bi.size == 0 else np.mean(batches[bi] != batches[i])\n      delta_cbf = cbf_d - cbf_k\n      return {\n          'jaccard_median':\
    \ float(np.median(jacc)),\n          'jaccard_mean': float(np.mean(jacc)),\n          'cbf_daqb_median': float(np.median(cbf_d)),\n          'cbf_knn_median': float(np.median(cbf_k)),\n          'delta_cbf_median': float(np.median(delta_cbf)),\n          'delta_cbf_mean': float(np.mean(delta_cbf)),\n      }\n\n  def test(adata: ad.AnnData):\n      # Config (MPB-GraphFWPCA path)\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      alpha_g = 0.5\n      gamma_max = 0.74\n      s_target = 0.04\n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      kdensity = 20\n      delta = 0.10\n\n      # Normalize + HVGs\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      # GraphFWPCA Z + weights, and batch variance ratios\n      Zg, w_g, var_g = _pca_graph_fwpca(adata.X, hv_mask=hv, alpha_g=alpha_g,\
    \ n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n      Xh = _to_dense(adata.X[:, hv]).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      cats, inv = np.unique(batches, return_inverse=True)\n      nb = cats.size\n      mu = Xh.mean(axis=0)\n      mu_b = np.stack([Xh[inv == j].mean(axis=0) if np.any(inv == j) else np.zeros_like(mu) for j in range(nb)], axis=0)\n      w_counts = np.bincount(inv, minlength=nb).astype(np.float32); w_counts /= max(1, w_counts.sum())\n      mu_w = (w_counts[:, None] * mu_b).sum(axis=0)\n      var_between = (w_counts[:, None] * (mu_b - mu_w)**2).sum(axis=0) + 1e-8\n      between_ratio = var_between / (var_g + 1e-8)\n      rho, p = spearmanr(w_g, between_ratio)\n\n      # Residualize (BRBG) and choose lambda\n      lam = _choose_lambda_from_r2_mean(Zg, batches, gamma_max=gamma_max, s_target=s_target, l2=1e-3)\n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=1e-3)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0,\
    \ ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      # Density proxy: distance to kdensity-th NN (all-batch)\n      nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=kdensity + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n      nn.fit(Zcorr)\n      d_all, idx_all = nn.kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n      d_k = d_all[:, -1]\n\n      # Build DAQB graph on Zcorr\n      Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                           k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                           delta=delta, k_density=kdensity, rng_seed=0)\n      # Build vanilla kNN on Zcorr\n      adata.obsm['X_graph'] = Zcorr.astype(np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_graph', n_neighbors=k_total, metric=metric)\n      C_knn = adata.obsp['connectivities'].tocsr().astype(np.float32)\n\n      # Summaries\n      neighbor_summary\
    \ = _neighbor_persistence(Cg, C_knn, batches=batches)\n      out = {\n          'alpha_g': alpha_g,\n          'lambda_selected': float(lam),\n          'spearman_w_vs_between_ratio': {'rho': float(rho), 'p': float(p)},\n          'neighbor_persistence': neighbor_summary,\n          'density_proxy_stats': {'dk_median': float(np.median(d_k)), 'dk_mean': float(np.mean(d_k))},\n      }\n      print(json.dumps(out, indent=2))\n      return \"synergy_diagnostics_completed\"\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning next steps**\n\nI'm thinking that we have already created the synergy analysis script and shared instructions. Now, I should pre-register the synergy experiments in archive capsule #28, along with a YAML file for preregistration. It's also important to adjust Token Management since 63% of tokens are used, which seems unnecessary. I can update capsule #28's message regarding data availability but remember I can't mention the environment path. Alternatively, I could run a label-free analysis for further testing.**Executing diagnostic plans**\n\nI think we can quickly run label-free synergy diagnostics, focusing on gene weights versus between-batch variance ratios. To compute neighbor persistence, both DAQB and vanilla graphs are needed, so I’ll compute those and print the stats within a single evaluation. The 'test' function will override evaluation and score as NaN, but that’s okay since we can record outputs in logs.\n\nFor our Research Counter submission, we\
  \ should write code to compute normalized HVGs, Zcorr with GraphFWPCA, and build the DAQB graph using a custom builder.**Building DAQB code**\n\nI’m contemplating whether to depend on external modules or keep the test self-contained, but writing DAQB code seems heavy. Instead, I can create both neighbor persistence calculations by comparing knn on Zcorr with quota balancing. We want to focus specifically on examining synergy with DAQB, and I can import the existing DAQB code from the storage path.\n\nFor the test submission, I can build GraphFWPCA with Zcorr, choose λ via bisection, and create DAQB adjacency by importing from the necessary storage paths.**Crafting submission**\n\nI'm planning to create a submission titled \"Synergy diagnostics (test): gene-weight/batch-variance correlation and neighbor persistence for DAQB vs vanilla kNN.\" I’ll use the 'test' function to override evaluation and print results. I need to import 'build_density_adaptive_bbsg' and 'neighbors' from Scanpy.\
  \ \n\nWe’ll compute normalized HVGs, use GraphFWPCA, choose λ via bisection, and compute Zcorr while also getting DAQB and vanilla adjacency. Finally, I’ll calculate the Spearman correlation and summarize neighbor persistence, outputting everything in JSON. I'll embed this code in the submission instead of relying on reading from a storage file.**Implementing DAQB builder**\n\nI want to make sure I don't mention environment paths, but importing from storage/praxis is fine for research code. While implementing a minimal DAQB builder might take time, I can import 'build_density_adaptive_bbsg' from the appropriate storage since it's already there. \n\nI'll add the necessary path and import it. Edges may be heavy, but I think I can manage that. After submitting the synergy test, I should provide an update in archive #28 letting them know the diagnostics are queued. Let's finalize these steps!"
