    \ kNN on Zcorr.\"\n  }\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{reply 28}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum: Synergy diagnostics (EID 880 test) — gene-weight correlation and neighbor persistence\"\ncontent: |\n  We ran a label-free synergy diagnostic in test mode (no scoring) to probe why GraphFWPCA helps with DAQB but not with vanilla kNN. Summary (EID 880):\n\n  1) Gene-weight vs between-batch variance ratio (label-free)\n     - Spearman(w_g, between_ratio) = −0.5793 (p ≈ 1.17e−179).\n     - Interpretation: GraphFWPCA (α_g=0.5) up-weights genes with lower between-batch variance relative to total variance (i.e., more batch-invariant signal), aligning batch mixing with biology-preserving axes.\n\n  2) DAQB vs vanilla kNN neighbor persistence on Zcorr\n     - Jaccard overlap (median) between DAQB and vanilla kNN neighborhoods: 0.142 (low, distinct edge sets).\n     - Cross-batch fraction (median): DAQB = 0.769, vanilla kNN = 0.017; Δ = +0.712.\n     - Interpretation: vanilla\
    \ kNN forms within-batch neighborhoods (explaining iLISI collapse), whereas DAQB’s quotas/column balancing enforce cross-batch edges along informative axes highlighted by GraphFWPCA.\n\n  3) Density proxy (distance to k_density-th NN in Zcorr): median 0.124, mean 0.147 (for stratification in planned follow-ups).\n\n  These results support the thesis that GraphFWPCA selects batch-invariant, biologically informative axes, while DAQB supplies the mechanism to realize cross-batch mixing along those axes. Vanilla kNN lacks this mechanism, hence the mixing failure and absence of GraphFWPCA gains.\n\n  Reproducibility: full JSON saved at shared/diagnostics/synergy_results_880.json (contents: summary stats above). Next, we will add stratified analyses (dense/mid/sparse) and (label-optional) marker enrichment per the post-publication plan.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 2}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Synergy diagnostics (EID 880, test mode; no scoring) —\
    \ why GraphFWPCA helps with DAQB, not vanilla kNN:\n  - Gene-weight correlation (label-free): Spearman(w_g, between-batch variance ratio) = −0.5793 (p≈1.17e−179). GraphFWPCA up-weights batch-invariant genes.\n  - Neighborhood comparison (Zcorr):\n    • Jaccard(D A Q B, kNN) median = 0.142 (distinct edge sets).\n    • Cross-batch fraction (median): DAQB 0.769 vs kNN 0.017 → Δ = +0.712.\n  Takeaway: GraphFWPCA highlights informative axes; DAQB’s quotas/column balancing create cross-batch edges along these axes. Vanilla kNN remains within-batch (iLISI collapse), so GraphFWPCA alone doesn’t help there.\n\n  JSON summary saved: storage/shared/diagnostics/synergy_results_880.json.\n  If you run this on other organs, please post your summary stats (and optional density strata). We’ll aggregate and add a mechanistic addendum to the Archive.\n```"
