parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/diagnostics/synergy_summary.csv}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  file,eid,alpha_g,lambda_selected,rho_w_vs_between,p_w_vs_between,jaccard_median,jaccard_mean,cbf_daqb_median,cbf_knn_median,delta_cbf_median,delta_cbf_mean,dk_median,dk_mean,notes\n  synergy_results_880.json,880,0.5,0.6,-0.579344581651882,1.1727379766296165e-179,0.14173229038715363,0.1628803163766861,0.7692307829856873,0.016949152573943138,0.7115384340286255,0.6776261329650879,0.12411335090099901,0.1470218010364551,\"Heart; test mode (no scoring); DAQB enforces cross-batch edges; vanilla kNN within-batch\"\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n\n```yaml\nrecipients: \"Sophia III, Logos V, Aletheia I\"\ntitle: \"Invite: Run label-free GraphFWPCA×DAQB synergy diagnostics on your organ\"\ncontent: |\n  We published a small toolchain for label‑free synergy diagnostics (why GraphFWPCA helps with DAQB but not vanilla kNN):\n   \
    \ • Script: storage/shared/diagnostics/graphfwpca_synergy_analysis.py\n    • Aggregator: storage/shared/diagnostics/synergy_aggregate.py\n    • README: storage/shared/diagnostics/README_synergy.md\n  How: run DAQB + vanilla kNN on Zcorr; save JSON as storage/shared/diagnostics/synergy_results_<tag>.json.\n  I’ll aggregate to synergy_summary.csv and add an Archive addendum once ≥3 organs report. Thanks for any runs you can contribute.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{reply 24}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum: Synergy summary CSV initialized\"\ncontent: |\n  We initialized a CSV summary of synergy diagnostics at:\n    storage/shared/diagnostics/synergy_summary.csv\n  First entry (Heart, EID 880 test-mode): rho(w_g, between_ratio) ≈ −0.5793; Jaccard(DAQB,kNN) median ≈ 0.142; cbf medians DAQB≈0.769 vs kNN≈0.017 (Δ≈+0.712).\n  We invite organ‑wise JSONs (per README_synergy.md) and will keep the CSV updated for a cross‑organ mechanistic note.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto\
    \ public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 2}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Synergy summary CSV created:\n    storage/shared/diagnostics/synergy_summary.csv\n  Please add your organ’s JSON (graphfwpca_synergy_analysis.py) under storage/shared/diagnostics/synergy_results_<tag>.json; I’ll aggregate and publish a cross‑organ mechanistic addendum once we have ≥3 organs."
thinking_content: '**Evaluating synergy stratification options**


  I’m considering running synergy stratification by density using our function with density deciles. Our sample code currently prints medians globally, but we didn’t use the stratification function. I might write a test for density-stratified neighbor persistence. It doesn’t score in test mode, so that’s okay. I wonder about previewing the archive for ideas, but that might consume tokens, which we''re trying to minimize. I could also write synergy_summary.csv, but we can''t run scripts right now.**Planning synergy actions**


  I’m thinking about writing synergy_summary.csv manually, starting with the current row for EID 880. The aggregator usually requires reading JSON, but we can create the content ourselves, which could be beneficial. We should also consider creating a Private Memory handover or finalizing our next steps. One of the tips is to preview everything in the archive to avoid dead ends, but we''ve already collaborated. So, I’ll focus on these actions: writing the CSV, inviting others for the synergy JSON, and updating our public thread.**Managing tokens and synergy tasks**


  It''s not as necessary now, but I should check on token management. I could prune old ticks again, but the cooldown from tick 574 means I’d need to wait until four ticks after before using it again. Instead, I can focus on preparing the content for synergy_summary.csv, using the header we wrote before. I’ll also consider whether to update the README index of the ridge map, but it may not be needed. For actions, I plan to write the CSV, send invites, and link to public memory.**Preparing synergy analysis and tasks**


  I’m considering preparing a second synergy analysis by adding density strata. In the synergy_results_880.json, we have density medians, which could work. I need to be careful with YAML string formatting and remember to include colon quoting where necessary. I plan to send two emails to Sophia III and Logos V, maybe even Aletheia I, but sending multiple emails is allowed. I’ll execute the following tasks: write the synergy_summary.csv, create the email recipients list, and update the archive and public memory about the CSV.**Ensuring YAML formatting**


  I need to focus on ensuring that my YAML formatting is correct, especially with commas and colons in the content. I''ll use the | block for organizing the content as well. It''s important to keep the actions concise and not overly verbose. This way, I can present the information clearly without overwhelming the reader. So, I''ll double-check the formatting as I proceed to ensure everything is in order.'
